            "content": "# Part `ledger` (1 of 6): checks T1, F1a-F1h (ledger commands, tool stamps, writer field) and the T5/T7 refusal logic in custody_history.py, with new tests\n\nThe commission is the frozen bar below (custody/bar.md, sha256 72e92dc7580e2447f19dfff66aaac02d8484157a6283dcfdda6c7bb2de7561c6). This request covers only the part named above; the parts, in order, are `ledger`, `emitter`, `verifier`, `edi`, `docs`, `guide`. Allowed paths for this part: kit/custody_ledger.py, kit/custody_history.py, new tests/test_custody_ledger*.py.\n\n## Frozen bar: allow-list (verbatim)\n\n## Allow-list (spec)\n- **Edit:** `kit/custody_ledger.py`, `kit/emit_custody.py`, `kit/custody_history.py`, `kit/plumbline_job.py` (only to pass `--allow-hand-times` through to the emitter at close, and to run the verifier at close and refuse on failure; V8), `tests/validate_schemas.py`, `docs/custody-emission.md`, `kit/README.md`.\n- **New files only:**\n  - `tools/edi/**`;\n  - `kit/plumbline_verify.py` (V1–V9);\n  - `docs/PLUMBLINE-ORCHESTRATOR-FIELD-GUIDE.md` (item 30; the only file for that item);\n  - `schemas/x-plumbline/x-plumbline-v1.schema.json` (the only new file allowed under `schemas/`);\n  - `tests/test_edi_*.py`, `tests/test_custody_ledger*.py`, `tests/test_plumbline_verify*.py`;\n  - new folders under `tests/fixtures/custody/` (new planted or clean cases).\n- **Unchanged, byte for byte:**\n  - every file under `tests/fixtures/` at 3df1ce5;\n  - everything under `dot-plumbline/jobs/`;\n  - every file under `schemas/` at 3df1ce5 (15 files; derived or vendored, pinned by `tools/pin.json`), plus `gate/` and `standards/`;\n  - `tools/pin.json` and `tools/build_schemas.py`.\n- **Fixture-only and test-only fixes are not acceptable** (approval item 16). A fixture or test change never counts as the fix for a finding. The Orchestrator names the kind of fix in each generation-close line.\n\n## Frozen bar: Maker output contract (verbatim)\n\n## Maker output contract\n- Whole files, between `<<<PLUMBLINE-FILE path=<path>>>>` / `<<<PLUMBLINE-END path=<path>>>>` markers, ending with `<<<PLUMBLINE-DONE files=N>>>` (job 1's format; `handoffs/extract_files.py`, which also limits each request to its part's paths). No diffs.\n- An iteration may take several Maker calls, for example one per part. The iteration's revision is the single commit made from all of them.\n- **The field guide is its own Maker request** (item 30), separate from every code-file request, so no single request risks `finish_reason` `length`. It counts under the same money bound, clock-time bound and cap.\n- The runbook names the command that writes the files (`extract_files.py` **without** `--check`) before the commit.\n- Commits: author `E-DI Maker`, committer `Steve Moitozo II <smoitozo@users.noreply.github.com>`.\n\n## Frozen bar: checks (verbatim, controls omitted)\n\n## Checks (artifact)\n\"The subject\" = the Maker's revision of the iteration. \"Base\" = 3df1ce5. \"Hand time\" = a time in the record whose only source is either a ledger line with `writer: \"hand\"`, a ledger line with no `writer`, or a value typed into `inputs/custody.json` with no ledger line behind it. \"Tool-checked reported time\" = a time a person reported (Owner decision, relay source time, amendment time). It was entered through a ledger command that bounds it, as in F1b, F1e and F1f, and names its source. It is not a hand time (approval item 14).\n\n### T: refuse hand-entered times (the real N3)\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T1 | Every line that any `custody_ledger.py` command appends (old and new commands) carries `writer: \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<first 12 hex of the sha256 of the file that ran>\"`. That value equals the file's sha256 at run time. Its `at` comes from the tool's clock, within ±5 s of the instrument's own clock around the call. | S1 | `evidence/T1.json` |\n| T2 | On held-out planted fixtures P-T2a (ledger lines with no `writer`), P-T2b (`writer: \"hand\"`), P-T2c (a time in `custody.json` with no ledger line) and P-T2d (a tool line overridden by a later hand line), the emitter **with no switch** exits 3 with refusal kind `hand-time`, names every hand-time field and its file:line, and writes nothing. | S1 | `evidence/T2.json` |\n| T3 | On the same fixtures **with `--allow-hand-times`**, the record is written and check.py reads OK at CL1. `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` lists exactly the hand-time fields, no more and no fewer, each with file:line, and the record carries the allowance `x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times` (`switch: \"--allow-hand-times\"`, the emitter's `writer`, and its tool-clock `at`). The listing is **not disclosure only**: `kit/plumbline_verify.py` fails a record whose flags lack the allowance or disagree with the ledger and logs (V3), and close refuses on that failure (V8). The switch silences nothing else: the repo overlay `failures/hand-times` (log contradicts the hand time) still exits 3 with the switch on. | S1 | `evidence/T3.json` |\n| T4 | A job built at batch time only by the subject's own tools emits with **no switch**, exit 0, check.py OK at CL1, and an empty `hand_times`. The tools used: `custody_ledger.py` freeze/approve/pin/generation/evaluation/dispose, plus `tools/edi/or_call.py` with its mocked transport writing the harness logs. | S1 | `evidence/T4.json` + the built job |\n| T5 | **Cross-checks no looser than at base.** (a) `custody_history.TOLERANCE_S` is still 60. (b) Every refusal case that exits 3 at base exits 3 on the subject, with a superset of base's refusal kinds, both without and with `--allow-hand-times`. The refusal cases are the repo overlays under `tests/fixtures/custody/failures/*` at base, plus the prior held-out refusal controls. (c) Every changed line in `cross_check`, `check_order`, `check_pin_order` and `check_approval` is listed for J1. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | S1 | `evidence/T5.json` + diff listing |\n| T6 | The prior job's N1–N8 procedure (frozen `ncheck.py`, held-out controls above) passes on the subject. It is run through the new subject runner with `--allow-hand-times`, because those synthetic fixtures are hand-typed by design. Every flagged field appears in `x-plumbline.hand_times`, and `kit/plumbline_verify.py` reads each emitted record OK. | S1 | `evidence/T6/` (prior summary format) |\n| T7 | **The emitter never writes its inputs, and a server time is not a logger time.** Found while drafting (about 13:43 EDT): at base, `custody_history.fill_logger_times` (called from `emit_custody.py` lines 798 and 849) rewrites harness logs in place, filling missing `sent_at`/`received_at` from the response's own `created` or `Date` header, and `tests/validate_schemas.py` line 469 runs the emitter on the committed fixture `job-rejected`, so a base test run dirties two tracked fixture logs. On the subject: (a) every file under the job dir except the record output is byte-identical before and after an emit (sha256 of the tree, on a copy of job-rejected and on the T4 job); (b) a call that has no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` is either refused as `hand-time` or, under `--allow-hand-times`, listed in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` with source `server-header`/`response-created`, never written back to the log; (c) after the full test suite runs in a fresh clone, `git status --porcelain` is empty. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | S1 | `evidence/T7.json` |\n\n### F1: ledger commands (tool-stamped, append-only, read by the emitter)\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1a | Each of `generation open`, `generation close`, `evaluation`, `amendment`, `relay`, `spend` and `dispose --decided-at` appends **exactly one** line when it succeeds. The bytes before the call equal the prefix of the bytes after it (the earlier lines are never rewritten). `custody.json` agrees with the new line. A refused call appends nothing and exits non-zero. | S1 | `evidence/F1a.json` |\n| F1b | `dispose --decided-at T --decided-source S` refuses a T earlier than the last logged check and a T later than the tool's clock. The last logged check is the latest of: evaluator `received_at` in the harness logs, `evaluation` line times, and instrument-summary `finished_at`. It accepts T equal to the last check. The line carries `at` (tool clock), `decided_at` and `decided_source`, and the record's `disposition.at` = `decided_at`. | S1 | `evidence/F1b.json` |\n| F1c | `generation open/close`: n starts at 1 and goes up by 1. A second open while one is open is refused, and so is a close without a matching open (same n and seat). `prompt_sha256` is computed by the tool from the named file. | S1 | `evidence/F1c.json` |\n| F1d | `evaluation --batch B --verdict FILE [--summary FILE]`: the tool computes the sha256 of FILE itself and refuses a missing file. With `--summary`, it takes `started_at`/`finished_at` and `writer` from the instrument's own stamp, and refuses a summary with no stamp. | S1 | `evidence/F1d.json` |\n| F1e | `amendment --file F --quote Q --channel C --said-at T`: the tool computes the sha256 of F. It refuses F inside `custody/` (amendments go beside the frozen set), and T before the freeze or after its own clock. Q is stored verbatim. | S1 | `evidence/F1e.json` |\n| F1f | `relay --quote Q --from BOT --source-chat C --source-at T`: stored verbatim, marked `relay`, with T bounded as in F1e. **The emitter never counts a relay as an approval.** Held-out fixture P-F1f, where a buyer approval exists only as a relay, is refused as a missing approval. | S1 | `evidence/F1f.json` |\n| F1g | `spend --spend-ledger L --key-reading R`: it records the reconciled total from the spend ledger and a key-usage reading file that `tools/edi/or_call.py --spend-status` wrote and stamped (`read_at`, writer). It refuses when `read_at` is less than 3 min after the last `settle` line (F5), or when R has no stamp. Both files' sha256 go in the line. | S1 | `evidence/F1g.json` |\n| F1h | The emitter reads every F1 line into the record. `x-plumbline` carries `generations[]`, `evaluations[]`, `amendments[]`, `relays[]` and `spend`, each with its file:line source. check.py reads OK at CL1. | S1 | `evidence/F1h.json` |\n\n### I and F7: instruments stamp their own times; fixture copies never inherit modes\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | Every instrument in `tools/edi/` that writes a summary writes `started_at` and `finished_at` (UTC, its own clock) and `writer: \"tools/edi/<file>@<sha12>\"`. The two times bracket the instrument's run as seen by S1's clock (±5 s). | S1 | `evidence/I1.json` |\n| F7a | `tools/edi/` fixture runner: a run from a `chmod -R a-w` copy of the controls gives outputs byte-identical (once the I1 stamps are removed) to a run from a writable copy. Every file in the working copy is writable by its owner. | S1 | `evidence/F7a.json` |\n\n### F8: spend caps in the product harness (`tools/edi/or_call.py`), with tests\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F8a | With a mocked key whose usage is at the job limit, the call is refused with the named exit **before anything is sent**: the mock transport records zero chat POSTs, and there is no harness-log entry. | S1 | `evidence/F8a.json` |\n| F8b | `--max-cost X`: if the projected worst case is greater than X, the call is refused before sending. If the `/generation` `total_cost` is greater than X, the call ends with a named non-zero exit, the entry is logged and marked over-cap in the spend ledger, and no reply is written. (Mocked.) | S1 | `evidence/F8b.json` |\n| F8c | The job total is `max(spend-ledger sum, key-usage delta)`. It is checked against GET `/api/v1/key` before **each** call, and the call is refused when total + worst case + reserve ≥ bound. The job id, bound, reserve and price snapshot come from a job spend file, with no job hard-coded, and a