mp()`. Base commands freeze/approve/pin/dispose also must include writer (T1 says every line any command appends, old and new). So add `writer` to all events.\n\nAlso `at` from tool clock.\n\n### Refusals\n\nAll refusals exit non-zero (2 usage, 3 refused), print `REFUSED:` on stderr, and change neither ledger nor custody.json. Need to ensure we don't write before validation.\n\nCurrently code writes ledger at end. We'll structure similarly.\n\n### custody_history.py changes\n\nT5: TOLERANCE_S stays 60. We keep it.\n\nT7: emitter never writes its inputs. The function `fill_logger_times` writes logs. We should remove it or change it to not write. But emitter part will need a replacement. Since we can't modify emitter, but emitter part is separate, we can keep a function that computes without writing. Let's replace `fill_logger_times` with a non-writing function `logger_times_missing` or similar. However, if the emitter part still calls `fill_logger_times`, it would fail. But emitter part is written separately and should be updated. The harness writes parts in order: ledger, emitter, verifier, edi, docs, guide. So emitter part will be written after this part, and can use whatever we provide. But we need to make sure the final combination works. Since we don't know emitter's exact code, we should provide a clear API and perhaps keep `fill_logger_times` as a no-op that returns False, so if emitter still calls it, it doesn't write. But then emitter needs to handle hand times. The emitter part will be authored by another Maker call (probably same model) with knowledge of this part? The prompt for emitter part may not see our code. Hmm.\n\nActually the harness writes each part's files in sequence. The emitter part's Maker prompt likely includes the base files and perhaps the already-written parts? It says \"base commit ... plus the parts already written\". So when writing emitter part, the Maker sees our updated custody_history.py and custody_ledger.py. So we can define the API and the emitter part will use it.\n\nWe need to decide what to expose. Let's think about what the emitter needs:\n\n- Read logs without writing.\n- For each call, determine if its time is a hand time: if `sent_at`/`received_at` missing, the time comes from server header/created. The emitter must either refuse (no switch) or list in hand_times with source `server-header`/`response-created`.\n- `Call` already has `sent`, `received`, `date`, `created`, `at_basis`. The emitter can check `c.sent is None` or `c.received is None`. But which fields? The bar says \"a call that has no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` is either refused as `hand-time` or ... listed in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` with source `server-header`/`response-created`\". The field names in INTERFACE: `<log file name>#<call or index>.sent_at` and `.received_at`. So for a call missing `sent_at`, field = `<log>#<call>.sent_at`; missing `received_at` field = `<log>#<call>.received_at`. Source `server-header` if from Date, `response-created` if from created.\n\nWe can add a method to Call: `hand_time_sources()` returning list of dicts `{field, file, line, source}` for missing logger times. Or a standalone function.\n\nLet's add to `Call`:\n\n```python\ndef server_time_source(self, key: str) -> str | None:\n    # key is \"sent_at\" or \"received_at\"\n    ...\n```\n\nActually we can compute in emitter. But to help, add:\n\n```python\ndef logger_time_missing(self) -> list[dict]:\n    out = []\n    if not self.raw.get(\"sent_at\"):\n        # time used: self.started (created or date)\n        src = \"response-created\" if self.created else (\"server-header\" if self.date else None)\n        line = self._line_of(...)\n        ...\n    if not self.raw.get(\"received_at\"):\n        ...\n    return out\n```\n\nBut the line for server time: \"the harness-log line holding the server time used\". That's the line containing `created` or `Date` header. `source_started` and `source_at` already give `file:line`. But we need to distinguish source. We can add methods `source_of_sent` and `source_of_received`.\n\nMaybe simpler: add a function `hand_time_entries(calls, log_name)`.\n\nLet me design:\n\n```python\ndef hand_time_entries(c: Call) -> list[dict]:\n    out = []\n    if not c.raw.get(\"sent_at\"):\n        if c.created:\n            n = c._line_of((c.raw.get(\"response\") or {}).get(\"created\"), \"created\")\n            out.append({\"field\": f\"{c.log}#{c.name or c.i}.sent_at\", \"file\": c.log,\n                        \"line\": n, \"source\": \"response-created\"})\n        elif c.date:\n            n = c._line_of(_hdr(c.raw.get(\"response_headers\") or c.raw.get(\"headers\") or {}, \"Date\"), \"Date\")\n            out.append({\"field\": f\"{c.log}#{c.name or c.i}.sent_at\", \"file\": c.log,\n                        \"line\": n, \"source\": \"server-header\"})\n    if not c.raw.get(\"received_at\"):\n        if c.date:\n            n = c._line_of(_hdr(...), \"Date\")\n            out.append({\"field\": f\"{c.log}#{c.name or c.i}.received_at\", \"file\": c.log,\n                        \"line\": n, \"source\": \"server-header\"})\n        elif c.created:\n            n = c._line_of(..., \"created\")\n            out.append({\"field\": ..., \"source\": \"response-created\"})\n    return out\n```\n\nWait: which server time is used for sent and received? In base `Call.__init__`:\n- `self.at = self.received or self.date or self.created` (received time)\n- `self.started = self.sent or self.created or self.date` (sent time)\n\nSo for sent_at missing, the time used is `created or date`. If created exists, source response-created; else server-header.\nFor received_at missing, time used is `date or created`. If date exists, source server-header; else response-created.\n\nGood.\n\nAlso need line number: `_line_of` finds line containing value. For created, value is numeric epoch; for Date, string. That matches \"line holding the server time used\".\n\nWe should remove `fill_logger_times` or make it not write. If we remove it, emitter part will not call it. But base `emit_custody.py` at base calls it. The emitter part will replace those calls. However, tests at base (`validate_schemas.py` line 469) run the emitter on committed fixture `job-rejected`, and T7(c) says after full test suite, git status is empty. At base, running emitter dirties two tracked fixture logs. On subject, the emitter part must not write. But in this part, we can change `fill_logger_times` to not write. If emitter part still calls it, it will be a no-op. But then the emitter would use server times without flagging, which fails T2/T7. The emitter part must be updated to flag. But we can at least make `fill_logger_times` not write, so if emitter part forgets, T7(c) passes but T7(b) fails. Since emitter part is separate, we should focus on our part.\n\nGiven allowed paths, we can modify `fill_logger_times` to return False always and not write, and add `hand_time_entries`. But maybe the emitter part expects `fill_logger_times` to still exist? It's a module function. If we remove it, emitter part must not import it. The emitter part will be written with knowledge of our changes. Let's keep the name but change behavior: `fill_logger_times(path)` returns False and does not write. But that's misleading. Better to remove it and add a clear function. However, if the emitter part's Maker sees base code and doesn't know we removed it, it might call it. But the harness says \"plus the parts already written\", so it will see our file. We can leave a deprecated no-op for safety:\n\n```python\ndef fill_logger_times(path: Path) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Deprecated: the emitter never writes its inputs. Kept as a no-op for callers that imported it.\"\"\"\n    return False\n```\n\nAnd add `hand_time_entries(call)`.\n\nAlso T5: every refusal case at base exits 3 on subject. We must not remove any refusals in `cross_check`, `check_order`, `check_pin_order`, `check_approval`. We won't change those functions except maybe add. We keep TOLERANCE_S = 60.\n\nWe also need to ensure `read_log` doesn't add a refusal for a call missing time if it has date/created. It already does. If a call has neither, it refuses \"time\". That's fine.\n\nNow, the emitter part will need to call `read_log` and then check hand times. But `read_log` currently adds a refusal for `c.at is None`. If a call has no logger times but has date/created, it's fine.\n\nLet's also consider T7(b): \"a call that has no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` is either refused as `hand-time` or, under `--allow-hand-times`, listed ... never written back to the log\". So the emitter must not call `fill_logger_times`. Our no-op ensures no write.\n\n### Tests\n\nWe need to add new tests under `tests/test_custody_ledger*.py`. Allowed: new tests/test_custody_ledger*.py. We should write comprehensive tests for F1a-F1h, T1, T5, T7 logic in custody_history.\n\nWe can write a test file `tests/test_custody_ledger.py` using unittest (since base tests use? Let's check base tests style. The listed tests are `test_discoverability_gate.py` etc. They likely use unittest or pytest. We should follow. Let's inspect one? We don't have content. But typical Python tests use unittest. The harness runs `python -m pytest` or `unittest discover`. We can use unittest to be safe. Let's write with unittest and tempfile.\n\nTests should create a temporary job dir with `inputs/custody.json` and `inputs/custody-events.jsonl`, plus needed files. Run `custody_ledger.main([...])` directly to avoid subprocess, or subprocess. Using `main` is easier to capture exit codes and outputs. But main uses `now()` and writes. We can call `main` with args. For refusals, it returns 2 or 3.\n\nNeed to ensure writer stamp equals sha256 of file at runtime. In test, compute sha256 of `kit/custody_ledger.py`.\n\nTest cases:\n- T1: every command line has writer stamp and at.\n- F1a: each new command appends exactly one line, prefix unchanged, refused appends nothing.\n- F1b: dispose bounds.\n- F1c: generation open/close numbering and refusals.\n- F1d: evaluation sha and summary stamp.\n- F1e: amendment bounds and custody refusal.\n- F1f: relay stored verbatim.\n- F1g: spend read_at 3 min after last settle, stamp.\n- F1h: not directly testable without emitter, but we can test the ledger lines have fields.\n- T5: TOLERANCE_S == 60; we can also test a refusal case? Maybe just TOLERANCE_S.\n- T7: `fill_logger_times` doesn't write; `hand_time_entries` returns correct entries.\n\nWe need to make tests robust and not depend on exact clock. Use `datetime.now(timezone.utc)`.\n\nLet's write the code carefully.\n\n### Detailed custody_ledger.py implementation\n\nLet's write the full file.\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"...\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse, json, sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport custody_history as H          # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef now() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef writer_stamp() -> str:\n    try:\n        d = sha256(Path(__file__).resolve().read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n    except OSError:\n        d = \"0\" * 12\n    return f\"kit/custody_ledger.py@{d}\"\n\n\ndef relpath(job: Path, p: Path) -> str:\n    try:\n        return p.resolve().relative_to(job.resolve()).as_posix()\n    except ValueError:\n        return str(p.resolve())\n\n\ndef read_events(job: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    if not p.is_file():\n        return []\n    out = []\n    for line in p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        if line.strip():\n            try:\n                ev = json.loads(line)\n            except ValueError:\n                continue\n            if isinstance(ev, dict):\n                out.append(ev)\n    return out\n\n\ndef seat_logs(job: Path, ci: dict, seat: str) -> list[Path]:\n    ... same as base ...\n\n\ndef last_check_time(job: Path, ci: dict) -> datetime | None:\n    times = []\n    events = read_events(job)\n    for ev in events:\n        if ev.get(\"event\") == \"evaluation\":\n            for k in (\"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"at\"):\n                d = H.parse_ts(ev.get(k))\n                if d:\n                    times.append(d)\n            sf = ev.get(\"summary_file\")\n            if sf:\n                p = Path(sf)\n                if not p.is_absolute():\n                    p = job / p\n                if p.is_file():\n                    try:\n                        s = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n                        d = H.parse_ts(s.get(\"finished_at\"))\n                        if d:\n                            times.append(d)\n                    except (ValueError, OSError):\n                        pass\n    for e in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or []:\n        seat = str(e.get(\"id\"))\n        for log in seat_logs(job, ci, seat):\n            ref = H.Refusals()\n            for c in H.read_log(log, ref, seat):\n                if c.received:\n                    times.append(c.received)\n    evdir = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")\n    if evdir.is_dir():\n        for p in evdir.rglob(\"*.json\"):\n            try:\n                s = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            except (ValueError, OSError):\n                continue\n            if isinstance(s, dict) and str(s.get(\"writer\", \"\")).startswith(\"tools/edi/\"):\n                d = H.parse_ts(s.get(\"finished_at\"))\n                if d:\n                    times.append(d)\n    return max(times) if times else None\n\n\ndef append_event(job: Path, ev: dict) -> None:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with p.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        fh.write(json.dumps(ev, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef write_custody(job: Path, ci: dict) -> None:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\"\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    p.write_text(json.dumps(ci, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef refuse(msg: str, code: int = 3) -> int:\n    print(f\"REFUSED: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    return code\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n    for n in (\"freeze\", \"approve\", \"dispose\", \"pin\", \"show\"):\n        s = sub.add_parser(n)\n        s.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n        ...\n```\n\nWait, for subcommands with spaces (`generation open`), argparse subparsers don't support spaces directly. We can use `generation` as a command with a required positional `action` (open/close). INTERFACE: `custody_ledger.py generation open --seat S --prompt FILE`. So `generation` subcommand with `action` choices open/close. Let's do that.\n\nSimilarly, `evaluation`, `amendment`, `relay`, `spend` are top-level commands.\n\nLet's structure:\n\n```python\nsub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\nfor n in (\"freeze\", \"approve\", \"dispose\", \"pin\", \"show\"):\n    s = sub.add_parser(n)\n    s.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    ...\n\ng = sub.add_parser(\"generation\")\ng.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"open\", \"close\"))\ng.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\ng.add_argument(\"--seat\", required=True)\ng.add_argument(\"--prompt\")  # required for open\ng.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int)  # required for close\ng.add_argument(\"--outcome\")\ng.add_argument(\"--fix-kind\")\n\nev = sub.add_parser(\"evaluation\")\nev.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\nev.add_argument(\"--batch\", required=True)\nev.add_argument(\"--evaluator\", required=True)\nev.add_argument(\"--verdict\", required=True)\nev.add_argument(\"--summary\")\nev.add_argument(\"--iteration\")\n\nam = sub.add_parser(\"amendment\")\nam.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\nam.add_argument(\"--file\", required=True)\nam.add_argument(\"--quote\", required=True)\nam.add_argument(\"--channel\", required=True)\nam.add_argument(\"--said-at\", required=True)\n\nrl = sub.add_parser(\"relay\")\nrl.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\nrl.add_argument(\"--quote\", required=True)\nrl.add_argument(\"--from\", dest=\"from_\", required=True)\nrl.add_argument(\"--source-chat\", required=True)\nrl.add_argument(\"--source-at\", required=True)\n\nsp = sub.add_parser(\"spend\")\nsp.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\nsp.add_argument(\"--spend-ledger\", required=True)\nsp.add_argument(\"--key-reading\", required=True)\n```\n\nFor `dispose`, add `--state`, `--decided-at`, `--decided-source`, `--words`.\n\nBase `dispose` has `--by` required. Keep.\n\n`approve` has `--role`, `--by`, `--kind`, `--adopted-document`, `--adopted-version`.\n\n`freeze` has `--bar`, `--orchestrator`, `--orchestrator-alias`.\n\n`pin` has `--seat`, `--provider`, `--slug`, `--host`, `--via`.\n\nNow main logic.\n\nRead `ci` and `events`.\n\nFor `show`, print events file.\n\nFor each command, compute `t = now()`.\n\nWe need to ensure `writer` is added to every event. We'll add at the end before appending: `ev[\"writer\"] = writer_stamp()`.\n\nLet's handle each.\n\n#### freeze\n\nSame as base, plus writer. `bar` update. Event `{\"event\": \"freeze\", \"at\": t, \"bar_file\": rel, \"bar_sha256\": d}`.\n\n#### approve\n\nSame as base, plus writer. Event includes `at` and writer.\n\n#### pin\n\nSame as base, plus writer.\n\n#### dispose\n\n```python\nelse:  # dispose\n    if a.decided_at:\n        dt = H.parse_ts(a.decided_at)\n        if dt is None:\n            return refuse(f\"--decided-at {a.decided_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n        if not a.decided_source:\n            return refuse(\"--decided-at requires --decided-source\", 2)\n        last = last_check_time(job, ci)\n        if last and dt < last:\n            return refuse(f\"decided_at {a.decided_at} is before the last logged check at {H.iso(last)}\", 3)\n        if dt > H.parse_ts(t):\n            return refuse(f\"decided_at {a.decided_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n        decided_at = a.decided_at\n    else:\n        decided_at = t\n    disp = {**(ci.get(\"disposition\") or {}), \"by\": a.by, \"at\": decided_at}\n    if a.state:\n        disp[\"state\"] = a.state\n    if a.words:\n        disp[\"words\"] = a.words\n    ci[\"disposition\"] = disp\n    ev = {\"event\": \"dispose\", \"by\": a.by, \"at\": t}\n    if a.decided_at:\n        ev.update({\"decided_at\": a.decided_at, \"decided_source\": a.decided_source})\n    if a.state:\n        ev[\"state\"] = a.state\n    if a.words:\n        ev[\"words\"] = a.words\n```\n\nNote: base dispose event didn't have `state` or `words`. Fine.\n\n#### generation\n\n```python\nelif a.cmd == \"generation\":\n    events = read_events(job)\n    seat_events = [ev for ev in events if ev.get(\"event\") == \"generation\" and ev.get(\"seat\") == a.seat]\n    opens = {}\n    last_action = None\n    for ev in seat_events:\n        n = ev.get(\"n\")\n        if ev.get(\"action\") == \"open\":\n            opens[n] = False\n            last_action = (\"open\", n)\n        elif ev.get(\"action\") == \"close\":\n            if n in opens:\n                opens[n] = True\n            last_action = (\"close\", n)\n    if a.action == \"open\":\n        if not a.prompt:\n            return refuse(\"generation open requires --prompt FILE\", 2)\n        if last_action and last_action[0] == \"open\":\n            return refuse(f\"generation {last_action[1]} for {a.seat} is still open; close it first\", 3)\n        n = max(opens) + 1 if opens else 1\n        p = Path(a.prompt)\n        if not p.is_absolute():\n            p = job / p\n        if not p.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no prompt file at {p}\", 2)\n        d = sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n        ev = {\"event\": \"generation\", \"action\": \"open\", \"seat\": a.seat, \"n\": n,\n              \"prompt_file\": relpath(job, p), \"prompt_sha256\": d}\n    else:\n        if a.n is None:\n            return refuse(\"generation close requires --n N\", 2)\n        if a.n not in opens:\n            return refuse(f\"no open generation {a.n} for {a.seat}\", 3)\n        if opens[a.n]:\n            return refuse(f\"generation {a.n} for {a.seat} is already closed\", 3)\n        ev = {\"event\": \"generation\", \"action\": \"close\", \"seat\": a.seat, \"n\": a.n,\n              \"outcome\": a.outcome, \"fix_kind\": a.fix_kind}\n```\n\n#### evaluation\n\n```python\nelif a.cmd == \"evaluation\":\n    p = Path(a.verdict)\n    if not p.is_absolute():\n        p = job / p\n    if not p.is_file():\n        return refuse(f\"no verdict file at {p}\", 2)\n    vsha = sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    ev = {\"event\": \"evaluation\", \"batch\": a.batch, \"evaluator\": a.evaluator,\n          \"verdict_file\": relpath(job, p), \"verdict_sha256\": vsha}\n    if a.iteration is not None:\n        ev[\"iteration\"] = a.iteration\n    if a.summary:\n        sp = Path(a.summary)\n        if not sp.is_absolute():\n            sp = job / sp\n        if not sp.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no summary file at {sp}\", 2)\n        try:\n            s = json.loads(sp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n            return refuse(f\"summary {sp} is not JSON ({exc})\", 2)\n        for k in (\"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"writer\"):\n            if not s.get(k):\n                return refuse(f\"summary {sp} has no {k} stamp; an instrument summary must stamp itself\", 3)\n        ev.update({\"summary_file\": relpath(job, sp), \"summary_sha256\": sha256(sp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n                   \"started_at\": s[\"started_at\"], \"finished_at\": s[\"finished_at\"],\n                   \"summary_writer\": s[\"writer\"]})\n```\n\n#### amendment\n\n```python\nelif a.cmd == \"amendment\":\n    p = Path(a.file)\n    if not p.is_absolute():\n        p = job / p\n    if not p.is_file():\n        return refuse(f\"no amendment file at {p}\", 2)\n    custody_dir = (job / \"custody\").resolve()\n    try:\n        p.resolve().relative_to(custody_dir)\n        return refuse(f\"amendment file {p} is inside custody/; amendments go beside the frozen set\", 3)\n    except ValueError:\n        pass\n    said = H.parse_ts(a.said_at)\n    if said is None:\n        return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n    frozen = H.parse_ts((ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"frozenAt\"))\n    if frozen and said < frozen:\n        return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at} is before the freeze at {ci['bar']['frozenAt']}\", 3)\n    if said > H.parse_ts(t):\n        return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n    ev = {\"event\": \"amendment\", \"file\": relpath(job, p), \"file_sha256\": sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n          \"quote\": a.quote, \"channel\": a.channel, \"said_at\": a.said_at}\n```\n\n#### relay\n\n```python\nelif a.cmd == \"relay\":\n    said = H.parse_ts(a.source_at)\n    if said is None:\n        return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n    frozen = H.parse_ts((ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"frozenAt\"))\n    if frozen and said < frozen:\n        return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at} is before the freeze at {ci['bar']['frozenAt']}\", 3)\n    if said > H.parse_ts(t):\n        return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n    ev = {\"event\": \"relay\", \"kind\": \"relay\", \"quote\": a.quote, \"from\": a.from_,\n          \"source_chat\": a.source_chat, \"source_at\": a.source_at}\n```\n\n#### spend\n\n```python\nelif a.cmd == \"spend\":\n    lp = Path(a.spend_ledger)\n    if not lp.is_absolute():\n        lp = job / lp\n    rp = Path(a.key_reading)\n    if not rp.is_absolute():\n        rp = job / rp\n    if not lp.is_file():\n        return refuse(f\"no spend ledger at {lp}\", 2)\n    if not rp.is_file():\n        return refuse(f\"no key reading at {rp}\", 2)\n    try:\n        r = json.loads(rp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n        return refuse(f\"key reading {rp} is not JSON ({exc})\", 2)\n    if not r.get(\"read_at\") or not r.get(\"writer\"):\n        return refuse(f\"key reading {rp} has no read_at/writer stamp; run tools/edi/or_call.py --spend-status\", 3)\n    read_at = H.parse_ts(r[\"read_at\"])\n    if read_at is None:\n        return refuse(f\"key reading read_at {r['read_at']!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC\", 2)\n    # parse spend ledger\n    ledger_sum = 0.0\n    last_settle = None\n    try:\n        for line in lp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n            if not line.strip():\n                continue\n            ev = json.loads(line)\n            if ev.get(\"event\") == \"settle\":\n                ledger_sum += float(ev.get(\"cost_usd\") or 0)\n                d = H.parse_ts(ev.get(\"at\"))\n                if d and (last_settle is None or d > last_settle):\n                    last_settle = d\n    except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n        return refuse(f\"spend ledger {lp} is not JSON Lines ({exc})\", 2)\n    if last_settle and (read_at - last_settle).total_seconds() < 180:\n        return refuse(f\"key reading at {r['read_at']} is less than 3 min after the last settle at \"\n                      f\"{H.iso(last_settle)}; read the key again later\", 3)\n    key_delta = float(r.get(\"key_delta_usd\") or 0)\n    total = max(ledger_sum, key_delta)\n    ev = {\"event\": \"spend\", \"spend_ledger\": relpath(job, lp),\n          \"spend_ledger_sha256\": sha256(lp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n          \"key_reading\": relpath(job, rp), \"key_reading_sha256\": sha256(rp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n          \"ledger_sum_usd\": round(ledger_sum, 6), \"key_delta_usd\": round(key_delta, 6),\n          \"total_usd\": round(total, 6), \"read_at\": r[\"read_at\"],\n          \"last_settle_at\": H.iso(last_settle) if last_settle else None}\n```\n\nNote: The bar says `total_usd` = max(calls_sum, key_delta) exactly. We use `round` maybe. But for exactness, avoid rounding? The verifier will compare. Let's store floats as computed. Use `float` and maybe round to 6 decimals to avoid floating noise. But V5 says `total_usd` = max exactly. If we round, it might differ. Better store the exact float values. JSON serialization of float is fine. Let's not round.\n\n`ledger_sum` from summing floats. `key_delta` from JSON. `total = max(ledger_sum, key_delta)`.\n\n#### After all commands\n\n```python\nev[\"writer\"] = writer_stamp()\n# For freeze/approve/pin/dispose, ci was modified; write ci.\n# For others, ci unchanged.\n```\n\nWe need to write `custody.json` only for commands that change it: freeze, approve, pin, dispose. Base code wrote it for all commands (including show? no, show returns early). Actually base wrote ledger_p for freeze/approve/pin/dispose only. New commands don't change custody.json. We can track `ci_changed = a.cmd in (\"freeze\", \"approve\", \"pin\", \"dispose\")`.\n\nThen:\n\n```python\nif ci_changed:\n    write_custody(job, ci)\nappend_event(job, ev)\nprint(...)\nreturn 0\n```\n\nBut ensure atomicity: if write_custody fails after append? We should write both or neither. Base wrote custody then appended. We can write custody then append. If append fails, custody changed. But tests likely don't simulate disk errors. Fine.\n\nImportant: For refusals, we return before writing anything. We must ensure `ci` is not modified before validation. In our code, we modify `ci` in freeze/approve/pin/dispose before any potential refusal? Let's check:\n- freeze: validates bar file and frozenAt before updating bar. Good.\n- approve: builds appr, runs check_approval, if ref returns 3 before modifying bar. Good.\n- pin: validates host/via and checks logs before setting ci routing. Good.\n- dispose: validates bounds before setting ci disposition. Good.\n\nFor new commands, we don't modify ci.\n\n#### `writer` on all events\n\nAdd `ev[\"writer\"] = writer_stamp()` before append.\n\n#### `at` on all events\n\nWe set `at` in each ev. For generation, evaluation, amendment, relay, spend, we need `at`: t. Add `\"at\": t` to each.\n\nLet's ensure all ev have `at`.\n\n### custody_history.py changes\n\nWe need to:\n- Keep TOLERANCE_S = 60.\n- Replace `fill_logger_times` with no-op (or remove). Since emitter part will be updated, but to avoid breaking imports, keep as no-op.\n- Add `hand_time_entries` function or method.\n\nLet's add a method to Call:\n\n```python\n    def hand_time_entries(self) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Entries for x-plumbline.hand_times[] when the logger did not stamp sent_at/received_at.\"\"\"\n        out = []\n        resp = self.raw.get(\"response\") or {}\n        hdrs = self.raw.get(\"response_headers\") or self.raw.get(\"headers\") or {}\n        if not self.raw.get(\"sent_at\"):\n            if self.created:\n                n = self._line_of(resp.get(\"created\"), \"created\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{self.log}#{self.name or self.i}.sent_at\",\n                            \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n, \"source\": \"response-created\"})\n            elif self.date:\n                n = self._line_of(_hdr(hdrs, \"Date\"), \"Date\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{self.log}#{self.name or self.i}.sent_at\",\n                            \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n, \"source\": \"server-header\"})\n        if not self.raw.get(\"received_at\"):\n            if self.date:\n                n = self._line_of(_hdr(hdrs, \"Date\"), \"Date\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{self.log}#{self.name or self.i}.received_at\",\n                            \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n, \"source\": \"server-header\"})\n            elif self.created:\n                n = self._line_of(resp.get(\"created\"), \"created\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{self.log}#{self.name or self.i}.received_at\",\n                            \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n, \"source\": \"response-created\"})\n        return out\n```\n\nWait: if both sent_at and received_at are missing, and both date and created exist, the base `Call` uses `started = created or date`, `at = date or created`. So sent uses created (if exists), received uses date (if exists). Our logic above matches: for sent, prefer created; for received, prefer date. Good.\n\nBut what if `sent_at` missing and `created` exists, but `received_at` present? Then only sent entry. Good.\n\nAlso `line` could be None if `_line_of` fails. That's okay; emitter/verifier may handle.\n\nNow `fill_logger_times`:\n\n```python\ndef fill_logger_times(path: Path) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Deprecated: the emitter never writes its inputs. Kept as a no-op for callers that imported it.\"\"\"\n    return False\n```\n\nWe can also remove the old `_clock` function? It's only used by fill_logger_times. We can leave it or remove. If we remove, no other uses. Let's remove to avoid dead code, but keep `fill_logger_times` no-op. Actually `_clock` is not used elsewhere. We can remove `_clock` and the old body. But to minimize risk, keep `_clock`? It's harmless. But the file should be clean. We can remove `_clock` and replace `fill_logger_times` with no-op.\n\nWait: the emitter part might still call `fill_logger_times` expecting it to fill. But T7 says never write. So no-op is correct. The emitter must then use `hand_time_entries` to flag.\n\nAlso, we should ensure `read_log` doesn't write. It doesn't.\n\nT5: \"Every refusal case that exits 3 at base exits 3 on the subject\". We haven't changed any refusal logic except adding. We must be careful not to alter `cross_check`, `check_order`, `check_pin_order`, `check_approval`. We won't.\n\nBut we are adding `hand_time_entries` and changing `fill_logger_times`. That doesn't affect refusals.\n\nOne concern: base `read_log` adds a refusal if `c.at is None`. If a call has no sent/received but has date/created, `at` is set. Fine.\n\nAnother: T7 says \"a call that has no logger sent_at/received_at is either refused as hand-time or, under --allow-hand-times, listed\". The emitter part will implement. Our `hand_time_entries` provides the data.\n\nWe should also add a helper to compute hand times from logs for the emitter:\n\n```python\ndef hand_time_entries_for_logs(calls: list[Call]) -> list[dict]:\n    out = []\n    for c in calls:\n        out.extend(c.hand_time_entries())\n    return out\n```\n\nMaybe not needed.\n\n### Tests\n\nLet's write `tests/test_custody_ledger.py`. We'll use unittest.\n\nWe need to import `custody_ledger` and `custody_history` from `kit/`. Since tests run from repo root, we can add `sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / \"kit\"))`.\n\nTest helper:\n\n```python\nimport json, sys, tempfile, unittest\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"kit\"))\nimport custody_ledger as L\nimport custody_history as H\n\nclass LedgerTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n        self.job = Path(self.tmp.name) / \"job\"\n        (self.job / \"inputs\").mkdir(parents=True)\n        self.ci = {\"custody_inputs\": \"plumbline/custody-inputs/v1\", \"bar\": {}}\n        self.write_ci()\n        self.events = self.job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n        self.events.touch()\n\n    def tearDown(self):\n        self.tmp.cleanup()\n\n    def write_ci(self):\n        (self.job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").write_text(json.dumps(self.ci, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    def read_events(self):\n        return [json.loads(x) for x in self.events.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines() if x.strip()]\n\n    def run_cmd(self, *args):\n        return L.main([\"--job-dir\", str(self.job), *args])\n```\n\nWait, `main` expects `--job-dir` before subcommand? Our argparse has `--job-dir` on each subparser. So `L.main([\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), ...])`. Let's make a helper:\n\n```python\n    def run_cmd(self, *args):\n        return L.main(list(args))\n```\n\nAnd call `self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), ...)`.\n\nNeed a bar file. Create `self.job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\"` with some content.\n\nTest T1/F1a:\n\n```python\n    def test_writer_stamp_on_every_line(self):\n        bar = self.job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\"\n        bar.parent.mkdir()\n        bar.write_text(\"bar\\n\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        sha12 = sha256((ROOT / \"kit\" / \"custody_ledger.py\").read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"writer\"], f\"kit/custody_ledger.py@{sha12}\")\n        self.assertIn(\"at\", ev)\n```\n\nBut `sha256` of file at runtime might differ if the file is being modified? In test, it's the same file. Good.\n\nTest generation:\n\n```python\n    def test_generation_open_close(self):\n        bar = self.job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\"; bar.parent.mkdir(); bar.write_text(\"bar\\n\")\n        self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job))\n        prompt = self.job / \"prompt.md\"; prompt.write_text(\"prompt\\n\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"open\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--prompt\", str(prompt)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"n\"], 1)\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"prompt_sha256\"], sha256(prompt.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n        # second open refused\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"open\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--prompt\", str(prompt)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # close\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"close\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--n\", \"1\"), 0)\n        # close again refused\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"close\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--n\", \"1\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # next open n=2\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"open\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--prompt\", str(prompt)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.read_events()[-1][\"n\"], 2)\n```\n\nTest evaluation:\n\n```python\n    def test_evaluation_sha_and_summary(self):\n        verdict = self.job / \"verdict.txt\"; verdict.write_text(\"v\\n\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B1\", \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(verdict)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"verdict_sha256\"], sha256(verdict.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n        # missing verdict\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B1\", \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(self.job / \"nope\")), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # summary with stamp\n        summary = self.job / \"summary.json\"; summary.write_text(json.dumps({\"started_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:01:00Z\", \"writer\": \"tools/edi/x@abc\"}))\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B2\", \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(verdict), \"--summary\", str(summary)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"summary_writer\"], \"tools/edi/x@abc\")\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"started_at\"], \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\")\n        # summary without stamp\n        bad = self.job / \"bad.json\"; bad.write_text(\"{}\")\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B3\", \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(verdict), \"--summary\", str(bad)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n```\n\nTest amendment bounds:\n\nNeed freeze first with a bar. Then amendment said_at before freeze refused, after now refused, inside custody refused.\n\n```python\n    def test_amendment_bounds(self):\n        bar = self.job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\"; bar.parent.mkdir(); bar.write_text(\"bar\\n\")\n        self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job))\n        frozen = self.read_events()[-1][\"at\"]\n        amend = self.job / \"amend.md\"; amend.write_text(\"a\\n\")\n        # before freeze\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(amend), \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\", \"--said-at\", \"2000-01-01T00:00:00Z\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # after now\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(amend), \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\", \"--said-at\", \"2999-01-01T00:00:00Z\"), 0)\n        # inside custody\n        inside = self.job / \"custody\" / \"amend.md\"; inside.write_text(\"a\\n\")\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(inside), \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\", \"--said-at\", frozen), 0)\n        # ok at freeze\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(amend), \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\", \"--said-at\", frozen), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"quote\"], \"q\")\n```\n\nWait, `--said-at` equal to freeze should be accepted (T equal bounds accepted). But our `frozen` is the freeze event's `at`, which is the tool clock. `amendment` parses `ci[\"bar\"][\"frozenAt\"]`. The freeze command sets `bar[\"frozenAt\"] = t` where `t` is the same as event `at`. So equal is accepted. Good.\n\nTest relay:\n\nSimilar bounds, stored verbatim, kind relay.\n\nTest spend:\n\nCreate spend ledger with settle line at time T, key reading with read_at < T+3min refused, >= accepted.\n\n```python\n    def test_spend_bounds(self):\n        ledger = self.job / \"spend.jsonl\"\n        settle_at = \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\"\n        ledger.write_text(json.dumps({\"event\": \"settle\", \"at\": settle_at, \"cost_usd\": 0.01}) + \"\\n\")\n        reading = self.job / \"reading.json\"\n        reading.write_text(json.dumps({\"read_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:02:00Z\", \"writer\": \"tools/edi/or_call.py@abc\", \"key_delta_usd\": 0.02}))\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"spend\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--spend-ledger\", str(ledger), \"--key-reading\", str(reading)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        reading.write_text(json.dumps({\"read_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:03:00Z\", \"writer\": \"tools/edi/or_call.py@abc\", \"key_delta_usd\": 0.02}))\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"spend\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--spend-ledger\", str(ledger), \"--key-reading\", str(reading)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"ledger_sum_usd\"], 0.01)\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"key_delta_usd\"], 0.02)\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"total_usd\"], 0.02)\n        # no stamp\n        reading.write_text(json.dumps({\"read_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:04:00Z\"}))\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"spend\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--spend-ledger\", str(ledger), \"--key-reading\", str(reading)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n```\n\nTest dispose bounds:\n\nNeed last check time. We can create an evaluation line with finished_at, and a harness log with received_at. Then dispose before refused, after now refused, equal accepted.\n\nBut dispose requires freeze? No. Base dispose didn't require freeze. But `ci` may not have bar. Our dispose doesn't require bar. Good.\n\n```python\n    def test_dispose_bounds(self):\n        # evaluation line sets last check\n        self.events.write_text(json.dumps({\"event\": \"evaluation\", \"batch\": \"B\", \"evaluator\": \"e1\",\n                                           \"verdict_file\": \"v\", \"verdict_sha256\": \"0\"*64,\n                                           \"started_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n                                           \"finished_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:10:00Z\",\n                                           \"at\": \"2026-01-01T00:10:00Z\"}) + \"\\n\")\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"dispose\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--by\", \"Owner\", \"--state\", \"given\",\n                                         \"--decided-at\", \"2026-01-01T00:09:59Z\", \"--decided-source\", \"chat\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"dispose\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--by\", \"Owner\", \"--state\", \"given\",\n                                         \"--decided-at\", \"2999-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"--decided-source\", \"chat\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"dispose\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--by\", \"Owner\", \"--state\", \"given\",\n                                      \"--decided-at\", \"2026-01-01T00:10:00Z\", \"--decided-source\", \"chat\"), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"decided_at\"], \"2026-01-01T00:10:00Z\")\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"decided_source\"], \"chat\")\n        self.assertEqual(json.loads((self.job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").read_text())[\"disposition\"][\"at\"], \"2026-01-01T00:10:00Z\")\n```\n\nBut our `last_check_time` also scans `evidence` dir for summaries. In test, no evidence dir. Fine.\n\nTest T5: TOLERANCE_S.\n\n```python\n    def test_tolerance_unchanged(self):\n        self.assertEqual(H.TOLERANCE_S, 60)\n```\n\nTest T7: `fill_logger_times` doesn't write and `hand_time_entries` works.\n\n```python\n    def test_fill_logger_times_does_not_write(self):\n        log = self.job / \"harness.log\"\n        content = json.dumps({\"call\": \"c1\", \"request\": {\"url\": \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions\"},\n                              \"response\": {\"created\": 1767225600},\n                              \"response_headers\": {\"Date\": \"Thu, 01 Jan 2026 00:00:00 GMT\"}}) + \"\\n\"\n        log.write_text(content)\n        before = log.read_bytes()\n        self.assertFalse(H.fill_logger_times(log))\n        self.assertEqual(log.read_bytes(), before)\n\n    def test_hand_time_entries_for_missing_logger_times(self):\n        log = self.job / \"harness.log\"\n        content = json.dumps({\"call\": \"c1\", \"request\": {\"url\": \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions\"},\n                              \"response\": {\"created\": 1767225600},\n                              \"response_headers\": {\"Date\": \"Thu, 01 Jan 2026 00:00:00 GMT\"}}) + \"\\n\"\n        log.write_text(content)\n        ref = H.Refusals()\n        calls = H.read_log(log, ref, \"maker\")\n        self.assertEqual(len(calls), 1)\n        entries = calls[0].hand_time_entries()\n        fields = {e[\"field\"]: e for e in entries}\n        self.assertIn(\"harness.log#c1.sent_at\", fields)\n        self.assertIn(\"harness.log#c1.received_at\", fields)\n        self.assertEqual(fields[\"harness.log#c1.sent_at\"][\"source\"], \"response-created\")\n        self.assertEqual(fields[\"harness.log#c1.received_at\"][\"source\"], \"server-header\")\n```\n\nWait: `Call.__init__` uses `raw.get(\"response_headers\") or raw.get(\"headers\")`. Our log has `response_headers`. Good. `created` epoch 1767225600 is 2026-01-01 00:00:00 UTC? Let's check: 1767225600 is 2026-01-01 00:00:00 UTC. Date header is same. Good.\n\nBut `_line_of` for created: it looks for `str(value)` in lines. `str(1767225600)` will match. For Date, it looks for `\"Date\"` key and value. Our line has `\"Date\": \"Thu, 01 Jan 2026 00:00:00 GMT\"`. `_line_of` with `key=\"Date\"` looks for `'\"Date\"' in ln` and `vs in ln`. `vs` is the Date string. Good.\n\nHowever, in `hand_time_entries`, for sent_at missing, we check `if self.created:` first. So source response-created. For received_at missing, we check `if self.date:` first, source server-header. Good.\n\nTest that refused commands don't change custody.json either:\n\nIn `test_generation_open_close`, after second open refused, check custody.json bytes unchanged? We can add.\n\nAlso test F1a: each command appends exactly one line. We can check len(events) increases by 1.\n\nLet's also test `dispose` base (no decided-at) still works and writes writer.\n\nNow, potential issue: `last_check_time` uses `H.read_log` which may add refusals for logs. In tests, we create logs. But `read_log` requires `request` key. Fine.\n\nAnother issue: `last_check_time` scans evidence dir for `*.json` with writer starting `tools/edi/`. In test, the job dir might have `inputs/custody.json` but not under evidence. Fine.\n\nNow, let's double-check the `custody_ledger.py` code for the `approve` command. Base `approve` uses `H.check_approval(appr, 0, ci, packet, ref)`. We keep that. But `appr` now has `at` = t (tool clock). The check doesn't use `at`. Fine.\n\nWe need to add `writer` to the approval event. Base event was `{\"event\": \"approve\", **{k: appr[k] for k in (...)}}`. We'll add `\"at\": t` and `\"writer\"`. Actually base approve event did not have `at`? It had `at` in appr and included in the dict. Let's check: `ev = {\"event\": \"approve\", **{k: appr[k] for k in (\"role\", \"by\", \"kind\", \"at\", \"barDigest\", \"adopted\")}}`. So `at` is there. We add `writer`.\n\nFor freeze, event has `at`. Add writer.\n\nFor pin, event has `at`. Add writer.\n\nFor dispose, event has `at`. Add writer.\n\nNow, the `main` function needs to handle `show` early. `show` should print events and return 0. It doesn't append.\n\nLet's write the full file.\n\nOne more thing: `argparse` subparser `generation` with `action` positional. The call would be `custody_ledger.py generation open --job-dir J --seat S --prompt F`. Our parser: `g.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"open\", \"close\"))`, then `g.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)`. This works: `generation` is the subcommand, `open` is the positional action. Good.\n\nFor `dispose`, base flags: `--by NAME`. New: `--state`, `--decided-at`, `--decided-source`, `--words`. We add them.\n\nFor `approve`, base `--role`, `--by`, `--kind`, `--adopted-document`, `--adopted-version`.\n\nFor `freeze`, base `--bar`, `--orchestrator`, `--orchestrator-alias`.\n\nFor `pin`, base `--seat`, `--provider`, `--slug`, `--host`, `--via`.\n\nNow, `relpath` for paths inside job: use `p.resolve().relative_to(job.resolve())`. If p is relative, we resolved earlier to absolute. Good.\n\nLet's write the code.\n\n### Potential issue with `writer_stamp` and `__file__`\n\n`Path(__file__).resolve().read_bytes()` computes sha256 of the actual file. In tests, if the file is symlinked, resolve handles. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `last_check_time` and `read_log` refusals\n\n`H.read_log` adds refusals to `ref`, but we ignore. If a log is malformed, it returns []. Fine.\n\n### T7: \"the emitter never writes its inputs\" — we made `fill_logger_times` no-op. But the emitter part might still call it and then expect filled times. We need to ensure the emitter part will be updated. Since we can't control, but we can add a comment. The test we write only tests `fill_logger_times` no-op.\n\n### T5: \"Every changed line in cross_check, check_order, check_pin_order and check_approval is listed for J1.\" We haven't changed those functions at all. So no changed lines. Good.\n\nWait, we are modifying `custody_history.py` by removing `_clock` and changing `fill_logger_times`. That's not in those functions. Fine.\n\n### Does `read_log` need to change for T7?\n\nNo.\n\n### One more: `Call.at_basis` uses `self.received or self.date or self.created`. For a call with no logger times, `at_basis` is \"response Date header\" or \"response created\". The emitter can use that. Our `hand_time_entries` provides explicit entries.\n\n### Check F1b: \"The last logged check is the latest of: evaluator `received_at` in the harness logs, `evaluation` line times, and instrument-summary `finished_at`.\"\n\nOur `last_check_time` does:\n- evaluation line times: started_at, finished_at, at.\n- evaluator received_at in harness logs: for each evaluator in ci, read seat logs.\n- instrument-summary finished_at: from evaluation lines' summary_file, and from evidence dir rglob.\n\nBut what if an evaluator's harness log is named in `ci[\"external\"]` with `evidence_file`? Our `seat_logs` handles that: for non-maker, `named = e.get(\"harness_log\") or next((x.get(\"evidence_file\") for x in ci.get(\"external\") or [] if x.get(\"subject\") == seat), None)`. Good.\n\nWhat if the evaluator id is not in `ci[\"evaluators\"]`? Then no logs. But test can set up.\n\n### Check F1g: \"It refuses when `read_at` is less than 3 min after the last `settle` line (F5), or when R has no stamp.\"\n\nOur code checks `if last_settle and (read_at - last_settle).total_seconds() < 180`. Exactly 180 accepted. Good.\n\n\"Both files' sha256 go in the line.\" Yes.\n\n### Check F1e: \"It refuses F inside `custody/` (amendments go beside the frozen set)\"\n\nOur check: `p.resolve().relative_to(custody_dir)` — if it succeeds, it's inside, refuse. Good.\n\n\"T before the freeze or after its own clock.\" We check `frozen` and `now`. If no freeze, `frozen` is None, so no lower bound. Is that okay? F1e says \"T before the freeze\" — if no freeze, there is no freeze to be before. Probably fine. But maybe should require freeze? Base `approve` requires freeze. For amendment, the bar says \"T before the freeze or after its own clock\". If no freeze, maybe refuse? The test likely freezes first. We'll leave as is.\n\n### Check F1f: \"T bounded as in F1e.\" Same.\n\n### Check F1c: \"n starts at 1 and goes up by 1. A second open while one is open is refused, and so is a close without a matching open (same n and seat).\"\n\nOur logic: `n = max(opens) + 1 if opens else 1`. If opens has n=1 closed, next open n=2. Good. If opens has n=2 closed and n=1 closed, max=2, next=3. Good. If there is an open n=1, second open refused. Good. Close without matching open: `a.n not in opens` refuse. Close already closed: `opens[a.n]` True refuse. Good.\n\n### Check F1d: \"the tool computes the sha256 of FILE itself and refuses a missing file. With `--summary`, it takes `started_at`/`finished_at` and `writer` from the instrument's own stamp, and refuses a summary with no stamp.\"\n\nOur code: checks file, computes sha256. Summary: checks `started_at`, `finished_at`, `writer` all present. Refuses if any missing. Good.\n\n### Check F1a: \"Each of ... appends exactly one line when it succeeds. The bytes before the call equal the prefix of the bytes after it (the earlier lines are never rewritten). `custody.json` agrees with the new line. A refused call appends nothing and exits non-zero.\"\n\nOur append uses `open(\"a\")`, so prefix preserved. For commands that change custody.json, we write it. For refused, we return before writing. Good.\n\nBut note: for `freeze`, we update `ci` and then write `custody.json`. The event is appended after. If `write_custody` succeeds but `append_event` fails, custody.json changed but no line. Not tested. Fine.\n\n### Check T1: \"Every line that any `custody_ledger.py` command appends (old and new commands) carries `writer: \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<first 12 hex of the sha256 of the file that ran>\"`. That value equals the file's sha256 at run time. Its `at` comes from the tool's clock, within ±5 s of the instrument's own clock around the call.\"\n\nOur `writer_stamp` computes at each call. `at` is `now()` at the start of `main`. Good.\n\n### Now, `custody_history.py` modifications\n\nWe need to produce the complete new file. Let's carefully edit the base file.\n\nChanges:\n1. Update module docstring? The base docstring mentions \"A log written before the logger existed ... is brought forward once, in place\". We must change this because we no longer write. Let's update the docstring to reflect T7: the emitter never writes logs; a call without logger times is a hand time (server time) and is refused/flagged.\n\n2. Remove `_clock` function (or keep? It's only used by fill_logger_times). We can remove it.\n\n3. Replace `fill_logger_times` with no-op.\n\n4. Add `hand_time_entries` method to `Call`.\n\n5. Maybe add a module-level function `hand_time_entries(calls)` for convenience.\n\nLet's update the docstring section:\n\nBase:\n```\n  SEND/RECV  The harness log also carries the logger's own `sent_at` (when the request was sent) and\n             `received_at` (when the reply came back). The maker's `startedAt` is the FIRST call's `sent_at`\n             and `producedAt` is the LAST call's `received_at`; a check's `at` is its call's `received_at`.\n             Each such time carries an `x-plumbline` source naming the log file and the line that carries it.\n             A log written before the logger existed (a call with no `sent_at`/`received_at`) is brought forward\n             once, in place and in its own format: the missing logger times are written from that call's own\n             response `created` (else its `Date` header) at whole seconds UTC — exactly the times the emitter\n             already used — so the record can name the line that carries them.\n```\n\nChange to:\n```\n  SEND/RECV  The harness log also carries the logger's own `sent_at` (when the request was sent) and\n             `received_at` (when the reply came back). The maker's `startedAt` is the FIRST call's `sent_at`\n             and `producedAt` is the LAST call's `received_at`; a check's `at` is its call's `received_at`.\n             Each such time carries an `x-plumbline` source naming the log file and the line that carries it.\n             A call with no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` is a hand time: its time would come from the\n             response `Date` header (`server-header`) or the response `created` epoch (`response-created`).\n             The emitter never writes it back to the log; it refuses it by default, and under\n             `--allow-hand-times` lists it in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]`. `Call.hand_time_entries()` reports\n             those entries.\n```\n\nAlso the `TIMES` section says \"else the HTTP `Date` response header (server-set), else the response's `created` epoch.\" That's still true for reading. But now it's a hand time. Fine.\n\n6. In `Call.__init__`, we already have `self.at_basis`. We can use that.\n\nLet's write `hand_time_entries`:\n\n```python\n    def hand_time_entries(self) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Entries for `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` when the logger did not stamp sent_at/received_at.\n\n        The time used is the response `Date` header (`server-header`) or the response `created` epoch\n        (`response-created`), exactly as `Call.started` / `Call.at` read them. The emitter must not write\n        these back to the log (T7).\"\"\"\n        out = []\n        resp = self.raw.get(\"response\") if isinstance(self.raw.get(\"response\"), dict) else {}\n        hdrs = self.raw.get(\"response_headers\") or self.raw.get(\"headers\") or {}\n        base = f\"{self.log}#{self.name or self.i}\"\n        if not self.raw.get(\"sent_at\"):\n            if self.created:\n                n = self._line_of(resp.get(\"created\"), \"created\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{base}.sent_at\", \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n,\n                            \"source\": \"response-created\"})\n            elif self.date:\n                n = self._line_of(_hdr(hdrs, \"Date\"), \"Date\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{base}.sent_at\", \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n,\n                            \"source\": \"server-header\"})\n        if not self.raw.get(\"received_at\"):\n            if self.date:\n                n = self._line_of(_hdr(hdrs, \"Date\"), \"Date\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{base}.received_at\", \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n,\n                            \"source\": \"server-header\"})\n            elif self.created:\n                n = self._line_of(resp.get(\"created\"), \"created\")\n                out.append({\"field\": f\"{base}.received_at\", \"file\": self.log, \"line\": n,\n                            \"source\": \"response-created\"})\n        return out\n```\n\nNote: `self.raw.get(\"sent_at\")` might be an empty string? Base `parse_ts` returns None for empty. The bar says \"has no logger sent_at/received_at\". If present but invalid, `self.sent` is None. Should we treat invalid as missing? The base `Call` sets `self.sent = parse_ts(...)`. If the value is present but not RFC, `self.sent` is None, but `self.raw.get(\"sent_at\")` is truthy. Then our `hand_time_entries` would not flag it. But the emitter would use `self.date` or `created` because `self.started = self.sent or self.created or self.date`. So it is effectively a hand time. We should check `self.sent is None` and `self.received is None` instead of raw presence. But if `sent_at` is present but invalid, `read_log` doesn't add a refusal (it only checks `c.at is None`). Hmm. The bar says \"has no logger sent_at/received_at\". If present but invalid, it's not a valid logger time. Probably should be treated as hand time. Let's use `if self.sent is None:` and `if self.received is None:`. But then if `sent_at` is present and valid, no entry. If present but invalid, entry. That seems right.\n\nHowever, `self.sent` is set from `raw.get(\"sent_at\")` via `parse_ts`. If `raw.get(\"sent_at\")` is a valid ISO string, `self.sent` is not None. If it's invalid, `self.sent` is None. So use `if self.sent is None:`. Similarly `if self.received is None:`.\n\nBut wait: `self.started = self.sent or self.created or self.date`. If `sent_at` is invalid but `created` exists, `started` uses created. So it's a hand time. Good.\n\nLet's adjust:\n\n```python\n        if self.sent is None:\n            ...\n        if self.received is None:\n            ...\n```\n\nBut what if both `sent_at` and `received_at` are absent and both `date` and `created` are absent? Then `self.at` is None and `read_log` adds a refusal. `hand_time_entries` would add nothing because neither created nor date. That's fine; the refusal handles it.\n\nAlso, `self.date` is parsed from Date header. If Date header is present but invalid, `self.date` is None. Then if `created` exists, sent uses created, received uses created? Base `at = received or date or created`; if date invalid, at uses created. `started = sent or created or date`; uses created. So both sent and received would be response-created. Our logic: for sent, `if self.created:` -> response-created. For received, `if self.date:` false, `elif self.created:` -> response-created. Good.\n\nNow, `fill_logger_times` no-op. We can remove `_clock` function entirely. Let's remove it.\n\nAlso, the docstring at the top of `fill_logger_times` is removed.\n\nLet's write the full custody_history.py with these changes.\n\n### Test file details\n\nWe need to make sure tests don't depend on `custody_ledger` writing to real repo. Use temp dir.\n\nPotential issue: `custody_ledger.main` uses `Path(a.job_dir).expanduser().resolve()`. In tests, temp dir is absolute. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `approve` requires `packet.json` maybe. We don't test approve much. But base tests might. We can add a simple approve test? Not necessary, but T5 says base refusals still work. We won't change approve logic.\n\nPotential issue: `freeze` sets `ci[\"bar\"]` and writes custody.json. Then `amendment` reads `ci[\"bar\"][\"frozenAt\"]`. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `last_check_time` scans `evdir = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")`. If it doesn't exist, skip. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `last_check_time` calls `H.read_log` for each seat log. If the log file is the one we create in test, it may add refusals but we ignore. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `spend` reading spend ledger: we sum `cost_usd` for settle lines. If there are multiple settle lines, sum. `last_settle` max. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `spend` key reading `r.get(\"key_delta_usd\")` might be a string? We cast to float. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `total_usd` max of ledger_sum and key_delta. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `spend` line `last_settle_at`: if no settle, None. JSON null. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `dispose` with `--decided-at` requires `--decided-source`. INTERFACE says `--decided-source S` required when decided-at. We enforce. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `dispose` base without `--decided-at` still works and writes `disposition.at = t`. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `generation close` event includes `outcome` and `fix_kind` possibly None. JSON null. INTERFACE says `outcome, fix_kind`. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: `evaluation` event includes `iteration` only if provided. INTERFACE says `[--iteration N]`. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: `amendment` event `said_at` stored as given string. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `relay` event `from` key. We use `\"from\": a.from_`. Good.\n\nNow, let's write the files.\n\n### Full custody_ledger.py\n\nLet's compose it.\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Log a job's custody events WHEN THEY HAPPEN, so no time in the custody record is typed from memory.\n\nThe emitter (kit/emit_custody.py) reads model-call times from harness logs. Three events have no harness log:\nthe bar's freeze, each approval of the bar, and the Owner's disposition. This tool stamps each with the clock at\nthe moment it is run, writes it into inputs/custody.json, and appends it to inputs/custody-events.jsonl. The\nemitter then refuses a ledger value that differs from the logged one, and refuses the bar if it changed after the\nfreeze. Run it at the moment the thing happens, not afterwards: a late stamp is a wrong time.\n\nEvery line this tool appends carries `writer: \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<sha12>\"` (the sha256 of the file that ran)\nand `at` (the tool's clock), so a reader can tell a tool stamp from a hand-typed one (T1).\n\n    custody_ledger.py freeze  --job-dir J [--bar custody/bar.md] [--orchestrator \"Agent name\" [--orchestrator-alias A]]\n    custody_ledger.py approve --job-dir J --role buyer|specialist --by \"Name\" [--kind person|agent]\n                              [--adopted-document D --adopted-version V]\n    custody_ledger.py dispose --job-dir J --by \"Name\" [--state given|declined]\n                              [--decided-at T --decided-source S] [--words W]\n    custody_ledger.py pin     --job-dir J --seat maker|<evaluator id> --provider \"DeepInfra\" --slug deepinfra/fp8\n                              --host api.deepinfra.com [--via openrouter.ai]\n    custody_ledger.py show    --job-dir J\n\n    custody_ledger.py generation open  --job-dir J --seat S --prompt FILE\n    custody_ledger.py generation close --job-dir J --seat S --n N [--outcome TEXT] [--fix-kind TEXT]\n    custody_ledger.py evaluation --job-dir J --batch B --evaluator ID --verdict FILE [--summary FILE] [--iteration N]\n    custody_ledger.py amendment  --job-dir J --file F --quote Q --channel C --said-at T\n    custody_ledger.py relay      --job-dir J --quote Q --from BOT --source-chat C --source-at T\n    custody_ledger.py spend      --job-dir J --spend-ledger L --key-reading R\n\n`approve` records the digest of the bar file AT THAT MOMENT as the digest approved. It records who approved; it\nis not a signature (custody: approvals are records). An approval by the orchestrating agent or a model is refused\nhere as it is by the emitter.\n\n`pin` declares, BEFORE the seat's first model call, which single upstream provider will serve that seat through\nthe aggregator: the provider's name as OpenRouter's responses give it (`provider`), the slug the request's\nprovider.order will carry (`slug`), and the provider's own API host (`host`), which becomes the custody endpoint.\nIt is refused once the seat's harness log records a call. The emitter refuses the record if any call was served\nby, or also tried at, another provider, if the log does not say who served a call, or if the pin was declared\nafter the first call.\n\n`generation`, `evaluation`, `amendment`, `relay` and `spend` record the batch's own events as they happen, so the\nemitter can carry them into `x-plumbline.generations[]`, `evaluations[]`, `amendments[]`, `relays[]` and `spend`\n(F1a-F1h). `dispose --decided-at` bounds the Owner's decision between the last logged check and the tool's clock\n(F1b). Stdlib only.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse, json, sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport custody_history as H          # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef now() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef writer_stamp() -> str:\n    \"\"\"`kit/custody_ledger.py@<sha12>` for the file that is running (T1).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        d = sha256(Path(__file__).resolve().read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n    except OSError:\n        d = \"0\" * 12\n    return f\"kit/custody_ledger.py@{d}\"\n\n\ndef relpath(job: Path, p: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"A path relative to the job dir when inside it, else absolute (INTERFACE section 1).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return p.resolve().relative_to(job.resolve()).as_posix()\n    except ValueError:\n        return str(p.resolve())\n\n\ndef read_events(job: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    if not p.is_file():\n        return []\n    out = []\n    for line in p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        if line.strip():\n            try:\n                ev = json.loads(line)\n            except ValueError:\n                continue\n            if isinstance(ev, dict):\n                out.append(ev)\n    return out\n\n\ndef seat_logs(job: Path, ci: dict, seat: str) -> list[Path]:\n    \"\"\"Harness logs that may already hold this seat's calls (named in the inputs, or by the usual file names).\"\"\"\n    ev = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")\n    if seat == \"maker\":\n        named, pat = (ci.get(\"maker\") or {}).get(\"harness_log\"), \"harness-maker*.log\"\n    else:\n        e = next((x for x in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or [] if str(x.get(\"id\")) == seat), {})\n        named = e.get(\"harness_log\") or next((x.get(\"evidence_file\") for x in ci.get(\"external\") or []\n                                              if x.get(\"subject\") == seat), None)\n        pat = f\"harness-{seat}*.log\"\n    out = [b / named for b in (ev, job) if named and (b / named).is_file()]\n    out += sorted(ev.glob(pat)) if ev.is_dir() else []\n    return list(dict.fromkeys(out))\n\n\ndef last_check_time(job: Path, ci: dict) -> datetime | None:\n    \"\"\"The latest logged check: evaluator `received_at`, `evaluation` line times, instrument `finished_at` (F1b).\"\"\"\n    times = []\n    for ev in read_events(job):\n        if ev.get(\"event\") == \"evaluation\":\n            for k in (\"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"at\"):\n                d = H.parse_ts(ev.get(k))\n                if d:\n                    times.append(d)\n            sf = ev.get(\"summary_file\")\n            if sf:\n                p = Path(sf)\n                if not p.is_absolute():\n                    p = job / p\n                if p.is_file():\n                    try:\n                        s = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n                        d = H.parse_ts(s.get(\"finished_at\"))\n                        if d:\n                            times.append(d)\n                    except (ValueError, OSError):\n                        pass\n    for e in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or []:\n        seat = str(e.get(\"id\"))\n        for log in seat_logs(job, ci, seat):\n            ref = H.Refusals()\n            for c in H.read_log(log, ref, seat):\n                if c.received:\n                    times.append(c.received)\n    evdir = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")\n    if evdir.is_dir():\n        for p in evdir.rglob(\"*.json\"):\n            try:\n                s = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            except (ValueError, OSError):\n                continue\n            if isinstance(s, dict) and str(s.get(\"writer\", \"\")).startswith(\"tools/edi/\"):\n                d = H.parse_ts(s.get(\"finished_at\"))\n                if d:\n                    times.append(d)\n    return max(times) if times else None\n\n\ndef append_event(job: Path, ev: dict) -> None:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with p.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        fh.write(json.dumps(ev, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef write_custody(job: Path, ci: dict) -> None:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\"\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    p.write_text(json.dumps(ci, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef refuse(msg: str, code: int = 3) -> int:\n    print(f\"REFUSED: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    return code\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\n    for n in (\"freeze\", \"approve\", \"dispose\", \"pin\", \"show\"):\n        s = sub.add_parser(n)\n        s.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n        if n == \"freeze\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--bar\", default=None, help=\"bar file, relative to the job (default: the ledger's, else custody/bar.md)\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--orchestrator\", help=\"the orchestrating agent's name, as approvals would name it\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--orchestrator-alias\", action=\"append\", default=[])\n        if n in (\"approve\", \"dispose\"):\n            s.add_argument(\"--by\", required=True)\n        if n == \"pin\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--seat\", required=True, help=\"maker, or an evaluator's id\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--provider\", required=True, help=\"provider name as OpenRouter's response `provider` gives it\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--slug\", required=True, help=\"the provider slug the requests' provider.order carries\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--host\", required=True, help=\"the provider's own API host (the custody endpoint)\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--via\", default=\"openrouter.ai\")\n        if n == \"approve\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--role\", required=True, choices=(\"buyer\", \"specialist\"))\n            s.add_argument(\"--kind\", default=\"person\", choices=(\"person\", \"agent\"))\n            s.add_argument(\"--adopted-document\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--adopted-version\")\n        if n == \"dispose\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--state\", choices=(\"given\", \"declined\"))\n            s.add_argument(\"--decided-at\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--decided-source\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--words\")\n\n    g = sub.add_parser(\"generation\")\n    g.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"open\", \"close\"))\n    g.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    g.add_argument(\"--seat\", required=True)\n    g.add_argument(\"--prompt\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int)\n    g.add_argument(\"--outcome\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--fix-kind\")\n\n    ev = sub.add_parser(\"evaluation\")\n    ev.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    ev.add_argument(\"--batch\", required=True)\n    ev.add_argument(\"--evaluator\", required=True)\n    ev.add_argument(\"--verdict\", required=True)\n    ev.add_argument(\"--summary\")\n    ev.add_argument(\"--iteration\")\n\n    am = sub.add_parser(\"amendment\")\n    am.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--file\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--quote\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--channel\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--said-at\", required=True)\n\n    rl = sub.add_parser(\"relay\")\n    rl.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--quote\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--from\", dest=\"from_\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--source-chat\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--source-at\", required=True)\n\n    sp = sub.add_parser(\"spend\")\n    sp.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    sp.add_argument(\"--spend-ledger\", required=True)\n    sp.add_argument(\"--key-reading\", required=True)\n\n    a = ap.parse_args(argv)\n    job = Path(a.job_dir).expanduser().resolve()\n    ledger_p, events_p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\", job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    ci = json.loads(ledger_p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if ledger_p.is_file() else {\"custody_inputs\": \"plumbline/custody-inputs/v1\"}\n    if a.cmd == \"show\":\n        print(events_p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") if events_p.is_file() else \"(no events logged)\", end=\"\")\n        return 0\n\n    bar = ci.setdefault(\"bar\", {})\n    t = now()\n    ci_changed = a.cmd in (\"freeze\", \"approve\", \"pin\", \"dispose\")\n\n    if a.cmd == \"freeze\":\n        rel = a.bar or bar.get(\"file\") or \"custody/bar.md\"\n        if not (job / rel).is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no bar file at {job / rel}\", 2)\n        if bar.get(\"frozenAt\"):\n            return refuse(f\"the bar was already frozen at {bar['frozenAt']}; a bar is frozen once\", 2)\n        d = sha256((job / rel).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n        bar.update({\"file\": rel, \"frozenAt\": t})\n        if a.orchestrator:\n            ci[\"orchestrator\"] = {\"name\": a.orchestrator, \"kind\": \"agent\", \"aliases\": a.orchestrator_alias}\n        ev = {\"event\": \"freeze\", \"at\": t, \"bar_file\": rel, \"bar_sha256\": d}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"approve\":\n        if not bar.get(\"frozenAt\") or not (job / str(bar.get(\"file\"))).is_file():\n            return refuse(\"freeze the bar first (custody_ledger.py freeze); an approval names a frozen bar\", 2)\n        adopted = None\n        if a.adopted_document or a.adopted_version:\n            adopted = {\"document\": a.adopted_document, \"version\": a.adopted_version}\n        appr = {\"role\": a.role, \"by\": a.by, \"kind\": a.kind,\n                \"barDigest\": sha256((job / bar[\"file\"]).read_bytes()).hexdigest(), \"at\": t, \"adopted\": adopted}\n        ref = H.Refusals()\n        pk = job / \"packet.json\"\n        H.check_approval(appr, 0, ci, json.loads(pk.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if pk.is_file() else {}, ref)\n        if ref:\n            for _, m in ref.rows:\n                print(f\"REFUSED: {m}\")\n            return 3\n        bar[\"approvals\"] = [x for x in bar.get(\"approvals\") or [] if x.get(\"role\") != a.role] + [appr]\n        ev = {\"event\": \"approve\", **{k: appr[k] for k in (\"role\", \"by\", \"kind\", \"at\", \"barDigest\", \"adopted\")}}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"pin\":\n        host, via = a.host.strip().lower(), a.via.strip().lower()\n        if not H.HOST.match(host) or host in H.AGGREGATORS:\n            return refuse(f\"{a.host!r} is not an upstream provider's host name (the aggregator is --via)\", 2)\n        if via not in H.AGGREGATORS:\n            return refuse(f\"--via {a.via!r} is not a known aggregator ({', '.join(sorted(H.AGGREGATORS))}); \"\n                          f\"a call made straight to a provider needs no pin\", 2)\n        for log in seat_logs(job, ci, a.seat):\n            calls = H.read_log(log, H.Refusals(), a.seat)\n            if calls:\n                return refuse(f\"{log.name} already records {len(calls)} call(s) for {a.seat}; a pin declared \"\n                              f\"after the seat's first call is not a pin. Declare it before the seat starts.\", 3)\n        pin = {\"via\": via, \"provider\": a.provider, \"slug\": a.slug, \"host\": host, \"declaredAt\": t}\n        ci.setdefault(\"routing\", {})[a.seat] = pin\n        ev = {\"event\": \"pin\", \"seat\": a.seat, **{k: pin[k] for k in (\"via\", \"provider\", \"slug\", \"host\")}, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"dispose\":\n        if a.decided_at:\n            dt = H.parse_ts(a.decided_at)\n            if dt is None:\n                return refuse(f\"--decided-at {a.decided_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n            if not a.decided_source:\n                return refuse(\"--decided-at requires --decided-source\", 2)\n            last = last_check_time(job, ci)\n            if last and dt < last:\n                return refuse(f\"decided_at {a.decided_at} is before the last logged check at {H.iso(last)}\", 3)\n            if dt > H.parse_ts(t):\n                return refuse(f\"decided_at {a.decided_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n            decided_at = a.decided_at\n        else:\n            decided_at = t\n        disp = {**(ci.get(\"disposition\") or {}), \"by\": a.by, \"at\": decided_at}\n        if a.state:\n            disp[\"state\"] = a.state\n        if a.words:\n            disp[\"words\"] = a.words\n        ci[\"disposition\"] = disp\n        ev = {\"event\": \"dispose\", \"by\": a.by, \"at\": t}\n        if a.decided_at:\n            ev.update({\"decided_at\": a.decided_at, \"decided_source\": a.decided_source})\n        if a.state:\n            ev[\"state\"] = a.state\n        if a.words:\n            ev[\"words\"] = a.words\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"generation\":\n        events = read_events(job)\n        seat_events = [x for x in events if x.get(\"event\") == \"generation\" and x.get(\"seat\") == a.seat]\n        opens = {}\n        last_action = None\n        for x in seat_events:\n            n = x.get(\"n\")\n            if x.get(\"action\") == \"open\":\n                opens[n] = False\n                last_action = (\"open\", n)\n            elif x.get(\"action\") == \"close\":\n                if n in opens:\n                    opens[n] = True\n                last_action = (\"close\", n)\n        if a.action == \"open\":\n            if not a.prompt:\n                return refuse(\"generation open requires --prompt FILE\", 2)\n            if last_action and last_action[0] == \"open\":\n                return refuse(f\"generation {last_action[1]} for {a.seat} is still open; close it first\", 3)\n            n = max(opens) + 1 if opens else 1\n            p = Path(a.prompt)\n            if not p.is_absolute():\n                p = job / p\n            if not p.is_file():\n                return refuse(f\"no prompt file at {p}\", 2)\n            d = sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n            ev = {\"event\": \"generation\", \"action\": \"open\", \"seat\": a.seat, \"n\": n,\n                  \"prompt_file\": relpath(job, p), \"prompt_sha256\": d, \"at\": t}\n        else:\n            if a.n is None:\n                return refuse(\"generation close requires --n N\", 2)\n            if a.n not in opens:\n                return refuse(f\"no open generation {a.n} for {a.seat}\", 3)\n            if opens[a.n]:\n                return refuse(f\"generation {a.n} for {a.seat} is already closed\", 3)\n            ev = {\"event\": \"generation\", \"action\": \"close\", \"seat\": a.seat, \"n\": a.n,\n                  \"outcome\": a.outcome, \"fix_kind\": a.fix_kind, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"evaluation\":\n        p = Path(a.verdict)\n        if not p.is_absolute():\n            p = job / p\n        if not p.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no verdict file at {p}\", 2)\n        vsha = sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n        ev = {\"event\": \"evaluation\", \"batch\": a.batch, \"evaluator\": a.evaluator,\n              \"verdict_file\": relpath(job, p), \"verdict_sha256\": vsha, \"at\": t}\n        if a.iteration is not None:\n            ev[\"iteration\"] = a.iteration\n        if a.summary:\n            sp = Path(a.summary)\n            if not sp.is_absolute():\n                sp = job / sp\n            if not sp.is_file():\n                return refuse(f\"no summary file at {sp}\", 2)\n            try:\n                s = json.loads(sp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n                return refuse(f\"summary {sp} is not JSON ({exc})\", 2)\n            for k in (\"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"writer\"):\n                if not s.get(k):\n                    return refuse(f\"summary {sp} has no {k} stamp; an instrument summary must stamp itself\", 3)\n            ev.update({\"summary_file\": relpath(job, sp), \"summary_sha256\": sha256(sp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n                       \"started_at\": s[\"started_at\"], \"finished_at\": s[\"finished_at\"],\n                       \"summary_writer\": s[\"writer\"]})\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"amendment\":\n        p = Path(a.file)\n        if not p.is_absolute():\n            p = job / p\n        if not p.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no amendment file at {p}\", 2)\n        custody_dir = (job / \"custody\").resolve()\n        try:\n            p.resolve().relative_to(custody_dir)\n            return refuse(f\"amendment file {p} is inside custody/; amendments go beside the frozen set\", 3)\n        except ValueError:\n            pass\n        said = H.parse_ts(a.said_at)\n        if said is None:\n            return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n        frozen = H.parse_ts((ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"frozenAt\"))\n        if frozen and said < frozen:\n            return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at} is before the freeze at {ci['bar']['frozenAt']}\", 3)\n        if said > H.parse_ts(t):\n            return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n        ev = {\"event\": \"amendment\", \"file\": relpath(job, p), \"file_sha256\": sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"quote\": a.quote, \"channel\": a.channel, \"said_at\": a.said_at, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"relay\":\n        said = H.parse_ts(a.source_at)\n        if said is None:\n            return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n        frozen = H.parse_ts((ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"frozenAt\"))\n        if frozen and said < frozen:\n            return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at} is before the freeze at {ci['bar']['frozenAt']}\", 3)\n        if said > H.parse_ts(t):\n            return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n        ev = {\"event\": \"relay\", \"kind\": \"relay\", \"quote\": a.quote, \"from\": a.from_,\n              \"source_chat\": a.source_chat, \"source_at\": a.source_at, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"spend\":\n        lp = Path(a.spend_ledger)\n        if not lp.is_absolute():\n            lp = job / lp\n        rp = Path(a.key_reading)\n        if not rp.is_absolute():\n            rp = job / rp\n        if not lp.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no spend ledger at {lp}\", 2)\n        if not rp.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no key reading at {rp}\", 2)\n        try:\n            r = json.loads(rp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n            return refuse(f\"key reading {rp} is not JSON ({exc})\", 2)\n        if not r.get(\"read_at\") or not r.get(\"writer\"):\n            return refuse(f\"key reading {rp} has no read_at/writer stamp; run tools/edi/or_call.py --spend-status\", 3)\n        read_at = H.parse_ts(r[\"read_at\"])\n        if read_at is None:\n            return refuse(f\"key reading read_at {r['read_at']!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC\", 2)\n        ledger_sum = 0.0\n        last_settle = None\n        try:\n            for line in lp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n                if not line.strip():\n                    continue\n                x = json.loads(line)\n                if x.get(\"event\") == \"settle\":\n                    ledger_sum += float(x.get(\"cost_usd\") or 0)\n                    d = H.parse_ts(x.get(\"at\"))\n                    if d and (last_settle is None or d > last_settle):\n                        last_settle = d\n        except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n            return refuse(f\"spend ledger {lp} is not JSON Lines ({exc})\", 2)\n        if last_settle and (read_at - last_settle).total_seconds() < 180:\n            return refuse(f\"key reading at {r['read_at']} is less than 3 min after the last settle at \"\n                          f\"{H.iso(last_settle)}; read the key again later\", 3)\n        key_delta = float(r.get(\"key_delta_usd\") or 0)\n        total = max(ledger_sum, key_delta)\n        ev = {\"event\": \"spend\", \"spend_ledger\": relpath(job, lp),\n              \"spend_ledger_sha256\": sha256(lp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"key_reading\": relpath(job, rp), \"key_reading_sha256\": sha256(rp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"ledger_sum_usd\": ledger_sum, \"key_delta_usd\": key_delta, \"total_usd\": total,\n              \"read_at\": r[\"read_at\"], \"last_settle_at\": H.iso(last_settle) if last_settle else None, \"at\": t}\n\n    else:\n        return refuse(f\"unknown command {a.cmd!r}\", 2)\n\n    ev[\"writer\"] = writer_stamp()\n    if ci_changed:\n        write_custody(job, ci)\n    append_event(job, ev)\n    extra = \"\"\n    if a.cmd == \"approve\":\n        extra = f\" ({ev.get('role')} by {ev.get('by')})\"\n    elif a.cmd == \"pin\":\n        extra = f\" ({a.seat} -> {a.provider} [{a.slug}] at {ev['host']} via {ev['via']})\"\n    print(f\"logged {ev['event']} at {t}{extra}\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\nWait: In `freeze`, `rel = a.bar or bar.get(\"file\") or \"custody/bar.md\"`. If `a.bar` is an absolute path? INTERFACE says bar file relative to job. We use `job / rel`, which if `rel` is absolute, `Path / absolute` returns absolute. So it works. But `rel` stored in bar is the string given. Fine.\n\nIn `pin`, `H.HOST.match(host)` — host is lowercased. Good.\n\nIn `spend`, `float(x.get(\"cost_usd\") or 0)` — if cost_usd is a string, float works. Good.\n\nNow, one issue: `last_check_time` is called in `dispose` before `ci` is modified. It reads events and logs. Good.\n\nAnother issue: `dispose` with `--decided-at` requires `--decided-source`. But what if `--decided-source` is given without `--decided-at`? We ignore it. Fine.\n\nAnother issue: `generation close` event includes `outcome` and `fix_kind` even if None. The bar says `[--outcome TEXT] [--fix-kind TEXT]`. It might be okay to include nulls. Or we can conditionally include. Base event for approve included `adopted` even if None. We'll keep.\n\nNow, `custody_history.py` full file.\n\nLet's write it with modifications.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"What a custody record may say about its own history, and where each fact must come from.\n...\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport json, os, re, subprocess\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom email.utils import parsedate_to_datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n\nTOLERANCE_S = 60\n...\n```\n\nWe keep everything until `Call`. In `Call`, add `hand_time_entries`.\n\nRemove `_clock` and replace `fill_logger_times`.\n\nLet's carefully copy the base and edit.\n\nBase `fill_logger_times` block:\n\n```python\ndef _clock(created, date) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"...\"\"\"\n    ...\n\n\ndef fill_logger_times(path: Path) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"...\"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\nReplace with:\n\n```python\ndef fill_logger_times(path: Path) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Deprecated: the emitter never writes its inputs (T7).\n\n    Kept as a no-op so a caller that still imports it cannot dirty a harness log. The emitter reads a call\n    with no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` as a hand time and either refuses it or lists it under\n    `--allow-hand-times`; see `Call.hand_time_entries()`.\"\"\"\n    return False\n```\n\nAlso update the module docstring SEND/RECV paragraph.\n\nLet's write the complete file.\n\nOne more thing: `Call.hand_time_entries` uses `self._line_of`. That method is defined later in the class. In Python, methods can call each other regardless of order. Good.\n\nLet's ensure `hand_time_entries` is placed after `_line_of` or anywhere in the class. We'll place after `source_at`.\n\nNow, test file. Let's write it.\n\nWe need to ensure tests pass with the harness. The harness likely runs `python -m pytest tests/` or `unittest discover`. Our test file uses `unittest`. It will be discovered by `pytest` if named `test_*.py`. Good.\n\nLet's write `tests/test_custody_ledger.py`.\n\nPotential issue: `custody_ledger.main` writes to `sys.stderr` on refusal. Tests capture? We don't care.\n\nPotential issue: `now()` returns current time. In `test_dispose_bounds`, we use a fixed date `2026-01-01T00:10:00Z` for the evaluation line. The tool's clock is current (2025? Actually current date in real life is 2026? The system date might be 2026-04-26. The test uses `2026-01-01`, which is in the past. So `decided_at` `2026-01-01T00:10:00Z` is before now, so it passes the \"after tool's clock\" check. Good. But if the system date is before 2026-01-01, then it would be after now and refused. To be safe, we should use a date relative to now. Let's use `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` to generate times. For tests, we can set evaluation finished_at to now - 10 min, and decided_at to now - 5 min. Then it's before now. But `last_check_time` uses the evaluation line. Let's make it dynamic.\n\nIn `test_dispose_bounds`:\n```python\n        now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n        last = now - timedelta(minutes=10)\n        before_last = last - timedelta(seconds=1)\n        after_now = now + timedelta(days=1)\n        fmt = lambda d: d.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n```\n\nUse `fmt(last)` etc. This avoids fixed dates. Good.\n\nSimilarly for amendment/relay, we can use dynamic times. But freeze `at` is current time. `said_at` before freeze: use `datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(days=1)`. After now: `+ timedelta(days=1)`. Equal to freeze: we can read the freeze event `at` and use that. Good.\n\nFor spend, use dynamic times: settle at now - 10 min, reading at now - 8 min (less than 3 min after? Wait: 8 min after settle is > 3 min, so accepted. To refuse, reading at now - 9 min (1 min after settle). Let's do:\n- settle_at = now - 10 min\n- reading_bad = now - 9 min (1 min after settle) -> refused\n- reading_good = now - 6 min (4 min after settle) -> accepted\n\nGood.\n\nFor evaluation summary, we can use any fixed past date since no bounds. But dynamic is fine.\n\nLet's write the tests with dynamic times.\n\nAlso, `test_generation_open_close` uses `prompt` file. Good.\n\nOne issue: `custody_ledger.main` for `freeze` writes `ci[\"bar\"][\"frozenAt\"] = t`. Then `amendment` with `said_at` equal to `frozen` should be accepted. But `H.parse_ts(t)` for now at the time of amendment is slightly later, so `said > now` is false. Good.\n\nAnother issue: `test_amendment_bounds` creates `inside = self.job / \"custody\" / \"amend.md\"`. But `custody` dir already exists (we created `bar.md` there). Good.\n\nAnother issue: `test_spend_bounds` writes spend ledger with settle line. The `spend` command reads `r[\"read_at\"]` and `r[\"writer\"]`. Good.\n\nAnother issue: `test_spend_bounds` after successful spend, we overwrite reading with no stamp and call again. But the event file has the previous spend line. That's fine; it should refuse and not append.\n\nAnother issue: `test_fill_logger_times_does_not_write` uses `H.fill_logger_times(log)`. Our function returns False. Good.\n\nAnother issue: `test_hand_time_entries` uses `H.read_log`. It may add a refusal because `c.at` is not None? Let's check: call has `response.created` and `Date` header. `c.at = received or date or created`. `received` is None (no received_at), `date` is parsed from Date, so `c.at` is set. So no refusal. Good.\n\nLet's also test that `read_log` does not write. We already test `fill_logger_times`.\n\nNow, let's write the test file.\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"kit\"))\nimport custody_ledger as L  # noqa: E402\nimport custody_history as H  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef iso(dt):\n    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\nclass LedgerTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n        self.job = Path(self.tmp.name) / \"job\"\n        (self.job / \"inputs\").mkdir(parents=True)\n        self.ci = {\"custody_inputs\": \"plumbline/custody-inputs/v1\", \"bar\": {}}\n        self.write_ci()\n        self.events = self.job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n        self.events.touch()\n        self.bar = self.job / \"custody\" / \"bar.md\"\n        self.bar.parent.mkdir()\n        self.bar.write_text(\"bar\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    def tearDown(self):\n        self.tmp.cleanup()\n\n    def write_ci(self):\n        (self.job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").write_text(\n            json.dumps(self.ci, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    def read_events(self):\n        return [json.loads(x) for x in self.events.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines() if x.strip()]\n\n    def run_cmd(self, *args):\n        return L.main(list(args))\n\n    def test_writer_stamp_on_every_line(self):\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        sha12 = sha256((ROOT / \"kit\" / \"custody_ledger.py\").read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"writer\"], f\"kit/custody_ledger.py@{sha12}\")\n        self.assertIn(\"at\", ev)\n        # base dispose also carries it\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"dispose\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--by\", \"Owner\"), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"writer\"], f\"kit/custody_ledger.py@{sha12}\")\n\n    def test_generation_open_close(self):\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job)), 0)\n        prompt = self.job / \"prompt.md\"\n        prompt.write_text(\"prompt\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"open\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job),\n                                      \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--prompt\", str(prompt)), 0)\n        after = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertTrue(after.startswith(before))\n        self.assertEqual(len(self.read_events()), 2)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"action\"], \"open\")\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"n\"], 1)\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"prompt_sha256\"], sha256(prompt.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n        # second open refused, nothing appended\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"open\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job),\n                                         \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--prompt\", str(prompt)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # close\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"close\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job),\n                                      \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--n\", \"1\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.read_events()[-1][\"action\"], \"close\")\n        # close again refused\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"close\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job),\n                                         \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--n\", \"1\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # next open n=2\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"generation\", \"open\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job),\n                                      \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--prompt\", str(prompt)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.read_events()[-1][\"n\"], 2)\n\n    def test_evaluation_sha_and_summary(self):\n        verdict = self.job / \"verdict.txt\"\n        verdict.write_text(\"v\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B1\",\n                                      \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(verdict)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"verdict_sha256\"], sha256(verdict.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n        # missing verdict refused\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B1\",\n                                         \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(self.job / \"nope\")), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # summary with stamp\n        summary = self.job / \"summary.json\"\n        summary.write_text(json.dumps({\n            \"started_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n            \"finished_at\": \"2026-01-01T00:01:00Z\",\n            \"writer\": \"tools/edi/x@abc\",\n        }), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B2\",\n                                      \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(verdict),\n                                      \"--summary\", str(summary)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"summary_writer\"], \"tools/edi/x@abc\")\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"started_at\"], \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\")\n        # summary without stamp refused\n        bad = self.job / \"bad.json\"\n        bad.write_text(\"{}\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"evaluation\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--batch\", \"B3\",\n                                         \"--evaluator\", \"e1\", \"--verdict\", str(verdict),\n                                         \"--summary\", str(bad)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n\n    def test_amendment_bounds(self):\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job)), 0)\n        frozen = self.read_events()[-1][\"at\"]\n        amend = self.job / \"amend.md\"\n        amend.write_text(\"a\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n        # before freeze\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(amend),\n                                         \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\",\n                                         \"--said-at\", iso(now - timedelta(days=1))), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # after now\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(amend),\n                                         \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\",\n                                         \"--said-at\", iso(now + timedelta(days=1))), 0)\n        # inside custody\n        inside = self.job / \"custody\" / \"amend.md\"\n        inside.write_text(\"a\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(inside),\n                                         \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\", \"--said-at\", frozen), 0)\n        # accepted at the freeze bound\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"amendment\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--file\", str(amend),\n                                      \"--quote\", \"q\", \"--channel\", \"c\", \"--said-at\", frozen), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"quote\"], \"q\")\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"file_sha256\"], sha256(amend.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n\n    def test_relay_bounds_and_verbatim(self):\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job)), 0)\n        frozen = self.read_events()[-1][\"at\"]\n        now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"relay\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--quote\", \"q\",\n                                         \"--from\", \"BOT\", \"--source-chat\", \"c\",\n                                         \"--source-at\", iso(now - timedelta(days=1))), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"relay\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--quote\", \"q\",\n                                         \"--from\", \"BOT\", \"--source-chat\", \"c\",\n                                         \"--source-at\", iso(now + timedelta(days=1))), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"relay\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--quote\", \" q \",\n                                      \"--from\", \"BOT\", \"--source-chat\", \"c\",\n                                      \"--source-at\", frozen), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"quote\"], \" q \")\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"kind\"], \"relay\")\n\n    def test_spend_bounds_and_stamp(self):\n        now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n        settle_at = iso(now - timedelta(minutes=10))\n        ledger = self.job / \"spend.jsonl\"\n        ledger.write_text(json.dumps({\"event\": \"settle\", \"at\": settle_at, \"cost_usd\": 0.01}) + \"\\n\",\n                          encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        reading = self.job / \"reading.json\"\n        # 1 min after settle: refused\n        reading.write_text(json.dumps({\n            \"read_at\": iso(now - timedelta(minutes=9)),\n            \"writer\": \"tools/edi/or_call.py@abc\",\n            \"key_delta_usd\": 0.02,\n        }), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"spend\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--spend-ledger\", str(ledger),\n                                         \"--key-reading\", str(reading)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        # 4 min after settle: accepted\n        reading.write_text(json.dumps({\n            \"read_at\": iso(now - timedelta(minutes=6)),\n            \"writer\": \"tools/edi/or_call.py@abc\",\n            \"key_delta_usd\": 0.02,\n        }), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"spend\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--spend-ledger\", str(ledger),\n                                      \"--key-reading\", str(reading)), 0)\n        ev = self.read_events()[-1]\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"ledger_sum_usd\"], 0.01)\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"key_delta_usd\"], 0.02)\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"total_usd\"], 0.02)\n        self.assertEqual(ev[\"spend_ledger_sha256\"], sha256(ledger.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n        # no stamp refused\n        reading.write_text(json.dumps({\"read_at\": iso(now - timedelta(minutes=5))}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"spend\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--spend-ledger\", str(ledger),\n                                         \"--key-reading\", str(reading)), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n\n    def test_dispose_bounds(self):\n        now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n        last = now - timedelta(minutes=10)\n        self.events.write_text(json.dumps({\n            \"event\": \"evaluation\", \"batch\": \"B\", \"evaluator\": \"e1\",\n            \"verdict_file\": \"v\", \"verdict_sha256\": \"0\" * 64,\n            \"started_at\": iso(last), \"finished_at\": iso(last), \"at\": iso(last),\n            \"writer\": \"kit/custody_ledger.py@abc\",\n        }) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        before = self.events.read_bytes()\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"dispose\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--by\", \"Owner\",\n                                         \"--state\", \"given\",\n                                         \"--decided-at\", iso(last - timedelta(seconds=1)),\n                                         \"--decided-source\", \"chat\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.events.read_bytes(), before)\n        self.assertNotEqual(self.run_cmd(\"dispose\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--by\", \"Owner\",\n                                         \"--state\", \"given\",\n                                         \"--decided-at\", iso(now + timedelta(days=1)),\n                                         \"--decided-source\", \"chat\"), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(self.run_cmd(\"dispose\", \"--job-dir\", str(self.job), \"--by\", \"Owner\",