efuses or keeps those keys only under .inputs when they try to set emitter's own keys (verdict, gaps, times, hand_times).\n\nAlso tests/validate_schemas.py coverage. And new fixture folders under tests/fixtures/custody/.\n\nBut wait: new fixture folders — the fixtures need to exist for tests/validate_schemas.py to use them. Hmm, but the harness writes files; I can create new fixture folders with files. Let me think about what new fixtures I need.\n\nActually, the T2/T3 fixtures P-T2a..P-T2d are held-out (the evaluator plants them). The bar says \"On held-out planted fixtures P-T2a (ledger lines with no writer), P-T2b (writer: \"hand\"), P-T2c (a time in custody.json with no ledger line) and P-T2d (a tool line overridden by a later hand line)\". Held-out means the evaluator builds them. So I don't need to create them — I need the emitter to handle them.\n\nBut \"new folders under tests/fixtures/custody/ (new planted or clean cases)\" are allowed, and I should add tests in tests/validate_schemas.py that cover the new behaviour. Since fixture-only/test-only fixes are not acceptable, the real work is in emit_custody.py.\n\nLet me now think about what the emitter must do.\n\nCurrent emit_custody.py build() reads inputs/custody.json, harness logs, events log. It does cross-checks (H.cross_check) which refuse on time mismatch. It does not currently implement hand-time detection or refusal.\n\nI need to add:\n1. A hand-time detector that scans:\n   - ledger lines (inputs/custody-events.jsonl) with `writer: \"hand\"` → source `ledger-hand`\n   - ledger lines with no `writer` → source `ledger-no-writer`\n   - values typed into inputs/custody.json with no ledger line behind them → source `inputs-no-ledger`\n   - harness-log calls with no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` → server-header/response-created\n2. Field names per INTERFACE.md section 2:\n   `bar.frozenAt`, `bar.approvals[<i>].at`, `routing.<seat>.declaredAt`, `disposition.at`, `startedAt`, `producedAt`, `passes.<id>.at`