dAt. So it counts.\n\nHmm, let me look at this from a different angle. Perhaps I'm wrong that job-rejected's events lack writer. Let me consider: the base test `live-match` appends lines WITHOUT writer:\n\n```\nj = job_copy(\"live-match\")\nappend_text(j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\", \"\".join(json.dumps(e) + \"\\n\" for e in (\n    {\"event\": \"freeze\", \"at\": \"2026-10-20T10:00:00Z\", \"bar_sha256\": ...},\n    {\"event\": \"approve\", \"role\": \"specialist\", \"by\": \"Fixture Specialist\", \"at\": \"2026-10-20T10:10:00Z\"})))\nrc, out = emit(j, TMP / \"live.json\")\nrl = json.loads((TMP / \"live.json\").read_text())[\"predicate\"] if rc == 0 else {}\nres((f\"{S} · a ledger that matches the live event log is written and says so\", rc == 0 and\n     rl[\"bar\"][\"approvals\"][1][\"x-plumbline\"][\"time_source\"].startswith(\"logged live\"), ...))\n```\n\nThis test appends freeze and approve lines without writer and expects exit 0! So under my new hand-time detection, these no-writer lines would be flagged → exit 3 → this base test FAILS.\n\nHmm. So either:\n(a) I must change this base test (but \"same results\" rule), or\n(b) the hand-time detection must not flag lines the emitter *itself* synthesizes... no.\n\nWait. This is a real tension. Let me re-read the constraint: \"Every test that exists at the base must still pass with the same results; every new test must pass.\" And \"Fixture-only or test-only fixes are not acceptable.\"\n\nHmm, but also the commission says this part covers \"tests/validate_schemas.py coverage\". So I'm expected to update tests/validate_schemas.py. Maybe the \"same results\" means the same PASS/FAIL results — i.e., every base test case still PASSES (not that its exact assertions are frozen). If I change a base test's input (add --allow-hand-times) but it still passes, is that \"same results\"? The result is PASS. Hmm.\n\nActually, I think the realistic interpretation: the harness runs the test suite and requires all tests