r/file for the record is \"the record output\". OK.\n\nAlso, `H.revision` runs git status but doesn't write. Good.\n\nWait — does anything else write? `events_log` reads. `load` reads. No writes except the record. Good. And `fill_logger_times` no-op. So T7 holds.\n\nBut I must make sure I don't accidentally call `fill_logger_times`. I'll remove both calls (or keep; no-op). Let me remove them and add a comment.\n\nActually, if I remove `H.fill_logger_times(log)`, the code still works because `Call.at` falls back. Let me remove.\n\n### Let me now also handle the `--allow-hand-times` in `plumbline_job.py`? That's part 4 (V8), not my part. My allowed paths don't include it. So skip.\n\n### tests/validate_schemas.py changes\n\nI need to:\n1. Modify `emit()` helper to accept `allow_hand=True` and pass `--allow-hand-times`.\n2. Keep all base cases passing.\n3. Add new cases for T2/T3/F1h/X1.\n\nBut careful: the `refused()` helper calls `emit(j, o, **kw)`. With allow_hand default True, refusals still work (other kinds). Good.\n\nBut the T2 new cases need allow_hand=False. I'll call emit directly.\n\nLet me design new test cases:\n\n**T2 (refuse hand times):**\n- P-T2a: copy job-rejected, remove `writer` from a ledger line (the pin line). Emit without switch → exit 3, \"[hand-time]\" in output, nothing written. But wait, removing writer from pin line makes routing.maker.declaredAt a hand time. But also other fields (frozenAt, approvals, disposition) are already hand times (inputs-no-ledger) in job-rejected! So even without the pin, job-rejected refuses. That's fine — P-T2a expects refusal.\n\nActually, for a clean T2 test, I can just use job-rejected without the switch → exit 3, [hand-time], nothing written. That tests P-T2c (inputs-no-ledger) at least. For P-T2a/b/d, I can craft.\n\nBut the base fixture already has hand times (approvals etc.), so any no-switch emit refuses. Good for T2.\n\nLet me write:\n```\no = TMP / \"t2-noswitch.json\"\nrc, out = emit(FIX, o, allow_hand