estrator names the kind of fix in each generation-close line.\n\n## Frozen bar: Maker output contract (verbatim)\n\n## Maker output contract\n- Whole files, between `<<<PLUMBLINE-FILE path=<path>>>>` / `<<<PLUMBLINE-END path=<path>>>>` markers, ending with `<<<PLUMBLINE-DONE files=N>>>` (job 1's format; `handoffs/extract_files.py`, which also limits each request to its part's paths). No diffs.\n- An iteration may take several Maker calls, for example one per part. The iteration's revision is the single commit made from all of them.\n- **The field guide is its own Maker request** (item 30), separate from every code-file request, so no single request risks `finish_reason` `length`. It counts under the same money bound, clock-time bound and cap.\n- The runbook names the command that writes the files (`extract_files.py` **without** `--check`) before the commit.\n- Commits: author `E-DI Maker`, committer `Steve Moitozo II <smoitozo@users.noreply.github.com>`.\n\n## Frozen bar: checks (verbatim, controls omitted)\n\n## Checks (artifact)\n\"The subject\" = the Maker's revision of the iteration. \"Base\" = 3df1ce5. \"Hand time\" = a time in the record whose only source is either a ledger line with `writer: \"hand\"`, a ledger line with no `writer`, or a value typed into `inputs/custody.json` with no ledger line behind it. \"Tool-checked reported time\" = a time a person reported (Owner decision, relay source time, amendment time). It was entered through a ledger command that bounds it, as in F1b, F1e and F1f, and names its source. It is not a hand time (approval item 14).\n\n### T: refuse hand-entered times (the real N3)\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T1 | Every line that any `custody_ledger.py` command appends (old and new commands) carries `writer: \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<first 12 hex of the sha256 of the file that ran>\"`. That value equals the file's sha256 at run time. Its `at` comes from the tool's clock, within ±5 s of the instrumen