SON = ledger.parent / \"custody.json\" as per interface. If not exists, maybe job/inputs/custody.json.\nRecord path = args.record.\n\nNeed recompute hand times. Let's design data structures.\n\n```\ndef ledger_lines(ledger):\n    rows = []\n    for n,line in enumerate(...):\n        parse dict, add _line\n```\nSame as emitter.\n\n`writer_source(e)` same.\n\n`hand_from_ledger(lines, ci, record)`:\n- hand = {}\n- latest freeze line? Emitter uses `ev_log.get(\"freeze\")` latest? `events_log` sets out[e[\"event\"]] = e for each, so last freeze wins. We'll use last.\n- For each line in order, if writer_source(line):\n  - event freeze -> field bar.frozenAt, file ledger rel, line, source\n  - approve -> find approval index in ci.bar.approvals with role == line.role. If found, field bar.approvals[i].at. If multiple, maybe last? Use index.\n  - dispose -> disposition.at\n  - pin -> if seat in used seats, routing.<seat>.declaredAt\n- But if later tool line overrides earlier hand line? \"When a later ledger line sets the same field as an earlier one, the later line's value, line and source are the ones used and reported.\" So iterate and overwrite. For approve, latest per role. For freeze, latest. For dispose, latest. For pin, latest per seat.\n- If line writer tool, should remove any earlier hand mark for same field? Yes later line sets same field. So if source None, `hand.pop(field, None)`.\n- For event generation/evaluation etc ignore.\n\n`hand_from_inputs`:\n- Only if no live event for field? Actually if there is a live event with tool writer, no hand. If live event hand, already. If no live event, and value present, mark.\n- For bar.frozenAt: if no freeze line (any) and ci.bar.frozenAt present -> inputs-no-ledger. But if freeze line exists with tool writer, no. If freeze line exists hand, already.\n- approvals: for each i,a in ci.bar.approvals, if no approve line with role a.role, and a.at present -> mark. If approve line exists, whether hand or tool, no inputs-no-ledger.