uting: for seat in seats: if no pin line for seat and ci.routing[seat].declaredAt: mark.\n  - disposition: if no dispose line and ci.disposition.at: mark.\n  - startedAt/producedAt: determine maker model log calls. If ci.startedAt and not maker_calls: mark. If ci.producedAt and not maker_calls: mark. But emitter marks only if `not mk.get(\"startedAt\")`. If maker kind model with log, mk has startedAt. If no log, emitter may refuse and no record. So okay.\n  - passes: for pid,f in ci.passes.items(): if f.at and not linked_call: mark. Need `linked_call` function.\n  - controls: for k in ci.controls: if k.at and not linked_call: mark.\n- Logs:\n  - for each log in evidence glob(\"*.log\") + job glob? Use evidence only and job root maybe. Read H.read_log(log, H.Refusals(), \"verify\"). For each call, for e in call.hand_time_entries(): add e. But H.read_log may return calls even if log malformed. Catch.\n  - Also if call has no sent_at/received_at but hand_time_entries empty? Trust.\n- Return sorted list by field? Emitter returns in insertion order. For comparison, sort.\n\nNeed `maker_calls` and evaluator calls for linked. We'll write `read_logs(job, evidence, ci)` returns dict seat->calls and all_calls. It should mimic emitter:\n- maker: if ci.maker.kind == \"model\": log = find_log(ci.maker.harness_log, \"harness-maker*.log\"); read.\n- evaluators: for each e kind model: log = e.harness_log or external evidence_file; read.\n- If no ci, scan all logs.\n- `find_log(job, evidence, rel, pattern)`.\n- H.read_log may need `H.Refusals()`. Use.\n- Filter calls with at? For hand times, include all.\n\nFor linked pass: if evaluator id in ev_calls and f.call in calls -> linked. If f.call missing and len(calls)==1 -> linked (emitter link_call). If f.call missing and len>1 -> not linked? Emitter would refuse. For hand detection, if no link, typed at is hand. Good.\n\n`expected_ledger_array(lines,event)`.\n\n`compute_spend(job, ci, lines, all_calls)`:\n- last spend line.\n- calls_sum = round(sum(call_cost(c)),6)\n- key_delta = float(sp.key_delta_usd or 0)\n- total = max\n- return dict.\n- `call_cost(c)` replicate:\n```\nraw = c.raw\nresp = raw.get(\"response\") if dict...\nusage = resp.get(\"usage\") ...\nfor v in (raw.get(\"total_cost\"), resp.get(\"total_cost\"), usage.get(\"total_cost\"), usage.get(\"cost\")): if number return float\n```\nNeed c.raw exists. H.Call likely has raw. Use getattr.\n\n`read_spend_ledger(job, lines)` find last spend line, path.\n\n`check_events`:\n- For event in generations,evaluations,relays,amendments: compare record array to expected. If mismatch add events with field.\n- For each evaluation line in ledger: verdict_file, verdict_sha256; read file relative job; if mismatch add events.\n- Relay as approval: `for r in relays: if any(a.get(\"by\")==r.get(\"from\") or a.get(\"kind\")==\"relay\" or a.get(\"relay\") for a in approvals): add relay-as-approval`.\n- Generation calls: for each generation open/close pair, find maker calls. If no call between -> events. Need parse `at` from open/close. If no maker calls -> events. Use all_calls filtered maker.\n- Maybe each generation has at least one call; if multiple, any.\n- \"No relay appears as an approval\" also check `predicate.bar.approvals` vs `x-plumbline.relays`.\n\n`check_spend`:\n- `sp = xp.get(\"spend\")`; if not dict -> spend.\n- require fields.\n- compute expected from all_calls and ledger. Compare calls_sum within 0.0001.\n- total == max exactly.\n- settle lines: read spend ledger file. For each settle, if `call` and not in labels -> spend. If no `call`, maybe check `id` in reserve? We can require `call` in labels.\n- key reading: if spend line exists, read key_reading file; check read_at, writer; if last_settle_at parse and delta < 180 -> spend. Also check key reading's `key_delta_usd`? Not.\n- If no spend line but calls_sum >0? Emitter would have no key delta but spend block. V5 says key reading stamped. If no spend line, can't. We can add spend if key_delta !=0 or calls_sum>0 and no spend line? But clean T4 likely has spend line. For readings job with no calls, no spend line, spend block zeros. We can allow.\n- \"Each spend-ledger settle line matches one logged call.\" If spend line exists, read ledger.\n\n`check_shadow`:\n- derive owned values.\n- `inputs = xp.get(\"inputs\")`.\n- For each owned key in list:\n  - if not isinstance(inputs, dict) or key not in inputs: continue\n  - derived = derived_values.get(key)\n  - if derived is not None and xp.get(key) == inputs[key] and xp.get(key) != derived: add shadow.\n  - Also if key == \"gaps\" and xp.get(\"gaps\") == inputs.get(\"gaps\") and inputs.get(\"gaps\"): add shadow? We'll do if top-level gaps equals inputs.gaps and any gap field in owned? Hmm. The planted P-V6 copies `inputs.verdict`/`inputs.hand_times` over owned keys. So derived for verdict and hand_times. Good.\n- Also check any owned key appears at predicate top-level? They are supposed to. The issue is values.\n- Derive verdict: read s5_record. If xp.s5_record.name, load job / name. If rec has verdict, derived = rec[\"verdict\"]. If no s5 record, derived = None.\n- Derive times: if maker calls -> \"harness log\" else \"hand-entered\".\n- Derive time_tolerance_s = H.TOLERANCE_S.\n- Derive schema = SCHEMA_VERSION.\n- Derive arrays.\n- Derive spend.\n- Derive hand_times.\n\nNeed `check_schema`:\n- Load schema file. If missing -> schema.\n- Validate record root against schema using `jsonschema` if available else custom.\n- Check `predicate.x-plumbline` exists.\n- Check `xp.schema` == version.\n- Validate xp against `$defs/xPlumbline`.\n- Walk for nested x-plumbline: validate against `$defs/xNested`.\n- If any failure -> add schema with field.\n\nCustom validator: Implement `validate(instance, schema, root, path)` returns list of (field, message). Support `$ref`, `type`, `required`, `properties`, `additionalProperties`, `items`, `const`, `enum`, `anyOf`, `oneOf`, `allOf`, `minLength`, `pattern`, `minimum`, `maximum`. For `$ref` local. Use `root[\"$defs\"]`.\n\nNeed ensure schema validation of record root: our schema root requires `_type`, `subject`, `predicateType`, `predicate`. If minimal record lacks -> schema fail. Good.\n\nNeed standard check:\n```\ndef checker_path(custody):\n    for rel in (\"checker/check.py\",\"check.py\",\"tools/checker/check.py\"):\n        p = Path(custody)/rel\n        if p.is_file(): return p\n    return None\n```\nPin:\n```\ndef find_pin(custody, checker):\n    sha = file_sha(checker)\n    candidates = [Path(custody)/\"tools\"/\"pin.json\", REPO/\"tools\"/\"pin.json\"]\n    for p in candidates:\n        if p.is_file():\n            doc = load\n            for val in walk_values(doc):\n                if isinstance(val,str) and val == sha: return sha\n                if isinstance(val,str) and val.startswith(\"aaeb7e05\") and val.endswith(\"bcd18\"): return val\n            # key containing checker/check.py\n            for k,v in walk_items(doc):\n                if \"checker/check.py\" in k and isinstance(v,str): return v\n    return None\n```\nIf pin None -> exit 2. But in tests, we create fake pin.\n- Compare `sha == pin`.\n- Run standard.\n\nNeed output:\n- `--json OUT` writes `{\"exit\": N, \"failures\": [...]}`.\n- Print each failure `FAIL <kind> <field> <file>:<line>`. If file/line None, use `-`? Interface says file:line. We can use `field` and `file`/`line`. For missing, `\"\"` and 0. Print `FAIL kind field file:line`.\n- Exit code: if standard fail -> 3, only standard. Else if any failures -> 4. Else 0. Cannot run -> 2.\n\nNeed `main` order:\n1. Parse args.\n2. Resolve job.\n3. Snapshot hashes for V7.\n4. Check static import? Do at end? If fail -> 4? V7 is Plumbline layer? It says V7 never writes, stands alone. Failure kind? Not named. We can use kind `standalone`? The bar's kinds list doesn't include. V7 held-out may check exit. We can add kind `standalone` if import found. But V7 says static import check; if it imports emit_cust