. `test_schema_missing_block_exit_4`: fake check ok, pin correct, record missing x-plumbline -> exit 4, kind schema.\n3. `test_schema_hand_times_string`: record with x-plumbline schema correct but hand_times string -> exit 4 schema.\n4. `test_hand_times_recompute`: unit call `compute_hand_times` with ledger line writer hand -> includes bar.frozenAt.\n5. `test_events_missing_generation`: unit call `check_events` with ledger generation but record generations empty -> failure events.\n6. `test_spend_mismatch`: unit call `check_spend` with spend calls_sum off -> failure spend.\n7. `test_shadow`: unit call `check_shadow` with inputs.verdict and xp.verdict same wrong -> shadow.\n8. `test_no_import_emit_custody`: read verifier source, assert \"import emit_custody\" not in.\n\nNeed make functions importable. In verifier, use `if __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())`.\n\nFor tests, `sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT/\"kit\"))` then `import plumbline_verify as V`. But verifier imports custody_history, which exists. Good.\n\nNeed create minimal record for schema tests. Our schema root requires `_type`, `subject`, `predicateType`, `predicate`. We'll create:\n```\n{\n \"_type\":\"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\",\n \"subject\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"digest\":{\"sha256\":\"0\"*64}}],\n \"predicateType\":\"https://evaluatordriven.com/custody/v1\",\n \"predicate\":{\"x-plumbline\":{\"schema\":\"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\",\"hand_times\":[],...}}\n}\n```\nBut schema xPlumbline requires many? We can make xPlumbline not require most, only schema. Then minimal passes schema but other checks may fail. For schema missing block, exit 4. For hand_times string, exit 4. Good.\n- To avoid standard check failing due record? Fake check returns 0 regardless.\n- Pin file: `{\"checker/check.py\": sha}`.\n\nNeed `compute_hand_times` function signature. We'll design `compute_hand_times(job, ledger_path, custody_path, record, evidence)`.\n\nNeed `check_events` signature. We'll design `check_events(job, ledger_path, record, all_calls, add)` where `add` is callback? Better return list of failures. For tests, call `V.check_events(job, ledger, record, calls)` returns list of dicts. We'll implement functions returning list.\n\nLet's design verifier with pure functions:\n- `hand_time_set(job, ledger_path, custody_path, record, evidence) -> list[dict]`\n- `check_hand_times(hand, record) -> list[dict]`\n- `check_events(job, ledger_path, record, calls_by_seat) -> list[dict]`\n- `check_spend(job, ledger_path, record, all_calls) -> list[dict]`\n- `check_shadow(job, ledger_path, record, all_calls) -> list[dict]`\n- `check_schema(record, schema_path) -> list[dict]`\n- `standard_check(record, custody) -> tuple[int, dict|None]`\n\nThen `verify(args)`.\n\nLet's implement `hand_time_set` carefully.\n\nNeed `line_in` for custody.json line? The emitter uses `line_in(inputs_path, value, \"at\")` to get line. We can implement similar:\n```\ndef line_of(path, value, key=None):\n    if value is None: return None\n    ...\n```\nFor inputs-no-ledger, file is rel path to job (e.g. `inputs/custody.json`). Line is line containing value.\n\nFor ledger hand, file `inputs/custody-events.jsonl`, line n.\n\nFor logs, H.hand_time_entries likely provides file/line/source already. We'll use as is.\n\nNeed `rel_inputs`: `custody_path.relative_to(job).as_posix()` if possible.\n\nNeed `used_seats`: from ci maker kind model + evaluators kind model. Emitter uses `m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\"` and evaluator kind model. Good.\n\nNeed `approval_index`: `ci.get(\"bar\",{}).get(\"approvals\",[])` list. Match role. If multiple same role, emitter's `ev_log[\"approve\"][role]` latest, and loop over approvals marks each with same role? Actually in build, for each approval i, `live = ev_log[\"approve\"].get(a.get(\"role\"))`. If two approvals same role, both get same live line and both mark `bar.approvals[i].at`. So our loop should mark all matching role. Good.\n\nFor ledger iterate approve line: mark all approvals