y returns `file` as log name, `line` as line number. Good.\n\n### Events check details\n\n`expected_ledger_array`:\n```\ndef ledger_array(lines,event):\n    return [{**{k:v for k,v in e.items() if k!=\"_line\"}, \"source\": f\"{LEDGER_REL}:{e['_line']}\"} for _,e in lines if e.get(\"event\")==event]\n```\nBut if ledger_path is absolute, source should be `inputs/custody-events.jsonl:<line>` relative to job. Emitter uses `LEDGER_REL`. We'll use `ledger_rel` computed relative to job, default `inputs/custody-events.jsonl`.\n\nCompare with record `xp[event+\"s\"]`. For generations, evaluations, relays, amendments.\n\nEvaluation sha: for each e in lines event evaluation:\n```\nvf = e.get(\"verdict_file\"); sha = e.get(\"verdict_sha256\")\np = job/vf if not abs\nif not p.is_file() or file_sha(p)!=sha -> events\n```\nP-V4b planted modifies record's evaluation array sha? They said \"an evaluation whose verdict sha differs from the file\". Could be ledger line sha differs from file. We check ledger vs file, not record. If record array matches ledger but ledger sha wrong, fail. Good. If record array sha changed but ledger correct, array mismatch -> events. Good.\n\nGeneration calls: For each generation open line and close line same seat,n. Need maker calls. Use calls_by_seat[\"maker\"] list. Find calls with time between open.at and close.at. If none -> events. If no close? Emitter may have open only; ledger array matches. The bar says each generation has at least one call between open and close. If no close, fail? We'll skip if no close? Better fail if open and no close? The ledger could be mid-generation but record at close should have close. We'll require close. If no close -> events.\n- Time parse: H.parse_ts(open[\"at\"]). Calls have `started`, `at`, `sent`, `received`. Use `c.started or c.at`. If any between. If no maker calls at all -> events.\n\nRelay as approval:\n```\nrelays = expected ledger event relay\napprovals = record.predicate.bar.approvals\nfor r in relays:\n 