thout at? Server-time calls have at from server. If no at, maybe. For spend, filter. We'll keep all_calls but compute sum over `[c for c in all_calls if getattr(c,\"at\",None)]`. For settle labels, use all. For hand times, use all.\n\nPotential issue: `call_cost` raw response. Use `c.raw`.\n\nPotential issue: `check_spend` key reading file path relative to job. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `check_shadow` derived spend uses all_calls filtered.\n\nPotential issue: `check_shadow` `inputs` could be non-dict. Skip.\n\nPotential issue: `check_schema` root schema may require `subject` items etc. Our minimal test record has subject. Good.\n\nPotential issue: Our schema `xPlumbline` additionalProperties false. If record has `x-plumbline` with key `sources` etc. We list all. But what about `x-plumbline` key `approvals`? Not emitted. What about `x-plumbline` key `spend`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `gaps`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `emitter`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `terminal_state`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `outcome`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `verdict`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `iteration`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `s5_record`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `earlier_iterations`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `pass_rule`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `disposition_source`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `packet`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `events_log`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `job_id`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `sources`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `timeSources`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `time_sources`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `emittedAt`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `schema`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `hand_times`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `allowances`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `generations`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `evaluations`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `relays`? yes. What about `x-plumbline` key `amen