t(\"read_at\") or not r.get(\"writer\"): add spend\n    else:\n        read_at=H.parse_ts(r[\"read_at\"]); last=H.parse_ts(sp_line.get(\"last_settle_at\"))\n        if read_at and last and (read_at-last).total_seconds() < 180: add spend\n        if abs(float(r.get(\"key_delta_usd\") or 0) - key_delta) > 1e-6: add spend\nelse: add spend\n```\n- If `last_settle_at` None but spend ledger has settles, maybe check? The spend line has last_settle_at. If None, skip.\n- Also check `read_at` >= last settle + 180. Good.\n\n#### Shadow check details\n\nNeed `calls_by_seat` to derive times. Signature `check_shadow(job, ledger_path, record, all_calls, hand, calls_by_seat)`.\n\nDerived:\n```\nderived = {}\nderived[\"schema\"]=SCHEMA_VERSION\nderived[\"time_tolerance_s\"]=H.TOLERANCE_S\nderived[\"hand_times\"]=hand\nfor ev,key in ...: derived[key]=ledger_array(...)\nderived[\"spend\"]=compute_spend_block(...)\ns5=...\nif s5 file: rec=load; if \"verdict\" in rec: derived[\"verdict\"]=rec[\"verdict\"]\nmcalls = calls_by_seat.get(\"maker\") or {}\nderived[\"times\"]={\"startedAt\":\"harness log\" if mcalls else \"hand-entered\", \"producedAt\": ...}\n```\nNeed `all_calls` for spend. Good.\n\nOwned keys list.\n\nFor each key:\n```\nif isinstance(inputs,dict) and key in inputs and key in xp and key in derived:\n    if xp[key] == inputs[key] and xp[key] != derived[key]:\n        add shadow key\n```\nAlso check `xp.get(key) != derived[key]` even if inputs doesn't have key? V6 says every emitter-owned key holds value verifier re-derives. So we should check all owned keys where derived is not None and key in xp, regardless of inputs. If xp[key] != derived[key], add shadow? But the kind `shadow` is specifically inputs shadowing. The bar V6 says every emitter-owned key holds the value re-derived. So mismatch -> shadow. We can add for all owned keys with derived not None and key in xp. But `gaps` no derived. `allowances` derived? We can skip. `verdict` derived if s5. `times` derived. `hand_times` derived. Arrays. Spend. Schema. time_tolerance_s. This would catch P-V6 and any tampering. But could false fail clean if our derivation differs from emitter. For hand_times, our recompute should match. For events, match. For spend, match. For times, maybe. For verdict, match. Good. We'll add for keys in derived if xp has key and xp[key] != derived[key] -> shadow. But the bar says \"Input data appears only under x-plumbline.inputs. Every emitter-owned key ... holds the value the verifier re-derives\". So mismatch -> shadow. However, if a field is absent in xp, should we fail? The bar says every owned key. But `inputs` optional, `allowances` optional. We'll only check present keys. For `verdict`, if no s5 and xp.verdict from ci, derived None -> skip.\n- For `gaps`, no derived. Skip.\n- For `allowances`, derive? If hand non-empty, the record must have allowance (V3). The value can be any valid. Skip.\n- For `inputs`, not owned? It's an owned key? The list doesn't include inputs. Good.\n\nBut if xp has `verdict` from ci and no s5, derived None, skip. If inputs.verdict copied over xp.verdict, no s5? Then can't derive. P-V6 likely has s5. Good.\n\nAlso check if `inputs` contains an owned key and xp top-level equals it but derived differs. The general check catches if derived. Good.\n\n#### V7 snapshot\n\nIn `main`, before checks:\n```\nsnap = snapshot(paths)\n...\nafter = snapshot(paths)\nif snap != after: add writes\n```\n`snapshot`:\n```\ndef snapshot(paths):\n    out={}\n    for p in paths:\n        p=Path(p)\n        if p.is_file(): out[str(p)] = file_sha(p)\n        elif p.is_dir():\n            for f in sorted(p.rglob(\"*\")):\n                if f.is_file(): out[str(f)] = file_sha(f)\n    return out\n```\nBut if record path doesn't exist before, after exists? The verifier never writes. If missing, snapshot includes no key. After same. Good.\n- The verifier writes `--json OUT` maybe under record? Not. Snapshot before JSON write. If OUT under input path, could change. But user. We'll snapshot before writing JSON.\n\n#### Main\n\n```\ndef main(argv=None):\n    ap=...\n    a=ap.parse_args(argv)\n    record=Path(a.record).expanduser()\n    ledger=Path(a.ledger).expanduser()\n    files=Path(a.files).expanduser()\n    evidence=Path(a.evidence).expanduser()\n    custody=Path(a.custody).expanduser()\n    job = ledger.parent.parent if ledger.parent.name==\"inputs\" else (files if (files/\"packet.json\").is_file() else files.parent.parent)\n    if not (job/\"packet.json\").is_file():\n        # try evidence parent parent\n        if (evidence.parent.parent/\"packet.json\").is_file(): job=evidence.parent.parent\n    custody_json = ledger.parent/\"custody.json\"\n    failures=[]\n    # V7 snapshot\n    snap = snapshot([record, files, evidence, ledger])\n    # standard\n    code, detail = standard_check(record, custody)\n    if code == 2:\n        failures.append({\"kind\":\"standard\",\"field\":\"checker\",\"file\":str(custody), \"line\":0})\n        return finish(2, failures, a.json)\n    if code != 0:\n        failures.append({\"kind\":\"standard\",\"field\":\"record\",\"file\":str(record), \"line\":0})\n        return finish(3, failures, a.json)\n    # schema\n    failures += check_schema(record, SCHEMA_PATH)\n    if failures:\n        return finish(4, failures, a.json)\n    # load record\n    try: rec=load(record)\n    except: return finish(2, [{\"kind\":\"standard\",...}], a.json)\n    # read calls\n    ci = load(custody_json) if custody_json.is_file() else {}\n    calls_by_seat, all_calls = read_calls(job, evidence, ci)\n    hand = hand_time_set(job, ledger, custody_json, rec, evidence)\n    failures += check_hand_times(hand, rec)\n    failures += check_events(job, ledger, rec, calls_by_seat)\n    failures += check_spend(job, ledger, rec, all_calls)\n    failures += check_shadow(job, ledger, rec, all_calls, hand, calls_by_seat)\n    # V7 snapshot after\n    if snapshot([record, files, evidence, ledger]) != snap:\n        failures.append({\"kind\":\"writes\",\"field\":\"inputs\",\"file\":str(job),\"line\":0})\n    return finish(4 if failures else 0, failures, a.json)\n```\nBut if schema failures, we exit 4 without running other checks. V2 says exit 4 kind schema. Good.\nIf standard fails, exit 3. Good.\nIf cannot run (missing record, missing ledger, missing custody) -> exit 2. We need check required paths:\n```\nif not record.is_file(): return finish(2, [{\"kind\":\"standard\",\"field\":\"record\",\"file\":str(record),\"line\":0}], a.json)\nif not ledger.is_file(): ...\nif not custody.is_dir(): ...\n```\nBut standard check should run first? If missing record, cannot run. Exit 2. V1 says wrong checker exit 2. Fine.\nNeed `finish`:\n```\ndef finish(exit_code, failures, json_out):\n    for f in failures:\n        print(f\"FAIL {f['kind']} {f['field']} {f.get('file','')}:{f.get('line',0)}\")\n    if json_out:\n        Path(json_out).write_text(json.dumps({\"exit\":exit_code,\"failures\":failures}, indent=2)+\"\\n\")\n    return exit_code\n```\nNeed `--json` optional.\n\nStandard check function:\n```\ndef standard_check(record, custody):\n    check = None\n    for rel in (\"checker/check.py\",\"check.py\",\"tools/checker/check.py\"):\n        p=Path(custody)/rel\n        if p.is_file(): check=p; break\n    if check is None:\n        # try repo\n        p=REPO/\"checker\"/\"check.py\"\n        if p.is_file(): check=p\n    if check is None: return 2, \"no checker\"\n    sha=file_sha(check)\n    pin=find_pin(custody, check)\n    if pin is None: return 2, \"no pin\"\n    if sha != pin: return 2, \"pin mismatch\"\n    level = \"CL1\"\n    try:\n        rec=load(record); level=rec.get(\"predicate\",{}).get(\"levelClaimed\") or \"CL1\"\n    except Exception: pass\n    forms=...\n    last=None\n    for form in forms:\n        rv=subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(check), *form], capture_output=True, text=True)\n        last=rv\n        if rv.returncode==0: return 0, rv\n        text=(rv.stdout+rv.stderr).lower()\n        if any(x in text for x in (\"usage\",\"unrecognized arguments\",\"error: argument\",\"no such option\",\"invalid choice\")):\n            continue\n        return rv.returncode, rv\n    return (last.returncode if last else 2), last\n```\nBut forms include `str(check)`? We call `[sys.executable, str(check), *form]` where form is args. Define:\n```\nforms = [\n [str(record), \"--level\", level],\n [\"--record\", str(record), \"--level\", level],\n [str(record), level],\n [\"--level\", level, str(record)],\n]\n```\nGood.\n\n`find_pin`:\n```\ndef _strip_sha(v):\n    if isinstance(v,str):\n        v=v.strip()\n        if v.startswith(\"sha256:\"): v=v[7:]\n        return v\n    return v\ndef _is_pin(v):\n    v=_strip_sha(v)\n    return isinstance(v,str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", v) is not None\ndef find_pin(custody, check):\n    sha=file_sha(check)\n    for p in (Path(custody)/\"tools\"/\"pin.json\", REPO/\"tools\"/\"pin.json\"):\n        if not p.is_file(): continue\n        try: doc=load(p)\n        except Exception: continue\n        found=_find_pin_in(doc, sha)\n        if found: return found\n    return None\n```\n`_find_pin_in(obj, sha)`:\n```\nif isinstance(obj,dict):\n    for k,v in obj.items():\n        if isinstance(v,str):\n            vv=_strip_sha(v)\n            if vv==sha: return vv\n            if vv.startswith(\"aaeb7e05\") and vv.endswith(\"bcd18\"): return vv\n            if \"checker/check.py\" in str(k) and _is_pin(v): return vv\n        if isinstance(v,dict):\n            path=str(v.get(\"path\") or v.get(\"file\") or \"\")\n            if \"checker/check.py\" in path:\n                for kk in (\"sha256\",\"digest\",\"hash\"):\n                    if _is_pin(v.get(kk)): return _strip_sha(v.get(kk))\n            r=_find_pin_in(v, sha)\n            if r: return r\n        if isinstance(v,list):\n            r=_find_pin_in(v, sha)\n            if r: return r\nelif isinstance(obj,list):\n    for v in obj:\n        r=_find_pin_in(v, sha)\n        if r: return r\nreturn None\n```\nBut if subject `tools/pin.json` has a pin for checker/check.py that is not our fake sha, and custody/tools/pin.json has our fake sha, we prefer custody first. Good.\nIf custody/tools/pin.json has pin but not matching check, we return None? `_find_pin_in` returns any pin starting aaeb... even if not sha. That could be wrong pin from subject. But we want the pin value, then compare. If custody pin file has a different pin, return it, then sha != pin -> exit 2. Good.\nIf no pin file, return None.\n\nNeed `_find_pin_in` for key \"checker/check.py\" with value sha. It returns if `_is_pin(v)` even if not sha. Good.\n\n#### Test code details\n\nNeed import verifier. It imports custody_history. Good.\n\nTest `test_hand_time_set`:\n- Create job, ledger line with writer \"hand\", at, event freeze, bar_file, bar_sha256.\n- custody.json with `{\"bar\":{\"frozenAt\":\"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"file\":\"custody/bar.md\",\"approvals\":[]}}`.\n- `record={\"predicate\":{\"x-plumbline\":{}}}`.\n- `hand = V.hand_time_set(job, ledger, custody, record, evidence)`.\n- assert any e[\"field\"]==\"bar.frozenAt\" and e[\"source\"]==\"ledger-hand\".\n\nNeed `hand_time_set` signature. We'll define `def hand_time_set(job, ledger_path, custody_path, record, evidence):`.\n\nTest `test_events_missing_generation`:\n- ledger lines: generation open and close with writer \"kit/custody_ledger.py@abc\", at. \n- record `{\"predicate\":{\"x-plumbline\":{\"generations\":[]}}}`.\n- `fails = V.check_events(job, ledger, record, {})`.\n- assert any kind events.\n\nTest `test_spend_mismatch`:\n- ledger spend line with key_delta 1.0, spend_ledger \"spend.jsonl\", key_reading \"key.json\", last_settle_at None, writer, at.\n- create spend.jsonl empty.\n- key.json with read_at, writer, key_delta_usd 1.0.\n- record xp spend calls_sum 2.0, key_delta 1.0, total 2.0, tolerance 0.0001.\n- `fails = V.check_spend(job, ledger, record, [])`.\n- assert spend.\n\nTest