Also check key reading's `key_delta_usd` equals sp.key_delta? Could. We'll check within 1e-6.\n\n### Shadow details\n\n`derived_values`:\n- schema = SCHEMA_VERSION\n- time_tolerance_s = H.TOLERANCE_S\n- hand_times = hand_time_set(...) (computed in verify; pass in)\n- generations = expected array\n- evaluations, relays, amendments\n- spend = compute_spend_block\n- verdict = read s5 record\n- times = {\"startedAt\": \"harness log\" if maker calls else \"hand-entered\", ...}\n- gaps = None (skip)\n- allowances = if hand and allowance present? Not an owned key? It is owned. The bar lists allowances. Derive: if hand non-empty and xp.allowances.hand_times present, then allowance object; else None. For shadow, if inputs has allowances and xp.allowances == inputs.allowances and derived differs? We can check.\n- For `gaps`, no derive. But we can check if inputs has `gaps` and xp.gaps == inputs.gaps and any gap has field in owned? Maybe skip.\n- For `verdict`: if s5_record present and file exists, load rec. If rec has verdict, derived. If no s5, derived = None.\n- `times`: derived from calls.\n- `spend`: expected.\n- `hand_times`: computed.\n- For each key in owned: if inputs is dict and key in inputs and key in xp:\n  - if derived is not None and xp[key] == inputs[key] and xp[key] != derived: add shadow.\n  - Special for `gaps`: if inputs has gaps and xp.gaps == inputs.gaps and inputs.gaps: add shadow? Could be false. But planted P-V6 uses verdict/hand_times. We'll not.\n\nAlso check if any owned key appears under `x-plumbline.inputs` and is a dict/list with same object? Not.\n\n### Schema\n\nWrite schema. Need decide required fields. To avoid failing clean records, make xPlumbline require only `schema`? But V2 P-V2a block missing handled by required at predicate. For valid clean, other fields present. We can require `schema`, `hand_times`, `generations`, `evaluations`, `relays`, `amendments`, `spend`, `inputs`? The emitter always writes these except inputs only if ci has x-