e_job(tmp)`:\n```\njob=tmp/\"job\"; (job/\"inputs\").mkdir(parents=True); (job/\"custody\"/\"evidence\").mkdir(parents=True); (job/\"custody\"/\"files\").mkdir(parents=True)\n(job/\"packet.json\").write_text(\"{}\")\n(job/\"inputs\"/\"custody.json\").write_text(\"{}\\n\")\n(job/\"inputs\"/\"custody-events.jsonl\").write_text(\"\")\nrecord=job/\"custody\"/\"record.custody.json\"\nreturn job, record\n```\nFor schema test record:\n```\ndef minimal_record(xp):\n    return {\"_type\":..., \"subject\":[], \"predicateType\":..., \"predicate\":{\"x-plumbline\":xp}}\n```\nsubject empty allowed.\n\nTest CLI:\n```\ndef run_v(record, job, custody):\n    return subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(VERIFIER), \"--record\", str(record), \"--files\", str(job/\"custody/files\"), \"--evidence\", str(job/\"custody/evidence\"), \"--ledger\", str(job/\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\"), \"--custody\", str(custody)], capture_output=True, text=True)\n```\nExpect returncode.\n\nFor schema missing block, record `{\"predicate\":{}}`. But root schema requires predicate.x-plumbline -> fail. Good.\n\nFor hand_times string, record with xp `{\"schema\":SCHEMA_VERSION,\"hand_times\":\"bad\"}`. Root passes, xPlumbline fails type. Good.\n\nFor unknown key, xp `{\"schema\":..., \"hand_times\":[], \"extra\":1}`. Fail.\n\nFor wrong checker, record can be anything; standard check runs first, pin mismatch -> exit 2. Need record file exists. Good.\n\nUnit tests:\n- `test_hand_time_set_reads_hand_ledger`: create job with ledger line writer hand. custody.json with bar.frozenAt. record empty. Call `V.hand_time_set(job, ledger, custody, record, evidence)`. Expect any e field bar.frozenAt source ledger-hand.\n- `test_events_missing_generation`: ledger with generation open+close. record xp generations empty. Call `V.check_events(job, ledger, record, {})`. Expect kind events. But check_events also tries generation calls with empty -> events. Good.\n- `test_spend_mismatch`: create ledger spend line, spend ledger file