-T2c (a time in `custody.json` with no ledger line) and P-T2d (a tool line overridden by a later hand line), the emitter **with no switch** exits 3 with refusal kind `hand-time`, names every hand-time field and its file:line, and writes nothing. | S1 | `evidence/T2.json` |\n| T3 | On the same fixtures **with `--allow-hand-times`**, the record is written and check.py reads OK at CL1. `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` lists exactly the hand-time fields, no more and no fewer, each with file:line, and the record carries the allowance `x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times` (`switch: \"--allow-hand-times\"`, the emitter's `writer`, and its tool-clock `at`). The listing is **not disclosure only**: `kit/plumbline_verify.py` fails a record whose flags lack the allowance or disagree with the ledger and logs (V3), and close refuses on that failure (V8). The switch silences nothing else: the repo overlay `failures/hand-times` (log contradicts the hand time) still exits 3 with the switch on. | S1 | `evidence/T3.json` |\n| T4 | A job built at batch time only by the subject's own tools emits with **no switch**, exit 0, check.py OK at CL1, and an empty `hand_times`. The tools used: `custody_ledger.py` freeze/approve/pin/generation/evaluation/dispose, plus `tools/edi/or_call.py` with its mocked transport writing the harness logs. | S1 | `evidence/T4.json` + the built job |\n| T5 | **Cross-checks no looser than at base.** (a) `custody_history.TOLERANCE_S` is still 60. (b) Every refusal case that exits 3 at base exits 3 on the subject, with a superset of base's refusal kinds, both without and with `--allow-hand-times`. The refusal cases are the repo overlays under `tests/fixtures/custody/failures/*` at base, plus the prior held-out refusal controls. (c) Every changed line in `cross_check`, `check_order`, `check_pin_order` and `check_approval` is listed for J1. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | S1 | `evidence/T5.json` + diff listing |\n| T6 | 