e is refused. `max_tokens` is always the endpoint max (no throttling). (Mocked.) | S1 | `evidence/F8c.json` |\n| F8d | **Live, at most US$0.07 per batch** (approval item 19). (i) One call through the subject's `or_call.py` with `--max-cost` below its worst case is refused: no harness-log entry, and key usage does not rise. (ii) One small call with a cap above its worst case is logged and settled, at or under the cap. Key usage is read ≥ 3 min later. | S1 (uses the shared key by path) | `evidence/F8d.json` |\n\n### P and X: promotion to `tools/edi/`, and the x-plumbline pass-through\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | `tools/edi/` holds `or_call.py`, `judge_batch.py` (the model-judge batch, with rotating order and per-batch `order` written out), `fixture_run.py`, `extract_files.py` and `README.md`, with tests under `tests/test_edi_*.py`. A log entry from the subject's `or_call.py` (mocked) has every key that job 1's frozen harness writes, and `custody_history.read_log` reads it. | S1 | `evidence/P1.json` |\n| X1 | An `x-plumbline` object in `inputs/custody.json` comes out deep-equal under the record's `predicate[\"x-plumbline\"].inputs`, and check.py reads OK. Held-out planted fixture P-X1 has input keys that try to set the emitter's own keys (`verdict`, `gaps`, `times`, `hand_times`): the emitter refuses it, or keeps those keys only under `.inputs`, and its own values are unchanged. | S1 | `evidence/X1.json` |\n\n### V: Plumbline verifier (`kit/plumbline_verify.py`), enforcing `x-plumbline` on top of the standard (approval item 29)\nInterface: `python3 kit/plumbline_verify.py --record R --files F --evidence E --ledger L --custody <checkout> [--json OUT]`. There is **no switch** that relaxes a check: the hand-time allowance is read from the record, never from the command line. Exits: `0` OK at both layers; `3` the standard layer failed; `4` the Plumbline layer failed; `2` cannot run (missing input, or checker bytes not the pin). Ever