b spend, our main requires job spend and exits 2. But interface says job spend required. Fine.\n\nNeed `--max-cost` type float. Good.\n\n### fixture_run details\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"...\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse, hashlib, json, os, shutil, stat, sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef now(): ...\ndef sha12(): ...\ndef writer(): ...\ndef _copy_file(src, dst):\n    dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    shutil.copyfile(src, dst, follow_symlinks=True)\n    os.chmod(dst, stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(dst).st_mode) | stat.S_IRUSR | stat.S_IWUSR)\ndef copy_tree(src, work):\n    if work.exists(): ...\n    work.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(src):\n        rel = Path(root).relative_to(src)\n        wroot = work / rel\n        wroot.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        os.chmod(wroot, stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(wroot).st_mode) | stat.S_IRWXU)\n        for f in files:\n            s = Path(root)/f; d = wroot/f\n            _copy_file(s,d)\n    # ensure dirs writable including empty\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(work):\n        os.chmod(root, stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(root).st_mode) | stat.S_IRWXU)\n        for f in files: ...\n```\nNeed handle source dirs with no write permission. os.walk on read-only dirs works if readable. Good. `shutil.copyfile` can read.\n\nNeed if src is file? Interface says DIR. We'll require dir.\n\nNeed summary:\n```\nfiles=[]\nfor root, dirs, names in os.walk(work):\n    for name in names:\n        p=Path(root)/name\n        rel=p.relative_to(work).as_posix()\n        h=sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n        mode=stat.S_IMODE(p.stat().st_mode)\n        files.append({\"path\":rel,\"sha256\":h,\"mode\":oct(mode)})\nfiles.sort(key=lambda x:x[\"path\"])\nsummary={\"started_at\":started,\"finished_at\":now(),\"writer\":writer(),\"files\":files}\n```\nShould summary include itself? It writes summary after collecting,