e `writer()`.\n\n`spend_status` uses `guard_state`? Could use direct to include even errors. We'll implement direct:\n```\ndef spend_status(a, job):\n    ledger=Path(job[\"spend_ledger\"])\n    base_f=...\n    key=read_key(a.key_file, allow_missing=bool(a.mock_transport))\n    u=key_usage(a,key,t)\n    baseline=None\n    if base_f.exists():\n        try: baseline=float(json.loads(... )[\"usage\"])\n        except: baseline=None\n    delta = round(u-baseline,6) if u is not None and baseline is not None else None\n    ledger_sum=round(ledger_spent(ledger),6)\n    total = round(max(ledger_sum, delta),6) if delta is not None else ledger_sum\n    last = ...\n    data = {...}\n    if a.out: write\n    else: print\n    return 0 if u is not None else 3\n```\nIf return 3 when key unavailable, F1g might fail if key reading file still written? It writes before return. Good.\n\nNeed `--spend-status --out R` with no key file but mock: read_key allow missing. Good.\n\nNeed `--init-spend` writer sha12. Good.\n\nNeed `file_sha256` for harness. Use full.\n\nNeed `writer_name` uses sha12 of current file. Good.\n\nNeed `__all__`? no.\n\nLet's write code fully.\n\n### Potential issue with `Path.with_suffix` on log path with no suffix\n`log.with_suffix(log.suffix + \".tmp\")` if suffix empty -> `.tmp`? Path(\"harness-maker\").with_suffix(\".tmp\") -> \"harness-maker.tmp\". Fine.\n\n### Potential issue with `append_entry` key scan for mock key \"mock-key\" in response? If mock body includes \"mock-key\"? no.\n\n### Potential issue with `read_key` mode check on Windows? Linux.\n\n### Potential issue with `os.fsync` in `_append_ledger`. Fine.\n\n### Potential issue with `fcntl` on Windows. Linux.\n\n### Potential issue with `json.dumps(messages, ensure_ascii=False).encode(\"utf-8\")` length. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `--max-cost` and `--max-tokens` conflict. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `--ledger` pin: if ledger path missing, SystemExit. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `pin_from_ledger` reading lines. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `served_by` if `resp` is not dict. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `pin_ok` if tag None. We validate.\n\n### Potential issue with `_send` if `a.out` not given. It doesn't write. After call, if a.out, write. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `_send` if over_cap but rc 0, we return 9 and no out. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `_send` if rc 5 and over_cap, return 9. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `_send` if rc 4 and over_cap, return 9. Fine.\n\n### Potential issue with settle line after transport error: cost worst, source worst case. If max_cost and worst > max_cost, over_cap false because source not total_cost. Good. But spend ledger settles worst. Fine.\n\n### Potential issue with `key_usage` using `t.request` for mock: MockTransport records GET /key. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `MockTransport` if key.json missing: raises FileNotFoundError, key_usage catches and returns None. Then guard error. For tests provide.\n\n### Potential issue with `MockTransport` if chat.json missing: raises, `_send` catches as transport error, logs, exit 3. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `MockTransport` request body for POST: we don't record body. Good.\n\n### Potential issue with `requests.jsonl` no headers/key. Good.\n\n## fixture_run code details\n\nNeed `writer()` sha12. Use `Path(__file__).read_bytes()`.\n\nNeed `_force_rmtree`:\n```\ndef _force_rmtree(path):\n    if path.is_symlink() or path.is_file():\n        path.unlink(); return\n    if not path.exists(): return\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(path):\n        for d in dirs: os.chmod(Path(root)/d, 0o700)\n        for f in files: os.chmod(Path(root)/f, 0o600)\n    os.chmod(path, 0o700)\n    shutil.rmtree(path)\n```\nNeed if path doesn't exist. Good.\n\nCopy:\n```\ndef copy_writable(src, work):\n    _force_rmtree(work)\n    work.mkdir(parents=True)\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(src):\n        rel = Path(root).relative_to(src)\n        wroot = work / rel\n        wroot.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        os.chmod(wroot, 0o700 | stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(wroot).st_mode))\n        for name in files:\n            s = Path(root)/name\n            d = wroot/name\n            shutil.copyfile(s, d)\n            os.chmod(d, 0o600 | stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(d).st_mode))\n    # ensure all dirs writable\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(work):\n        os.chmod(root, 0o700 | stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(root).st_mode))\n        for name in files:\n            p=Path(root)/name\n            os.chmod(p, 0o600 | stat.S_IMODE(os.stat(p).st_mode))\n```\nThis sets owner rw for files, owner rwx for dirs. Good. `0o600 | mode` preserves group/other read bits, adds owner rw. Good. For dirs `0o700 | mode` adds owner rwx. Good.\n\nNeed if source has symlinks: `shutil.copyfile` follows. Good.\n\nNeed summary file list after copy. Use `os.walk(work)`. Include files. Sort. `mode` as `oct(stat.S_IMODE(...))`. Good.\n\nNeed `started_at` before copy. `finished_at` after copy before summary. Good.\n\nNeed if summary path parent doesn't exist, create. Good.\n\n## extract_files code details\n\nNeed parse. We can copy base and adjust.\n\nPotential issue: `RE_DONE` with `\\n?\\Z` and `lines` from split includes newline. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `check_path` allows paths like `a/../b`? We reject segments \".\" and \"..\". Good.\n\nPotential issue: path with spaces rejected by RE_PATH. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `line.strip(b\" \\t\\r\\n\")` outside blocks allows whitespace-only lines. Good.\n\nPotential issue: content line starting `<<<PLUMBLINE-` detection: We scan until line starts with PFX. If content line starts with PFX but not END, we stop and then `RE_END` fails -> error. Good.\n\nPotential issue: if content line contains END marker not at start, we check `endtxt in lines[j]` and raise. Good.\n\nPotential issue: if END marker line has `\\r\\n`, RE_END won't match because `\\n\\Z` but line includes `\\r\\n`; it expects `>>>\\n\\Z`; line `...>>>\\r\\n` doesn't match. Good, rejects CRLF.\n\nPotential issue: `--check` should validate target? Base validates target. We'll do. It prints ok. Good.\n\nPotential issue: write file with parent mkdir. Good.\n\nPotential issue: target symlink check. Good.\n\nNeed main parse. Use `argparse`? Base manual. We can use argparse simpler, but need exit 2 usage. Use argparse with `parser.error` exits 2. Fine. But tests may check exact? Not. We'll use manual or argparse. Argparse with positional reply, target, `--list`, `--check`. Good. `parser.add_argument(\"reply\")`, `target`. `--list` dest. `--check`. `main(argv)`.\n\nNeed `parse` returns list. Good.\n\nNeed if no files -> error. Base rejects. Good.\n\n## judge_batch code details\n\nNeed ensure `or_call.py` path exists. If not, error. Good.\n\nNeed `--items` JSON list. Validate. If empty, order []. Summary. Maybe return 0. Fine.\n\nNeed `--batch` int. `k = (batch - 1) % len(items)` if len else 0. Good.\n\nNeed `--rubric` read. Good.\n\nNeed `--out` create. Good.\n\nNeed `--log` path. For seat derivation:\n```\ndef seat_from_log(log):\n    name = Path(log).name\n    m = re.match(r\"harness-([A-Za-z0-9]+)\", name)\n    return m.group(1) if m else \"judge\"\n```\nIf log `harness-judge.log`, seat judge. Good.\n\nNeed `--seat` optional override. If given, use. Else derive.\n\nNeed pass `--key-file` if given. Need pass `--base-url` if given. Good.\n\nNeed `--mock-transport` pass.\n\nNeed messages. Use `json.dumps(..., indent=2) + \"\\n\"`.\n\nNeed call name sanitize. `safe_id = re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]+\", \"_\", str(item[\"id\"])) or \"item\"`. Could duplicate if ids sanitize same. Use index prefix? Use `f\"{idx:03d}_{safe_id}\"`. Call name `batch{batch}_{idx:03d}_{safe_id}`. Summary id original. Reply file `reply-{idx:03d}-{safe_id}.txt`. Good.\n\nNeed results append `{\"id\": id, \"call\": call_name, \"exit\": rc, \"reply_file\": reply_name}`. Good.\n\nNeed summary writer. Good.\n\nNeed overall exit. If all rc 0 -> 0 else 1. Good.\n\nNeed print summary path? Not necessary.\n\n## Tests code details\n\nNeed ensure no `pytest` import. Use unittest. Pytest will collect. Good.\n\nLet's draft tests.\n\n#### test_edi_fixture_run.py\n\n```\nimport hashlib, json, os, stat, subprocess, sys, tempfile, unittest\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nFIXTURE_RUN = ROOT / \"tools\" / \"edi\" / \"fixture_run.py\"\n\ndef _chmod_tree(root, file_mode=0o644, dir_mode=0o755):\n    for base, dirs, files in os.walk(root):\n        for d in dirs:\n            os.chmod(Path(base)/d, dir_mode)\n        for f in files:\n            os.chmod(Path(base)/f, file_mode)\n    os.chmod(root, dir_mode)\n\nclass TestFixtureRun(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_read_only_source_copies_writable_and_reproducible(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:\n            td = Path(td)\n            src = td / \"src\"\n            (src / \"sub\").mkdir(parents=True)\n            (src / \"a.txt\").write_text(\"alpha\\n\")\n            (src / \"sub\" / \"b.bin\").write_bytes(b\"\\x00\\x01\")\n            os.chmod(src / \"a.txt\", 0o444)\n            os.chmod(src / \"sub\" / \"b.bin\", 0o400)\n            os.chmod(src / \"sub\", 0o555)\n            os.chmod(src, 0o555)\n            try:\n                work1 = td / \"work1\"; sum1 = td / \"sum1.json\"\n                r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(FIXTURE_RUN), \"--src\", str(src), \"--work\", str(work1), \"--summary\", str(sum1)], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                self.assertEqual(r.returncode, 0, r.stderr)\n                for p in work1.rglob(\"*\"):\n                    if p.is_file():\n                        self.assertTrue(os.access(p, os.W_OK), f\"{p} is not writable\")\n                self.assertEqual((work1/\"a.txt\").read_bytes(), b\"alpha\\n\")\n                s1 = json.loads(sum1.read_text())\n                self.assertIn(\"started_at\", s1); self.assertIn(\"finished_at\", s1)\n                self.assertTrue(s1[\"writer\"].startswith(\"tools/edi/fixture_run.py@\"))\n                self.assertEqual({f[\"path\"] for f in s1[\"files\"]}, {\"a.txt\", \"sub/b.bin\"})\n                for f in s1[\"files\"]:\n                    self.assertIsInstance(f[\"mode\"], str)\n                    self.assertTrue(int(f[\"mode\"], 8) & 0o200)\n                work2 = td / \"work2\"; sum2 = td / \"sum2.json\"\n                r = subprocess.run([...], ...)\n                self.assertEqual(r.returncode, 0, r.stderr)\n                s2 = json.loads(sum2.read_text())\n                self.assertEqual(s1[\"files\"], s2[\"files\"])\n            finally:\n                _chmod_tree(src)\n```\nNeed `int(\"0o644\", 8)` works. Yes.\n\n#### test_edi_or_call.py\n\nLet's write helpers.\n\n```\nimport json, os, subprocess, sys, tempfile, unittest\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nOR_CALL = ROOT / \"tools\" / \"edi\" / \"or_call.py\"\n\ndef _write(path, obj):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(obj, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\ndef _job(td, bound=1.0, reserve=0.0):\n    spend = td / \"spend\" / \"ledger.jsonl\"\n    job = {\"job_id\":\"test-job\",\"bound_usd\":bound,\"reserve_usd\":reserve,\"spend_ledger\":str(spend),\"prices\":[{\"model\":\"test/model\",\"tag\":\"test/fp8\",\"prompt_usd_per_token\":0.001,\"completion_usd_per_token\":0.002,\"max_completion_tokens\":100}]}\n    _write(td/\"job-spend.json\", job)\n    return job, td/\"job-spend.json\"\n\ndef _messages(td):\n    _write(td/\"messages.json\", [{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"hi\"}])\n\ndef _mock(mock, usage=0.0, total_cost=0.01, provider=\"test\"):\n    mock.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    _write(mock/\"key.json\", {\"status\":200,\"headers\":{},\"body\":{\"data\":{\"usage\":usage}}})\n    _write(mock/\"chat.json\", {\"status\":200,\"headers\":{\"Date\":\"Wed, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:00 GMT\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"gen-1\",\"provider\":provider,\"choices\":[{\"message\":{\"content\":\"reply\"}}],\"usage\":{\"cost\":0.01}}})\n    _write(mock/\"generation.json\", {\"status\":200,\"headers\":{},\"body\":{\"data\":{\"total_cost\":total_cost,\"provider_name\":provider}}})\n\ndef _run(td, mock, *extra, log_name=\"harness-maker.log\", out_name=\"reply.txt\"):\n    cmd = [sys.executable, str(OR_CALL), \"--seat\",\"maker\",\"--log\",str(td/log_name), \"--model\",\"test/model\",\"--tag\",\"test/fp8\",\"--pin-provider\",\"test\",\"--messages\",str(td/\"messages.json\"),\"--out\",str(td/out_name),\"--job-spend\",str(td/\"job-spend.json\"),\"--mock-transport\",str(mock)]\n    cmd += list(extra)\n    return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n```\n\nTest:\n```\ndef test_mock_call_writes_job1_log_entry_and_status(self):\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:\n        td=Path(td); _job(td); _messages(td); mock=td/\"mock\"; _mock(mock)\n        r=_run(td, mock)\n        self.assertEqual(r.returncode,0,r.stderr)\n        self.assertEqual((td/\"reply.txt\").read_text(), \"reply\")\n        entries=json.loads((td/\"harness-maker.log\").read_text())\n        self.assertEqual(len(entries),1)\n        e=entries[0]\n        for k in (\"call\",\"seat\",\"request\",\"sent_at\",\"response_status\",\"response_headers\",\"response\",\"received_at\",\"generation\",\"generation_status\",\"generation_fetched_at\",\"harness\",\"verdict\"):\n            self.assertIn(k,e)\n        self.assertEqual(e[\"request\"][\"headers\"][\"Authorization\"], \"Bearer [REDACTED]\")\n        self.assertTrue(e[\"verdict\"][\"ok\"])\n        # spend ledger\n        rows=[json.loads(l) for l in (td/\"spend\"/\"ledger.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines() if l.strip()]\n        self.assertEqual([r[\"event\"] for r in rows], [\"reserve\",\"settle\"])\n        # status\n        status=td/\"status.json\"\n        r=subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(OR_CALL), \"--spend-status\", \"--out\", str(status), \"--job-spend\", str(td/\"job-spend.json\"), \"--mock-transport\", str(mock)], capture_output=True, text=True)\n        self.assertEqual(r.returncode,0,r.stderr)\n        st=json.loads(status.read_text())\n        for k in (\"read_at\",\"writer\",\"job_id\",\"key_usage_usd\",\"baseline_usd\",\"key_delta_usd\",\"ledger_sum_usd\",\"total_usd\",\"last_settle_at\"):\n            self.assertIn(k,st)\n        self.assertTrue(st[\"writer\"].startswith(\"tools/edi/or_call.py@\"))\n```\nWait baseline missing (we didn't init). spend_status baseline null, delta null. It still writes. Good. `last_settle_at` non-null.\n\nTest F8a:\n```\ndef test_key_at_job_limit_refused_before_chat(self):\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:\n        td=Path(td); _job(td); _messages(td); mock=td/\"mock\"; _mock(mock, usage=0.0)\n        r=subprocess.run([... --init-spend ...], capture_output=True, text=True)\n        self.assertEqual(r.returncode,0,r.stderr)\n        _mock(mock, usage=5.0)  # at/above bound\n        # clear requests? keep, but check no POST after\n        r=_run(td, mock)\n        self.assertEqual(r.returncode,6,r.stderr)\n        self.assertFalse((td/\"harness-maker.log\").exists())\n        reqs=[json.loads(l) for l in (mock/\"requests.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines() if l.strip()]\n        self.assertFalse(any(x[\"method\"]==\"POST\" for x in reqs))\n```\nBut `_mock` rewrites key.json, chat.json, generation.json. It doesn't clear requests. Fine. The init spend GET /key recorded. After call, guard GET /key recorded. No POST. Good.\n\nTest F8b pre:\n```\ndef test_max_cost_before_send(self):\n    ...\n    r=_run(td,mock,\"--max-cost\",\"0.0001\")\n    self.assertEqual(r.returncode,8,r.stderr)\n    self.assertFalse((td/\"harness-maker.log\").exists())\n    self.assertFalse((mock/\"requests.jsonl\").exists())\n```\nBecause max-cost check before guard, no requests. Good.\n\nTest F8b post:\n```\ndef test_over_cap_after_settle(self):\n    with ...:\n        _job(td,bound=1.0); _messages; mock usage=0 total_cost=0.9\n        r=_run(td,mock,\"--max-cost\",\"0.5\")\n        self.assertEqual(r.returncode,9,r.stderr)\n        self.assertFalse((td/\"reply.txt\").exists())\n        self.assertTrue((td/\"harness-maker.log\").exists())\n        rows=...\n        settles=[x for x in rows if x[\"event\"]==\"settle\"]\n        self.assertEqual(len(settles),1)\n        self.assertTrue(settles[0].get(\"over_cap\"))\n```\nNeed worst ~0.24 < 0.5. Good. Bound 1.0. total 0 + worst 0.24 < 1.0. Good.\n\nTest F8c max:\n```\ndef test_job_total_uses_max_of_ledger_and_key_delta(self):\n    with ...:\n        job, jobf = _job(td, bound=1.0)\n        _messages\n        mock usage=0.1 total_cost=0.01\n        ledger=Path(job[\"spend_ledger\"])\n        ledger.parent.mkdir(parents=True)\n        ledger.write_text(json.dumps({\"event\":\"settle\",\"id\":\"old\",\"at\":\"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"call\":\"old\",\"cost_usd\":0.8})+\"\\n\")\n        (ledger.parent/\"key-usage-baseline.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"job\":\"test-job\",\"usage\":0.0,\"at\":\"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"writer\":\"test\"})+\"\\n\")\n        r=_run(td,mock)\n        self.assertEqual(r.returncode,6,r.stderr)\n        self.assertFalse((td/\"harness-maker.log\").exists())\n        reqs=...\n        self.assertFalse(any(x[\"method\"]==\"POST\" for x in reqs))\n```\nWait guard: ledger_spent = 0.8 (settle with no reserve? Our ledger_spent only sums reserves, ignoring standalone settle! Oops. Our `ledger_spent` from base sums reserve lines, using settled cost. If ledger has only a settle line with no reserve, ledger_spent returns 0. That's a problem for manual ledger test and F8c. The spend ledger may have settle lines without reserve? In real, every settle has reserve. But F8c \"spend-ledger sum\" likely sum of settle cost. Base `ledger_spent` only sums reserves. Hmm. The base says `ledger = sum(settled cost) + sum(worst of reserves never settled)`. That implementation iterates reserves and uses settled cost if id.