for r in rows:\n        if r.get(\"event\") == \"settle\":\n            settled[str(r.get(\"id\"))] = float(r.get(\"cost_usd\", 0.0))\n        elif r.get(\"event\") == \"reserve\":\n            reserved[str(r.get(\"id\"))] = float(r.get(\"worst_usd\", 0.0))\n    total = sum(settled.values())\n    total += sum(worst for rid, worst in reserved.items() if rid not in settled)\n    return total\n```\nNeed if duplicate settle id? Last wins. Fine.\n\n`last_settle_at`:\n```\ndef last_settle_at(ledger):\n    rows = _ledger_rows(ledger)\n    vals = [r.get(\"at\") for r in rows if r.get(\"event\")==\"settle\" and r.get(\"at\")]\n    return max(vals) if vals else None\n```\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `init_spend` should check ledger exists? Base checks ledger or baseline exists. If ledger path parent doesn't exist, ledger.exists false. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `init_spend` writes baseline with `writer`. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `spend_status` `last_settle_at` from ledger. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `spend_status` with `--out` not given. We'll print. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `main` `--init-spend` and `--spend-status` both? Argparse allows. We check init first. Fine.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `--check-key` with `--mock-transport`. `check_key` uses `read_key` allow missing. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `check_key` uses `t.request` and prints. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `main` for `--check-key` doesn't require job spend. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `main` for `--init-spend` requires job spend. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `main` for call loads job spend before checking required flags. If missing job spend, exit 2. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `load_job_spend` raises SystemExit with print. Good.\n\nLet's write `load_job_spend`:\n```\ndef load_job_spend(path):\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.is_file():\n        print(f\"or_call: no job spend file at {path}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        raise SystemExit(2)\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"or_call: job spend file {path} is not JSON: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        raise SystemExit(2)\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        ...\n    for k in (\"job_id\",\"bound_usd\",\"reserve_usd\",\"spend_ledger\",\"prices\"):\n        if k not in data: ...\n    try:\n        float(data[\"bound_usd\"]); float(data[\"reserve_usd\"])\n    except...\n    if not isinstance(data[\"prices\"], list) or not data[\"prices\"]:\n        ...\n    for e in data[\"prices\"]:\n        for k in (\"model\",\"tag\",\"prompt_usd_per_token\",\"completion_usd_per_token\",\"max_completion_tokens\"):\n            if k not in e: ...\n        float(e[\"prompt_usd_per_token\"]); ...\n        int(e[\"max_completion_tokens\"])\n    return data\n```\nNeed `spend_ledger` non-empty string. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `call` uses `a.max_tokens` set from price. If `a.max_tokens` provided as int. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `_send` body includes `\"max_tokens\": a.max_tokens`. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `_send` log entry `request.headers` includes `Authorization: Bearer [REDACTED]`. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `_send` log entry `response_headers` maybe dict with Date. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `_send` if response status 200 and id but generation.json missing -> transport exception in generation loop caught, gstatus set to exception, gen None. Then entry generation null, verdict may still be ok if response provider says test. `generation_reply` false. Return 5. Good. Writes out after settle. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `_send` if generation status 500, gen None, return 5 if pin ok. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `_send` if response provider bad but generation good? bad set. Refusal. Good.\n\n## Potential issue: `or_call` `_send` fallback detection. Good.\n\n## P