ld set baseline to limit, then calls allowed, maybe not desired? Judge batch not F8a. Hmm.\n\nMaybe leave judge_batch simple. Our own test init.\n\nNeed ensure tests don't leave network. Use mock.\n\nNeed also test I1 writer stamps for `fixture_run` and `judge_batch` and `or_call --spend-status`. Good.\n\nPotential issue: Tests are run from repo root. Our tests use `sys.executable` and tools path. Good.\n\nNeed code quality.\n\nLet's design `or_call.py` in detail.\n\n### or_call.py code structure\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"...\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse, fcntl, hashlib, json, os, re, stat, sys, time, uuid, urllib.error, urllib.request\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\"\nKEY_FILE = \"/workspace/.openrouter-key\"\nMETA_HEADER = (\"X-OpenRouter-Metadata\", \"enabled\")\nREDACTED = \"Bearer [REDACTED]\"\nWRITER_FILE = \"tools/edi/or_call.py\"\n\ndef now(): ...\ndef sha12(): ...\ndef writer(): ...\ndef norm...\nclass Transport...\nclass MockTransport...\ndef read_key(path, allow_missing=False): ...\ndef load_job_spend(path): ...\ndef pin_from_ledger...\ndef served_by...\ndef pin_ok...\ndef append_entry...\ndef _ledger_rows...\ndef ledger_spent...\ndef _append_ledger...\nclass SpendLock...\ndef key_usage...\ndef baseline_path(ledger)\ndef read_baseline\ndef guard_state(a, key, t, ledger, job):\n...\ndef init_spend...\ndef spend_status...\ndef call...\ndef _send...\ndef check_key...\ndef parser...\ndef main...\n```\n\nNeed `MockTransport`:\n```\nclass MockTransport:\n    def __init__(self, directory):\n        self.dir = Path(directory)\n        self.dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        self.requests = self.dir / \"requests.jsonl\"\n    def _record(self, method, url):\n        with open(self.requests, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(json.dumps({\"method\": method, \"url\": url, \"at\": now()}, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n    def _reply(self, name):\n        p = self.dir / name\n        if not p.exists():\n            raise FileNotFoundError(p)\n        data = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        status = int(data.get(\"status\", 200))\n        headers = dict(data.get(\"headers\") or {})\n        body = data.get(\"body\", {})\n        raw = body if isinstance(body, bytes) else json.dumps(body, ensure_ascii=False).encode()\n        return status, headers, raw\n    def request(self, method, url, headers, body=None, timeout=300):\n        self._record(method, url)\n        if method == \"GET\" and url.endswith(\"/key\"):\n            return self._reply(\"key.json\")\n        if method == \"POST\" and url.endswith(\"/chat/completions\"):\n            return self._reply(\"chat.json\")\n        if method == \"GET\" and \"/generation\" in url:\n            return self._reply(\"generation.json\")\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"no mock reply for {method} {url}\")\n```\nNeed record every request including before checking file. Good. If missing file, request recorded then error.\n\nNeed `Transport.request` returns headers dict with `Date`. Fine.\n\n`read_key`:\n```\ndef read_key(path, allow_missing=False):\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.is_file():\n        if allow_missing: return \"mock-key\"\n        raise SystemExit(...)\n    mode = stat.S_IMODE(p.stat().st_mode)\n    if mode & 0o077: raise SystemExit(...)\n    key = p.read_text().strip()\n    if not key: raise SystemExit(...)\n    return key\n```\nFor mock allow_missing.\n\n`load_job_spend`:\n```\ndef load_job_spend(path):\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.is_file(): print(...); raise SystemExit(2)\n    try: data=json.loads...\n    except...\n    required...\n    prices...\n    return data\n```\nWe should not raise SystemExit with code? `SystemExit(2)`. main returns? Use helper returns None? Simpler:\n```\ndef load_job_spend(path):\n    if not p.is_file(): raise UsageError(...)\n...\nclass UsageError(Exception)\n```\nIn