ll_name = a.call or f\"{a.seat}_call\"\n- with SpendLock(ledger):\n    st = guard_state(job,key,t,ledger)\n    st.update(...)\n    if \"error\" in st or st[\"spent_usd\"] + worst + float(job[\"reserve_usd\"]) >= float(job[\"bound_usd\"]):\n        print json st stderr; print REFUSED; return 6\n    rid=uuid...\n    _append_ledger(ledger, {\"event\":\"reserve\",\"id\":rid,\"at\":now(),\"job\":job[\"job_id\"],\"seat\":a.seat,\"call\":call_name,\"model\":a.model,\"tag\":tag,\"max_tokens\":a.max_tokens,\"worst_usd\":round(worst,8),\"spent_before_usd\":st[\"spent_usd\"]})\n```\n- holder = {}\n- try: rc = _send(...)\n- finally: compute cost and settle. Need avoid settle if _send raises? _send should catch.\n- Need capture `over_cap` from cost. `_send` returns rc and sets holder[\"cost_source\"], holder[\"content\"], holder[\"over_cap\"]? Better compute in finally.\n\nLet's design `_send` returns `(rc, entry)` and writes log. It sets holder[\"resp\"], holder[\"gen\"], holder[\"status\"], holder[\"content\"], holder[\"refusal\"], holder[\"generation_reply\"], holder[\"transport_error\"].\nBut settle needs cost. We can compute in finally from holder.\n\nPseudo:\n```\ndef call(...):\n    ...\n    holder = {}\n    try:\n        rc = _send(a, t, sleep, key, tag, provider, messages, call_name, holder)\n    finally:\n        resp, gen = holder.get(\"resp\"), holder.get(\"gen\")\n        cost, src = worst, \"worst case (no cost stated)\"\n        g = ...\n        u = ...\n        if g total_cost: cost, src = ...\n        elif u cost: ...\n        elif holder.get(\"status\") not in (None,200) and not (isinstance(resp,dict) and resp.get(\"id\")): cost, src = 0.0, ...\n        over_cap = bool(a.max_cost is not None and cost > a.max_cost and src in (...))\n        holder[\"over_cap\"] = over_cap\n        with SpendLock(ledger):\n            settle = {\"event\":\"settle\",\"id\":rid,\"at\":now(),\"call\":call_name,\"cost_usd\":cost,\"source\":src}\n            if over_cap: settle[\"over