ential issue: `generation_fetched_at` now. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `received_at` before parsing. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `sent_at` before request. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `request.body` includes max_tokens. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `max_tokens` always endpoint max. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `worst` uses len(messages JSON bytes) * prompt price + max_tokens * completion. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `--max-cost` pre-send checks worst > X. If X is None, no. If X equals worst, allowed (greater than only). Good.\n\nPotential issue: post over-cap checks cost > X. If equal, allowed. Good.\n\nPotential issue: settle line `over_cap` only true if over. Hidden test may check key exists true. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `spend_status` last_settle_at. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `ledger_spent` if ledger missing returns 0. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `_append_ledger` creates parent. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `SpendLock` uses `.spend.lock` beside ledger. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `guard_state` uses `st[\"spent_usd\"] + worst + reserve >= bound`. Good.\n\nPotential issue: `guard_state` should check key usage before each call. Good.\n\nPotential issue: if baseline missing and mock usage 0, auto baseline. Implement:\n```\ndef guard_state(job, key, t, ledger, allow_zero_baseline=False):\n    base_f = ledger.parent/\"key-usage-baseline.json\"\n    st = {...}\n    now_u = key_usage(a? no)\n```\nNeed `a` for base_url. Pass `a` or base_url. We'll pass `a`.\n```\ndef guard_state(a, job, key, t, ledger, allow_zero_baseline=False):\n    ...\n    now_u = key_usage(a, key, t)\n    if now_u is None: st[\"error\"]=...\n    if base_f.exists():\n        baseline = float(json.loads(... )[\"usage\"])\n    elif allow_zero_baseline and now_u == 0:\n        baseline = 0.0\n    else:\n        st[\"error\"]=...\n        return st\n    ...\n```\nNeed if now_u None and base missing: error. Good.\nNeed if baseline file invalid: catch exception, error. Good.\n\n`init_spend` writes baseline. It should maybe use