ally` and writing out after.\n\nPseudo:\n```\ndef call(a, job, transport=None, sleep=time.sleep):\n    t = transport or (MockTransport(a.mock_transport) if a.mock_transport else Transport())\n    ...\n    holder = {}\n    rc = 3\n    try:\n        rc = _send(a, t, sleep, key, tag, provider, messages, call_name, holder)\n    except SystemExit:\n        raise\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(...)\n        rc = 3\n    finally:\n        ...\n        over_cap = ...\n        holder[\"over_cap\"] = over_cap\n        with SpendLock(ledger):\n            settle = ...\n            _append_ledger(ledger, settle)\n    if holder.get(\"over_cap\"):\n        print(...); return 9\n    if rc in (0,5) and a.out and \"content\" in holder:\n        Path(a.out).write_text(holder[\"content\"], encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return rc\n```\nNeed if exception before `_send` sets holder status, settle cost worst. Good.\n\nNeed `over_cap` compute:\n```\nover_cap = False\nif a.max_cost is not None and cost > a.max_cost and src in (\"generation.total_cost\",\"response.usage.cost\"):\n    over_cap = True\n```\nShould we include `response.usage.cost`? F8b says `/generation total_cost`. But response usage cost also a stated cost. Fine.\n\nNeed `cost` extraction:\n```\ng = (gen.get(\"data\") if isinstance(gen, dict) and isinstance(gen.get(\"data\"), dict) else gen) or {}\nu = (resp.get(\"usage\") if isinstance(resp, dict) else None) or {}\nif isinstance(g, dict) and g.get(\"total_cost\") is not None:\n    cost=float(g[\"total_cost\"]); src=\"generation.total_cost\"\nelif isinstance(u, dict) and u.get(\"cost\") is not None:\n    cost=float(u[\"cost\"]); src=\"response.usage.cost\"\nelif holder.get(\"status\") not in (None,200) and not (isinstance(resp, dict) and resp.get(\"id\")):\n    cost=0.0; src=...\nelse:\n    cost=worst; src=...\n```\nGood.\n\nNeed if `gen` is None but `resp` usage cost present, use. Good.\n\nNeed settle line includes `job`. Extra. Fine.\n\nNeed print over cap message.\