rom the Maker prompt] | **E-GLM** | `evidence/J4-<call>.json` + harness log + generation reply |\n\n## INTERFACE.md (frozen; how the instrument calls the subject)\n\n```\n# INTERFACE: the command lines, file shapes and exit codes the S1 instrument drives (job 2026-10-28-custody-times-ledger-spend)\n\nSTATUS: FROZEN-BUILD 2026-10-28T20:36:28Z — part of the freeze set; sha256 in ../MANIFEST.sha256. Maker-visible. Referenced from bar.md.\n\nThe bar says WHAT must hold. This file pins HOW S1 calls the subject, so that a check scores the behaviour and not a\nguess about flag names. Anything not named here is the Maker's choice. Where the bar and this file disagree, the\nbar wins and the disagreement is a finding against the bar (filed as an amendment), not a reason to fail a check.\n\"UTC Z\" = `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` (fractional seconds allowed). \"sha12\" = first 12 hex of the sha256 of the file.\n\n## 1. `kit/custody_ledger.py` (T1, F1a–F1h)\nEvery command takes `--job-dir J` (the job folder holding `inputs/custody-events.jsonl` and `inputs/custody.json`).\nBase commands keep their base flags (`freeze`, `approve`, `pin`, `show`, and `dispose --by`).\n\nEvery line any command appends carries `\"writer\": \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<sha12>\"` (sha12 of the file that ran)\nand `\"at\"`: the tool's UTC Z clock at the append. A **refusal** exits non-zero (2 = usage, 3 = refused), prints a\nline starting `REFUSED:` on stderr, and changes neither the ledger nor `custody.json` (byte-identical).\n\n| command | appends one line with (besides `writer`, `at`) | custody.json |\n|---|---|---|\n| `generation open --seat S --prompt FILE` | `event:\"generation\", action:\"open\", seat, n, prompt_file, prompt_sha256` | unchanged |\n| `generation close --seat S --n N [--outcome TEXT] [--fix-kind TEXT]` | `event:\"generation\", action:\"close\", seat, n, outcome, fix_kind` | unchanged |\n| `evaluation --batch B --evaluator ID --verdict FILE [--summary FILE] [--iteration N]` | `event:\"evaluation\", batch, evaluator, verdict_file, verdict_sha256`; with `--summary`: `summary_file, summary_sha256, started_at, finished_at, summary_writer` (copied from the summary's own stamp) | unchanged |\n| `amendment --file F --quote Q --channel C --said-at T` | `event:\"amendment\", file, file_sha256, quote, channel, said_at` | unchanged |\n| `relay --quote Q --from BOT --source-chat C --source-at T` | `event:\"relay\", kind:\"relay\", quote, from, source_chat, source_at` | unchanged |\n| `spend --spend-ledger L --key-reading R` | `event:\"spend\", spend_ledger, spend_ledger_sha256, key_reading, key_reading_sha256, ledger_sum_usd, key_delta_usd, total_usd, read_at, last_settle_at` | unchanged |\n| `dispose --by NAME --state given\\|declined --decided-at T --decided-source S [--words W]` | `event:\"dispose\", by, state, decided_at, decided_source, words` | `disposition.by`, `disposition.at = decided_at` |\n\nFile paths in lines are stored relative to the job dir when they are inside it, else absolute. Bounds (F1b, F1e, F1f,\nF1g) are as the bar states; T equal to a bound is accepted. `generation` numbering is per seat.\n\n## 2. `kit/emit_custody.py` (T2–T7, F1h, X1)\nBase flags unchanged, plus `--allow-hand-times`.\n- **Hand-time refusal** (no switch): exit 3, nothing written, stderr carries the base `REFUSED (history)` header and\n  one line per hand time: `  [hand-time] <field> <file>:<line> (<source>)`.\n- **Field names** (used in the refusal lines, in `hand_times[].field`, and by the verifier):\n  `bar.frozenAt`, `bar.approvals[<i>].at`, `routing.<seat>.declaredAt`, `disposition.at`, `startedAt`,\n  `producedAt`, `passes.<id>.at`, `controls[<id>].at`, `<log file name>#<call or index>.sent_at` and `.received_at`.\n- **Sources**: `ledger-hand` (`writer:\"hand\"`), `ledger-no-writer`, `inputs-no-ledger` (typed into custody.json, no\n  ledger line behind it), `server-header` (a log time taken from the response `Date`), `response-created` (from the\n  response `created`). `<file>:<line>` is the 1-based line that carries the value: the ledger line, the custody.json\n  line (the file is indent-2 JSON, one key per line), or the harness-log line holding the server time used.\n  `<i>` is the 0-based index in `bar.approvals`; `<file>` is relative to the job dir. When a later ledger line\n  sets the same field as an earlier one, the later line's value, line and source are the ones used and reported.\n- A pass or control with no typed `at` gets its time from a tool: a model pass from its `call`'s logger\n  `received_at`; a script pass from the `finished_at` of the `evaluation` line for its batch and evaluator.\n  `startedAt`/`producedAt` with no typed value come from the Maker log's logger times.\n- **`x-plumbline`** (predicate level), keys: `schema` (`\"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"`), `hand_times[]`\n  (`{field, file, line, source}`), `allowances` (`hand_times: {switch:\"--allow-hand-times\", writer:\n  \"kit/emit_custody.py@<sha12>\", at}` only when the switch was given and the set is non-empty), `generations[]`,\n  `evaluations[]`, `relays[]`, `amendments[]` (each the ledger line's fields plus `source:\n  \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl:<line>\"`), `spend` (`calls_sum_usd, key_delta_usd, total_usd, tolerance_usd: 0.0001,\n  source`), `inputs` (a deep copy of `inputs/custody.json`'s `x-plumbline` object, when there is one).\n- The emitter never writes any file under the job dir other than the record it is asked to write (T7).\n\n## 3. `kit/plumbline_verify.py` (V1–V9)\nAs in the bar: `--record R --files F --evidence E --ledger L --custody <checkout> [--json OUT]`; the job's\n`custody.json` is the file `custody.json` beside L. Exits 0/3/4/2: 0 = all checks pass; 3 = the standard check.py\nis not OK (kind `standard`, nothing else is checked); 4 = check.py is OK and any other kind fails; 2 = cannot run\n(usage, a missing input, or a checker whose `check.py` sha256 is not the pin). Each failure is printed as one stdout line\n`FAIL <kind> <field> <file>:<line>`; `--json OUT` writes `{\"exit\": N, \"failures\": [{\"kind\",\"field\",\"file\",\"line\"}]}`.\nKinds: `standard`, `schema`, `allowance`, `hand-time-unflagged`, `flag-without-source`, `events`,\n`relay-as-approval`, `spend`, `shadow`. The spend ledger and key reading are the files named in the ledger's\n`spend` line (relative to the job dir when relative).\n\n## 4. `kit/plumbline_job.py` (V8)\n`close` and `custody` accept `--allow-hand-times` (passed to the emitter) and `--custody <checkout>` (default: env\n`PLUMBLINE_CUSTODY`). Both run `kit/emit_custody.py` and then `kit/plumbline_verify.py` **as subprocesses of those\nfiles** (as base runs the emitter). If the verifier cannot run, close fails with its exit code. The run-log row on\nrefusal is `{\"event\":\"close_refused\",\"kind\":<first failure kind>, ...}`.\n\n## 5. `tools/edi/` (F7a, F8a–F8d, I1, P1)\n**`or_call.py`**: job 1's harness flags (`--seat --log --model --tag --pin-provider | --ledger, --messages --out\n--call --max-tokens --temperature --key-file --base-url`), plus:\n- `--job-spend FILE` (required for every call and for `--init-spend` / `--spend-status`): JSON\n  `{job_id, bound_usd, reserve_usd, spend_ledger, prices: [{model, tag, prompt_usd_per_token,\n  completion_usd_per_token, max_completion_tokens}]}`. Missing or invalid → exit 2, nothing sent.\n- `--init-spend`: writes `key-usage-baseline.json` beside `spend_ledger` (`{job, usage, at, writer}`).\n- `--spend-status --out R`: writes R = `{read_at, writer, job_id, key_usage_usd, baseline_usd, key_delta_usd,\n  ledger_sum_usd, total_usd, last_settle_at}`.\n- Spend-ledger lines are job 1's harness's: `{\"event\": \"reserve\", \"id\", \"at\", \"job\", \"seat\", ..., \"worst_usd\"}` before\n  sending and `{\"event\": \"settle\", \"id\", \"at\", \"call\", ..., \"cost_usd\"}` after (plus `\"over_cap\": true` for exit 9).\n- `--max-cost X`: refused before sending if the worst case > X; over-cap after settle if `total_cost` > X.\n- `--mock-transport DIR`: nothing goes on the network. Replies come from `DIR/key.json`, `DIR/chat.json`,\n  `DIR/generation.json`, each `{\"status\": N, \"headers\": {...}, \"body\": <JSON>}`; every request is appended to\n  `DIR/requests.jsonl` as `{\"method\", \"url\", \"at\"}` (real openrouter.ai URLs; no headers, no key).\n- Exits: job 1's 0/2/3/4/5, plus `6` refused by the job bound (nothing sent, no log entry), `8` refused by\n  `--max-cost` before sending (nothing sent, no log entry), `9` over the cap after settle (logged, settle line\n  `\"over_cap\": true`, no `--out`).\n- Log entries carry every key job 1's harness writes (`harness.name` may say `tools/edi/or_call.py`).\n\n**`fixture_run.py --src DIR --work DIR --summary FILE`**: copies src into work (every copied file `u+rw`, dirs\n`u+rwx`, whatever src's modes), and writes the summary `{started_at, finished_at, writer, files: [{path, sha256,\nmode}]}` (paths relative to work, mode as an octal string). Two runs differ only in `started_at`/`finished_at`.\n\n**`judge_batch.py --items ITEMS.json --batch N --rubric FILE --out DIR --job-spend F --log L --model M (--tag T\n--pin-provider P | --ledger LED) [--mock-transport D]`**: ITEMS.json is a list of `{id, text}`; the order for batch N\nis the list rotated left by `(N-1) mod len`. One `or_call.py` call per item. Writes `DIR/summary.json` `{started_at,\nfinished_at, writer, batch, order: [ids], results: [{id, call, exit, reply_file}]}`.\n\n**`extract_files.py`**: the whole-file reply extractor (job 1's format), with `--check` (verify only) and without it\n(write).\n\nEvery summary-writing instrument stamps `started_at`, `finished_at` (UTC Z, its own clock) and\n`writer: \"tools/edi/<file>@<sha12>\"` (I1).\n\n## 6. Anchors S1's mutation controls rely on (keep these lines' form)\n- `kit/custody_history.py` keeps a module-level line `TOLERANCE_S = 60` (C-T5p1 rewrites it to 600).\n- `kit/emit_custody.py` keeps the \"after the close\" refusal in `check_order` as one line containing both\n  `ref.add(` and the text `is after the job's close` (C-T5p2 disables that line).\n- C-T7p, C-V7p and P-V8 wrap whole files (`kit/emit_custody.py`, `kit/plumbline_verify.py`) and need no anchor.\nA missing anchor makes that control unbuildable, which voids the batch (bar: a control that comes out wrong).\n```\n\n## CONTEXT (read only; not in this part) dot-plumbline/jobs/2026-10-28-doctrine-reader-pointer/custody/freeze/harness/or_call.py\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# STATUS: FROZEN-BUILD 2026-10-28T16:18:50Z — part of the freeze set of job 2026-10-28-doctrine-reader-pointer; sha256 in ../../MANIFEST.sha256.\n# Derived from job 2026-10-27-custody-emitter-gaps or_call.py (sha256 55e8981c...) + the job-wide SPEND GUARD (approval item 6, Owner 2026-10-28 11:58 EDT).\n\"\"\"or_call.py: one logged OpenRouter chat call for a seat of an E-DI job (Maker or model evaluator).\n\n    or_call.py --seat maker --log custody/evidence/harness-maker-deepseek.log \\\n               --model deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 --tag deepinfra/fp8 --pin-provider DeepInfra \\\n               --messages msgs.json --out reply.txt [--call maker_call_2] [--max-tokens N] [--temperature T]\n    (or take tag + provider from the ledger:  --ledger inputs/custody-events.jsonl  instead of --tag/--pin-provider)\n\nWhat it does, in order:\n  1. Reads the OpenRouter key from --key-file (default /workspace/.openrouter-key) by path. Refuses when the file\n     is missing, empty, or readable by group/other. The key is never printed and never written anywhere.\n  2. POSTs /api/v1/chat/completions with body.provider = {\"order\":[TAG], \"allow_fallbacks\":false, \"zdr\":true}\n     and header \"X-OpenRouter-Metadata: enabled\".\n  3. GETs /api/v1/generation?id=<response id> (retrying while the stats are not ready).\n  4. Appends ONE entry to the seat's harness log (a JSON list; the format kit/custody_history.py read_log reads):\n       call, seat, request {method, url, headers (Authorization redacted), body}, sent_at,\n       response_status, response_headers (all, incl. Date), response (raw JSON), received_at,\n       generation (raw /api/v1/generation JSON reply, or null), generation_status, generation_fetched_at,\n       harness {name, sha256 of this file}, verdict {served_by, pin, ok, refusal}.\n     Times are this host's UTC clock (ISO 8601 Z); the server clock is in response_headers.Date.\n  5. Checks who served the call (response.provider, openrouter_metadata selected endpoint, generation\n     provider_name, generation provider_responses). Anything other than the pinned provider, or no statement\n     at all, is a REFUSAL: the entry is still logged (it is evidence), but no reply is written to --out.\n\nExit codes: 0 logged, served by the pin, reply written · 2 usage/key error, nothing sent · 3 HTTP/transport\nerror (logged when a request was sent) · 4 REFUSED: served by another provider, a fallback was tried, or the\nresponse does not say who served it (logged, no --out) · 5 served by the pin but the /api/v1/generation reply\nwas not obtained (logged with generation null, --out written; the record must then flag it, bar N4).\n\nThe log never contains the key: the Authorization header is replaced before logging, and the serialized entry\nis scanned for the key string before it is written (exit 2, nothing written, if it would appear).\n\nSPEND GUARD (job 2026-10-28-doctrine-reader-pointer, approval item 6: the shared key, bound < US$2):\n  * Only the (model, tag) pairs in PRICES may be called (prices = the saved ZDR snapshot 2026-10-28T15:59:42Z).\n  * NO THROTTLING: max_tokens is always the endpoint maximum from PRICES (omitted = set to it; any other value\n    = exit 2). No reasoning/effort parameter is ever sent.\n  * Before anything is sent, under an exclusive lock on the job spend ledger (JSON lines, outside the repo):\n        worst  = bytes(messages JSON) x prompt price + max_tokens x completion price   (bytes >= tokens)\n        ledger = sum(settled cost) + sum(worst of reserves never settled)\n        keyuse = key usage now (GET /api/v1/key, free) - key usage at --init-spend   (shared key: conservative)\n        spent  = max(ledger, keyuse)\n     REFUSE (exit 6, nothing sent, no harness log entry) when spent + worst + RESERVE_USD >= BOUND_USD, or the key\n     usage cannot be read, or the baseline is missing. Otherwise append a `reserve` line (worst case) and send.\n  * After the call, append a `settle` line: cost = generation reply total_cost, else response usage.cost, else the\n    worst case (HTTP error without an id: 0, OpenRouter bills no failed request; key usage reconciles it).\n  * --spend-ledger other than the job ledger = TEST MODE: the guard runs and decides, then exit 6 (refused) or\n    exit 7 (would send), and NOTHING is sent (with the real transport).\n  * --init-spend: write key-usage-baseline.json beside the ledger (refuses if a ledger or baseline exists).\n  * --spend-status: print ledger total, key-usage delta, remaining headroom; sends nothing paid.\nExit 6 = REFUSED by the spend guard (nothing sent) · 7 = test mode, guard would allow (nothing sent).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport uuid\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\"\nKEY_FILE = \"/workspace/.openrouter-key\"\nMETA_HEADER = (\"X-OpenRouter-Metadata\", \"enabled\")\nREDACTED = \"Bearer [REDACTED]\"\nJOB_ID = \"2026-10-28-doctrine-reader-pointer\"\nSPEND_LEDGER = f\"/workspace/edi-work/{JOB_ID}/spend/spend-ledger.jsonl\"\nBOUND_USD = 2.00        # strict: total job spend must stay < BOUND_USD\nRESERVE_USD = 0.05      # margin kept free under the bound (pricing/estimate error)\n# (model, tag) -> USD per prompt token, USD per completion token, endpoint max_completion_tokens.\n# Source: /api/v1/models/<model>/endpoints snapshot 2026-10-28T15:59:42Z (custody/zdr-endpoints-*.json + models-*.json).\nPRICES = {\n    (\"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\", \"deepinfra/fp8\"): (0.000000098, 0.000000294, 131072),\n    (\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\", \"z-ai/fp8\"): (0.00000015, 0.0000005, 131072),\n}\n\n\ndef now() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%fZ\")\n\n\ndef norm(v) -> str:\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]\", \"\", str(v or \"\").lower())\n\n\nclass Transport:\n    \"\"\"urllib transport; tests swap it for a fake. Returns (status, headers dict, body bytes).\"\"\"\n    def request(self, method: str, url: str, headers: dict, body: bytes | None, timeout: float = 300):\n        req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, method=method, headers=headers)\n        try:\n            with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as r:\n                return r.status, dict(r.headers.items()), r.read()\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            return e.code, dict(e.headers.items()) if e.headers else {}, e.read()\n\n\ndef read_key(path: str) -> str:\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.is_file():\n        raise SystemExit(f\"or_call: no key file at {path}\")\n    mode = stat.S_IMODE(p.stat().st_mode)\n    if mode & 0o077:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"or_call: key file {path} is readable by group/other (mode {oct(mode)}); chmod 600 it\")\n    key = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").strip()\n    if not key:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"or_call: key file {path} is empty\")\n    return key\n\n\ndef pin_from_ledger(ledger: str, seat: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    pins = [json.loads(ln) for ln in Path(ledger).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines() if ln.strip()]\n    pins = [e for e in pins if e.get(\"event\") == \"pin\" and e.get(\"seat\") == seat]\n    if not pins:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"or_call: ledger {ledger} has no pin for seat {seat!r} (custody_ledger.py pin first)\")\n    return pins[-1][\"slug\"], pins[-1][\"provider\"]\n\n\ndef served_by(resp: dict, gen: dict | None) -> tuple[dict, list]:\n    \"\"\"({source: provider}, [providers tried]) as the response and the generation reply state them.\"\"\"\n    served, tried = {}, []\n    if isinstance(resp, dict):\n        if resp.get(\"provider\"):\n            served[\"response.provider\"] = str(resp[\"provider\"])\n        om = resp.get(\"openrouter_metadata\") if isinstance(resp.get(\"openrouter_metadata\"), dict) else {}\n        sel = [e.get(\"provider\") for e in ((om.get(\"endpoints\") or {}).get(\"available\") or [])\n               if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"selected\") and e.get(\"provider\")]\n        if sel:\n            served[\"openrouter_metadata.endpoints.selected\"] = str(sel[-1])\n        tried += [str(a.get(\"provider\")) for a in (om.get(\"attempts\") or []) if isinstance(a, dict) and a.get(\"provider\")]\n    if isinstance(gen, dict):\n        g = gen.get(\"data\") if isinstance(gen.get(\"data\"), dict) else gen\n        if g.get(\"provider_name\"):\n            served[\"generation.provider_name\"] = str(g[\"provider_name\"])\n        tried += [str(x.get(\"provider_name\") or x.get(\"provider\")) for x in (g.get(\"provider_responses\") or [])\n                  if isinstance(x, dict) and (x.get(\"provider_name\") or x.get(\"provider\"))]\n    return served, tried\n\n\ndef pin_ok(name, provider: str, tag: str) -> bool:\n    n = norm(name)\n    return bool(n) and n in {norm(provider), norm(tag.split(\"/\")[0])}\n\n\ndef append_entry(log: Path, entry: dict, key: str) -> None:\n    text = json.dumps(entry, ensure_ascii=False)\n    if key and key in text:\n        raise SystemExit(\"or_call: the log entry would contain the key; nothing written\")\n    items = []\n    if log.exists() and log.stat().st_size:\n        items = json.loads(log.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        if not isinstance(items, list):\n            raise SystemExit(f\"or_call: {log} is not a JSON list harness log; refusing to append\")\n    items.append(entry)\n    log.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp = log.with_suffix(log.suffix + \".tmp\")\n    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(items, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    os.replace(tmp, log)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spend guard\ndef _ledger_rows(ledger: Path) -> list:\n    if not ledger.exists():\n        return []\n    return [json.loads(ln) for ln in ledger.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines() if ln.strip()]\n\n\ndef ledger_spent(ledger: Path) -> float:\n    rows = _ledger_rows(ledger)\n    settled = {r[\"id\"]: float(r[\"cost_usd\"]) for r in rows if r.get(\"event\") == \"settle\"}\n    total = 0.0\n    for r in rows:\n        if r.get(\"event\") == \"reserve\":\n            total += settled.get(r[\"id\"], float(r[\"worst_usd\"]))\n    return total\n\n\ndef _append_ledger(ledger: Path, row: dict) -> None:\n    ledger.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(ledger, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(row, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n        f.flush()\n        os.fsync(f.fileno())\n\n\nclass SpendLock:\n    def __init__(self, ledger: Path):\n        self.path = ledger.parent / \".spend.lock\"\n\n    def __enter__(self):\n        self.path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        self.f = open(self.path, \"a\")\n        fcntl.flock(self.f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        return self\n\n    def __exit__(self, *exc):\n        fcntl.flock(self.f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n        self.f.close()\n\n\ndef key_usage(a, key: str, t) -> float | None:\n    try:\n        status, _, raw = t.request(\"GET\", f\"{a.base_url}/key\", {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {key}\"}, None, timeout=60)\n        if status != 200:\n            return None\n        u = json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8\")).get(\"data\", {}).get(\"usage\")\n        return float(u) if u is not None else None\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\n\ndef guard_state(a, key: str, t, ledger: Path) -> dict:\n    base_f = ledger.parent / \"key-usage-baseline.json\"\n    st = {\"ledger\": str(ledger), \"ledger_spent_usd\": round(ledger_spent(ledger), 6), \"bound_usd\": BOUND_USD,\n          \"reserve_usd\": RESERVE_USD, \"key_usage_baseline\": None, \"key_usage_now\": None, \"key_usage_delta_usd\": None}\n    if not base_f.exists():\n        st[\"error\"] = f\"no key-usage baseline at {base_f} (run --init-spend once, before the job's first call)\"\n        return st\n    st[\"key_usage_baseline\"] = float(json.loads(base_f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"usage\"])\n    now_u = key_usage(a, key, t)\n    if now_u is None:\n        st[\"error\"] = \"could not read key usage (GET /api/v1/key)\"\n        return st\n    st[\"key_usage_now\"] = now_u\n    st[\"key_usage_delta_usd\"] = round(now_u - st[\"key_usage_baseline\"], 6)\n    st[\"spent_usd\"] = round(max(st[\"ledger_spent_usd\"], st[\"key_usage_delta_usd\"]), 6)\n    st[\"headroom_usd\"] = round(BOUND_USD - RESERVE_USD - st[\"spent_usd\"], 6)\n    return st\n\n\ndef init_spend(a, transport=None) -> int:\n    t = transport or Transport()\n    ledger = Path(a.spend_ledger)\n    base_f = ledger.parent / \"key-usage-baseline.json\"\n    if ledger.exists() or base_f.exists():\n        print(f\"or_call: {ledger} or {base_f} already exists; --init-spend runs once per job\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    key = read_key(a.key_file)\n    u = key_usage(a, key, t)\n    if u is None:\n        print(\"or_call: could not read key usage\", file=sys.stderr); return 3\n    ledger.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    base_f.write_text(json.dumps({\"job\": JOB_ID, \"usage\": u, \"at\": now()}) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(json.dumps({\"baseline\": str(base_f), \"usage\": u}))\n    return 0\n\n\ndef spend_status(a, transport=None) -> int:\n    t = transport or Transport()\n    key = read_key(a.key_file)\n    print(json.dumps(guard_state(a, key, t, Path(a.spend_ledger))))\n    return 0\n\n\ndef call(a, transport: Transport | None = None, sleep=time.sleep) -> int:\n    t = transport or Transport()\n    if not re.fullmatch(r\"harness-[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\.log\", Path(a.log).name):\n        print(f\"or_call: log name {Path(a.log).name!r} must be harness-<seat>[-...].log\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    if not Path(a.log).name.startswith(f\"harness-{a.seat}\"):\n        print(f\"or_call: log {Path(a.log).name!r} is not this seat's (harness-{a.seat}*.log)\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    if a.ledger:\n        tag, provider = pin_from_ledger(a.ledger, a.seat)\n        if a.tag and a.tag != tag:\n            print(f\"or_call: --tag {a.tag} differs from the ledger pin {tag}\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    else:\n        tag, provider = a.tag, a.pin_provider\n    if not tag or not provider:\n        print(\"or_call: need --tag and --pin-provider, or --ledger\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    price = PRICES.get((a.model, tag))\n    if price is None:\n        print(f\"or_call: ({a.model}, {tag}) is not in the frozen PRICES table; refusing\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    p_in, p_out, max_out = price\n    if a.max_tokens is None:\n        a.max_tokens = max_out\n    elif a.max_tokens != max_out:\n        print(f\"or_call: --max-tokens {a.max_tokens} != endpoint max {max_out}; throttling is not allowed\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    messages = json.loads(Path(a.messages).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    if not isinstance(messages, list):\n        print(\"or_call: --messages must hold a JSON list of chat messages\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    key = read_key(a.key_file)\n    ledger = Path(a.spend_ledger)\n    test_mode = ledger.resolve() != Path(SPEND_LEDGER).resolve()\n    worst = len(json.dumps(messages, ensure_ascii=False).encode(\"utf-8\")) * p_in + a.max_tokens * p_out\n    call_name = a.call or f\"{a.seat}_call\"\n    with SpendLock(ledger):\n        st = guard_state(a, key, t, ledger)\n        st.update({\"call\": call_name, \"seat\": a.seat, \"model\": a.model, \"tag\": tag, \"worst_usd\": round(worst, 6),\n                   \"test_mode\": test_mode})\n        if \"error\" in st or st[\"spent_usd\"] + worst + RESERVE_USD >= BOUND_USD:\n            st[\"decision\"] = \"REFUSED\"\n            print(json.dumps(st), file=sys.stderr)\n            print(f\"or_call: REFUSED by the spend guard ({st.get('error') or 'spent + worst case + reserve >= bound'}); \"\n                  \"nothing sent, nothing logged\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 6\n        st[\"decision\"] = \"ALLOWED\"\n        if test_mode and transport is None:\n            print(json.dumps(st))\n            print(\"or_call: TEST MODE (non-job spend ledger): guard would allow; nothing sent\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 7\n        rid = uuid.uuid4().hex\n        _append_ledger(ledger, {\"event\": \"reserve\", \"id\": rid, \"at\": now(), \"job\": JOB_ID, \"seat\": a.seat,\n                                \"call\": call_name, \"model\": a.model, \"tag\": tag, \"max_tokens\": a.max_tokens,\n                                \"worst_usd\": round(worst, 8), \"spent_before_usd\": st[\"spent_usd\"]})\n    holder = {}\n    try:\n        rc = _send(a, t, sleep, key, tag, provider, messages, call_name, holder)\n    finally:\n        resp, gen = holder.get(\"resp\"), holder.get(\"gen\")\n        cost, src = worst, \"worst case (no cost stated)\"\n        g = (gen.get(\"data\") if isinstance(gen, dict) and isinstance(gen.get(\"data\"), dict) else gen) or {}\n        u = (resp.get(\"usage\") if isinstance(resp, dict) else None) or {}\n        if isinstance(g, dict) and g.get(\"total_cost\") is not None:\n            cost, src = float(g[\"total_cost\"]), \"generation.total_cost\"\n        elif isinstance(u, dict) and u.get(\"cost\") is not None:\n            cost, src = float(u[\"cost\"]), \"response.usage.cost\"\n        elif holder.get(\"status\") not in (None, 200) and not (isinstance(resp, dict) and resp.get(\"id\")):\n            cost, src = 0.0, f\"HTTP {holder.get('status')} without a generation id (not billed; key usage reconciles)\"\n        with SpendLock(ledger):\n            _append_ledger(ledger, {\"event\": \"settle\", \"id\": rid, \"at\": now(), \"call\": call_name,\n                                    \"cost_usd\": cost, \"source\": src})\n    return rc\n\n\ndef _send(a, t, sleep, key, tag, provider, messages, call_name, holder) -> int:\n    body = {\"model\": a.model, \"messages\": messages,\n            \"provider\": {\"order\": [tag], \"allow_fallbacks\": False, \"zdr\": True}, \"max_tokens\": a.max_tokens}\n    if a.temperature is not None:\n        body[\"temperature\"] = a.temperature\n    url = f\"{a.base_url}/chat/completions\"\n    send_headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {key}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", META_HEADER[0]: META_HEADER[1]}\n    log_headers = {**send_headers, \"Authorization\": REDACTED}\n    entry = {\"call\": call_name, \"seat\": a.seat,\n             \"request\": {\"method\": \"POST\", \"url\": url, \"headers\": log_headers, \"body\": body},\n             \"harness\": {\"name\": \"freeze/harness/or_call.py\",\n                         \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(Path(__file__).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}}\n    entry[\"sent_at\"] = now()\n    try:\n        status, hdrs, raw = t.request(\"POST\", url, send_headers, json.dumps(body).encode())\n    except Exception as exc:  # transport failure: nothing came back\n        entry.update({\"received_at\": now(), \"response_status\": None, \"response_headers\": {}, \"response\": None,\n                      \"transport_error\": f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\", \"generation\": None,\n                      \"verdict\": {\"ok\": False, \"refusal\": \"transport error\"}})\n        append_entry(Path(a.log), entry, key)\n        print(f\"or_call: transport error, logged: {type(exc).__name__}\", file=sys.stderr); return 3\n    entry[\"received_at\"] = now()\n    entry[\"response_status\"], entry[\"response_headers\"] = status, hdrs\n    holder[\"status\"] = status\n    try:\n        resp = json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n    except ValueError:\n        resp = {\"_raw_text\": raw.decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")}\n    entry[\"response\"] = resp\n    holder[\"resp\"] = resp\n    if status != 200 or not isinstance(resp, dict) or not resp.get(\"id\"):\n        entry.update({\"generation\": None, \"verdict\": {\"ok\": False, \"refusal\": f\"HTTP {status}\"}})\n        append_entry(Path(a.log), entry, key)\n        print(f\"or_call: HTTP {status}, logged\", file=sys.stderr); return 3\n    gen, gstatus = None, None\n    for attempt in range(a.gen_tries):\n        gurl = f\"{a.base_url}/generation?id={resp['id']}\"\n        try:\n            gstatus, _, graw = t.request(\"GET\", gurl, {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {key}\"}, None, timeout=60)\n            if gstatus == 200:\n                gen = json.loads(graw.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n                break\n        except Exception as exc:\n            gstatus = f\"{type(exc).__name__}\"\n        if attempt + 1 < a.gen_tries:\n            sleep(a.gen_wait)\n    entry[\"generation\"], entry[\"generation_status\"], entry[\"generation_fetched_at\"] = gen, gstatus, now()\n    holder[\"gen\"] = gen\n    served, tried = served_by(resp, gen)\n    bad = {s: n for s, n in served.items() if not pin_ok(n, provider, tag)}\n    fallback = sorted({n for n in tried if not pin_ok(n, provider, tag)})\n    refusal = None\n    if not served:\n        refusal = \"the response and generation reply do not say which provider served the call\"\n    elif bad:\n        refusal = \"served by \" + \", \".join(f\"{n!r} ({s})\" for s, n in bad.items()) + f\", not the pin {provider!r} ({tag})\"\n    elif fallback:\n        refusal = f\"a fallback was tried: {fallback}\"\n    entry[\"verdict\"] = {\"pin\": {\"tag\": tag, \"provider\": provider}, \"served_by\": served, \"tried\": tried,\n                        \"ok\": refusal is None, \"refusal\": refusal, \"generation_reply\": gen is not None}\n    append_entry(Path(a.log), entry, key)\n    if refusal:\n        print(f\"or_call: REFUSED ({refusal}); logged to {a.log}; no reply written\", file=sys.stderr); return 4\n    content = ((resp.get(\"choices\") or [{}])[0].get(\"message\") or {}).get(\"content\") or \"\"\n    if a.out:\n        Path(a.out).write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if gen is None:\n        print(f\"or_call: served by the pin, but no /api/v1/generation reply after {a.gen_tries} tries \"\n              f\"(last status {gstatus}); logged with generation null\", file=sys.stderr); return 5\n    print(json.dumps({\"logged\": a.log, \"call\": entry[\"call\"], \"id\": resp[\"id\"], \"served_by\": served,\n                      \"date\": next((v for k, v in hdrs.items() if k.lower() == \"date\"), None)}))\n    return 0\n\n\ndef check_key(a, transport: Transport | None = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Read-only GET /api/v1/key: proves the key works; prints only status, limit and usage.\"\"\"\n    t = transport or Transport()\n    key = read_key(a.key_file)\n    status, _, raw = t.request(\"GET\", f\"{a.base_url}/key\", {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {key}\"}, None, timeout=60)\n    d = json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8\")).get(\"data\", {}) if status == 200 else {}\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\": status, \"limit\": d.get(\"limit\"), \"usage\": d.get(\"usage\")}))\n    return 0 if status == 200 else 3\n\n\ndef parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"One logged OpenRouter call for a job seat.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--key-file\", default=KEY_FILE)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--base-url\", default=BASE)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--check-key\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"read-only GET /api/v1/key, then exit\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seat\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--log\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--model\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--tag\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--pin-provider\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ledger\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--messages\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--call\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-tokens\", type=int)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--gen-tries\", type=int, default=6)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--gen-wait\", type=float, default=5.0)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--spend-ledger\", default=SPEND_LEDGER, help=\"job spend ledger (other path = TEST MODE, nothing sent)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--init-spend\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"record the key-usage baseline once, then exit\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--spend-status\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"print guard state (free GET /api/v1/key), then exit\")\n    return ap\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    a = parser().parse_args(argv)\n    if a.check_key:\n        return check_key(a)\n    if a.init_spend:\n        return init_spend(a)\n    if a.spend_status:\n        return spend_status(a)\n    for k in (\"seat\", \"log\", \"model\", \"messages\"):\n        if not getattr(a, k):\n            print(f\"or_call: --{k.replace('_', '-')} is required\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    return call(a)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n## CONTEXT (read only; not in this part) dot-plumbline/jobs/2026-10-28-doctrine-reader-pointer/handoffs/extract_files.py\n\n````\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Job 2026-10-28-doctrine-reader-pointer (adapted from job 2026-10-27-custody-emitter-gaps; only ALLOWED changed).\nWrite the Maker's whole-file reply into a checkout, byte for byte. Stdlib only; no network; no model call.\n\n  extract_files.py REPLY.txt TARGET_DIR [--list OUT.txt] [--check]\n\nREPLY FORMAT (the Maker's OUTPUT CONTRACT; build_maker_messages.py states the same rules to the model):\n  The reply is a sequence of file blocks followed by one DONE line, then optional NOTES lines:\n\n    <<<PLUMBLINE-FILE path=README.md>>>\n    ...complete new contents of the file...\n    <<<PLUMBLINE-END path=README.md>>>\n    <<<PLUMBLINE-DONE files=1>>>\n    NOTES: ...\n\n  * A marker line is exactly the marker text followed by \"\\\\n\" (a \"\\\\r\" before the \"\\\\n\" is NOT accepted).\n  * A file's contents are the bytes from just after the \"\\\\n\" ending its FILE line up to (not including) the first\n    byte of its END line. So the newline that ends the last content line is part of the file: the extractor\n    adds no trailing newline, strips none, and changes no other byte (no decoding, no line-ending or whitespace\n    normalization). A FILE line followed directly by its END line is an empty file. A file whose last byte is not\n    \"\\\\n\" cannot be expressed (every editable file at the base ends in \"\\\\n\").\n  * The END line repeats the FILE line's path exactly. DONE's count equals the number of FILE blocks.\n  * Outside blocks only blank lines may appear before DONE; after DONE only blank lines and up to 20 lines starting\n    with \"NOTES:\". No other text, no ``` fences around the blocks.\n  * No content line may start with \"<<<PLUMBLINE-\" (that is how a missing END is detected).\n  * Each path at most once. Paths: exactly one of ALLOWED (README.md, AGENTS.md, dot-plumbline/README.md, docs/custody-emission.md); relative, \"/\"\n    separated, no \".\" / \"..\" / empty segments, no backslash, no leading \"/\", printable ASCII without spaces.\n  * There is no delete operation; a file not returned stays as it is.\n\nAll checks run before anything is written: any violation (malformed marker, unterminated block = truncation,\nmissing or wrong DONE, an END marker not at a line start, stray text, bad or disallowed path, duplicate path, target is a symlink or a directory)\n→ exit 1, a one-line reason on stderr starting \"extract_files: \", and NOTHING is written. Exit 0: every file\nwritten (parents created as needed), \"extract_files: wrote <path> (<n> bytes, sha256 <hex>)\" per file on stdout,\nand the paths one per line in --list OUT.txt if given. --check validates only (writes nothing).\nExit 2: usage error.\n\"\"\"\nimport hashlib, re, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nALLOWED = (\"README.md\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"dot-plumbline/README.md\", \"docs/custody-emission.md\")\nALLOWED_PREFIX = None  # job 2026-10-28-doctrine-reader-pointer: the four docs only (approval items 12, 14)\nPFX = b\"<<<PLUMBLINE-\"\nRE_FILE = re.compile(rb\"<<<PLUMBLINE-FILE path=([^\\s>]+)>>>\\n\\Z\")\nRE_END = re.compile(rb\"<<<PLUMBLINE-END path=([^\\s>]+)>>>\\n\\Z\")\nRE_DONE = re.compile(rb\"<<<PLUMBLINE-DONE files=(0|[1-9][0-9]*)>>>\\n?\\Z\")\nRE_PATH = re.compile(r\"[!-~]+\\Z\")\n\n\nclass Refuse(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\ndef check_path(p: str) -> None:\n    if not RE_PATH.match(p) or \"\\\\\" in p or p.startswith(\"/\"):\n        raise Refuse(f\"bad path {p!r}\")\n    if any(s in (\"\", \".\", \"..\") for s in p.split(\"/\")):\n        raise Refuse(f\"bad path {p!r}\")\n    if p in ALLOWED:\n        return\n    raise Refuse(f\"path not allowed: {p}\")\n\n\ndef parse(data: bytes) -> list[tuple[str, bytes]]:\n    lines = [ln for ln in re.split(rb\"(?<=\\n)\", data) if ln]   # split on \"\\n\" only; every byte kept\n    files: list[tuple[str, bytes]] = []\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    i, n, done = 0, len(lines), None\n    while i < n:\n        ln = lines[i]\n        if ln.startswith(PFX):\n            m = RE_FILE.match(ln)\n            if m:\n                path = m.group(1).decode(\"ascii\")\n                check_path(path)\n                if path in seen:\n                    raise Refuse(f\"path returned twice: {path}\")\n                seen.add(path)\n                start = i + 1\n                j = start\n                endtxt = f\"<<<PLUMBLINE-END path={path}>>>\".encode()\n                while j < n and not lines[j].startswith(PFX):\n                    if endtxt in lines[j]:\n                        raise Refuse(f\"line {j + 1}: END marker for {path} is not at the start of a line (the file's \"\n                                     f\"last line must end with a newline before the END line)\")\n                    j += 1\n                if j >= n:\n                    raise Refuse(f\"block for {path} (FILE at line {i + 1}) has no END line: reply truncated\")\n                e = RE_END.match(lines[j])\n                if not e:\n                    raise Refuse(f\"line {j + 1}: expected <<<PLUMBLINE-END path={path}>>>, got a malformed or \"\n                                 f\"other marker line (a content line may not start with <<<PLUMBLINE-)\")\n                if e.group(1).decode(\"ascii\", \"replace\") != path:\n                    raise Refuse(f\"line {j + 1}: END path {e.group(1).decode('ascii', 'replace')!r} \"\n                                 f\"does not match FILE path {path!r}\")\n                files.append((path, b\"\".join(lines[start:j])))\n                i = j + 1\n                continue\n            d = RE_DONE.match(ln)\n            if d:\n                done = (i, int(d.group(1)))\n                break\n            raise Refuse(f\"line {i + 1}: malformed or unexpected marker line {ln[:80]!r}\")\n        if ln.strip(b\" \\t\\r\\n\"):\n            raise Refuse(f\"line {i + 1}: text outside a file block before DONE: {ln[:80]!r}\")\n        i += 1\n    if done is None:\n        raise Refuse(\"no <<<PLUMBLINE-DONE files=N>>> line: reply truncated or malformed\")\n    at, count = done\n    if count != len(files):\n        raise Refuse(f\"DONE says files={count} but the reply has {len(files)} file block(s)\")\n    if not files:\n        raise Refuse(\"the reply returns no files\")\n    notes = 0\n    for k in range(at + 1, n):\n        ln = lines[k]\n        if not ln.strip(b\" \\t\\r\\n\"):\n            continue\n        if ln.startswith(b\"NOTES:\"):\n            notes += 1\n            if notes > 20:\n                raise Refuse(\"more than 20 NOTES: lines after DONE\")\n            continue\n        raise Refuse(f\"line {k + 1}: text after DONE that is not a NOTES: line: {ln[:80]!r}\")\n    if not lines[at].endswith(b\"\\n\") and at != n - 1:\n        raise Refuse(\"malformed DONE line\")\n    return files\n\n\ndef main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    args, lst, check = [], None, False\n    it = iter(argv)\n    for a in it:\n        if a == \"--list\":\n            lst = next(it, None)\n            if lst is None:\n                print(\"usage: extract_files.py REPLY.txt TARGET_DIR [--list OUT.txt] [--check]\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n        elif a == \"--check\":\n            check = True\n        else:\n            args.append(a)\n    if len(args) != 2:\n        print(\"usage: extract_files.py REPLY.txt TARGET_DIR [--list OUT.txt] [--check]\", file=sys.stderr); return 2\n    reply, root = Path(args[0]), Path(args[1])\n    try:\n        files = parse(reply.read_bytes())\n        if not root.is_dir():\n            raise Refuse(f\"target dir {root} does not exist\")\n        rr = root.resolve()\n        for path, _ in files:\n            t = root / path\n            cur = root\n            for seg in path.split(\"/\"):\n                cur = cur / seg\n                if cur.is_symlink():\n                    raise Refuse(f\"{path}: {cur} is a symlink\")\n            if t.exists() and not t.is_file():\n                raise Refuse(f\"{path}: target exists and is not a regular file\")\n            if rr not in t.resolve().parents:\n                raise Refuse(f\"{path}: resolves outside the target dir\")\n    except Refuse as e:\n        print(f\"extract_files: {e}; nothing written\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    if check:\n        for path, body in files:\n            print(f\"extract_files: ok {path} ({len(body)} bytes, sha256 {hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest()})\")\n        return 0\n    for path, body in files:\n        t = root / path\n        t.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        t.write_bytes(body)\n        print(f\"extract_files: wrote {path} ({len(body)} bytes, sha256 {hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest()})\")\n    if lst:\n        Path(lst).write_text(\"\".join(p + \"\\n\" for p, _ in files), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))\n````\n\n## Tests present now under tests/\n\ntest_custody_ledger.py\ntest_discoverability_gate.py\ntest_discoverability_gate_doors.py\ntest_discoverability_gate_host_shape.py\ntest_plumbline_verify.py\nvalidate_audit.py\nvalidate_constitution.py\nvalidate_pin_prose.py\nvalidate_schemas.py\n\nReturn your files now, following the OUTPUT CONTRACT exactly.\n"
