 S1 | `evidence/G5.json` |\n| G6 | **Required rules present** (anchored phrases; each group needs one alternative from every list). B1 tripwire: `same failure class` + `3 times`/`three times`/`third time` + `change the request`. B2: `shared key` + `spend guard` + `upper bound`. B3: `pre-read` + `optional` + `approval sheet`. C1: `finish_reason` + `length` + `empty content` + `own failure class`. C2: `no throttling` + `endpoint max` + `reasoning limit`. C3: `size each task`/`sized task`/`size the task`/`size each request`/`sized request`/`size the request`. C4: `finish_reason` + `every call`. C5: `cap counts` + `iterations`. C6: `command that writes`. C7: `standing rules`. C8: `live test` + `freeze gate`. C9: `write-once`. C10: `relayed approval(s)` + `not an approval`/`not approvals`. C11: `/tmp`. F: `carried forward`, plus a heading containing it. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | S1 | `evidence/G6.json` |\n| G7 | **Leak scan.** None of: `Steve`, `Moitozo`, `S2` (case-sensitive), an email address, `/workspace`, `/Users/`, `/home/`, key material (`sk-or-`, `sk-` + 16 or more key characters) or a key fingerprint; and none of the denylisted verbatim phrases from the Owner's card answers and quoted messages (28 phrases in `fg_rules.json`, matched on letters and digits only). Model and organization names that the drafts cite (for example VizH, evaluatordriven) are allowed. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | S1 | `evidence/G7.json` |\n\n### J: model-read checks (E-GLM), each with one clean and **two planted failure types** in the same batch (J3 and J4: one clean and one planted, as item 30 says)\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| J1 | Reading the base→subject diff of `kit/emit_custody.py`, `kit/custody_history.py`, `kit/custody_ledger.py` and `kit/plumbline_job.py`, plus the new `kit/plumbline_verify.py` (numbered listing): no cross-check