check. So decided_at = F+2 works, and requires real now >= F+2. Sleep until F+2.2. That's ~2s.\n\nBut also, `before(\"the last check\", last, \"disposition.at\", D)` — last = F+2, D = F+2 → ok (non-strict).\n\nAnd `disposition.at` in the record = decided_at = F+2. Fine.\n\nSo: sleep until real >= F+2.5, dispose with decided_at = F+2. About 2s sleep. OK.\n\nHmm wait, one more: the `evaluation` ledger command requires `--verdict FILE` (or --summary). The verdict file must exist. I can use an existing file, e.g., the bar file or a pass file. Actually, `evaluation --verdict` computes sha256 of the file; the emitter doesn't check the verdict file against anything (it just carries the line into x-plumbline.evaluations). So any file works. But `last_check_time` (ledger's dispose bound) reads the evaluation line's `at` (F) and, if `summary_file`, its finished_at. And evaluator received_at from logs (F+2). So last check = F+2.\n\nOK. Also `generation open --prompt FILE`: the prompt file must exist. Use the bar file or a pass file.\n\n`amendment`, `relay` — not needed for T4 (bar lists freeze/approve/pin/generation/evaluation/dispose).\n\n`spend` — not in T4's list. But the record's `x-plumbline.spend` would be from the spend line; without one, `calls_sum_usd` from logs, key_delta 0. Fine (no gap).\n\nHmm wait, actually `spend_block` returns total = max(calls_sum, 0) = calls_sum. If calls have total_cost, fine. If not, 0. OK.\n\nNow, the T4 job also needs passes/controls in custody.json without typed `at`. And the fixture's passes reference calls. Let me make sure removing `at` doesn't break `link_call`.\n\nFrom `link_call`: for passes, `link_call(ev_calls, f.get(\"evaluator\"), f.get(\"call\"), \"eval_artifact\" if n_passes == 1 else None, ...)`. The evaluator is \"eval-a\" (from the ledger test data). The fixture's passes: pass-a with evaluator \"eval-a\". n_passes = 1 (only one pass in pfacts with evaluator eval-a). So default \"eval_artifact\". Does the eval log have a ca