ses if `bar.frozenAt` set — we pop it.\n\nNow `pin`: as discussed, delete the maker log first.\n\nHmm, but wait: does `pin` require anything else? `--seat maker --provider ... --slug ... --host ...`. The host must be a valid upstream host, not an aggregator. The fixture's routing.maker: from the test, `mxx[\"upstream_provider\"] == \"DeepInfra\"`, `provider_slug == \"deepinfra/fp8\"`, endpoint \"api.deepinfra.com\". So pin with those values reproduces the fixture's routing. Good — and the maker log's request/generation must match (it does, since the fixture emits).\n\nNow, after all this, the emitter runs on the rebuilt job. Hand times: \n- bar.frozenAt: freeze line (tool) → no hand time.\n- approvals: approve lines (tool) → no hand.\n- routing.maker.declaredAt: pin line (tool) → no hand.\n- disposition.at: dispose line (tool) → no hand.\n- startedAt/producedAt: maker log sent_at/received_at (stamped) → no hand.\n- passes/controls: no typed at, times from calls (stamped) → no hand. But E3 flags every call's sent_at/received_at — all stamped → no hand.\n\nSo empty hand_times. \n\nBut wait — are there other calls in the evaluator log? If the fixture's eval log has 3 calls, all get stamped. Good.\n\nHmm, and the maker log: 1 call, stamped.\n\nAlso `external` entries reference the eval log; no times.\n\nSo hand_times = []. \n\nNow `rc == 0`: any hard gaps? The rebuilt job should be the same as the fixture minus typed times. The fixture emits exit 0 (no gaps). So the rebuilt should too, as long as times resolve. \n\nPotential gap: `controls` — \"evaluator X batch Y has no control expecting conforms/does_not_conform\". Unchanged.\n\nPotential issue: `xp[\"times\"]` = {\"startedAt\": \"harness log\", ...} since mk.get(\"startedAt\") is set. Good.\n\nOK, now let me also handle E2's test: a typed pass `at` with a linked call is a hand time.\n\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"t2-pass-at\")\nledger_edit(j, lambda c: c[\"passes\"][\"pass-a\"].update(at=\"2026-10-20T12:00:03Z\"))\nrc,