pin_for(ci, ev_log, \"maker\", ref), gaps, hand) if m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\" else {}\n```\n\nAnd evaluator:\n```python\n            eh = evaluator_history(job, ev_dir, ci, e, ref, pin_for(ci, ev_log, str(e.get(\"id\")), ref), gaps)\n```\n→ add `, hand`.\n\nThen remove the us/ua block in build and the per-link `call_hand` blocks.\n\nWait, but `call_hand` function is still used? Let me check all usages:\n- build mcalls block (remove)\n- checks loop (remove)\n- controls loop (remove)\n\nAfter removal, `call_hand` is unused. I could remove the function, but leaving an unused function is fine. Hmm, but it's dead code. Let me remove it to keep things tidy? Risk: no. Actually, let me keep it — no, unused code is a smell. Let me remove `call_hand` since it's no longer used. Hmm, but if I miss a usage, NameError. Let me grep mentally: `call_hand(` appears in:\n1. `def call_hand(c, which)` definition\n2. build: `e = call_hand(min(us...), \"sent_at\")`\n3. build: `e = call_hand(max(ua...), \"received_at\")`\n4. checks: `e = call_hand(call, \"received_at\")`\n5. controls: `e = call_hand(call, \"received_at\")`\n\nI'll remove all and the def. Safe.\n\nNow, one more consideration for E3: the evaluator_history's `calls` are filtered by `c.at`. But `flag_calls(log_calls, hand)` flags all, including those without at. A call without `at` — `hand_time_entries` returns entries for missing sent/received. If a call has no at (no received, no date, no created), then both sent_at and received_at are missing → two entries. But read_log already refused. Fine.\n\nNow, another important detail: `hand_time_entries` uses `self._line_of(...)` which searches `self.lines` for the value. `self.lines` is `text.splitlines()` of the log. Good — file:line is accurate.\n\nNow, the field name: `f\"{self.log}#{self.name or self.i}\"`. INTERFACE: `<log file name>#<call or index>.sent_at`. Good.\n\nNow let's think about whether flagging every call could break existing tests.\n\nTest \"same-family\": rewrites maker log replacing \"fixture/maker-1\" → \"example-1\". If the maker log has sent_at/received_at, no new hand times. Fine.\n\nTest \"pin-attempt\", \"pin-deny\", \"pin-nobody\": these modify the log. `pin-nobody` sets `x[\"request\"] = {\"url\":..., \"model\":...}` (no body). The emitter's routing_request returns None → hard gap, exit 1. But does the call still have sent_at/received_at? Yes (unchanged). Fine.\n\nTest \"pin-deny\": changes request.provider. Fine.\n\nHmm, what about `ledger-pin-ok`: deletes the maker log and the events log, pops routing, runs pin, then... the test ends there (doesn't emit). Fine.\n\nTest \"no-maker-log\": deletes the maker log → refused \"time\" (no log). Fine.\n\nNow the eval log: does it have sent_at? E3 says no. So every test that emits a fixture will now have extra hand times. With allow_hand=True, fine (record written). With allow_hand=False (T2 test), more refusals — still exit 3. Fine.\n\nBut: the test `res((f\"{S} · fixture job emits with no gap (exit 0)\", rc == 0, ...))` — with allow_hand=True, rc=0. Hand times don't cause gaps. Good.\n\nHmm, wait: but do the evaluator calls' missing sent_at cause any *gap*? No, hand times are refusals/allowances, not gaps. Good.\n\nBut hold on: what about `check_order`? The evaluator calls' `at` = created (2026-10-20T12:00:0x). The checks' times use `H.iso(call.at)`. The record's check at = created-based. Ordering vs producedAt (maker received_at). If the maker log has received_at and the eval has created, the order should be fine (fixture designed so). Iteration 1 passed T5 and base tests, so ordering is fine.\n\nNow, one more: the T3 test asserts `all(e.get(\"file\") and e.get(\"source\") for e in ht)`. For server-header entries, `file` = self.log, `source` = \"server-header\". Good.\n\nNow let me also double-check: E3 flags `.received_at` too. For the eval calls, `received_at` is missing but `created` exists → source \"response-created\" (since `if self.date: ... elif self.created`). Wait:\n\n```python\n        if self.received is None:\n            if self.date:\n                n = self._line_of(_hdr(hdrs, \"Date\"), \"Date\")\n                out.append({... \"source\": \"server-header\"})\n            elif self.created:\n                n = self._line_of(resp.get(\"created\"), \"created\")\n                out.append({... \"source\": \"response-created\"})\n```\n\nSo if the log has a Date header, received_at → server-header. Otherwise response-created. Either way flagged. Good.\n\nNow, let's also think: does the emitter's `evaluator_history` get called for every model evaluator? Yes, in the loop `for i, e in enumerate(ci.get(\"evaluators\") or [])`. Only if `e.get(\"kind\") == \"model\"`. For script evaluators, no log. Good.\n\nNow — the `maker_history` is only called if `m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\"`. Good.\n\n### Now the test additions\n\nLet me write the test code. I need `time` imported (for sleep). And maybe `datetime`.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n```python\n# ---- E1/E3: a job whose every time comes from the kit's own tools (T4 shape) ----\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n\n\ndef _iso(dt):\n    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef _parse(s):\n    return datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef stamp_log(path, base, step=2):\n    \"\"\"Write the logger's own sent_at/received_at into every call, as tools/edi/or_call.py does (a harness log\n    without them makes every call a hand time, T7b). The response created/Date stay as the fixture wrote them.\"\"\"\n    doc = json.loads(path.read_text())\n    items = doc if isinstance(doc, list) else [doc]\n    for i, c in enumerate(items):\n        if not isinstance(c, dict):\n            continue\n        c[\"sent_at\"] = _iso(base + timedelta(seconds=step * i))\n        c[\"received_at\"] = _iso(base + timedelta(seconds=step * i + 1))\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(doc, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef tool_built_job(name):\n    \"\"\"The fixture's static facts with every typed time removed, rebuilt only by kit/custody_ledger.py:\n    freeze/approve/pin/generation/evaluation/dispose --decided-at (T4). Returns (job dir, decided_at).\"\"\"\n    j = job_copy(name)\n    cj = json.loads((j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").read_text())\n    roles = [(a.get(\"role\"), a.get(\"by\")) for a in (cj.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"approvals\") or []]\n    for k in (\"frozenAt\", \"approvals\"):\n        (cj.get(\"bar\") or {}).pop(k, None)\n    cj.pop(\"disposition\", None)\n    cj.pop(\"routing\", None)\n    cj.pop(\"startedAt\", None)\n    cj.pop(\"producedAt\", None)\n    for f in (cj.get(\"passes\") or {}).values():\n        f.pop(\"at\", None)\n    for k in cj.get(\"controls\") or []:\n        k.pop(\"at\", None)\n    (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cj, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    # a job's packet close is the ledger's own clock's business; keep it from pre-dating the tool stamps\n    pk = json.loads((j / \"packet.json\").read_text())\n    pk.pop(\"close\", None)\n    (j / \"packet.json\").write_text(json.dumps(pk, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    # pin before the seat's first call: the fixture's maker log is put back after the pin is logged\n    log = j / \"custody\" / \"evidence\" / \"harness-maker-fixture.log\"\n    saved = log.read_bytes() if log.is_file() else None\n    if saved is not None:\n        log.unlink()\n    ledger = [str(LEDGER), \"--job-dir\", str(j)]\n    rc, out = run_py([str(LEDGER), \"freeze\", \"--job-dir\", str(j)])\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, wait: the `freeze` command's `at` is captured. I need it. Let me read the event log after freeze:\n\n```python\n    ev = [json.loads(x) for x in (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines()]\n    fz = _parse(ev[-1][\"at\"])\n```\n\nThen approve, pin, generation, evaluation.\n\nWait, order: pin 