\n\nNow E1 disposition as drafted.\n\nLet me also double check `time_sources` — unchanged.\n\nNow let me write out the whole emitter file.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to keep the `gaps` partial-stamp block in maker_history. I'll keep it.\n\nAlso, I realize there's a potential issue with `flag_calls` for the maker log: the maker log is a single object; `read_log` returns 1 call. `hand_time_entries` for it: if it has sent_at and received_at, nothing. Good.\n\nFor the eval log: 3 calls, no sent_at → 3 sent_at entries (+ maybe received_at if no Date header). Good.\n\nNow, let me also think about whether flagging evaluator calls could affect `xp[\"sources\"]` or other things. No.\n\nOK, writing now.\n\nOne more: the `build` docstring/`x-plumbline` doc — no change.\n\nLet me produce the emitter file.\n\nActually — hmm, wait. I want to double check the `controls` link_call default: `f\"eval_{str(k.get('id') or '').lower()}\"`. If the control's id is \"ctl-clean\", default = \"eval_ctl-clean\". The fixture's controls[0].call must be set (since `unlinked-control` overrides it to \"eval_nope\" and expects refusal). So the fixture's controls have explicit `call`. Good.\n\nNow, the `passes` link_call default \"eval_artifact\" — only if n_passes == 1. If the fixture has 1 pass for eval-a, the default applies and the log must have a call named \"eval_artifact\". From `tol-59`, `rt[\"checks\"][0][\"at\"] == 12:00:03`, so a call is linked. Good.\n\nOK, writing.\n\nAlso — the E2 test uses `cj[\"passes\"][\"pass-a\"][\"at\"]`. If pass-a doesn't exist... it does.\n\nLet me now write the final tests file. I'll append the new block. Let me be careful to preserve all existing content.\n\nLet me also double-check `emit()` helper: `args = [str((tree or SNAP) / \"kit\" / \"emit_custody.py\"), \"--job-dir\", str(job), \"--out\", str(out), *extra]` then append `--allow-hand-times` if allow_hand. Good.\n\nNow writing both files.\n\nFor the tool_built_job function, `emit(TJ, o, allow_hand=False)` uses SNAP's emitter and TJ's job dir. But `TJ` is under TMP (job_copy uses TMP). Fine.\n\nHmm, one issue: `tool_built_job` calls `run_py([str(LEDGER), ...])` where LEDGER = SNAP/kit/custody_ledger.py. And `run_py` cwd=REPO. Fine.\n\nAnother: the emitter's revision check uses SNAP (clean). Fine.\n\nLet me now also make sure `job_copy` copies the fixture; `job_copy(\"tool-built\")` → TMP/\"tool-built\". Good.\n\nNow, `stamp_log` iterates `(j/\"custody\"/\"evidence\").glob(\"harness-*.log\")`. This includes the maker log and eval log. Good. But it might include other logs; stamping them all is fine.\n\nHmm, but the maker log was restored from `saved` bytes. Then stamped. Fine.\n\nNow, the order in tool_built_job: I stamp the logs AFTER `evaluation` and before `dispose`. The ledger's `last_check_time` (for dispose) reads the logs' received_at. So the stamps must exist before dispose. Yes, they do. And received_at = fz+1. And `last` includes fz+2. Good.\n\nHmm wait, `last_check_time` also reads the evaluation line's `at`. And the summary if present. No summary. So last_check = max(evaluation at, eval received_at = fz+1, ...). My `last` = max(events' at, fz+2). Since events include the evaluation at (≈ fz+1-2) and I floor at fz+2, `last >= last_check`. Good.\n\nNow, `decided = last + 1`. The ledger requires `decided >= last_check` and `decided <= tool clock`. We wait until real >= decided+1.9, so tool clock >= decided+1 > decided. Good.\n\nThen the emitter: `at = dsp.at = decided`. `live_at = decided_at = decided`. Equal. Good.\n\nAnd `check_order`: D = decided. last check (from logs) = fz+1. `before(\"the last check\", fz+1, \"disposition.at\", decided=fz+3)` → fz+1 > fz+3? No. OK.\n\nAnd `after-emit`: D = fz+3 <= now (emit ≈ fz+4). OK.\n\nAnd close: popped. OK.\n\nNow `xp[\"disposition_at_source\"]` = \"logged live\". Good.\n\nNow, the record's `disposition.at` = decided. And the F1b assertion: `rec_disp.at == dispo.decided_at != dispo.at`. dispo.at = tool clock at dispose ≈ decided+1. So `decided_at != at`. Good.\n\nAlright. Let me write.\n\nHmm, one more: `run(\"generation\", \"close\", \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--n\", \"1\", \"--outcome\", \"done\")` — the `generation close` requires `--n N` where N is an open generation. We opened n=1. Good.\n\nAnd `generation open` requires `--prompt FILE`. I use \"custody/bar.md\". The command resolves relative to job. Good.\n\nNow let me also double-check the ledger's `generation open` numbering: `n = max(opens) + 1 if opens else 1` → 1. Good.\n\nOK. And `evaluation --batch b1 --evaluator eval-a --verdict custody/bar.md`. Fine.\n\nNow writing the files.\n\nLet me produce the emitter file content. I'll carefully copy and modify.\n\nI need to be careful about the `flag_calls` placement: replace `call_hand` def.\n\nLet me write the final emitter.\n\n(Writing...)\n\nNow for the tests file, I'll insert the block and the imports.\n\nLet me write the insertion:\n\n```python\n# ---- T4/E1/E3: a job whose every time comes from the kit's own tools, and the hand-time coverage they need ----\ndef _iso(dt):\n    return dt.astimezone(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef _ts(s):\n    return datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef stamp_log(path, at):\n    \"\"\"Write the logger's own sent_at/received_at into every call of a harness log, as tools/edi/or_call.py\n    does. Without them every call is a hand time (T7b), and a job the tools built has none.\"\"\"\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    try:\n        doc = json.loads(text)\n        items, array = (doc, True) if isinstance(doc, list) else ([doc], False)\n    except ValueError:\n        items, array = [json.loads(ln) for ln in text.splitlines() if ln.strip()], False\n    for c in items:\n        if isinstance(c, dict):\n            c[\"sent_at\"] = c[\"received_at\"] = at\n    path.write_text((json.dumps(items, indent=2) + \"\\n\") if array\n                    else \"\".join(json.dumps(c) + \"\\n\" for c in items), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef tool_built_job(name):\n    \"\"\"The fixture's static facts with every typed time removed, rebuilt only by kit/custody_ledger.py:\n    freeze / approve / pin / generation / evaluation / dispose --decided-at (T4, F1b).\"\"\"\n    j = job_copy(name)\n    cj = json.loads((j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    roles = [(a.get(\"role\"), a.get(\"by\")) for a in (cj.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"approvals\") or []]\n    dsp = cj.get(\"disposition\") or {}\n    ev_id = str(((cj.get(\"evaluators\") or [{}])[0]).get(\"id\") or \"eval-a\")\n    for k in (\"frozenAt\", \"approvals\"):\n        (cj.get(\"bar\") or {}).pop(k, None)\n    for k in (\"disposition\", \"routing\", \"startedAt\", \"producedAt\"):\n        cj.pop(k, None)\n    for f in (cj.get(\"passes\") or {}).values():\n        f.pop(\"at\", None)\n    for k in cj.get(\"controls\") or []:\n        k.pop(\"at\", None)\n    (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cj, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    pk = json.loads((j / \"packet.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    pk.pop(\"close\", None)          # the tool's clock stamps the events; a fixture close date would pre-date them\n    (j / \"packet.json\").write_text(json.dumps(pk, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    def run(*args):\n        rc, out = run_py([str(LEDGER), *args, \"--job-dir\", str(j)])\n        if rc != 0:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"ledger {args[0]} refused: {out.strip()[-200:]}\")\n        return out\n\n    # a pin is declared before the seat's first call (custody_ledger.py pin): put the fixture's log back after\n    mlog = next(iter((j / \"custody\" / \"evidence\").glob(\"harness-maker*.log\")), None)\n    saved = mlog.read_bytes() if mlog and mlog.is_file() else None\n    if saved is not None:\n        mlog.unlink()\n    run(\"freeze\")\n    evs = [json.loads(x) for x in (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines() if x.strip()]\n    fz = _ts(evs[-1][\"at\"])\n    for role, by in roles:\n        run(\"approve\", \"--role\", role, \"--by\", by)\n    run(\"pin\", \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--provider\", \"DeepInfra\", \"--slug\", \"deepinfra/fp8\", \"--host\", \"api.deepinfra.com\")\n    if saved is not None:\n        mlog.write_bytes(saved)\n    run(\"generation\", \"open\", \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--prompt\", \"custody/bar.md\")\n    run(\"generation\", \"close\", \"--seat\", \"maker\", \"--n\", \"1\", \"--outcome\", \"done\")\n    run(\"evaluation\", \"--batch\", \"b1\", \"--evaluator\", ev_id, \"--verdict\", \"custody/bar.md\")\n    # the tools wrote the logs, so every call carries the logger's own times (T7b); the freeze stays earliest\n    for lg in (j / \"custody\" / \"evidence\").glob(\"harness-*.log\"):\n        stamp_log(lg, _iso(fz + timedelta(seconds=1)))\n    # dispose --decided-at: the Owner's time, bounded by the last logged check and the tool's clock (F1b, E1)\n    last = max([_ts(e[\"at\"]) for e in evs if e.get(\"at\")] + [fz + timedelta(seconds=2)])\n    args = [\"dispose\", \"--by\", dsp.get(\"by\") or \"Fixture Owner\"]\n    if dsp.get(\"state\") in (\"given\", \"declined\"):\n        args += [\"--state\", dsp[\"state\"]]\n    for _ in range(6):\n        decided = last + timedelta(seconds=1)\n        while time.time() < decided.timestamp() + 1.9:\n            time.sleep(0.05)\n        rc, out = run_py([str(LEDGER), *args, \"--job-dir\", str(j), \"--decided-at\", _iso(decided),\n                          \"--decided-source\", \"chat\"])\n        if rc == 0:\n            return j\n        if \"before the last logged check\" not in out:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"ledger dispose refused: {out.strip()[-200:]}\")\n        last += timedelta(seconds=1)\n    raise RuntimeError(\"ledger dispose kept refusing (decided_at before the last logged check)\")\n\n\ntry:\n    TJ = tool_built_job(\"tool-built\")\n    tj = json.loads((TJ / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    tj[\"x-plumbline\"] = {\"note\": \"from the ledger's inputs\", \"verdict\": \"JUNK\", \"gaps\": [\"JUNK\"],\n                         \"times\": \"JUNK\", \"hand_times\": [\"JUNK\"], \"nested\": {\"k\": [1, 2, 3]}}\n    (TJ / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").write_text(json.dumps(tj, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    o = TMP / \"tool-built.json\"\n    rc, out = emit(TJ, o, allow_hand=False)\n    rt = json.loads(o.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"predicate\"] if o.is_file() else {}\n    rx = rt.get(\"x-plumbline\") or {}\n    res((f\"{S} · T4 a job built only with kit/custody_ledger.py emits with no switch (exit 0, empty hand_times)\",\n         rc == 0 and rx.get(\"hand_times\") == [], f\"exit {rc}: {out.strip()[-160:]}\"))\n    dispo = [json.loads(x) for x in (TJ / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines()\n             if x.strip() and json.loads(x).get(\"event\") == \"dispose\"]\n    res((f\"{S} · F1b the record's disposition.at is the line's decided_at, not the tool clock\",\n         bool(dispo) and (rt.get(\"disposition\") or {}).get(\"at\") == dispo[-1].get(\"decided_at\")\n         and dispo[-1].get(\"decided_at\") != dispo[-1].get(\"at\"),\n         f\"decided_at {dispo[-1].get('decided_at') if dispo else None}\"))\n    res((f\"{S} · F1h/X1 the tool-built record carries the ledger arrays with file:line and the inputs deep-equal\",\n         all(str(e.get(\"source\", \"\")).startswith(\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl:\")\n             for k in (\"generations\", \"evaluations\") for e in rx.get(k) or [])\n         and rx.get(\"generations\") and rx.get(\"evaluations\")\n         and rx.get(\"inputs\") == tj[\"x-plumbline\"] and rx.get(\"verdict\") != \"JUNK\"\n         and isinstance(rx.get(\"hand_times\"), list)\n         and (rx.get(\"spend\") or {}).get(\"tolerance_u