\"\"\"\n    for e in c.hand_time_entries():\n        if str(e.get(\"field\", \"\")).endswith(\".\" + which):\n            return e\n    return None\n```\n\nNew:\n```python\ndef flag_calls(calls, hand: dict | None) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Every call of a harness log the emitter reads: a `.sent_at`/`.received_at` the logger did not stamp is a\n    hand time (T7b), named with the server time's source and the file:line that carries it. The log is never\n    rewritten; a call the logger did stamp adds nothing.\"\"\"\n    if hand is None:\n        return\n    for c in calls:\n        for e in c.hand_time_entries():\n            hand[e[\"field\"]] = e\n```\n\n3. maker_history: add `hand` param, flag log_calls.\n\n4. evaluator_history: add `hand` param, flag log_calls.\n\n5. build: pass hand; remove us/ua; remove per-link call_hand; E2 marks; E1 disposition.\n\nLet me write the full file now.\n\nActually, wait. One more thing about `maker_history`: the current code:\n\n```python\n    calls = H.read_log(log, ref, \"maker\")\n    if m.get(\"calls\"):\n        calls = [c for c in calls if c.name in m[\"calls\"]]\n    calls = [c for c in calls if c.at]\n    if not calls:\n        return {}\n```\n\nI'll change to:\n\n```python\n    log_calls = H.read_log(log, ref, \"maker\")\n    flag_calls(log_calls, hand)\n    calls = log_calls\n    if m.get(\"calls\"):\n        calls = [c for c in calls if c.name in m[\"calls\"]]\n    calls = [c for c in calls if c.at]\n    if not calls:\n        return {}\n```\n\n6. Also the `gaps` block in maker_history uses `calls` — fine.\n\nNow let me write the tests file additions.\n\nLet me look at where to insert. After the X1 block:\n\n```python\nres((f\"{S} · X1 an inputs x-plumbline is deep-equal under .inputs and cannot shadow the emitter's own keys\",\n     rc == 0 and rx.get(\"inputs\") == inp and rx.get(\"verdict\") != \"JUNK\"\n     and isinstance(rx.get(\"gaps\"), list) and isinstance(rx.get(\"hand_times\"), list)\n     and rx.get(\"times\") != \