hand_times\": {\"switch\": \"--allow-hand-times\", \"writer\": \"kit/emit_custody.py@0123456789ab\", \"at\": \"2026-01-01T00:05:00Z\"}}`.\n\n`hand/record-no-allowance.json`: hand_times entry, no allowances.\n\n`hand/record-unflagged.json`: hand_times [], allowances as above.\n\n`events/record-missing-generation.json`: clean record without `generations`.\n\n`relay/record.json`: clean + predicate.bar.approvals + relays array.\n\n`shadow/record.json`: clean + s5_record, verdict, inputs.\n\nNow let me double-check the shadow record's `inputs` field: `\"inputs\": {\"verdict\": \"accept\"}`. Schema: `inputs` object ✓.\n\nAnd check_shadow's second loop: `key=\"verdict\"`, `key in inputs` ✓, `key in xp` ✓, `key in derived` ✓ (derived verdict = \"reject\"); `xp.get(\"verdict\") == inputs.get(\"verdict\")` (\"accept\"==\"accept\") and `xp.get(\"verdict\") != derived[\"verdict\"]` → shadow ✓.\n\nNow — one thing I missed: `check_shadow`'s first loop includes `\"verdict\"` in OWNED; `xp[\"verdict\"]=\"accept\"`, derived=\"reject\" → shadow. So two shadow failures. Fine.\n\nNow let's also confirm the shadow record passes schema: `s5_record` object ✓; `verdict` string ✓; `inputs` object ✓.\n\nNow, will `check_events` on the shadow job (clean ledger = freeze only) pass? Arrays: xp generations [] = [] ✓, etc. ✓\n\nNow let me write the test file.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"The verifier's own tests: every failure kind V1-V8 names, from repo fixtures, plus the clean control.\n\nFixtures live in tests/fixtures/custody/verify/. Each job is a copy of the clean job with a different\ninputs/custody-events.jsonl (a hand freeze, a generation pair, a relay) or an extra §5 record; the records are\nwritten by hand to plant exactly one fault. The standard layer is a stand-in checker pinned in the temp copy (the\nreal checker is pinned in the custody checkout, which a unit test cannot reach).\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nNow the code. One thing: `import plumbline_job as J` — plumbline_job imports argparse etc. at mod