ous.\n\nFor the test file, one more test idea: `test_verifier_does_not_import_emitter` should assert no \"emit_custody\" anywhere in the file. Since the docstring must not contain it, ✓.\n\nLet me also grep my verifier for \"emit\": \"the emitter's logic\" appears in the docstring — the word \"emitter\" is fine; R2 is about the *path* reference. The static check \"reads that as a reference to the emitter\" was about the string literal `kit/emit_custody.py@`. To be safe, I'll avoid the token \"emit_custody\" entirely, and also avoid \"emit_custody.py\". The word \"emitter\" alone should be fine (V7 says \"does not import kit/emit_custody.py\"). I'll keep \"the emitter\" in prose. Actually, to be extra safe against a naive grep for \"emit_custody\", ensure zero occurrences. Yes.\n\nAlso the test's `assertNotIn(\"emit_custody\", text)` enforces it.\n\nNow write.\n\nLet me draft the verifier's `main` fully:\n\n```python\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Verify a custody/v1 record at the standard and Plumbline layers.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--record\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--files\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--evidence\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ledger\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--custody\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--json\")\n    a = ap.parse_args(argv)\n\n    record = Path(a.record).expanduser()\n    files = Path(a.files).expanduser()\n    evidence = Path(a.evidence).expanduser()\n    ledger = Path(a.ledger).expanduser()\n    custody = Path(a.custody).expanduser()\n\n    if not record.is_file():\n        return finish(2, [{\"kind\": \"standard\", \"field\": \"record\", \"file\": str(record), \"line\": 0}], a.json)\n    if not ledger.is_file():\n        return finish(2, [{\"kind\": \"standard\", \"field\": \"ledger\", \"file\": str(ledger), \"line\": 0}], a.json)\n    if not custody.is_dir():\n        return finish(2, [{\"kind\": \"standard\", \"field\"