es),\n                         \"--evidence\", str(evidence)], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if rv.returncode == 0:\n        return 0, rv\n    return 1, rv\n```\n\nR1 says: \"run `[sys.executable, check.py, RECORD, \"--files\", FILES, \"--evidence\", EVIDENCE]` once (no guessing forms); exit 0 = OK; any other exit = kind `standard`, exit 3.\"\n\nHmm — \"any other exit = kind standard, exit 3\" — including exit 2 from check.py? The bar V1 says the checker exit 2 is \"not checkable\"; but R1 says any other exit → standard, exit 3. Wait, but our exit 2 is reserved for cannot-run. Let me re-read: \"exit 0 = OK; any other exit = kind `standard`, exit 3.\" OK, so checker exit 1 or 2 → 3. Only our own cannot-run conditions (missing input, missing pin, wrong bytes) → 2. Fine.\n\nBut note the checker may not exist and no pin → exit 2 (cannot run). Keep.\n\nWait — one problem: the standard check currently happens before loading the record; we need the record path. Also the `--bar` flag: optional. Skip.\n\nAlso V1 says \"runs it on the record at the claimed level\" — the checker reads the claimed level from the record. No --level needed.\n\nNow, R2: remove `\"kit/emit_custody.py@\"` from check_hand_times. Replace with form check:\n\n```python\nWRITER_FORM = re.compile(r\"^kit/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.py@[0-9a-f]{12}$\")\n\ndef allowance_writer_ok(w) -> bool:\n    return isinstance(w, str) and WRITER_FORM.match(w) is not None and \"..\" not in w\n```\n\nGood.\n\nAlso check: does anything else in the verifier reference the emitter? The docstring says \"This file must not import kit/emit_custody.py...\" — R2 says remove every reference to the emitter's module or path from kit/plumbline_verify.py. The static check \"reads that as a reference to the emitter and exits 2\" — probably a check for the string \"emit_custody\" in the file. The docstring contains \"kit/emit_custody.py\"! Must remove that too. Also \"the emitter's logic is checked by separate code\" — reword without the p