n\nLedger line: `{\"event\": \"freeze\", \"at\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"bar_file\": \"custody/bar.md\", \"bar_sha256\": \"0000...\", \"writer\": \"kit/custody_ledger.py@0123456789ab\"}`.\ncustody.json: `{\"custody_inputs\": \"plumbline/custody-inputs/v1\", \"bar\": {\"file\": \"custody/bar.md\", \"frozenAt\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}}`.\n\nDoes that create any other verifier failure? `line_of` not called since freeze in seen. Good.\n\nDo I need `custody/bar.md` to exist? The verifier doesn't check. Fine, but add it for realism? Not necessary. Keep files minimal.\n\n`.../clean/job/custody/files/artifact.txt`: `\"plumbline verifier fixture\\n\"`. Exists so the dir isn't empty in git (git doesn't track empty dirs). Also `custody/evidence/` needs a file: add `evidence/README.txt`? Hmm, `read_calls` globs `*.log` in evidence — a README.txt is not a .log. But `hand_time_set` also globs `*.log`. Fine. Add `custody/evidence/.gitkeep`? A dotfile is fine. Let me add `custody/evidence/notes.txt` with a line.\n\n`.../clean/record.custody.json`: the clean record.\n\nNow the hand fixture: `tests/fixtures/custody/verify/hand/job/`:\n- packet.json same.\n- inputs/custody.json: `{\"custody_inputs\": \"...\", \"bar\": {\"file\": \"custody/bar.md\", \"frozenAt\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}}`\n- inputs/custody-events.jsonl: `{\"event\":\"freeze\",\"at\":\"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"bar_file\":\"custody/bar.md\",\"bar_sha256\":\"00...\",\"writer\":\"hand\"}` (line 1)\n- custody/files/artifact.txt, custody/evidence/notes.txt\n\nThe record variants (stored in the hand folder or generated by the test):\n- `record-allowance-ok.json` (flags + allowance) — should pass? hand set non-empty, flags match, allowance valid → hand checks pass. But then exit 0? That would be a second clean record. Fine, but it's not needed. Let me create the variants the tests need:\n  - `record-no-allowance.json`: hand_times matches, no allowances → `allowance`.\n  - `record-unflagged.json`: hand_times [], allowances valid → `hand-time-unflagged`? Wait: recomp non-empty, got empty → hand-time-unflagged. And `if recomp:` → allowance present and valid → no allowance failure. Good, only hand-time-unflagged.\n\nHmm — but also check_shadow: hand_times derived vs xp. In check_shadow, for hand_times the comparison uses sets; `{...} != {...}` → shadow fires too! Order: hand_times check first (hand-time-unflagged), then shadow. First kind is hand-time-unflagged. OK.\n\n  - For `flag-without-source`, use the clean job (no hand lines) with a record whose hand_times has an entry → flag-without-source. Where to store? `.../verify/clean/record-flag-without-source.json`. But then check_shadow also fires (hand_times differ) — first is flag-without-source (hand check before shadow). Good.\n\n  - `record-allowance-bad-writer.json`? Optional. Skip.\n\n- `record-flag-without-source.json` in clean folder.\n\nNow the events fixture: `.../verify/events/job/` with a ledger containing a generation open/close, custody.json minimal, and `record-missing-generation.json` (no `generations` key). Wait — if the record omits `generations`, check_schema passes (not required). check_events → events. Good.\n\nBut also: with a generation line in the ledger, does hand_time_set mark anything? No.\n\nBut `used_seats` empty. Fine.\n\nThe record for events: the clean record minus `generations`. But the clean record has `generations: []`; the events record omits it.\n\nHmm wait: check_shadow's derived has generations; xp lacks it → skipped. ✓.\n\nAlso: check_events' maker-call check needs `calls_by_seat` — empty → fails with events. Same kind.\n\n- Relay-as-approval fixture: `.../verify/relay/job/` with a relay ledger line; record with `relays` matching the ledger (with source) and `predicate.bar.approvals = [{\"role\":\"relay\",\"by\":\"BuyerBot\",\"at\":\"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}]`. Then check_events: arrays match; approvals match relay → relay-as-approval. check_shadow: relays match; hand_times: no hand → ok; spend ok. Also `approvals` — not checked by shadow. Good. Only relay-as-approval.\n\nWait — one thing: `ledger_array` includes all fields of the line plus source. The relay line must be reproduced exactly in the record: `{\"event\":\"relay\",\"kind\":\"relay\",\"quote\":\"...\",\"from\":\"BuyerBot\",\"source_chat\":\"...\",\"source_at\":\"...\",\"at\":\"...\",\"writer\":\"...\",\"source\":\"inputs/custody-events.jsonl:1\"}`. The fixture record must match byte-for-byte in structure. I'll write it carefully.\n\nAlso `check_events` line: for a relay, `r.get(\"_line\")` — the ledger lines get `_line`; in `ledger_array` the `_line` is stripped and `source` added. In check_events, `relays = [e for _, e in lines if e.get(\"event\") == \"relay\"]` — these retain `_line`. Fine.\n\n- Spend fixture: reuse the clean job with a record whose spend.calls_sum_usd = 0.01, total 0.01. Store as `.../verify/clean/record-spend-off.json`.\n\n- Shadow fixture: a job with `iteration-1-eval-record.json` `{\"verdict\": \"reject\"}`, and a record with s5_record name, verdict \"accept\", inputs {\"verdict\": \"accept\"}. Store under `.../verify/shadow/job/` and `record.json`.\n\n- Schema fixtures: records derived from the clean record: missing x-plumbline; hand_times string; unknown key; schema \"v0\"/absent. Store in `.../verify/clean/` as variants:\n  - `record-no-block.json`\n  - `record-hand-times-string.json`\n  - `record-unknown-key.json`\n  - `record-v0.json`\n\n- Standard fixture: `.../verify/clean/record-bad-subject.json` with subject naming artifact.txt and digest \"0\"*64.\n\nHmm, wait: for the standard failure the stub checker must be given `--files` pointing at the job's files dir, where artifact.txt exists with a different sha. ✓.\n\nNow the tests. Structure:\n\n```python\nimport json, subprocess, sys, tempfile, unittest\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nVERIFIER = ROOT / \"kit\" / \"plumbline_verify.py\"\nFIX = ROOT / \"tests\" / \"fixtures\" / \"custody\" / \"verify\"\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"kit\"))\nimport plumbline_verify as V\n```\n\nHelper:\n\n```python\ndef checkout(tmp: Path, wrong: bool = False) -> Path:\n    c = tmp / (\"bad-checkout\" if wrong else \"checkout\")\n    src = FIX / \"checkout\" / \"checker\" / \"check.py\"\n    (c / \"checker\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    (c / \"tools\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    (c / \"checker\" / \"check.py\").write_bytes(src.read_bytes())\n    pin = sha256((c / \"checker\" / \"check.py\").read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    if wrong:\n        pin = \"0\" * 64\n    (c / \"tools\" / \"pin.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"checker/check.py\": pin}))\n    return c\n```\n\n```python\ndef job_copy(tmp: Path, name: str) -> Path:\n    src = FIX / name / \"job\"\n    dst = tmp / name / \"job\"\n    shutil.copytree(src, dst)\n    return dst\n```\n\n```python\ndef run(record: Path, job: Path, custody: Path):\n    return subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(VERIFIER), \"--record\", str(record),\n                           \"--files\", str(job / \"custody\" / \"files\"),\n                           \"--evidence\", str(job / \"custody\" / \"evidence\"),\n                           \"--ledger\", str(job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"),\n                           \"--custody\", str(custody)], capture_output=True, text=True)\n```\n\n```python\ndef kinds(rv):\n    return [ln.split()[1] for ln in rv.stdout.splitlines() if ln.startswith(\"FAIL \")]\n```\n\nTests:\n1. `test_clean_record_exit_0` — clean job + clean record → rc 0, no FAIL.\n2. `test_standard_failure` — bad subject → rc 3, kinds[0] == \"standard\".\n3. `test_wrong_checker_bytes_exit_2` — wrong pin → rc 2.\n4. `test_schema_*` — four variants → rc 4, \"schema\" in kinds.\n5. `test_allowance` — hand job + record-no-allowance → rc 4, kinds[0] == \"allowance\".\n6. `test_hand_time_unflagged` — hand job + record-unflagged → \"hand-time-unflagged\" in kinds.\n7. `test_flag_without_source` — clean job + record-flag-without-source → \"flag-without-source\" in kinds.\n8. `test_events` — events job + record-missing-generation → \"events\" in kinds.\n9. `test_relay_as_approval` — relay job + record → \"relay-as-approval\" in kinds.\n10. `test_spend` — clean job + record-spend-off → \"spend\" in kinds.\n11. `test_shadow` — shadow job + record → \"shadow\" in kinds.\n12. `test_does_not_import_emitter` — no \"emit_custody\" in the file text.\n13. `test_writes_nothing` — snapshot sha of record/job files before/after a run → equal.\n14. `test_json_out` — `--json OUT` writes exit/failures. (optional)\n15. V8 close test: build a scratch copy of the repo kit? That's heavy. R4 says \"make sure a test covers both outcomes\". Hmm.\n\nFor V8, I need `plumbline_job.py close` to run the emitter then the verifier. The emitter part is being fixed separately; a close test needs a full job with packet.json etc. and the emitter to succeed. That's a large integration fixture. In iteration 1 there was no such test. R4 asks for it.\n\nAlternative: test `run_verifier` / the close wiring by invoking `plumbline_job.py custody` on a scratch copy of the subject whose emitter... hmm.\n\nLet me think about a minimal close fixture: `plumbline_job.py close` requires `--job-dir` with packet.json, a corpus (`--corpus` or $EDI_CORPUS) with `tools/validate_job_packet.py`, runs `emit_record.py` for each --run, then `plumbline.py --job-close ...`. That's the whole kit; too heavy for a fixture.\n\nBut `plumbline_job.py custody` only runs `emit_custody.py` and then the verifier. A test could:\n- create a temp \"repo\" copy? No — `call()` runs `HERE / script` where HERE is the kit dir of the actual checkout. So `plumbline_job.py custody --job-dir <fixture> --custody <fake checkout>` runs the real `kit/emit_custody.py` on the fixture job. The fixture job needs to be emittable: packet.json with terminal_state accepted, inputs/custody.json with enough facts... The emitter has many requirements; on