th(job).is_dir(): logs += sorted(Path(job).glob(\"*.log\"))\n```\n\nNo .log files → fine.\n\nNow let me finalize the verifier file. Let me rewrite it cleanly.\n\nAlso remove `import math`.\n\nLet me write the full verifier:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Verify a custody/v1 record at two layers: the standard checker, then x-plumbline.\n...\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\nimport custody_history as H  # noqa: E402\n\nSCHEMA_VERSION = \"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"\nSCHEMA_PATH = REPO / \"schemas\" / \"x-plumbline\" / \"x-plumbline-v1.schema.json\"\nSPEND_TOL = 0.0001\nLEDGER_REL = \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\"\nOWNED = (...)\nWRITER_FORM = re.compile(r\"^kit/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.py@[0-9a-f]{12}$\")\n```\n\nDocstring: I must not include \"emit_custody\". Let me phrase: \"This file must not import the record emitter: the emitter's logic is checked by separate code (V7). It may use kit/custody_history.py to parse harness logs.\"\n\nNow, careful: `H.TOLERANCE_S` must exist. It's referenced in the emitter (`H.TOLERANCE_S`), so yes.\n\n`H.parse_ts`, `H.read_log`, `H.Refusals`, `H.iso` used. `hand_time_entries()` on calls. All exist per the emitter usage.\n\nNow, `read_calls` catches exceptions from `H.read_log` broadly — fine.\n\nOne more consideration for R2: does `check_spend` or anything reference \"emit_custody\"? No.\n\nLet me also make sure there's no \"emit_custody\" in the schema file — no.\n\nNow let me also double check `find_pin` — it looks for `\"checker/check.py\" in str(k)` and `_is_pin(v)`, or a dict with path/file containing \"checker/check.py\" and sha256. Our fixture pin is `{\"checker/check.py\": \"<sha>\"}` → `k = \"checker/check.py\"`, v = sha → `vv == sha` → return vv. ✓ For the wrong pin, `vv != sha` (sha is th