ce/G1.json` |\n| G2 | Every test that exists at base passes on the subject with the frozen venv, and its result equals its result at 3df1ce5 when run the same way (base-test isolation). Every new test passes. Each part has at least one new test file (T, F1, I/F7, F8, P, X, V). | S1 | `evidence/G2.json` + both logs |\n| G3 | `docs/custody-emission.md` names every new command, `--allow-hand-times`, the `writer` field, `x-plumbline.hand_times`, `x-plumbline.inputs` and `tools/edi/`. It also explains **the two layers**: the standard layer (custody check.py at CL1, which ignores every `x-` key per SPEC.md line 141) and the Plumbline layer (`kit/plumbline_verify.py`, which runs check.py first and then enforces `x-plumbline`). It says plainly that `x-` keys are enforced by Plumbline only, and it names the verifier's exit codes and failure kinds. `kit/README.md` names `tools/edi/` and `kit/plumbline_verify.py`. | S1 | `evidence/G3.json` |\n\n### G4–G7: the Orchestrator field guide (approval item 30), script checks\n\"The guide\" = `docs/PLUMBLINE-ORCHESTRATOR-FIELD-GUIDE.md` at the subject. Phrase matching works on the normalized text: lower case; `*`, `_`, backtick and backslash removed; curly quotes straightened; en/em dashes become `-`; whitespace collapsed. The exact anchors and the denylist are published in `fg_rules.json` (pinned above).\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G4 | The guide exists at that exact path, is added in the diff (`A`), is non-empty UTF-8, and the whole diff passes G1's allow-list. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | S1 | `evidence/G4.json` |\n| G5 | **Status line.** One of the first 15 lines contains `status`, `non-normative` and `doctrine wins` (the doc is non-normative, and the doctrine wins on conflict). [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | S1 | `evidence/G5.json` |\n| G6 | **Required rules present** (anchored phra