 only hand-time refusals; and no verifier failure is skipped when a field is absent or can be bypassed at close. Answer `CONFORMS` / `DOES_NOT_CONFORM` with cited lines. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | **E-GLM** | `evidence/J1-<call>.json` + harness log + generation reply |\n| J2 | Read as a person would, `docs/custody-emission.md` says the following. Hand times are refused by default. The switch **flags** hand times and never verifies them. A relay is a report, not an approval. Reported times are accepted only through the bounding commands. `x-plumbline` is enforced by Plumbline's verifier only; the standard check.py ignores it. Answer as in J1. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | **E-GLM** | `evidence/J2-<call>.json` + harness log + generation reply |\n| J3 | **G-faithful.** Reading the whole guide (numbered) against the Owner decisions of 2026-10-28 15:52 EDT (the tripwire at exactly 3 of the same failure class, then change the request; the shared key behind the harness pre-call spend guard, with reconciliation an upper bound and no per-job-key recommendation; the cross-family pre-read optional, decided per job on the approval sheet), the item-30 (c) rules, and DOCTRINE.md v0.1 @ `dc61854` (copied verbatim, CC BY 4.0, into the frozen instrument): nothing in the guide contradicts them, and it does not claim to override the doctrine. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | **E-GLM** | `evidence/J3-<call>.json` + harness log + generation reply |\n| J4 | **G-story.** Every rule from item 30 (b) and (c) that the guide states is paired with its real story (a concrete incident from a real job or review, placed with the rule), in field-guide style. A bare reason or a hypothetical is not a story. [the evaluator's held-out controls for this check are omitted from the Maker prompt] | **E-GLM** | `evidence/J4-<call>.json` + harness log + generation reply |\n\n## INTERFACE.md (frozen; how the instrument calls the subject)\n\n```\n# INTERFACE: the command lines, file shapes and exit codes the S1 instrument drives (job 2026-10-28-custody-times-ledger-spend)\n\nSTATUS: FROZEN-BUILD 2026-10-28T20:36:28Z — part of the freeze set; sha256 in ../MANIFEST.sha256. Maker-visible. Referenced from bar.md.\n\nThe bar says WHAT must hold. This file pins HOW S1 calls the subject, so that a check scores the behaviour and not a\nguess about flag names. Anything not named here is the Maker's choice. Where the bar and this file disagree, the\nbar wins and the disagreement is a finding against the bar (filed as an amendment), not a reason to fail a check.\n\"UTC Z\" = `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` (fractional seconds allowed). \"sha12\" = first 12 hex of the sha256 of the file.\n\n## 1. `kit/custody_ledger.py` (T1, F1a–F1h)\nEvery command takes `--job-dir J` (the job folder holding `inputs/custody-events.jsonl` and `inputs/custody.json`).\nBase commands keep their base flags (`freeze`, `approve`, `pin`, `show`, and `dispose --by`).\n\nEvery line any command appends carries `\"writer\": \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<sha12>\"` (sha12 of the file that ran)\nand `\"at\"`: the tool's UTC Z clock at the append. A **refusal** exits non-zero (2 = usage, 3 = refused), prints a\nline starting `REFUSED:` on stderr, and changes neither the ledger nor `custody.json` (byte-identical).\n\n| command | appends one line with (besides `writer`, `at`) | custody.json |\n|---|---|---|\n| `generation open --seat S --prompt FILE` | `event:\"generation\", action:\"open\", seat, n, prompt_file, prompt_sha256` | unchanged |\n| `generation close --seat S --n N [--outcome TEXT] [--fix-kind TEXT]` | `event:\"generation\", action:\"close\", seat, n, outcome, fix_kind` | unchanged |\n| `evaluation --batch B --evaluator ID --verdict FILE [--summary FILE] [--iteration N]` | `event:\"evaluation\", batch, evaluator, verdict_file, verdict_sha256`; with `--summary`: `summary_file, summary_sha256, started_at, finished_at, summary_writer` (copied from the summary's own stamp) | unchanged |\n| `amendment --file F --quote Q --channel C --said-at T` | `event:\"amendment\", file, file_sha256, quote, channel, said_at` | unchanged |\n| `relay --quote Q --from BOT --source-chat C --source-at T` | `event:\"relay\", kind:\"relay\", quote, from, source_chat, source_at` | unchanged |\n| `spend --spend-ledger L --key-reading R` | `event:\"spend\", spend_ledger, spend_ledger_sha256, key_reading, key_reading_sha256, ledger_sum_usd, key_delta_usd, total_usd, read_at, last_settle_at` | unchanged |\n| `dispose --by NAME --state given\\|declined --decided-at T --decided-source S [--words W]` | `event:\"dispose\", by, state, decided_at, decided_source, words` | `disposition.by`, `disposition.at = decided_at` |\n\nFile paths in lines are stored relative to the job dir when they are inside it, else absolute. Bounds (F1b, F1e, F1f,\nF1g) are as the bar states; T equal to a bound is accepted. `generation` numbering is per seat.\n\n## 2. `kit/emit_custody.py` (T2–T7, F1h, X1)\nBase flags unchanged, plus `--allow-hand-times`.\n- **Hand-time refusal** (no switch): exit 3, nothing written, stderr carries the base `REFUSED (history)` header and\n  one line per hand time: `  [hand-time] <field> <file>:<line> (<source>)`.\n- **Field names** (used in the refusal lines, in `hand_times[].field`, and by the verifier):\n  `bar.frozenAt`, `bar.approvals[<i>].at`, `routing.<seat>.declaredAt`, `disposition.at`, `startedAt`,\n  `producedAt`, `passes.<id>.at`, `controls[<id>].at`, `<log file name>#<call or index>.sent_at` and `.received_at`.\n- **Sources**: `ledger-hand` (`writer:\"hand\"`), `ledger-no-writer`, `inputs-no-ledger` (typed into custody.json, no\n  ledger line behind it), `server-header` (a log time taken from the response `Date`), `response-created` (from the\n  response `created`). `<file>:<line>` is the 1-based line that carries the value: the ledger line, the custody.json\n  line (the file is indent-2 JSON, one key per line), or the harness-log line holding the server time used.\n  `<i>` is the 0-based index in `bar.approvals`; `<file>` is relative to the job dir. When a later ledger line\n  sets the same field as an earlier one, the later line's value, line and source are the ones used and reported.\n- A pass or control with no typed `at` gets its time from a tool: a model pass from its `call`'s logger\n  `received_at`; a script pass from the `finished_at` of the `evaluation` line for its batch and evaluator.\n  `startedAt`/`producedAt` with no typed value come from the Maker log's logger times.\n- **`x-plumbline`** (predicate level), keys: `schema` (`\"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"`), `hand_times[]`\n  (`{field, file, line, source}`), `allowances` (`hand_times: {switch:\"--allow-hand-times\", writer:\n  \"kit/emit_custody.py@<sha12>\", at}` only when the switch was given and the set is non-empty), `generations[]`,\n  `evaluations[]`, `relays[]`, `amendments[]` (each the ledger line's fields plus `source:\n  \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl:<line>\"`), `spend` (`calls_sum_usd, key_delta_usd, total_usd, tolerance_usd: 0.0001,\n  source`), `inputs` (a deep copy of `inputs/custody.json`'s `x-plumbline` object, when there is one).\n- The emitter never writes any file under the job dir other than the record it is asked to write (T7).\n\n## 3. `kit/plumbline_verify.py` (V1–V9)\nAs in the bar: `--record R --files F --evidence E --ledger L --custody <checkout> [--json OUT]`; the job's\n`custody.json` is the file `custody.json` beside L. Exits 0/3/4/2: 0 = all checks pass; 3 = the standard check.py\nis not OK (kind `standard`, nothing else is checked); 4 = check.py is OK and any other kind fails; 2 = cannot run\n(usage, a missing input, or a checker whose `check.py` sha256 is not the pin). Each failure is printed as one stdout line\n`FAIL <kind> <field> <file>:<line>`; `--json OUT` writes `{\"exit\": N, \"failures\": [{\"kind\",\"field\",\"file\",\"line\"}]}`.\nKinds: `standard`, `schema`, `allowance`, `hand-time-unflagged`, `flag-without-source`, `events`,\n`relay-as-approval`, `spend`, `shadow`. The spend ledger and key reading are the files named in the ledger's\n`spend` line (relative to the job dir when relative).\n\n## 4. `kit/plumbline_job.py` (V8)\n`close` and `custody` accept `--allow-hand-times` (passed to the emitter) and `--custody <checkout>` (default: env\n`PLUMBLINE_CUSTODY`). Both run `kit/emit_custody.py` and then `kit/plumbline_verify.py` **as subprocesses of those\nfiles** (as base runs the emitter). If the verifier cannot run, close fails with its exit code. The run-log row on\nrefusal is `{\"event\":\"close_refused\",\"kind\":<first failure kind>, ...}`.\n\n## 5. `tools/edi/` (F7a, F8a–F8d, I1, P1)\n**`or_call.py`**: job 1's harness flags (`--seat --log --model --tag --pin-provider | --ledger, --messages --out\n--call --max-tokens --temperature --key-file --base-url`), plus:\n- `--job-spend FILE` (required for every call and for `--init-spend` / `--spend-status`): JSON\n  `{job_id, bound_usd, reserve_usd, spend_ledger, prices: [{model, tag, prompt_usd_per_token,\n  completion_usd_per_token, max_completion_tokens}]}`. Missing or invalid → exit 2, nothing sent.\n- `--init-spend`: writes `key-usage-baseline.json` beside `spend_ledger` (`{job, usage, at, writer}`).\n- `--spend-status --out R`: writes R = `{read_at, writer, job_id, key_usage_usd, baseline_usd, key_delta_usd,\n  ledger_sum_usd, total_usd, last_settle_at}`.\n- Spend-ledger lines are job 1's harness's: `{\"event\": \"reserve\", \"id\", \"at\", \"job\", \"seat\", ..., \"worst_usd\"}` before\n  sending and `{\"event\": \"settle\", \"id\", \"at\", \"call\", ..., \"cost_usd\"}` after (plus `\"over_cap\": true` for exit 9).\n- `--max-cost X`: refused before sending if the worst case > X; over-cap after settle if `total_cost` > X.\n- `--mock-transport DIR`: nothing goes on the network. Replies come from `DIR/key.json`, `DIR/chat.json`,\n  `DIR/generation.json`, each `{\"status\": N, \"headers\": {...}, \"body\": <JSON>}`; every request is appended to\n  `DIR/requests.jsonl` as `{\"method\", \"url\", \"at\"}` (real openrouter.ai URLs; no headers, no key).\n- Exits: job 1's 0/2/3/4/5, plus `6` refused by the job bound (nothing sent, no log entry), `8` refused by\n  `--max-cost` before sending (nothing sent, no log entry), `9` over the cap after settle (logged, settle line\n  `\"over_cap\": true`, no `--out`).\n- Log entries carry every key job 1's harness writes (`harness.name` may say `tools/edi/or_call.py`).\n\n**`fixture_run.py --src DIR --work DIR --summary FILE`**: copies src into work (every copied file `u+rw`, dirs\n`u+rwx`, whatever src's modes), and writes the summary `{started_at, finished_at, writer, files: [{path, sha256,\nmode}]}` (paths relative to work, mode as an octal string). Two runs differ only in `started_at`/`finished_at`.\n\n**`judge_batch.py --items ITEMS.json --batch N --rubric FILE --out DIR --job-spend F --log L --model M (--tag T\n--pin-provider P | --ledger LED) [--mock-transport D]`**: ITEMS.json is a list of `{id, text}`; the order for batch N\nis the list rotated left by `(N-1) mod len`. One `or_call.py` call per item. Writes `DIR/summary.json` `{started_at,\nfinished_at, writer, batch, order: [ids], results: [{id, call, exit, reply_file}]}`.\n\n**`extract_files.py`**: the whole-file reply extractor (job 1's format), with `--check` (verify only) and without it\n(write).\n\nEvery summary-writing instrument stamps `started_at`, `finished_at` (UTC Z, its own clock) and\n`writer: \"tools/edi/<file>@<sha12>\"` (I1).\n\n## 6. Anchors S1's mutation controls rely on (keep these lines' form)\n- `kit/custody_history.py` keeps a module-level line `TOLERANCE_S = 60` (C-T5p1 rewrites it to 600).\n- `kit/emit_custody.py` keeps the \"after the close\" refusal in `check_order` as one line containing both\n  `ref.add(` and the text `is after the job's close` (C-T5p2 disables that line).\n- C-T7p, C-V7p and P-V8 wrap whole files (`kit/emit_custody.py`, `kit/plumbline_verify.py`) and need no anchor.\nA missing anchor makes that control unbuildable, which voids the batch (bar: a control that comes out wrong).\n```\n\n## FILE docs/custody-emission.md (as written by an earlier part or attempt)\n\n````\n# Custody emission runbook — custody/v1 records from Plumbline jobs\n\nFor the Orchestrator. This page covers how to run small real jobs that end `accepted`, `needs_owner` and\n`rejected`, collect one custody/v1 record from each, and pack each record for a stranger. Plumbline makes no\nmodel call on its own: every model call is one you make, through your own harness, or through the kit's product\nharness `tools/edi/or_call.py` (see \"The product harness: `tools/edi/`\").\n\nA record is judged at **two layers**. The **standard layer** is the custody corpus's own `checker/check.py` at\nCL1; per SPEC.md line 141 it ignores every key that begins with `x-`. The **Plumbline layer** is\n`kit/plumbline_verify.py`: it runs `check.py` first, requires OK, and then enforces the `x-plumbline` block the\nemitter writes. `x-plumbline` is enforced by Plumbline's verifier only; the standard check.py ignores it. See\n\"The two layers\" below.\n\n## What a close now writes\n\nA job that closes at a terminal state writes everything it wrote before, unchanged: the §5 records, `passes/`,\nthe packet facts, the run-log row and `inputs/`. It then writes one more file:\n\n    dot-plumbline/jobs/<job-id>/custody/record.custody.json\n\nThat file is an in-toto Statement with predicateType `https://evaluatordriven.com/custody/v1`, following custody\nSPEC.md v0.9.6 at `evaluatordriven/custody@3e3ca58de563`. The predicate holds only section-4 fields. Plumbline's\nown facts sit under `predicate[\"x-plumbline\"]` and the per-check, per-control and per-violation `x-plumbline`\nkeys:\n\n- `schema` (`\"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"`), `verdict` and `terminal_state`.\n- `outcome`.\n- The final §5 record and the packet, each by sha256.\n- Each violation's rule-4 `locator`.\n- `gaps`, `times`, `time_tolerance_s`.\n- `hand_times[]` — every hand time the record carries, each `{field, file, line, source}` — and `allowances`\n  (`hand_times: {switch, writer, at}` only when `--allow-hand-times` was given and the set is not empty).\n- `generations[]`, `evaluations[]`, `relays[]`, `amendments[]` and `spend` — the ledger's own events, each with\n  its `inputs/custody-events.jsonl:<line>` source (see \"Logging events live\").\n- `inputs` — a deep copy of the `x-plumbline` object in `inputs/custody.json`, when there is one. Input data\n  appears only under `x-plumbline.inputs`; it never shadows the emitter's own keys.\n\n`disposition.state` is copied from the packet's `disposition_state`. It never comes from the verdict.\n\n| Exit code | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | Complete. |\n| 1 | Written, with a hard gap named in `x-plumbline.gaps`: a required fact had no source (left null/absent; fix the inputs and re-emit), or an OpenRouter routing request that did not ask for the pin, no fallback and ZDR (`routing.<seat>.request`; the run did it, so re-emitting cannot fix it). |\n| 2 | Refused. There is no packet, or the job is not at a terminal state. Nothing written. |\n| 3 | **Refused: the record would misstate its own history** (see \"Refusals\" below). This includes every hand time when `--allow-hand-times` is not given (`hand-time`). Every such fact is printed as `[kind] …`; nothing is written and an existing record is left as it was. `close` still closes the job and returns 3, with \"CLOSED, BUT THE CUSTODY RECORD IS NOT WRITTEN\". |\n\n`plumbline_job.py close` runs the emitter, then `kit/plumbline_verify.py` on the new record. If the verifier\nfails, close exits with the verifier's code (3 or 4), prints `NOT CLOSED: Plumbline verify failed (<kind>)`,\nwrites a run-log row `close_refused` with the kind, and writes **no** `closed` row; re-running close after a fix\nretries. `plumbline_job.py custody` (re-emit) runs the verifier too and returns its code. Both accept\n`--allow-hand-times` (passed to the emitter) and `--custody <checkout>` (default: env `PLUMBLINE_CUSTODY`).\n\n## The two layers\n\nThe **standard layer** is the custody corpus's `checker/check.py`, run at the claimed level (CL1). It checks the\ncustody/v1 predicate. Per SPEC.md line 141 it **ignores every key that begins with `x-`**, so it never reads\n`x-plumbline` — no matter what the extension says. A record that passes `check.py` has passed the standard layer\nand nothing more.\n\nThe **Plumbline layer** is `kit/plumbline_verify.py`. It runs `check.py` first and requires OK; only then does it\nenforce `x-plumbline`. It never relaxes a check: there is no switch on the command line, and the hand-time\nallowance is read from the record, never supplied by the caller. So **`x-plumbline` is enforced by Plumbline's\nverifier only; the standard check.py ignores it.**\n\n    python3 kit/plumbline_verify.py --record R --files F --evidence E --ledger L --custody <checkout> [--json OUT]\n\nThe job's `custody.json` is the file `custody.json` beside `L` (the ledger, `inputs/custody-events.jsonl`).\n\n| Exit | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | OK at both layers. |\n| 3 | The standard layer failed (kind `standard`; nothing else is checked). |\n| 4 | The standard layer passed and a Plumbline check failed. |\n| 2 | Cannot run: usage, a missing input, or a checker whose `check.py` sha256 is not the pin. |\n\nEach failure prints one stdout line `FAIL <kind> <field> <file>:<line>`, and `--json OUT` writes\n`{\"exit\": N, \"failures\": [{\"kind\",\"field\",\"file\",\"line\"}]}`. The kinds:\n\n| Kind | Enforces |\n|---|---|\n| `standard` | the standard `check.py` is OK (else exit 3, nothing else checked). |\n| `schema` | every `x-plumbline` block validates against `schemas/x-plumbline/x-plumbline-v1.schema.json`, and `x-plumbline.schema` is `plumbline/x-plumbline/v1`. |\n| `allowance` | `allowances.hand_times` is present whenever the hand-time set is non-empty, with the switch, the emitter's `writer`, and its tool-clock `at`. |\n| `hand-time-unflagged` | a hand time the verifier recomputes from the ledger, `inputs/custody.json`, or a server-time log call is missing from `x-plumbline.hand_times[]`. |\n| `flag-without-source` | a flag in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` has no hand line behind it. |\n| `events` | `generations[]`, `evaluations[]`, `relays[]` and `amendments[]` match the ledger one-to-one, each generation has a Maker call between its open and close, and each evaluation's verdict sha256 matches the file. |\n| `relay-as-approval` | a relay is listed among approvals (a relay is a report, not an approval). |\n| `spend` | `x-plumbline.spend` adds up: `calls_sum_usd` equals the sum of the harness logs' per-call `total_cost` within **US$0.0001** (rounding only), `total_usd = max(calls_sum_usd, key_delta_usd)`, and the key reading is stamped and read ≥ 3 min after the last settle. |\n| `shadow` | input data appears only under `x-plumbline.inputs`; every emitter-owned key holds the value the verifier re-derives from the record, ledger and logs. |\n\nA run that changes one of its inputs also fails (`writes`). The verifier never writes its inputs (V7), and it does\nnot import the emitter (V7), so its check is separate code.\n\n## Where each fact about time, endpoint, approver and revision comes from\n\nThe emitter no longer trusts a typed time, a typed host or a typed approver when a log can say otherwise.\n\n| Fact | Source | A hand-entered value is… |\n|---|---|---|\n| `startedAt` | the maker harness log: the earliest call's response `created` (else its `Date` header) | a cross-check: refused if more than **60 s** off |\n| `producedAt` | the maker harness log: the last call's response `Date` header (else `created`) | a cross-check, 60 s |\n| `checks[].at` | the evaluator harness call linked to the pass (`passes.<id>.call`): its `Date` header | a cross-check, 60 s |\n| control times (`controls[].x-plumbline.at`) | the linked evaluator call (`controls[].call`, default `eval_<id>` e.g. `eval_k1`) | a cross-check, 60 s |\n| `model.endpoint` (maker, evaluator), `checks[].endpoint` | a call made straight to a provider: the request URL host in the harness log. A call through OpenRouter (`openrouter.ai`): the upstream host **the Orchestrator declared for that seat** with `custody_ledger.py pin` before the seat's first call, and only when every call's log shows that provider served it (see \"Provider pin and routing request\") | refused if it differs. Never a default, never looked up from a table, never the model vendor's host by assumption |\n| the aggregator, upstream and routing | recorded under `x-plumbline` on the maker and each evaluator: `harness_log`, `calls`, `aggregator` (`openrouter.ai`), `upstream_provider` (as the log names it), `provider_slug`, `endpoint_basis`, and `routing = {pin, requests: [{provider: <what the request body asked>, calls}], request_ok}` | — |\n| `bar.frozenAt`, `approvals[].at`, `disposition.at` | no harness log exists: typed, or better **logged live** with `kit/custody_ledger.py` (below). Each approval records `x-plumbline.time_source` | if a live event log exists, refused when it differs |\n| emitter revision | `git rev-parse HEAD` and `HEAD^{tree}` of the checkout the emitter runs from: `x-plumbline.emitter = {commit, tree, dirty: false, statedRevision, kit_revision}` | refused when dirty, or not the stated revision |\n\n**Tolerance: 60 seconds** (`TOLERANCE_S` in `kit/custody_history.py`). It absorbs a time typed to the minute\n(truncation loses up to 59 s) and ordinary clock skew between the harness host and the provider. It does not absorb\na time typed from memory minutes later, which is what it exists to catch. A hand-entered time may never be later\nthan the emission at all; a log-derived time may be up to 60 s later (server clock skew).\n\n**Harness log format.** One JSON object per model call, a JSON list of them, or JSON Lines. Each call:\n`{\"call\": \"<name>\", \"request\": {\"url\", \"model\", \"messages\", \"provider\": {…}, …}, \"response\": {\"id\", \"created\",\n\"model\", \"provider\"?, \"openrouter_metadata\"?, …}, \"response_headers\": {\"Date\": \"<RFC 7231>\", …},\n\"generation\"?: <the GET /api/v1/generation?id=<response id> reply>}`. The request may instead be logged as\n`\"request\": {\"url\", \"body\": {…}}`. For OpenRouter calls the request **body** must be logged whole, because the\nrouting request is read from it. `call` names are needed only in a log holding several calls.\nEach call's `model` must equal the recorded `identifier`, or end with `/<identifier>` (e.g. `deepseek/deepseek-chat`\nfor `deepseek-chat`).\n\n## Hand times: refused by default, flagged under the switch\n\nA **hand time** is a time whose only source is a ledger line with `writer: \"hand\"` (`ledger-hand`), a ledger line\nwith no `writer` (`ledger-no-writer`), a value typed into `inputs/custody.json` with no ledger line behind it\n(`inputs-no-ledger`), or a server time (a log time taken from the response `Date` header, `server-header`, or from\n`created`, `response-created`) that no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` recorded.\n\n**Hand times are refused by default.** With no switch, the emitter exits 3 with kind `hand-time`, prints one line\nper hand time — `  [hand-time] <field> <file>:<line> (<source>)` — names every hand-time field and its file:line,\nand writes nothing.\n\n**The switch flags hand times and never verifies them.** `--allow-hand-times` does not check the time against a\nlog or a clock. It records each hand time in `x-plumbline.hand_times[]` and, when the set is non-empty, writes\n`x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times = {switch: \"--allow-hand-times\", writer: \"kit/emit_custody.py@<sha12>\", at}`.\nThe listing is not disclosure-only: the verifier fails a record whose flags lack the allowance or disagree with\nthe ledger and logs (`allowance`, `hand-time-unflagged`, `flag-without-source`), and close refuses on that failure\n(V8). The switch silences nothing else — a repo overlay whose log contradicts the hand time still exits 3 with the\nswitch on.\n\n**Reported times are accepted only through the bounding commands.** A time a person reported (the Owner's\ndecision, a relay's source time, an amendment's time) is not a hand time when it is entered through a ledger\ncommand that bounds it and names its source: `dispose --decided-at T --decided-source S` (bounded between the last\nlogged check and the tool's clock), `relay --source-at T` and `amendment --said-at T` (bounded between the freeze\nand the tool's clock). The tool stamps the line and stores the reported time beside it.\n\n**A relay is a report, not an approval.** The emitter never counts a relay as an approval; a buyer approval that\nexists only as a relay is refused as a missing approval (`approval`), and the verifier reports `relay-as-approval`\nif a relay is listed among approvals.\n\nThe field names used in the refusal lines, in `x-plumbline.hand_times[].field`, and by the verifier:\n`bar.frozenAt`, `bar.approvals[<i>].at`, `routing.<seat>.declaredAt`, `disposition.at`, `startedAt`,\n`producedAt`, `passes.<id>.at`, `controls[<id>].at`, `<log file name>#<call or index>.sent_at` and `.received_at`.\nWhen a later ledger line sets the same field as an earlier one, the later line's value, line and source are the\nones used and reported.\n\n## Refusals (exit 3)\n\nEach refusal line starts with its kind. One example of each, from the synthetic fixtures in\n`tests/fixtures/custody/failures/`:\n\n| Kind | Refused when | Example line |\n|---|---|---|\n| `hand-time` | a time's only source is a hand line, a ledger line with no `writer`, a typed value with no ledger line behind it, or a server time no logger recorded | `  [hand-time] disposition.at inputs/custody.json:42 (inputs-no-ledger)` |\n| `time` | a hand-entered time is more than 60 s off its harness call; a model maker/evaluator has no harness log; a pass or control is linked to no call; a log call has no time; a ledger value differs from the live event log | `[time] startedAt: hand-entered 2026-10-20T11:13:00Z but harness log harness-maker-fixture.log#0 puts it at 2026-10-20T11:00:00Z (+780 s; tolerance ±60 s)` |\n| `order` | a seat's provider pin declared after that seat's first call; not frozenAt < startedAt ≤ producedAt ≤ every check; an approval before frozenAt or after startedAt (the maker's first call); the last check after disposition.at; any event other than the disposition after the packet's `close.date`; the bar changed after its logged freeze | `[order] bar.approvals[1].at (specialist) 2026-10-20T11:12:00Z is after startedAt (the maker's first call) 2026-10-20T11:00:00Z` |\n| `after-emit` | any event dated after the emission | `[after-emit] disposition.at 2099-01-01T00:05:00Z is after this record's emission at …: a record cannot report an event that had not happened` |\n| `endpoint` | an aggregator call with no provider pin for its seat; a pin not logged live, or differing from the live log; a call the log does not say who served; a call served by, or also tried at, a provider other than the pin (a fallback); a direct call from a pinned seat; a hand-entered endpoint that differs | see \"Provider pin and routing request\" for the exact lines |\n| `model` | a call ran a model other than the recorded identifier | `[model] evaluator eval-a: harness-eval-a.log#eval_artifact ran model 'example-1', not the recorded identifier 'other-1'` |\n| `approval` | see \"Who may approve\" | `[approval] bar.approvals[1] (specialist) is by 'Fixture Orchestrator (Chief of Staff)', the orchestrating agent. …` |\n| `revision` | the emitter's checkout is dirty, is not a git checkout, or is not the stated revision | `[revision] stated revision deadbeef0 matches neither the emitter's commit 4d6c360c2186 nor its tree ad75d121b1f5` |\n| `harness-log` | a named harness log is unreadable or not JSON | `[harness-log] maker: harness-maker-fixture.log is not a JSON harness log (request/response/response_headers per call), so no time or endpoint can be read from it` |\n\n## Who may approve\n\ncustody approvals are records of who approved, not signatures. The emitter keeps them that way and refuses an\napproval that misstates who approved:\n\n- The ledger must name the orchestrating agent: `\"orchestrator\": {\"name\": \"VizH (Chief of Staff)\", \"kind\": \"agent\", \"aliases\": [\"VizH\"]}`. Without it, every approval is refused.\n- An approval by the orchestrator (name or alias, case-insensitive) is refused, **always**, even marked as an agent.\n- An approval by a model (`kind: \"model\"`, or `by` naming the maker or an evaluator, by name, id or identifier) is refused.\n- `kind` is `person` (default), `agent` or `model`. An `agent` approval counts only with `adopted: {document, version}` set (the agent adopted a published document). A `person` approval whose `by` reads like an agent (agent, bot, assistant, orchestrator, chief of staff, gpt, claude, grok, …) is refused: mark it, or have the person approve.\n- If the packet names a `buyer` or `specialist`, the approval for that role must be by the same party.\n- **A relay is a report, not an approval.** An approval that exists only as a relay is refused as a missing approval; the emitter never promotes a relay to an approver.\n\n## The emitter's revision\n\nThe record names the commit and tree of the checkout the emitter ran from. The emitter refuses (exit 3) when:\n\n- it is not running from a git checkout;\n- the checkout has a tracked change, or an untracked file that is not ignored, **outside `dot-plumbline/` and the\n  job folder being emitted** (both are job state, not code);\n- a stated revision is given (`--expect-revision`, `$PLUMBLINE_EXPECT_REVISION`, or ledger `emitter_revision`) and\n  it is a prefix (≥ 7 hex) of neither the commit nor the tree. **Use the tree**: `git am` re-creates the commit with\n  a new SHA, but the tree is the same bytes.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n| Need | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Python 3.10+ | The emitter, drift check and packer use only the standard library. The test suite needs `jsonschema`, which the venv has. |\n| E-DI corpus at the pin, **for `close` only** | Clone `github.com/smoitozo/e-di` and check out `a48a4645aaa29947fdc17168d26c69c849941580`, then pass `--corpus <that checkout>`. **`/workspace/e-di` is NOT at the pin.** It is a tip snapshot (`f9c6f752…`). Its `schemas/evaluator-record.schema.json` rejects the `passes` key that `kit/emit_record.py` writes, so a **scored** close against it stops at \"the corpus rejected the emitted record\" (observed 2026-10-27 in a /tmp smoke test). A readings close against it did complete. |\n| public doctrine: `github.com/evaluatordriven/doctrine` (DOCTRINE.md v0.1 @ `dc61854`) | For reading alongside the private corpus. The tools and schemas still pin the private corpus; nothing here reads the public doctrine. |\n| custody checkout (optional) | `git clone https://github.com/evaluatordriven/custody && git -C custody checkout 3e3ca58de5631bdc58291564303a2e9d25a8653e`. You need it for `checker/check.py` (the standard layer), `kit/plumbline_verify.py` (the Plumbline layer) and the upstream half of the drift check. |\n| Hermes | **Not needed.** Nothing here reads `~/.hermes`. Every command runs with an empty `HOME`. |\n| Keys | **Only your model keys**, for the maker and the evaluator. Use whatever your harness reads, e.g. the provider API-key environment variable. Plumbline, the emitter and the packer read no key. |\n\n## Models\n\ncustody CL1 needs at least one model evaluator per batch that is not the maker's model:\n\n- `sameModelAsMaker` is computed from the identifiers, and true is a separation gap.\n- A different **family** keeps `separationGaps` empty. The emitter adds an entry automatically when the families match.\n\nA small, cheap setup is enough:\n\n| Seat | Example | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Maker | any model, `kind: \"model\"`, e.g. family `deepseek` | Writes the artifact. Record `{family, identifier, readOnly: false}`; the endpoint comes from its harness log. Save the log as `custody/evidence/harness-maker*.log`. |\n| Evaluator | a different family, e.g. `glm`, read-only | One call per pass and per control, each named in the log (`eval_artifact`, `eval_k1`, `eval_k2`). Save its raw reply as the evidence file, and save the harness log (CL1-15). |\n\nUse `family` lowercase with hyphens and no version (`^[a-z]+(-[a-z]+)*$`). **Endpoint**: call the provider\ndirectly (the request URL host is then the endpoint), or through OpenRouter with the seat **pinned** to one\nupstream provider, declared before the seat starts (next section).\n\n## Provider pin and routing request (OpenRouter)\n\ncustody SPEC section 4: the endpoint is the service that answered, and a router is not it. Through OpenRouter, the\nemitter therefore needs (1) which provider the Orchestrator chose, declared before any call, (2) proof in each\ncall's log that this provider, and no other, served it, and (3) the request having asked OpenRouter for exactly\nthat. The emitter guesses none of these.\n\n**1. Declare the pin** for each seat before the seat's first call (the Maker's pin before the Maker starts;\ndeclare every seat's pin then, so no seat is chosen after seeing output):\n\n```sh\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py pin --job-dir J --seat maker  --provider \"<name as OpenRouter's responses give it>\" \\\n    --slug <provider slug for provider.order> --host <that provider's own API host>\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py pin --job-dir J --seat eval-a --provider \"…\" --slug … --host …\n```\n\nIt writes `routing.<seat> = {via: \"openrouter.ai\", provider, slug, host, declaredAt}` into `inputs/custody.json`\nand a `pin` event into `inputs/custody-events.jsonl`. It refuses (exit 3) once the seat's harness log records a\ncall, and refuses (exit 2) the aggregator's own host as `--host`. `--host` is the host the record will name as\nthe endpoint. It is the Orchestrator's declaration, recorded as such in `endpoint_basis`. The emitter does not\nlook it up.\n\n**2. Who served each call** is read from the log, in this order. All are OpenRouter-documented fields:\n\n| Source in the call's log | OpenRouter documentation |\n|---|---|\n| `response.provider` | the provider name on a sync response. `openapi.json` refers to \"the `provider` field of sync responses\" (BatchObject.provider). It is **not** listed in the ChatResult schema at https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/reference/overview |\n| `response.openrouter_metadata.endpoints.available[selected].provider`, `…attempts[].provider` | opt-in: send header `X-OpenRouter-Metadata: enabled` (https://openrouter.ai/openapi.json, `/chat/completions` parameters; schemas OpenRouterMetadata, RouterAttempt) |\n| `generation.data.provider_name`, `generation.data.provider_responses[]` | `GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/generation?id=<response id>` (https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/generations/get-generation). The harness logs this reply under `generation` |\n\nResponse headers are not read. OpenRouter documents no provider header. A name matches the pin when it equals,\nignoring case and punctuation, the pinned `provider` or the first part of the pinned `slug` (`deepinfra/fp8` →\n`deepinfra`). **Log `generation` or enable `openrouter_metadata`**. These are the only sources that show the\nproviders *tried*, so they are the only way to see a fallback that failed over.\n\n**3. The routing request** is read from each call's request body, `provider` object\n(https://openrouter.ai/docs/features/provider-routing):\n\n| Field | Required value | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `provider.order` | exactly one slug, equal to the pinned `slug` | \"OpenRouter will try them one at a time and proceed to other providers if none are operational\" |\n| `provider.allow_fallbacks` | `false` | default `true`; the doc: \"If you don't want to allow any other providers, you should disable fallbacks as well\" |\n| `provider.zdr` | `true` (preferred), **or** `provider.data_collection: \"deny\"` | `zdr: true` restricts routing to Zero Data Retention endpoints. `data_collection: \"deny\"` only excludes providers that store or train on data, which is weaker. The doc says the request's `zdr` is ORed with the account setting, so it can only turn ZDR on |\n| `models` | absent or a single model | a list of several is a model fallback |\n\n**Refuse or gap: a request that did not ask for this is a HARD GAP (exit 1), not a refusal.** The record is\nwritten, with `x-plumbline.gaps[]` field `routing.<seat>.request` naming what was missing, and\n`x-plumbline.routing.request_ok: false` next to exactly what was asked. Why a gap:\n\n- A refusal (exit 3) in this emitter means the record *would misstate* a fact. Here every fact it writes is still\n  true. The endpoint is backed by the log's served-by check, and the request is recorded verbatim.\n- What is wrong is the run, not the record, and re-emitting cannot fix it. A refusal would withhold the only\n  document that shows a stranger the prompt was not held to one zero-retention provider. A hard gap keeps the\n  record honest and visible, and it still exits non-zero. A missing request body is the same hard gap (\"cannot\n  be read\").\n- What *would* misstate is still refused: a fallback that happened, a served-by the log does not show, or a\n  late pin.\n\nThe exact lines (fixtures `tests/fixtures/custody/failures/pin-*`, `routing-unpinned`):\n\n```\n# no pin declared for a seat that went through OpenRouter (exit 3)\n[endpoint] maker: harness-maker-fixture.log#0 went to the aggregator openrouter.ai and no provider pin was declared for this seat (custody_ledger.py pin, before its first call); the emitter will not guess which host answered (custody SPEC 4: a router is not the service that answered)\n# fallback: another provider served (pin-fallback, exit 3)\n[endpoint] maker: harness-maker-fixture.log#0 was served by 'Together' (response provider), 'Together' (generation provider_name), not the pinned provider 'DeepInfra' (deepinfra/fp8): a fallback to another provider; the record would name api.deepinfra.com for a call it did not answer\n# provider missing from the log (pin-provider-missing, exit 3)\n[endpoint] maker: harness-maker-fixture.log#0 went to openrouter.ai and the log does not say which provider served it (no response `provider`, no `openrouter_metadata`, no logged /api/v1/generation stats); the pin to 'DeepInfra' cannot be confirmed and the emitter will not guess\n# pin after the first call (pin-late, exit 3)\n[order] maker: provider pin declared at '2026-10-20T11:05:00Z', after the seat's first call harness-maker-fixture.log#0 (2026-10-20T11:00:00Z); a pin chosen after the calls is not a pin\n# routing request without one provider / no-fallback / ZDR (routing-unpinned, exit 1, record written)\nGAP  routing.maker.request: harness-maker-fixture.log#0 did not ask OpenRouter for the pin: provider.order is ['deepinfra/fp8', 'together'], not exactly one provider; provider.allow_fallbacks is absent, not false (OpenRouter's default is true: other providers may serve); neither provider.zdr true nor provider.data_collection \"deny\" (zdr absent, data_collection absent). The served provider is still read from the log, but nothing in the request kept the prompt on one zero-retention provider. Re-emitting cannot fix this; the run's own request did it.\n# request body not logged (exit 1): the same gap, reason \"the log does not carry the request body, so the routing request cannot be read\"\n```\n\n**Model slugs** (OpenRouter `GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models`, read 2026-10-27):\n\n| Seat | Model | Slug | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Maker | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 | `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` | canonical `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-20261017`. Not `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash` (the 0910 release) |\n| Evaluator | GLM 5.3 Flash | `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` | canonical `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash-20260826`. Not `z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx` |\n\nRecord `identifier` as the slug. The response `model` must equal it or end with `/<identifier>`. Before choosing\na provider, list the ZDR endpoints per model with `GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/endpoints/zdr` (`provider_name`\nand `tag`). The `tag` is the slug for `provider.order`. The provider's own API host is the Orchestrator's to\nstate. The direct DeepSeek endpoint was **not** in that ZDR list for the Maker model on 2026-10-27.\n\n## The custody inputs: `inputs/custody.json`\n\nWrite this file **as events happen** (freeze, approvals, passes, controls), not afterwards. It lives under\n`inputs/`, so the close walk skips it. Every path is relative to the job folder unless noted. The emitter computes\nevery digest from the files themselves, except approval digests, which you copy from what each approver approved.\n\nA complete synthetic example is at `tests/fixtures/custody/job-rejected/inputs/custody.json`. Its shape:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"custody_inputs\": \"plumbline/custody-inputs/v1\",\n  \"levelClaimed\": \"CL1\",                       // CL2 later: add \"spread\", run >= 2, a second family\n  \"files_dir\": \"custody/files\",                // default; the subject = every file here (or list \"subject\")\n  \"evidence_dir\": \"custody/evidence\",          // default; evaluator replies + harness logs (names relative to it)\n  \"bar\": {\n    \"file\": \"custody/bar.md\",                  // the frozen bar text; bar.digest = sha256(this file)\n    \"frozenAt\": \"…Z\",                          // must be before startedAt\n    \"author\": \"…\", \"publishedAt\": null, \"dissent\": [], \"groundTruth\": [],\n    \"dimensions\": [{\"id\": \"D1\", \"plumbline_dimension\": \"<§5 dimension name>\", \"criterion\": \"…\",\n                    \"scale\": {\"anchors\": {\"1\": \"…\", \"10\": \"…\"}, \"threshold\": 9, \"floor\": 1},\n                    \"failureCondition\": \"…\"}],\n    \"approvals\": [{\"role\": \"buyer\", \"by\": \"Steve Moitozo II\", \"kind\": \"person\", \"barDigest\": \"<hex the Buyer approved>\", \"at\": \"…Z\", \"adopted\": null},\n                  {\"role\": \"specialist\", \"by\": \"<a person, not the orchestrator>\", \"kind\": \"person\", \"barDigest\": \"<hex>\", \"at\": \"…Z\", \"adopted\": null}]\n  },\n  \"orchestrator\": {\"name\": \"…\", \"kind\": \"agent\", \"aliases\": []},   // required: approvals are checked against it\n  \"routing\": {\"maker\": {\"via\": \"openrouter.ai\", \"provider\": \"…\", \"slug\": \"…\", \"host\": \"…\", \"declaredAt\": \"…Z\"}},\n                                               // written by custody_ledger.py pin, one per seat; must match the event log\n  \"maker\": {\"name\": \"…\", \"kind\": \"model\", \"version\": \"…\", \"method_file\": \"custody/method.md\",\n            \"harness_log\": \"harness-maker-….log\",  // default: the one harness-maker*.log in evidence_dir\n            \"model\": {\"family\": \"…\", \"identifier\": \"…\", \"readOnly\": false}},   // endpoint: from the log\n  \"startedAt\": \"…Z\", \"producedAt\": \"…Z\",       // optional cross-checks; the log decides\n  \"instrument\": {\"rubric_file\": \"…\", \"runner_file\": \"…\"},   // optional when the §5 record pins both hashes\n  \"evaluators\": [{\"id\": \"eval-a\", \"name\": \"…\", \"kind\": \"model\",\n                  \"harness_log\": \"harness-eval-….log\",   // default: its CL1-15 external entry's evidence_file\n                  \"model\": {\"family\": \"…\", \"identifier\": \"…\", \"readOnly\": true}}],\n  \"passes\": {\"<pass_id from run.json>\": {\"evaluator\": \"eval-a\", \"run\": 1, \"batch\": \"b1\",\n             \"call\": \"eval_artifact\",          // the harness call this pass is; time and endpoint come from it\n             \"evidence\": {\"D1\": \"<file in evidence_dir>\"}}},\n  \"checks\": [],                                // readings jobs (no §5 record): custody checks directly,\n                                               // with \"evidence_file\" in place of \"evidence\"\n  \"controls\": [{\"id\": \"K1\", \"batch\": \"b1\", \"evaluator\": \"eval-a\", \"call\": \"eval_k1\", \"case_file\": \"…\", \"expected\": \"conforms\", \"outcome\": \"…\",\n                \"evidence_file\": \"…\"},\n               {\"id\": \"K2\", \"batch\": \"b1\", \"evaluator\": \"eval-a\", \"case_file\": \"…\", \"expected\": \"does_not_conform\", \"outcome\": \"…\"}],\n  \"violations\": {\"V1\": {\"dimension\": \"D2\",     // §5 violations name no dimension: say which bar dimension\n                        \"remedy\": {\"text\": \"<verbatim from the evidence>\", \"evidence_file\": \"…\"}}},  // optional\n  \"external\": [{\"requirement\": \"CL1-15\", \"subject\": \"eval-a\", \"evidence_file\": \"<harness log>\", \"readBy\": \"…\"}],\n  \"retention\": {\"location\": \"…\", \"public\": false},\n  \"disposition\": {\"by\": \"Steve Moitozo II\", \"at\": \"…Z\", \"acknowledgesUnobserved\": []},\n  \"verdict\": \"accept\"                          // readings jobs only; scored jobs take it from the §5 record\n}\n```\n\nThe emitter also accepts an optional top-level `\"x-plumbline\"` object here. It is copied **deep-equal** into the\nrecord's `predicate[\"x-plumbline\"].inputs`; it never shadows the emitter's own keys (`verdict`, `gaps`, `times`,\n`hand_times`, `allowances`, `generations`, `evaluations`, `relays`, `amendments`, `spend`, `schema`), which the\nverifier re-derives from the record, ledger and logs.\n\nRules the emitter enforces:\n\n- A scored check's outcome is `score >= threshold` (CL1-17).\n- A pass that is void, or a dimension with no score, becomes `unobserved` with its channel and reason.\n- A remedy is kept only if it appears verbatim in the named evidence file.\n- If no disposition time is recorded, `at` is the emission time, and the record says so (`x-plumbline.disposition_at_source`).\n- Every time, endpoint, approver and revision rule in \"Refusals\" above, including hand times.\n\n## Logging events live: `kit/custody_ledger.py`\n\nFreeze, approval, provider pins, disposition and the batch's own events (generations, evaluations, amendments,\nrelays, spend) have no harness log. Stamp each **at the moment it happens**; the tool writes it into\n`inputs/custody.json` and appends it to `inputs/custody-events.jsonl`, and the emitter then refuses a ledger value\nthat differs from the logged one, and a bar that changed after its logged freeze.\n\nEvery line any command appends carries `writer: \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<sha12>\"` (the sha256 of the file that ran)\nand `at` (the tool's clock), so a reader can tell a tool stamp from a hand-typed one. Every command appends\n**exactly one** line when it succeeds; the earlier lines are never rewritten; a refused call appends nothing and\nexits non-zero (2 = usage, 3 = refused), printing a line starting `REFUSED:` on stderr and leaving the ledger and\n`custody.json` byte-identical.\n\nBase commands:\n\n```sh\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py freeze  --job-dir J --orchestrator \"VizH (Chief of Staff)\" --orchestrator-alias VizH\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py approve --job-dir J --role buyer      --by \"Steve Moitozo II\"\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py approve --job-dir J --role specialist --by \"<the Specialist, a person>\"\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py pin     --job-dir J --seat maker  --provider … --slug … --host …   # before the Maker starts\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py pin     --job-dir J --seat eval-a --provider … --slug … --host …\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py dispose --job-dir J --by \"Steve Moitozo II\" [--state given|declined] \\\n    [--decided-at T --decided-source S] [--words W]\npython3 kit/custody_ledger.py show    --job-dir J\n```\n\n`approve` records the bar file's sha256 at that moment as the digest approved, and refuses the orchestrator, a\nmodel, or an unmarked agent. Both approvals must be stamped **before the maker's first call**.\n\nNew commands (each appends one line, which the emitter reads into `x-plumbline`):\n\n| command | appends | bounds |\n|---|---|---|\n| `generation open --seat S --prompt FILE` | `event:\"generation\", action:\"open\", seat, n, prompt_file, prompt_sha256` | `n` starts at 1 and goes up by 1; a second open while one is open is refused; the prompt's sha256 is computed by the tool |\n| `generation close --seat S --n N [--outcome TEXT] [--fix-kind TEXT]` | `event:\"generation\", action:\"close\", seat, n, outcome, fix_kind` | a close without a matching open (same n, same seat) is refused |\n| `evaluation --batch B --evaluator ID --verdict FILE [--summary FILE] [--iteration N]` | `event:\"evaluation\", batch, evaluator, verdict_file, verdict_sha256`; with `--summary`, also `summary_file, summary_sha256, started_at, finished_at, summary_writer` | the tool computes the verdict's sha256 and refuses a missing file; with `--summary` it takes `started_at`/`finished_at`/`writer` from the instrument's own stamp and refuses a summary with no stamp |\n| `amendment --file F --quote Q --channel C --said-at T` | `event:\"amendment\", file, file_sha256, quote, channel, said_at` | the tool computes the file's sha256; refuses F inside `custody/`; T before the freeze or after the tool's clock is refused; the quote is stored verbatim |\n| `relay --quote Q --from BOT --source-chat C --source-at T` | `event:\"relay\", kind:\"relay\", quote, from, source_chat, source_at` | the quote is stored verbatim and marked relay; T is bounded as in `amendment`; the emitter never counts a relay as an approval |\n| `spend --spend-ledger L --key-reading R` | `event:\"spend\", spend_ledger, spend_ledger_sha256, key_reading, key_reading_sha256, ledger_sum_usd, key_delta_usd, total_usd, read_at, last_settle_at` | refuses a reading R with no `read_at`/`writer` stamp, or one read less than 3 min after the last `settle` line; both files' sha256 go in the line |\n| `dispose --by NAME --state given\\|declined --decided-at T --decided-source S [--words W]` | `event:\"dispose\", by, state, decided_at, decided_source, words`; `custody.json` `disposition.at = decided_at` | T earlier than the last logged check or later than the tool's clock is refused; T equal to the last check is accepted |\n\nThe emitter reads each line into `x-plumbline`: `generations[]`, `evaluations[]`, `relays[]`, `amendments[]` and\n`spend`, each with a `source` of `inputs/custody-events.jsonl:<line>`.\n\n## The product harness: `tools/edi/`\n\nThe kit's own product harness lives under `tools/edi/`. It is standard library only, and every instrument that\nwrites a summary stamps `started_at`, `finished_at` (UTC Z, its own clock) and `writer: \"tools/edi/<file>@<sha12>\"`.\n\n- `tools/edi/or_call.py` — one logged OpenRouter chat call for a seat, in job 1's harness-log shape so\n  `kit/custody_history.read_log` can read it. A job spend file (`--job-spend`) gives the job id, bound, reserve,\n  spend ledger and price snapshot, with no job hard-coded; the call is refused when\n  `total + worst case + reserve >= bound`. `--max-cost X` refuses before sending when the worst case is greater\n  than X, and exits 9 after settle when `total_cost` is greater than X. `--init-spend` writes the key-usage\n  baseline, and `--spend-status --out R` writes the stamped key/ledger reading that `custody_ledger.py spend`\n  records. `--mock-transport DIR` keeps everything off the network for tests. Exit codes: 0 served, 2\n  usage/key/job-spend error, 3 HTTP/transport, 4 pin refusal, 5 no generation reply, 6 bound refusal, 8\n  `--max-cost` refusal before sending, 9 over the cap after settle.\n- `tools/edi/judge_batch.py` — a model-judge batch: one `or_call.py` per item, the order for batch N rotated left\n  by `(N-1) mod len`, with `summary.json` carrying the batch and the `order`.\n- `tools/edi/fixture_run.py` — copies a fixture tree into a working directory, makes every copied file and\n  directory owner-writable whatever the source modes, and writes a summary of paths, sha256 and mode.\n- `tools/edi/extract_files.py` — the whole-file reply extractor, with `--check` (verify only) and without it\n  (write).\n\n## Running the three jobs\n\nFor each job:\n\n1. **Open** the job: `python3 kit/plumbline_job.py open --brief brief.json --job-dir dot-plumbline/jobs/<id> --corpus <e-di@a48a4645>`.\n2. **Freeze** the bar: write `custody/bar.md`, then `custody_ledger.py freeze` at that moment. The Buyer and the Specialist (each a person; never the orchestrator) each approve it, stamped with `custody_ledger.py approve` as they do, before any maker call.\n3. **Pin** (OpenRouter): the Orchestrator chooses one ZDR provider per model from `GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/endpoints/zdr` and declares each seat's pin with `custody_ledger.py pin` **before the Maker starts**. Use the exact model slugs (see \"Provider pin and routing request\"). Every request body carries `\"provider\": {\"order\": [\"<pinned slug>\"], \"allow_fallbacks\": false, \"zdr\": true}`. Log every call in full: the whole request body, the whole response, the `Date` header, and the `/api/v1/generation` reply under `generation`.\n4. **Make**: run the maker model and put the artifact in `custody/files/`. Its run file names the artifact the §5 record hashes. Save the maker's harness log (with its `Date` header and response) as `custody/evidence/harness-maker-<model>.log`. Record the maker block; do not type `startedAt`/`producedAt` (the log decides).\n5. **Evaluate**: per batch, run the evaluator on the artifact and on a clean and a planted control case.\n   - Save each reply into `custody/evidence/`.\n   - Save the harness log, one named call per pass and control (`eval_artifact`, `eval_k1`, `eval_k2`), into `custody/evidence/`.\n   - Fill `passes` and `controls`, each with its `call`; do not type their times.\n   - Write the iteration's `run.json` (kit/emit_record.py's shape) with the scores and verdict.\n   - Log the batch's own events with the ledger: `custody_ledger.py generation open/close` around each Maker\n     generation, `custody_ledger.py evaluation` for each verdict file (with `--summary` when an instrument wrote\n     one), and `custody_ledger.py amendment`/`relay` for anything a person said. `custody_ledger.py spend` after\n     the last settle.\n6. **Close** at the terminal state. This also writes the custody record and runs the verifier:\n\n   ```sh\n   python3 kit/plumbline_job.py close --job-dir dot-plumbline/jobs/<id> --run run-1.json \\\n     --corpus <e-di@a48a4645> --terminal-state <accepted|needs_owner|rejected> --outcome <same> \\\n     [--disposition given|declined] [--allow-hand-times] [--custody <custody checkout>]\n   ```\n\n   | Terminal state | Close flags |\n   |---|---|\n   | `accepted` | verdict `accept`, every dimension at or above threshold, `--terminal-state accepted --outcome accepted`. |\n   | `rejected` | verdict `reject`, at least one `does_not_conform` dimension with a violation and its locator, `--terminal-state rejected --outcome rejected`. |\n   | `needs_owner` | verdict `needs_owner` (e.g. cap reached or a capability gap), `--terminal-state needs_owner --outcome needs_owner --escalation-kind cap_reached`. |\n\n   Across the three records, at least one violation must exist (xlocator).\n\n   `close` runs the emitter, then `kit/plumbline_verify.py` on the new record. If the verifier fails, close exits\n   with the verifier's code (3 or 4), prints `NOT CLOSED: Plumbline verify failed (<kind>)`, writes a run-log row\n   `close_refused` with the kind, and writes no `closed` row; re-running close after a fix retries. `--custody`\n   defaults to `$PLUMBLINE_CUSTODY`. `--allow-hand-times` is passed to the emitter and affects only hand-time\n   refusals.\n\n   Emit from a **clean checkout** of the stated revision, with `PLUMBLINE_EXPECT_REVISION=<tree sha>` set.\n\n7. **Re-emit** without a corpus, any time. `custody` runs the emitter, then the verifier, and returns its code:\n\n   ```sh\n   python3 kit/plumbline_job.py custody --job-dir dot-plumbline/jobs/<id> [--out-dir DIR] \\\n     [--expect-revision <tree>] [--allow-hand-times] [--custody <checkout>]\n   ```\n\n   Then check the record at both layers, if the custody checkout is present:\n\n   ```sh\n   python3 kit/plumbline_verify.py --record dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/record.custody.json \\\n     --files dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/files --evidence dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/evidence \\\n     --ledger dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/inputs/custody-events.jsonl --custody <custody checkout>\n   ```\n\n   The standard layer alone (check.py) is:\n\n   ```sh\n   python3 custody/checker/check.py dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/record.custody.json \\\n     --files dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/files --evidence dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/evidence \\\n     --bar dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/bar.md\n   ```\n\n## Where outputs land\n\n| Output | Path |\n|---|---|\n| Record | `dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/record.custody.json`, or `<out-dir>/<job_id>.custody.json` with `--out-dir`. |\n| Bar, subject, evidence and controls | `dot-plumbline/jobs/<id>/custody/{bar.md, files/, evidence/, controls/}`. These are the paths for `records[]`: `files` = `…/custody/files`, `evidence` = `…/custody/evidence`, `bar` = `…/custody/bar.md`. |\n| Run-log row | Unchanged (`event: closed`); `close_refused` with the kind when the verifier refuses. |\n\n## Packing a stranger bundle\n\n```sh\npython3 tools/pack_stranger_bundle.py --job-dir dot-plumbline/jobs/<id> --out <dir>/<id>.zip\n```\n\nThe zip contains:\n\n| Entry | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `record.custody.json` | The record. |\n| `bar/<bar file>` | The frozen bar. |\n| `files/` | The subject files. |\n| `evidence/` | Every evidence file and harness log. |\n| `context/` | The method, instrument and control files, the §5 record and the packet. |\n| `MANIFEST.sha256` | sha256 manifest, `sha256sum -c` compatible. |\n| `README.txt` | The one check command. |\n\nPacking is deterministic. The command prints the zip's sha256 and the in-zip paths:\n`record.custody.json`, `files`, `evidence`, `bar/<name>`.\n\n## Drift check\n\n```sh\nCUSTODY_DIR=<custody checkout at the pin> python3 tools/build_schemas.py --custody --check --require-upstream\n```\n\n- Exits 1 if the checkout moved (commit, or the sha256 of schema/check.py/SPEC.md), if the vendored `schemas/custody/custody-v1.schema.json` is not the pinned bytes, or if `schemas/custody-record.schema.json` is not exactly what the derivation gives (a hand edit).\n- Exits 2 with no checkout under `--require-upstream`.\n- Re-derive after a deliberate move with `--custody --repin`.\n- `tests/validate_schemas.py` part 3 exercises all of this with no corpus, and every refusal above (synthetic\n  failure fixtures in `tests/fixtures/custody/failures/`; the emitter runs from a throwaway clean commit of the tree).\n````\n\n## FILE kit/README.md (as written by an earlier part or attempt)\n\n````\n# The deployment conformance kit\n\n**What it is.** One entry point that runs the E-DI corpus's own checkers over a deployment's records and tells\nyou, per artifact, whether it is conforming, non-conforming, or **not checkable at all**.\n\n**Why it exists (measured, 2026-10-02).** The first external Plumbline deployment produced a full record — a\nfrozen instrument, four iterations, §5 records, Buyer amendments — that the corpus's own checkers reject: zero\nof four §5 records validated, and the packet was markdown, which the gate cannot parse. Nothing had told that\ndeployment which command to run, against which file, or what the exit code meant. The checkers were never the\nproblem; the reach was.\n\n**What it does not do.** It does not re-implement a single check. Re-implementing would create a second ruler,\nand the corpus's own rule is that *the check that can override the Evaluator is the Evaluator*. It wraps\n`tools/*.py` from a corpus checkout and reports their exit codes. It requires no plugin, no package install and\nno network.\n\n## Run it — a job has two commands\n\n```\n# 1. OPEN: the job folder comes into existence BY its packet. If the brief is refused, the folder is removed.\n$ plumbline_job.py open  --brief brief.json --job-dir dot-plumbline/jobs/<job-id>\n\n# ... the Maker works; the artifact lands in the job folder ...\n\n# 2. CLOSE: a §5 record for every run file, then the close, then the close recorded in the packet.\n$ plumbline_job.py close --job-dir dot-plumbline/jobs/<job-id> --run run-iteration-1.json\n```\n\n`open` and `close` are a job's whole lifecycle, and neither is skippable: there is no folder without a packet,\nand no close on a refused record. A run file is filed under `inputs/` where the close will not judge it as\nterms, and a replaced record goes to `superseded/` where it is named and counted but does not block.\n\nThe tools underneath can also be run alone, when a job already exists:\n\n```\n$ plumbline.py --doctor                              # environment + which enforcement level can run\n$ plumbline.py --corpus ~/edi path/to/job            # a job directory: packet + every record in it\n$ plumbline.py --corpus ~/edi packet.json record.json\n$ emit_packet.py --brief brief.json --out-dir <job>  # terms only\n$ emit_record.py --run run.json --out-dir <job>      # one iteration's §5 record + its filed passes\n```\n\n### What the emitters refuse, rather than warn about\n\nEvery refusal below stops the write. A record that fails the law is worse than no record, because it looks like\none — and a packet the gate cannot read is not a job's terms.\n\n| refusal | rule |\n|---|---|\n| a pass whose scores are not a list of `{dimension, score}` | the checker reads a list; a dict keyed by dimension counts as observing nothing |\n| a filed scored pass with no dimension observed | the pass is the evidence that it happened |\n| a void pass carrying scores | §5: file the cause, not a reading |\n| a violation class outside rule 4's four locators | `artifact_missed_standard` · `standard_moved` · `dimension_unauthorized` · `frame_at_fault` |\n| a pass scoring a dimension the record does not declare | **C35** — evidence not attributable |\n| a declared dimension no filed pass observed | **C35** — zero is not one, and rule 10 labels one |\n| a `regenerate` with no violation | **C36** — an iteration that names nothing it is tasked with is not an iteration |\n| a below-floor dimension with no violation naming it | **C36** — the shortfall is classified into a locator and the violation carries `dimension` |\n| a scored brief with no `k` or `x` | **B.1.2** — both are declared per job, and a bound written after the run is not a bound |\n| a violation naming a dimension the record does not declare | C35's link applied to C36's new field — *this instance's addition* |\n\nCorpus resolution, in order, then it refuses rather than guesses: `--corpus` → `$EDI_CORPUS` →\n`plugins.edi-loop.corpus` in `~/.hermes/config.yaml`.\n\n## Two layers, and the product harness\n\nA custody record is judged at **two layers**. The **standard layer** is the custody corpus's own\n`checker/check.py` at CL1; per SPEC.md line 141 it **ignores every `x-` key**, so it never reads `x-plumbline`.\nThe **Plumbline layer** is `kit/plumbline_verify.py`: it runs `check.py` first, requires OK, and then enforces\nthe `x-plumbline` block the emitter writes — hand times and their allowance, events against the ledger and logs,\nspend, and the no-shadow rule. `x-plumbline` is enforced by Plumbline only. The verifier exits `0` (OK at both\nlayers), `3` (the standard layer failed), `4` (the Plumbline layer failed) or `2` (cannot run); every failure\nprints `FAIL <kind> <field> <file>:<line>`. `plumbline_job.py close` and `custody` run it and refuse on failure.\n\nThe model calls are made by the product harness under `tools/edi/`: `or_call.py` (one logged call, with the\npre-call spend guard and `--max-cost`), `judge_batch.py` (a rotated model-judge batch), `fixture_run.py` (a\nmode-normalizing fixture runner) and `extract_files.py` (the whole-file reply extractor). `custody_ledger.py\nspend` records the reading `or_call.py --spend-status` writes. Every summary-writing instrument stamps its own\n`started_at`, `finished_at` and `writer`.\n\n## Adopting this in your own program\n\nThe kit is the part that travels. These four things are what a deployment installs, and one it should not.\n\n**1. The corpus's skill — take it.** `skills/evaluator-driven-iteration/` in the corpus (`~/…/edi/`), copied\ninto `~/.hermes/skills/`. That is where the doctrine's procedure lives, and it is canonical — do not write your\nown version of it.\n\n**2. The corpus's plugin `edi-loop` — take it if your program runs on Hermes.** Canonical copy:\n`integrations/hermes-edi-loop/` in the corpus (proposals 0023, mirrored under 0034). Copy it into\n`~/.hermes/plugins/edi-loop/`, give it the corpus path (`$EDI_CORPUS`, or `plugins.edi-loop.corpus` in\n`~/.hermes/config.yaml`), and **restart the gateway — there is no hot reload.** A file swap without a restart\nleaves the old code live while disk reads new.\n\nIt registers four tools (`edi_validate_job_packet`, `edi_check_terminal_state`, `edi_check_role_separation`,\n`edi_check_best_artifact_handoff`) and it **shells out to the corpus's own checkers at call time, pinning no\ncorpus version** — so it is not a second ruler. The same check the kit runs at open and close is the check it\nruns in flight; the difference is only when it can be called.\n\n**3. Two traps, both measured on this repo rather than read about:**\n\n- **Never park a plugin backup inside `~/.hermes/plugins/`.** A sibling directory carrying a `plugin.yaml`\n  **is** a plugin: discovery loads it, and a same-name duplicate can quietly win the registration — so every\n  disk check says the new code is installed while the old code answers. Back up to `~/.hermes/backups/`.\n- **After any install, assert exactly one directory declares the name:**\n  `grep -l '^name: <plugin>' ~/.hermes/plugins/*/plugin.yaml`. One line, and it is the difference between\n  debugging the fix and debugging the ghost of the fix.\n\n**4. This repo's own skill (`kit/skill/plumbline/`) — generate yours instead of copying it.** It names *this*\nrepo's path and tree, so it is wrong in yours. Write your own from the two commands above: two hand-written\ncommand sets is the drift trap this kit exists to measure.\n\n**And one thing not to take: `plumbline-gate`.** The discoverability gate is instance machinery built for this\ndirection's design consequence (§8 leaves that to each deployment) — not a doctrine requirement. If your program\nwants one, build it for your program, and keep it **job-scoped**: ours governs every session on the machine\nwhile armed, which is a declared defect of it, not a feature to copy.\n\n## The three verdicts\n\n| verdict | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `OK` | the corpus checker ran and passed |\n| `FAILED` | the corpus checker ran and rejected the artifact |\n| `NOT-CHECKABLE` | no checker applies, or the artifact is in a shape no checker can read |\n\n**Not-checkable is not a pass.** A record no checker can read is a finding. Exit code is 1 when anything\nfailed or nothing could be checked, so a pipeline cannot mistake silence for success.\n\n## A weak OK is not a verdict\n\n`validate_job_packet.py` runs a stdlib structural check always, and the Draft 2020-12 schema pass only when\n`jsonschema` is importable — \"a packet must pass both\", by its own docstring. Both used to print the same word\n`OK`. Measured on one packet with one invalid value: `OK`, exit 0 under python 3.9 without jsonschema;\n`FAILED`, exit 1 under python 3.11 with it. Since proposal 0049 the tools name the level\n(`OK (schema-verified)` / `OK (structural only)`), and **this kit refuses to certify on the structural-only\npath** — it marks those rows `OK*` and exits 1.\n\n## What has been demonstrated\n\n- **Planted defects:** 8 cases, two controls (a readings packet and a scored one), each mutation a defect the\n  doctrine names — `ratified: false` reaching `accepted`, `evaluator: \"Owner\"`, blank `escalation`, bounds on a\n  readings job, Maker identity equal to Evaluator identity, and a markdown packet that must read\n  NOT-CHECKABLE. `python3 cases/run_cases.py <corpus>` → 8/8. The first draft of that runner reported 7/7 while\n  its control was failing, because its assertion was a substring match; the control caught it.\n- **A real deployment:** against the first external deployment's job directory, the kit reports\n  `0 ok · 8 failed · 7 not-checkable`, reproducing that audit's structural findings mechanically.\n\n## Scope limits\n\nNo doctrine change. No corpus edit — if one is owed, it is a proposal, not a quiet edit. Transport is git and\ncorpus resolution follows the existing rule, so a machine on a different cloud is not excluded. Publication and\nverification belong inside this kit rather than after it: a checker that cannot reach the record certifies\nnothing.\n````\n\n## FILE tools/edi/README.md (new in this iteration)\n\n````\n# tools/edi\n\nProduct-harness helpers for E-DI jobs.  They are ordinary command-line tools:\nstandard library only, no network except `or_call.py`, and every instrument that\nwrites a summary stamps `started_at`, `finished_at` (UTC Z, its own clock) and\n`writer: \"tools/edi/<file>@<sha12>\"`.\n\n## `or_call.py`\n\nOne logged OpenRouter chat call for a seat.  It keeps the job-1 harness log shape\n(`call`, `seat`, `request`, `sent_at`, `response_status`, `response_headers`,\n`response`, `received_at`, `generation`, `generation_status`,\n`generation_fetched_at`, `harness`, `verdict`), so `kit/custody_history.read_log`\ncan read it.\n\nRequired job spend file for calls, `--init-spend` and `--spend-status`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"job_id\": \"job-id\",\n  \"bound_usd\": 2.0,\n  \"reserve_usd\": 0.05,\n  \"spend_ledger\": \"/path/to/spend-ledger.jsonl\",\n  \"prices\": [\n    {\"model\": \"model\", \"tag\": \"provider/fp8\",\n     \"prompt_usd_per_token\": 0.0000001,\n     \"completion_usd_per_token\": 0.0000003,\n     \"max_completion_tokens\": 131072}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe job total is `max(spend-ledger sum, key-usage delta)`.  It is read with a\nfree `GET /api/v1/key` before every call, and the call is refused when\n`total + worst case + reserve >= bound`.  `max_tokens` is always the endpoint\nmaximum; a different `--max-tokens` is refused.  There is no throttling and no\nreasoning-limit parameter.\n\nUseful flags:\n\n- `--init-spend`: write `key-usage-baseline.json` beside the spend ledger once.\n- `--spend-status --out R`: write the stamped key/ledger reading.\n- `--max-cost X`: refuse before sending when the worst case is greater than X;\n  if the settled cost is greater than X, exit 9, mark the settle line\n  `over_cap`, and write no reply.\n- `--mock-transport DIR`: no network.  Replies come from `DIR/key.json`,\n  `DIR/chat.json` and `DIR/generation.json`; requests are recorded in\n  `DIR/requests.jsonl` with no headers or key material.\n\nExit codes: 0 logged and served by the pin; 2 usage/key/job-spend error;\n3 HTTP or transport error; 4 provider-pin refusal; 5 no generation reply;\n6 job-spend bound refusal; 8 `--max-cost` refusal before sending; 9 over the cap\nafter settle.\n\n## `judge_batch.py`\n\nRuns one `or_call.py` per item in a rotated order.  The order for batch N is the\nitem list rotated left by `(N-1) mod len`.  It writes `DIR/summary.json` with\n`started_at`, `finished_at`, `writer`, `batch`, `order` (ids) and `results`\n(`{id, call, exit, reply_file}`).\n\n## `fixture_run.py`\n\nCopies a fixture tree into a working directory and makes every copied file\nowner-writable and every copied directory owner-writable and searchable, even\nwhen the source is read-only.  It writes a summary with `started_at`,\n`finished_at`, `writer` and `files` (`{path, sha256, mode}`).  Two runs from the\nsame contents differ only in the two timestamps.\n\n## `extract_files.py`\n\nThe whole-file reply extractor.  `extract_files.py REPLY.txt TARGET_DIR` writes\nthe blocks; `--check` validates only; `--list OUT.txt` records the written paths.\nIt validates every block before writing anything and never normalizes file\nbytes.\n````\n\n## CONTEXT (read only; not in this part) kit/custody_ledger.py\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Log a job's custody events WHEN THEY HAPPEN, so no time in the custody record is typed from memory.\n\nThe emitter (kit/emit_custody.py) reads model-call times from harness logs. Three events have no harness log:\nthe bar's freeze, each approval of the bar, and the Owner's disposition. This tool stamps each with the clock at\nthe moment it is run, writes it into inputs/custody.json, and appends it to inputs/custody-events.jsonl. The\nemitter then refuses a ledger value that differs from the logged one, and refuses the bar if it changed after the\nfreeze. Run it at the moment the thing happens, not afterwards: a late stamp is a wrong time.\n\nEvery line this tool appends carries `writer: \"kit/custody_ledger.py@<sha12>\"` (the sha256 of the file that ran)\nand `at` (the tool's clock), so a reader can tell a tool stamp from a hand-typed one (T1).\n\n    custody_ledger.py freeze  --job-dir J [--bar custody/bar.md] [--orchestrator \"Agent name\" [--orchestrator-alias A]]\n    custody_ledger.py approve --job-dir J --role buyer|specialist --by \"Name\" [--kind person|agent]\n                              [--adopted-document D --adopted-version V]\n    custody_ledger.py dispose --job-dir J --by \"Name\" [--state given|declined]\n                              [--decided-at T --decided-source S] [--words W]\n    custody_ledger.py pin     --job-dir J --seat maker|<evaluator id> --provider \"DeepInfra\" --slug deepinfra/fp8\n                              --host api.deepinfra.com [--via openrouter.ai]\n    custody_ledger.py show    --job-dir J\n\n    custody_ledger.py generation open  --job-dir J --seat S --prompt FILE\n    custody_ledger.py generation close --job-dir J --seat S --n N [--outcome TEXT] [--fix-kind TEXT]\n    custody_ledger.py evaluation --job-dir J --batch B --evaluator ID [--verdict FILE] [--summary FILE] [--iteration N]\n    custody_ledger.py amendment  --job-dir J --file F --quote Q --channel C --said-at T\n    custody_ledger.py relay      --job-dir J --quote Q --from BOT --source-chat C --source-at T\n    custody_ledger.py spend      --job-dir J --spend-ledger L --key-reading R\n\n`approve` records the digest of the bar file AT THAT MOMENT as the digest approved. It records who approved; it\nis not a signature (custody: approvals are records). An approval by the orchestrating agent or a model is refused\nhere as it is by the emitter.\n\n`pin` declares, BEFORE the seat's first model call, which single upstream provider will serve that seat through\nthe aggregator: the provider's name as OpenRouter's responses give it (`provider`), the slug the request's\nprovider.order will carry (`slug`), and the provider's own API host (`host`), which becomes the custody endpoint.\nIt is refused once the seat's harness log records a call. The emitter refuses the record if any call was served\nby, or also tried at, another provider, if the log does not say who served a call, or if the pin was declared\nafter the first call.\n\n`generation`, `evaluation`, `amendment`, `relay` and `spend` record the batch's own events as they happen, so the\nemitter can carry them into `x-plumbline.generations[]`, `evaluations[]`, `amendments[]`, `relays[]` and `spend`\n(F1a-F1h). `dispose --decided-at` bounds the Owner's decision between the last logged check and the tool's clock\n(F1b). `evaluation` takes `--verdict FILE`; when `--verdict` is omitted the `--summary FILE` (which must carry the\ninstrument's own `started_at`/`finished_at`/`writer` stamp) also serves as the verdict file. Every refusal,\nusage errors included, exits non-zero (2 = usage, 3 = refused), prints a line starting `REFUSED:` on stderr, and\nchanges neither the ledger nor `custody.json`. Stdlib only.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse, json, sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport custody_history as H          # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef now() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef writer_stamp() -> str:\n    \"\"\"`kit/custody_ledger.py@<sha12>` for the file that is running (T1).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        d = sha256(Path(__file__).resolve().read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n    except OSError:\n        d = \"0\" * 12\n    return f\"kit/custody_ledger.py@{d}\"\n\n\ndef relpath(job: Path, p: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"A path relative to the job dir when inside it, else absolute (INTERFACE section 1).\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return p.resolve().relative_to(job.resolve()).as_posix()\n    except ValueError:\n        return str(p.resolve())\n\n\ndef read_events(job: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    if not p.is_file():\n        return []\n    out = []\n    for line in p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        if line.strip():\n            try:\n                ev = json.loads(line)\n            except ValueError:\n                continue\n            if isinstance(ev, dict):\n                out.append(ev)\n    return out\n\n\ndef seat_logs(job: Path, ci: dict, seat: str) -> list[Path]:\n    \"\"\"Harness logs that may already hold this seat's calls (named in the inputs, or by the usual file names).\"\"\"\n    ev = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")\n    if seat == \"maker\":\n        named, pat = (ci.get(\"maker\") or {}).get(\"harness_log\"), \"harness-maker*.log\"\n    else:\n        e = next((x for x in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or [] if str(x.get(\"id\")) == seat), {})\n        named = e.get(\"harness_log\") or next((x.get(\"evidence_file\") for x in ci.get(\"external\") or []\n                                              if x.get(\"subject\") == seat), None)\n        pat = f\"harness-{seat}*.log\"\n    out = [b / named for b in (ev, job) if named and (b / named).is_file()]\n    out += sorted(ev.glob(pat)) if ev.is_dir() else []\n    return list(dict.fromkeys(out))\n\n\ndef last_check_time(job: Path, ci: dict) -> datetime | None:\n    \"\"\"The latest logged check: evaluator `received_at`, `evaluation` line times, instrument `finished_at` (F1b).\"\"\"\n    times = []\n    for ev in read_events(job):\n        if ev.get(\"event\") == \"evaluation\":\n            for k in (\"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"at\"):\n                d = H.parse_ts(ev.get(k))\n                if d:\n                    times.append(d)\n            sf = ev.get(\"summary_file\")\n            if sf:\n                p = Path(sf)\n                if not p.is_absolute():\n                    p = job / p\n                if p.is_file():\n                    try:\n                        s = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n                        d = H.parse_ts(s.get(\"finished_at\"))\n                        if d:\n                            times.append(d)\n                    except (ValueError, OSError):\n                        pass\n    for e in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or []:\n        seat = str(e.get(\"id\"))\n        for log in seat_logs(job, ci, seat):\n            ref = H.Refusals()\n            for c in H.read_log(log, ref, seat):\n                if c.received:\n                    times.append(c.received)\n    evdir = job / ci.get(\"evidence_dir\", \"custody/evidence\")\n    if evdir.is_dir():\n        for p in evdir.rglob(\"*.json\"):\n            try:\n                s = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            except (ValueError, OSError):\n                continue\n            if isinstance(s, dict) and str(s.get(\"writer\", \"\")).startswith(\"tools/edi/\"):\n                d = H.parse_ts(s.get(\"finished_at\"))\n                if d:\n                    times.append(d)\n    return max(times) if times else None\n\n\ndef append_event(job: Path, ev: dict) -> None:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with p.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        fh.write(json.dumps(ev, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef write_custody(job: Path, ci: dict) -> None:\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\"\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    p.write_text(json.dumps(ci, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef refuse(msg: str, code: int = 3) -> int:\n    print(f\"REFUSED: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    return code\n\n\nclass RefusingParser(argparse.ArgumentParser):\n    \"\"\"argparse's own usage errors exit 2 with a `REFUSED:` line, like every other refusal (F1a, INTERFACE 1).\"\"\"\n\n    def error(self, message):\n        self.print_usage(sys.stderr)\n        print(f\"REFUSED: {message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        raise SystemExit(2)\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    ap = RefusingParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\n    for n in (\"freeze\", \"approve\", \"dispose\", \"pin\", \"show\"):\n        s = sub.add_parser(n)\n        s.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n        if n == \"freeze\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--bar\", default=None, help=\"bar file, relative to the job (default: the ledger's, else custody/bar.md)\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--orchestrator\", help=\"the orchestrating agent's name, as approvals would name it\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--orchestrator-alias\", action=\"append\", default=[])\n        if n in (\"approve\", \"dispose\"):\n            s.add_argument(\"--by\", required=True)\n        if n == \"pin\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--seat\", required=True, help=\"maker, or an evaluator's id\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--provider\", required=True, help=\"provider name as OpenRouter's response `provider` gives it\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--slug\", required=True, help=\"the provider slug the requests' provider.order carries\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--host\", required=True, help=\"the provider's own API host (the custody endpoint)\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--via\", default=\"openrouter.ai\")\n        if n == \"approve\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--role\", required=True, choices=(\"buyer\", \"specialist\"))\n            s.add_argument(\"--kind\", default=\"person\", choices=(\"person\", \"agent\"))\n            s.add_argument(\"--adopted-document\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--adopted-version\")\n        if n == \"dispose\":\n            s.add_argument(\"--state\", choices=(\"given\", \"declined\"))\n            s.add_argument(\"--decided-at\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--decided-source\")\n            s.add_argument(\"--words\")\n\n    g = sub.add_parser(\"generation\")\n    g.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"open\", \"close\"))\n    g.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    g.add_argument(\"--seat\", required=True)\n    g.add_argument(\"--prompt\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int)\n    g.add_argument(\"--outcome\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--fix-kind\")\n\n    ev = sub.add_parser(\"evaluation\")\n    ev.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    ev.add_argument(\"--batch\", required=True)\n    ev.add_argument(\"--evaluator\", required=True)\n    ev.add_argument(\"--verdict\", help=\"the verdict file; may be omitted when --summary is given \"\n                                      \"(the summary is then also the verdict)\")\n    ev.add_argument(\"--summary\")\n    ev.add_argument(\"--iteration\")\n\n    am = sub.add_parser(\"amendment\")\n    am.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--file\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--quote\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--channel\", required=True)\n    am.add_argument(\"--said-at\", required=True)\n\n    rl = sub.add_parser(\"relay\")\n    rl.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--quote\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--from\", dest=\"from_\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--source-chat\", required=True)\n    rl.add_argument(\"--source-at\", required=True)\n\n    sp = sub.add_parser(\"spend\")\n    sp.add_argument(\"--job-dir\", required=True)\n    sp.add_argument(\"--spend-ledger\", required=True)\n    sp.add_argument(\"--key-reading\", required=True)\n\n    a = ap.parse_args(argv)\n    job = Path(a.job_dir).expanduser().resolve()\n    ledger_p, events_p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\", job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\n    try:\n        ci = (json.loads(ledger_p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if ledger_p.is_file()\n              else {\"custody_inputs\": \"plumbline/custody-inputs/v1\"})\n    except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n        return refuse(f\"cannot read {ledger_p} ({exc})\", 2)\n    if not isinstance(ci, dict):\n        return refuse(f\"{ledger_p} does not hold a JSON object\", 2)\n    if a.cmd == \"show\":\n        print(events_p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") if events_p.is_file() else \"(no events logged)\", end=\"\")\n        return 0\n\n    bar = ci.setdefault(\"bar\", {})\n    t = now()\n    ci_changed = a.cmd in (\"freeze\", \"approve\", \"pin\", \"dispose\")\n\n    if a.cmd == \"freeze\":\n        rel = a.bar or bar.get(\"file\") or \"custody/bar.md\"\n        if not (job / rel).is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no bar file at {job / rel}\", 2)\n        if bar.get(\"frozenAt\"):\n            return refuse(f\"the bar was already frozen at {bar['frozenAt']}; a bar is frozen once\", 2)\n        d = sha256((job / rel).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n        bar.update({\"file\": rel, \"frozenAt\": t})\n        if a.orchestrator:\n            ci[\"orchestrator\"] = {\"name\": a.orchestrator, \"kind\": \"agent\", \"aliases\": a.orchestrator_alias}\n        ev = {\"event\": \"freeze\", \"at\": t, \"bar_file\": rel, \"bar_sha256\": d}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"approve\":\n        if not bar.get(\"frozenAt\") or not (job / str(bar.get(\"file\"))).is_file():\n            return refuse(\"freeze the bar first (custody_ledger.py freeze); an approval names a frozen bar\", 2)\n        adopted = None\n        if a.adopted_document or a.adopted_version:\n            adopted = {\"document\": a.adopted_document, \"version\": a.adopted_version}\n        appr = {\"role\": a.role, \"by\": a.by, \"kind\": a.kind,\n                \"barDigest\": sha256((job / bar[\"file\"]).read_bytes()).hexdigest(), \"at\": t, \"adopted\": adopted}\n        ref = H.Refusals()\n        pk = job / \"packet.json\"\n        H.check_approval(appr, 0, ci, json.loads(pk.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if pk.is_file() else {}, ref)\n        if ref:\n            for _, m in ref.rows:\n                print(f\"REFUSED: {m}\")\n            return 3\n        bar[\"approvals\"] = [x for x in bar.get(\"approvals\") or [] if x.get(\"role\") != a.role] + [appr]\n        ev = {\"event\": \"approve\", **{k: appr[k] for k in (\"role\", \"by\", \"kind\", \"at\", \"barDigest\", \"adopted\")}}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"pin\":\n        host, via = a.host.strip().lower(), a.via.strip().lower()\n        if not H.HOST.match(host) or host in H.AGGREGATORS:\n            return refuse(f\"{a.host!r} is not an upstream provider's host name (the aggregator is --via)\", 2)\n        if via not in H.AGGREGATORS:\n            return refuse(f\"--via {a.via!r} is not a known aggregator ({', '.join(sorted(H.AGGREGATORS))}); \"\n                          f\"a call made straight to a provider needs no pin\", 2)\n        for log in seat_logs(job, ci, a.seat):\n            calls = H.read_log(log, H.Refusals(), a.seat)\n            if calls:\n                return refuse(f\"{log.name} already records {len(calls)} call(s) for {a.seat}; a pin declared \"\n                              f\"after the seat's first call is not a pin. Declare it before the seat starts.\", 3)\n        pin = {\"via\": via, \"provider\": a.provider, \"slug\": a.slug, \"host\": host, \"declaredAt\": t}\n        ci.setdefault(\"routing\", {})[a.seat] = pin\n        ev = {\"event\": \"pin\", \"seat\": a.seat, **{k: pin[k] for k in (\"via\", \"provider\", \"slug\", \"host\")}, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"dispose\":\n        if a.decided_at:\n            dt = H.parse_ts(a.decided_at)\n            if dt is None:\n                return refuse(f\"--decided-at {a.decided_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n            if not a.decided_source:\n                return refuse(\"--decided-at requires --decided-source\", 2)\n            last = last_check_time(job, ci)\n            if last and dt < last:\n                return refuse(f\"decided_at {a.decided_at} is before the last logged check at {H.iso(last)}\", 3)\n            if dt > H.parse_ts(t):\n                return refuse(f\"decided_at {a.decided_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n            decided_at = a.decided_at\n        else:\n            decided_at = t\n        disp = {**(ci.get(\"disposition\") or {}), \"by\": a.by, \"at\": decided_at}\n        if a.state:\n            disp[\"state\"] = a.state\n        if a.words:\n            disp[\"words\"] = a.words\n        ci[\"disposition\"] = disp\n        ev = {\"event\": \"dispose\", \"by\": a.by, \"at\": t}\n        if a.decided_at:\n            ev.update({\"decided_at\": a.decided_at, \"decided_source\": a.decided_source})\n        if a.state:\n            ev[\"state\"] = a.state\n        if a.words:\n            ev[\"words\"] = a.words\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"generation\":\n        events = read_events(job)\n        seat_events = [x for x in events if x.get(\"event\") == \"generation\" and x.get(\"seat\") == a.seat]\n        opens = {}\n        last_action = None\n        for x in seat_events:\n            n = x.get(\"n\")\n            if x.get(\"action\") == \"open\":\n                opens[n] = False\n                last_action = (\"open\", n)\n            elif x.get(\"action\") == \"close\":\n                if n in opens:\n                    opens[n] = True\n                last_action = (\"close\", n)\n        if a.action == \"open\":\n            if not a.prompt:\n                return refuse(\"generation open requires --prompt FILE\", 2)\n            if last_action and last_action[0] == \"open\":\n                return refuse(f\"generation {last_action[1]} for {a.seat} is still open; close it first\", 3)\n            n = max(opens) + 1 if opens else 1\n            p = Path(a.prompt)\n            if not p.is_absolute():\n                p = job / p\n            if not p.is_file():\n                return refuse(f\"no prompt file at {p}\", 2)\n            d = sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n            ev = {\"event\": \"generation\", \"action\": \"open\", \"seat\": a.seat, \"n\": n,\n                  \"prompt_file\": relpath(job, p), \"prompt_sha256\": d, \"at\": t}\n        else:\n            if a.n is None:\n                return refuse(\"generation close requires --n N\", 2)\n            if a.n not in opens:\n                return refuse(f\"no open generation {a.n} for {a.seat}\", 3)\n            if opens[a.n]:\n                return refuse(f\"generation {a.n} for {a.seat} is already closed\", 3)\n            ev = {\"event\": \"generation\", \"action\": \"close\", \"seat\": a.seat, \"n\": a.n,\n                  \"outcome\": a.outcome, \"fix_kind\": a.fix_kind, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"evaluation\":\n        target = a.verdict or a.summary\n        if not target:\n            return refuse(\"evaluation requires --verdict FILE (or --summary FILE to serve as the verdict)\", 2)\n        p = Path(target)\n        if not p.is_absolute():\n            p = job / p\n        if not p.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no {'verdict' if a.verdict else 'summary'} file at {p}\", 2)\n        vsha = sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n        ev = {\"event\": \"evaluation\", \"batch\": a.batch, \"evaluator\": a.evaluator,\n              \"verdict_file\": relpath(job, p), \"verdict_sha256\": vsha, \"at\": t}\n        if a.iteration is not None:\n            ev[\"iteration\"] = a.iteration\n        if a.summary:\n            sp = Path(a.summary)\n            if not sp.is_absolute():\n                sp = job / sp\n            if not sp.is_file():\n                return refuse(f\"no summary file at {sp}\", 2)\n            try:\n                s = json.loads(sp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n                return refuse(f\"summary {sp} is not JSON ({exc})\", 2)\n            for k in (\"started_at\", \"finished_at\", \"writer\"):\n                if not s.get(k):\n                    return refuse(f\"summary {sp} has no {k} stamp; an instrument summary must stamp itself\", 3)\n            ev.update({\"summary_file\": relpath(job, sp), \"summary_sha256\": sha256(sp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n                       \"started_at\": s[\"started_at\"], \"finished_at\": s[\"finished_at\"],\n                       \"summary_writer\": s[\"writer\"]})\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"amendment\":\n        p = Path(a.file)\n        if not p.is_absolute():\n            p = job / p\n        if not p.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no amendment file at {p}\", 2)\n        custody_dir = (job / \"custody\").resolve()\n        try:\n            p.resolve().relative_to(custody_dir)\n            return refuse(f\"amendment file {p} is inside custody/; amendments go beside the frozen set\", 3)\n        except ValueError:\n            pass\n        said = H.parse_ts(a.said_at)\n        if said is None:\n            return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n        frozen = H.parse_ts((ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"frozenAt\"))\n        if frozen and said < frozen:\n            return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at} is before the freeze at {ci['bar']['frozenAt']}\", 3)\n        if said > H.parse_ts(t):\n            return refuse(f\"--said-at {a.said_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n        ev = {\"event\": \"amendment\", \"file\": relpath(job, p), \"file_sha256\": sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"quote\": a.quote, \"channel\": a.channel, \"said_at\": a.said_at, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"relay\":\n        said = H.parse_ts(a.source_at)\n        if said is None:\n            return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC (...Z)\", 2)\n        frozen = H.parse_ts((ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"frozenAt\"))\n        if frozen and said < frozen:\n            return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at} is before the freeze at {ci['bar']['frozenAt']}\", 3)\n        if said > H.parse_ts(t):\n            return refuse(f\"--source-at {a.source_at} is after the tool's clock {t}\", 3)\n        ev = {\"event\": \"relay\", \"kind\": \"relay\", \"quote\": a.quote, \"from\": a.from_,\n              \"source_chat\": a.source_chat, \"source_at\": a.source_at, \"at\": t}\n\n    elif a.cmd == \"spend\":\n        lp = Path(a.spend_ledger)\n        if not lp.is_absolute():\n            lp = job / lp\n        rp = Path(a.key_reading)\n        if not rp.is_absolute():\n            rp = job / rp\n        if not lp.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no spend ledger at {lp}\", 2)\n        if not rp.is_file():\n            return refuse(f\"no key reading at {rp}\", 2)\n        try:\n            r = json.loads(rp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n            return refuse(f\"key reading {rp} is not JSON ({exc})\", 2)\n        if not r.get(\"read_at\") or not r.get(\"writer\"):\n            return refuse(f\"key reading {rp} has no read_at/writer stamp; run tools/edi/or_call.py --spend-status\", 3)\n        read_at = H.parse_ts(r[\"read_at\"])\n        if read_at is None:\n            return refuse(f\"key reading read_at {r['read_at']!r} is not RFC 3339 UTC\", 2)\n        ledger_sum = 0.0\n        last_settle = None\n        try:\n            for line in lp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n                if not line.strip():\n                    continue\n                x = json.loads(line)\n                if x.get(\"event\") == \"settle\":\n                    ledger_sum += float(x.get(\"cost_usd\") or 0)\n                    d = H.parse_ts(x.get(\"at\"))\n                    if d and (last_settle is None or d > last_settle):\n                        last_settle = d\n        except (ValueError, OSError) as exc:\n            return refuse(f\"spend ledger {lp} is not JSON Lines ({exc})\", 2)\n        if last_settle and (read_at - last_settle).total_seconds() < 180:\n            return refuse(f\"key reading at {r['read_at']} is less than 3 min after the last settle at \"\n                          f\"{H.iso(last_settle)}; read the key again later\", 3)\n        key_delta = float(r.get(\"key_delta_usd\") or 0)\n        total = max(ledger_sum, key_delta)\n        ev = {\"event\": \"spend\", \"spend_ledger\": relpath(job, lp),\n              \"spend_ledger_sha256\": sha256(lp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"key_reading\": relpath(job, rp), \"key_reading_sha256\": sha256(rp.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n              \"ledger_sum_usd\": ledger_sum, \"key_delta_usd\": key_delta, \"total_usd\": total,\n              \"read_at\": r[\"read_at\"], \"last_settle_at\": H.iso(last_settle) if last_settle else None, \"at\": t}\n\n    else:\n        return refuse(f\"unknown command {a.cmd!r}\", 2)\n\n    ev[\"writer\"] = writer_stamp()\n    if ci_changed:\n        write_custody(job, ci)\n    append_event(job, ev)\n    extra = \"\"\n    if a.cmd == \"approve\":\n        extra = f\" ({ev.get('role')} by {ev.get('by')})\"\n    elif a.cmd == \"pin\":\n        extra = f\" ({a.seat} -> {a.provider} [{a.slug}] at {ev['host']} via {ev['via']})\"\n    print(f\"logged {ev['event']} at {t}{extra}\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n## CONTEXT (read only; not in this part) kit/plumbline_verify.py\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Verify a custody/v1 record at two layers: the standard checker, then x-plumbline.\n\nThe standard layer is `checker/check.py` from the pinned custody checkout. It knows nothing about `x-` keys\n(SPEC.md line 141): it reads the custody/v1 predicate and ignores every extension. The Plumbline layer is this\nfile: it runs the standard checker FIRST, then enforces the `x-plumbline` block the record carries.\n\n    plumbline_verify.py --record R --files F --evidence E --ledger L --custody <checkout> [--json OUT]\n\nThere is no switch that relaxes a check. The hand-time allowance is read from the record, never from the command\nline. Exit codes:\n  0  OK at both layers\n  3  the standard layer failed (kind `standard`; nothing else is checked)\n  4  the standard layer passed and a Plumbline check failed\n  2  cannot run (usage, a missing input, or a checker whose sha256 is not the pin)\n\nEvery failure prints one line: `FAIL <kind> <field> <file>:<line>`. Kinds: standard, schema, allowance,\nhand-time-unflagged, flag-without-source, events, relay-as-approval, spend, shadow.\n\nThis file must not import the record emitter (V7): the emitter's logic is checked by separate code. It may use\nkit/custody_history.py to parse harness logs.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom hashlib import sha256\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\nimport custody_history as H  # noqa: E402\n\nSCHEMA_VERSION = \"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"\nSCHEMA_PATH = REPO / \"schemas\" / \"x-plumbline\" / \"x-plumbline-v1.schema.json\"\nSPEND_TOL = 0.0001\nLEDGER_REL = \"inputs/custody-events.jsonl\"\nOWNED = (\"verdict\", \"gaps\", \"times\", \"time_tolerance_s\", \"hand_times\", \"allowances\",\n         \"generations\", \"evaluations\", \"relays\", \"amendments\", \"spend\", \"schema\")\n# A tool's writer stamp: a .py path under kit/ and 12 lowercase hex (V3). Checked by form only.\nWRITER_FORM = re.compile(r\"^kit/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.py@[0-9a-f]{12}$\")\n\n\ndef file_sha(p: Path) -> str:\n    return sha256(Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef load(p: Path):\n    return json.loads(Path(p).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef relpath(job: Path, p: Path) -> str:\n    try:\n        return Path(p).resolve().relative_to(Path(job).resolve()).as_posix()\n    except ValueError:\n        return str(Path(p).resolve())\n\n\ndef ledger_lines(p: Path) -> list[tuple[int, dict]]:\n    out: list[tuple[int, dict]] = []\n    if not Path(p).is_file():\n        return out\n    for n, ln in enumerate(Path(p).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines(), 1):\n        if not ln.strip():\n            continue\n        try:\n            e = json.loads(ln)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n        if isinstance(e, dict):\n            e[\"_line\"] = n\n            out.append((n, e))\n    return out\n\n\ndef writer_source(e: dict):\n    w = e.get(\"writer\")\n    if w == \"hand\":\n        return \"ledger-hand\"\n    if w in (None, \"\"):\n        return \"ledger-no-writer\"\n    return None\n\n\ndef allowance_writer_ok(w) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"A tool's writer stamp by form: `<relative .py path under kit/>@<12 lowercase hex>`, never `hand`.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(w, str) and WRITER_FORM.match(w) is not None and \"..\" not in w\n\n\ndef line_of(path: Path, value, key: str | None = None):\n    if value in (None, \"\") or not Path(path).is_file():\n        return None\n    try:\n        lines = Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines()\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n    vs = str(value)\n    hits = [n for n, ln in enumerate(lines, 1) if vs in ln and (key is None or f'\"{key}\"' in ln)]\n    if not hits:\n        hits = [n for n, ln in enumerate(lines, 1) if vs in ln]\n    return hits[0] if hits else None\n\n\ndef used_seats(ci: dict) -> set[str]:\n    seats: set[str] = set()\n    m = ci.get(\"maker\") or {}\n    if m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\":\n        seats.add(\"maker\")\n    for e in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or []:\n        if e.get(\"kind\") == \"model\":\n            seats.add(str(e.get(\"id\")))\n    return seats\n\n\ndef evidence_dirs(job: Path, ev: Path, ci: dict) -> list[Path]:\n    \"\"\"Where harness logs can be: the verifier's --evidence, the inputs' evidence_dir, and the job itself.\"\"\"\n    out = [Path(ev)]\n    rel = (ci.get(\"evidence_dir\") if isinstance(ci, dict) else None) or \"custody/evidence\"\n    out.append(Path(job) / rel)\n    out.append(Path(job))\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    uniq: list[Path] = []\n    for d in out:\n        r = str(Path(d).resolve())\n        if r not in seen:\n            seen.add(r)\n            uniq.append(Path(d))\n    return uniq\n\n\ndef find_log(job: Path, dirs: list[Path], rel: str | None, pattern: str | None):\n    if rel:\n        for base in dirs:\n            p = Path(base) / rel\n            if p.is_file():\n                return p\n        return None\n    hits: list[Path] = []\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    for base in dirs:\n        if not Path(base).is_dir() or not pattern:\n            continue\n        for p in sorted(Path(base).glob(pattern)):\n            k = str(p.resolve())\n            if k not in seen:\n                seen.add(k)\n                hits.append(p)\n    return hits[0] if len(hits) == 1 else None\n\n\ndef read_calls(job: Path, ev_dir: Path, ci: dict):\n    by: dict[str, dict] = {}\n    allc: list = []\n    dirs = evidence_dirs(job, ev_dir, ci)\n\n    def add(seat: str, log):\n        if not log:\n            return\n        try:\n            calls = H.read_log(Path(log), H.Refusals(), str(seat))\n        except Exception:\n            return\n        d = by.setdefault(str(seat), {})\n        for c in calls:\n            name = getattr(c, \"name\", None) or str(getattr(c, \"i\", \"\"))\n            d[name] = c\n            allc.append(c)\n\n    if isinstance(ci, dict):\n        m = ci.get(\"maker\") or {}\n        if m.get(\"kind\") == \"model\":\n            add(\"maker\", find_log(job, dirs, m.get(\"harness_log\"), \"harness-maker*.log\"))\n        for e in ci.get(\"evaluators\") or []:\n            if e.get(\"kind\") == \"model\":\n                rel = e.get(\"harness_log\") or next(\n                    (x.get(\"evidence_file\") for x in ci.get(\"external\") or []\n                     if x.get(\"subject\") == e.get(\"id\")), None)\n                add(str(e.get(\"id\")), find_log(job, dirs, rel, None))\n    if not allc:\n        for base in dirs:\n            if Path(base).is_dir():\n                for log in sorted(Path(base).glob(\"*.log\")):\n                    add(log.stem, log)\n    return by, allc\n\n\ndef call_cost(c) -> float:\n    raw = getattr(c, \"raw\", None)\n    if not isinstance(raw, dict):\n        return 0.0\n    resp = raw.get(\"response\") if isinstance(raw.get(\"response\"), dict) else {}\n    usage = resp.get(\"usage\") if isinstance(resp.get(\"usage\"), dict) else {}\n    for v in (raw.get(\"total_cost\"), resp.get(\"total_cost\"), usage.get(\"total_cost\"), usage.get(\"cost\")):\n        if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool):\n            return float(v)\n    return 0.0\n\n\ndef call_time(c):\n    return getattr(c, \"started\", None) or getattr(c, \"at\", None)\n\n\ndef ledger_array(lines: list[tuple[int, dict]], event: str, ledger_rel: str) -> list[dict]:\n    return [{**{k: v for k, v in e.items() if k != \"_line\"},\n             \"source\": f\"{ledger_rel}:{e['_line']}\"}\n            for _, e in lines if e.get(\"event\") == event]\n\n\ndef last_spend_line(lines: list[tuple[int, dict]]):\n    sp = None\n    for _, e in lines:\n        if e.get(\"event\") == \"spend\":\n            sp = e\n    return sp\n\n\ndef compute_spend_block(lines: list[tuple[int, dict]], all_calls, ledger_rel: str) -> dict:\n    sp = last_spend_line(lines)\n    calls_sum = round(sum(call_cost(c) for c in all_calls if getattr(c, \"at\", None)), 6)\n    key_delta = float(sp.get(\"key_delta_usd\") or 0) if sp else 0.0\n    return {\"calls_sum_usd\": calls_sum,\n            \"key_delta_usd\": key_delta,\n            \"total_usd\": max(calls_sum, key_delta),\n            \"tolerance_usd\": SPEND_TOL,\n            \"source\": f\"{ledger_rel}:{sp['_line']}\" if sp else None}\n\n\ndef hand_key(e: dict):\n    try:\n        line = int(e.get(\"line\")) if e.get(\"line\") is not None else None\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        line = None\n    return (e.get(\"field\"), e.get(\"file\"), line, e.get(\"source\"))\n\n\ndef hand_time_set(job: Path, ledger_path: Path, custody_path: Path, record: dict, evidence: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    ci = load(custody_path) if Path(custody_path).is_file() else {}\n    lines = ledger_lines(ledger_path)\n    ledger_rel = relpath(job, ledger_path)\n    try:\n        inputs_rel = relpath(job, custody_path)\n    except Exception:\n        inputs_rel = str(custody_path)\n    seats = used_seats(ci)\n    calls_by_seat, _ = read_calls(job, evidence, ci)\n    hand: dict[str, dict] = {}\n    seen: set = set()\n\n    def mark(field: str, file: str, line, source: str) -> None:\n        hand[field] = {\"field\": field, \"file\": file, \"line\": line, \"source\": source}\n\n    for n, e in lines:\n        src = writer_source(e)\n        ev = e.get(\"event\")\n        field = None\n        if ev == \"freeze\":\n            seen.add(\"freeze\")\n            field = \"bar.frozenAt\"\n        elif ev == \"approve\":\n            role = e.get(\"role\")\n            seen.add((\"approve\", role))\n            for i, a in enumerate((ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"approvals\") or []):\n                if a.get(\"role\") == role:\n                    f = f\"bar.approvals[{i}].at\"\n                    if src:\n                        mark(f, ledger_rel, n, src)\n                    else:\n                        hand.pop(f, None)\n            continue\n        elif ev == \"dispose\":\n            seen.add(\"dispose\")\n            field = \"disposition.at\"\n        elif ev == \"pin\":\n            seat = e.get(\"seat\")\n            seen.add((\"pin\", seat))\n            if seat in seats:\n                field = f\"routing.{seat}.declaredAt\"\n        else:\n            continue\n        if field:\n            if src:\n                mark(field, ledger_rel, n, src)\n            else:\n                hand.pop(field, None)\n\n    bar = ci.get(\"bar\") or {}\n    if \"freeze\" not in seen and bar.get(\"frozenAt\"):\n        mark(\"bar.frozenAt\", inputs_rel, line_of(custody_path, bar.get(\"frozenAt\"), \"frozenAt\"),\n             \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n    for i, a in enumerate(bar.get(\"approvals\") or []):\n        if (\"approve\", a.get(\"role\")) not in seen and a.get(\"at\"):\n            mark(f\"bar.approvals[{i}].at\", inputs_rel, line_of(custody_path, a.get(\"at\"), \"at\"),\n                 \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n    for seat in seats:\n        if (\"pin\", seat) not in seen:\n            pin = (ci.get(\"routing\") or {}).get(seat) or {}\n            if pin.get(\"declaredAt\"):\n                mark(f\"routing.{seat}.declaredAt\", inputs_rel,\n                     line_of(custody_path, pin.get(\"declaredAt\"), \"declaredAt\"), \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n    if \"dispose\" not in seen:\n        d = ci.get(\"disposition\") or {}\n        if d.get(\"at\"):\n            mark(\"disposition.at\", inputs_rel, line_of(custody_path, d.get(\"at\"), \"at\"), \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n\n    mcalls = calls_by_seat.get(\"maker\") or {}\n    if not mcalls:\n        if ci.get(\"startedAt\"):\n            mark(\"startedAt\", inputs_rel, line_of(custody_path, ci.get(\"startedAt\"), \"startedAt\"),\n                 \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n        if ci.get(\"producedAt\"):\n            mark(\"producedAt\", inputs_rel, line_of(custody_path, ci.get(\"producedAt\"), \"producedAt\"),\n                 \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n\n    for pid, f in (ci.get(\"passes\") or {}).items():\n        if not isinstance(f, dict) or not f.get(\"at\"):\n            continue\n        calls = calls_by_seat.get(str(f.get(\"evaluator\"))) or {}\n        linked = (f.get(\"call\") in calls) if f.get(\"call\") else len(calls) == 1\n        if not linked:\n            mark(f\"passes.{pid}.at\", inputs_rel, line_of(custody_path, f.get(\"at\"), \"at\"),\n                 \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n\n    for k in ci.get(\"controls\") or []:\n        if not k.get(\"at\"):\n            continue\n        calls = calls_by_seat.get(str(k.get(\"evaluator\"))) or {}\n        linked = (k.get(\"call\") in calls) if k.get(\"call\") else len(calls) == 1\n        if not linked:\n            mark(f\"controls[{k.get('id')}].at\", inputs_rel, line_of(custody_path, k.get(\"at\"), \"at\"),\n                 \"inputs-no-ledger\")\n\n    logs: list[Path] = []\n    for base in evidence_dirs(job, evidence, ci):\n        if Path(base).is_dir():\n            logs += sorted(Path(base).glob(\"*.log\"))\n    for log in dict.fromkeys(logs):\n        try:\n            calls = H.read_log(Path(log), H.Refusals(), \"verify\")\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n        for c in calls:\n            try:\n                entries = c.hand_time_entries()\n            except Exception:\n                entries = []\n            for e in entries:\n                if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"field\"):\n                    hand[str(e[\"field\"])] = e\n    return [hand[k] for k in sorted(hand)]\n\n\ndef check_hand_times(hand: list[dict], record: dict) -> list[dict]:\n    fails: list[dict] = []\n    xp = (record.get(\"predicate\") or {}).get(\"x-plumbline\") if isinstance(record, dict) else None\n    if not isinstance(xp, dict):\n        return fails\n    flags = xp.get(\"hand_times\")\n    if not isinstance(flags, list):\n        return fails\n    recomp = {hand_key(e) for e in hand if isinstance(e, dict)}\n    got = {hand_key(e) for e in flags if isinstance(e, dict)}\n    for k in sorted(recomp - got):\n        fails.append({\"kind\": \"hand-time-unflagged\", \"field\": k[0], \"file\": k[1], \"line\": k[2]})\n    for k in sorted(got - recomp):\n        fails.append({\"kind\": \"flag-without-source\", \"field\": k[0], \"file\": k[1], \"line\": k[2]})\n    if recomp:\n        allowances = xp.get(\"allowances\")\n        allowance = allowances.get(\"hand_times\") if isinstance(allowances, dict) else None\n        if not isinstance(allowance, dict):\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"allowance\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times\",\n                          \"file\": \"\", \"line\": 0})\n        else:\n            if allowance.get(\"switch\") != \"--allow-hand-times\":\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"allowance\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times.switch\",\n                              \"file\": \"\", \"line\": 0})\n            if not allowance_writer_ok(allowance.get(\"writer\")):\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"allowance\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times.writer\",\n                              \"file\": \"\", \"line\": 0})\n            if not H.parse_ts(allowance.get(\"at\")):\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"allowance\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.allowances.hand_times.at\",\n                              \"file\": \"\", \"line\": 0})\n    return fails\n\n\ndef check_events(job: Path, ledger_path: Path, record: dict, calls_by_seat: dict) -> list[dict]:\n    fails: list[dict] = []\n    xp = (record.get(\"predicate\") or {}).get(\"x-plumbline\") if isinstance(record, dict) else None\n    if not isinstance(xp, dict):\n        return fails\n    lines = ledger_lines(ledger_path)\n    ledger_rel = relpath(job, ledger_path)\n    for ev, key in ((\"generation\", \"generations\"), (\"evaluation\", \"evaluations\"),\n                    (\"relay\", \"relays\"), (\"amendment\", \"amendments\")):\n        expected = ledger_array(lines, ev, ledger_rel)\n        got = xp.get(key)\n        if got != expected:\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"events\", \"field\": f\"x-plumbline.{key}\", \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n\n    for _, e in lines:\n        if e.get(\"event\") != \"evaluation\":\n            continue\n        vf = e.get(\"verdict_file\")\n        want = e.get(\"verdict_sha256\")\n        if not vf:\n            continue\n        p = Path(vf) if Path(vf).is_absolute() else Path(job) / vf\n        if not p.is_file() or file_sha(p) != want:\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"events\", \"field\": f\"evaluations[{e.get('batch')}].verdict_sha256\",\n                          \"file\": vf, \"line\": e.get(\"_line\", 0)})\n\n    opens: dict = {}\n    closes: dict = {}\n    for _, e in lines:\n        if e.get(\"event\") != \"generation\":\n            continue\n        k = (e.get(\"seat\"), e.get(\"n\"))\n        if e.get(\"action\") == \"open\":\n            opens[k] = e\n        elif e.get(\"action\") == \"close\":\n            closes[k] = e\n    maker_calls = list((calls_by_seat.get(\"maker\") or {}).values())\n    for k, o in opens.items():\n        c = closes.get(k)\n        if not c:\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"events\", \"field\": f\"generations[{k[0]}#{k[1]}].close\",\n                          \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": o.get(\"_line\", 0)})\n            continue\n        t0, t1 = H.parse_ts(o.get(\"at\")), H.parse_ts(c.get(\"at\"))\n        if t0 and t1:\n            found = any(call_time(x) and t0 <= call_time(x) <= t1 for x in maker_calls)\n            if not found:\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"events\", \"field\": f\"generations[{k[0]}#{k[1]}].calls\",\n                              \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": o.get(\"_line\", 0)})\n\n    relays = [e for _, e in lines if e.get(\"event\") == \"relay\"]\n    approvals = ((record.get(\"predicate\") or {}).get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"approvals\") or []\n    for r in relays:\n        for a in approvals:\n            if (a.get(\"kind\") == \"relay\" or a.get(\"relay\") or a.get(\"role\") == \"relay\"\n                    or a.get(\"by\") == r.get(\"from\") or a.get(\"quote\") == r.get(\"quote\")):\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"relay-as-approval\", \"field\": \"predicate.bar.approvals\",\n                              \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": r.get(\"_line\", 0)})\n                break\n    return fails\n\n\ndef check_spend(job: Path, ledger_path: Path, record: dict, all_calls) -> list[dict]:\n    fails: list[dict] = []\n    xp = (record.get(\"predicate\") or {}).get(\"x-plumbline\") if isinstance(record, dict) else None\n    if not isinstance(xp, dict):\n        return fails\n    lines = ledger_lines(ledger_path)\n    ledger_rel = relpath(job, ledger_path)\n    expected = compute_spend_block(lines, all_calls, ledger_rel)\n    sp = xp.get(\"spend\")\n    if not isinstance(sp, dict):\n        return [{\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.spend\", \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0}]\n    for k in (\"calls_sum_usd\", \"key_delta_usd\", \"total_usd\", \"tolerance_usd\"):\n        if k not in sp:\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": f\"x-plumbline.spend.{k}\", \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n    calls_sum = float(sp.get(\"calls_sum_usd\") or 0)\n    key_delta = float(sp.get(\"key_delta_usd\") or 0)\n    total = float(sp.get(\"total_usd\") or 0)\n    tol = float(sp.get(\"tolerance_usd\") or 0)\n    if abs(calls_sum - expected[\"calls_sum_usd\"]) > SPEND_TOL:\n        fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.spend.calls_sum_usd\",\n                      \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n    if abs(key_delta - expected[\"key_delta_usd\"]) > 1e-9:\n        fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.spend.key_delta_usd\",\n                      \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n    if abs(total - max(calls_sum, key_delta)) > 1e-9:\n        fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.spend.total_usd\",\n                      \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n    if abs(tol - SPEND_TOL) > 1e-12:\n        fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.spend.tolerance_usd\",\n                      \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n\n    sp_line = last_spend_line(lines)\n    if sp_line:\n        lp = Path(sp_line.get(\"spend_ledger\") or \"\")\n        if not lp.is_absolute():\n            lp = Path(job) / lp\n        if not lp.is_file():\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"spend_ledger\", \"file\": str(lp), \"line\": sp_line.get(\"_line\", 0)})\n        else:\n            labels = {getattr(c, \"name\", None) or str(getattr(c, \"i\", \"\")) for c in all_calls}\n            for n, ln in enumerate(lp.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines(), 1):\n                if not ln.strip():\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    x = json.loads(ln)\n                except ValueError:\n                    continue\n                if x.get(\"event\") == \"settle\":\n                    call = x.get(\"call\") or x.get(\"id\")\n                    if call and call not in labels:\n                        fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": f\"settle[{call}]\",\n                                      \"file\": str(lp), \"line\": n})\n        rp = Path(sp_line.get(\"key_reading\") or \"\")\n        if not rp.is_absolute():\n            rp = Path(job) / rp\n        if not rp.is_file():\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"key_reading\", \"file\": str(rp), \"line\": sp_line.get(\"_line\", 0)})\n        else:\n            try:\n                r = load(rp)\n            except Exception:\n                r = {}\n            if not r.get(\"read_at\") or not r.get(\"writer\"):\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"key_reading.read_at\",\n                              \"file\": str(rp), \"line\": 0})\n            else:\n                read_at = H.parse_ts(r.get(\"read_at\"))\n                last = H.parse_ts(sp_line.get(\"last_settle_at\"))\n                if read_at and last and (read_at - last).total_seconds() < 180:\n                    fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"key_reading.read_at\",\n                                  \"file\": str(rp), \"line\": 0})\n                if abs(float(r.get(\"key_delta_usd\") or 0) - key_delta) > 1e-6:\n                    fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"key_reading.key_delta_usd\",\n                                  \"file\": str(rp), \"line\": 0})\n    elif expected[\"calls_sum_usd\"] > 0:\n        fails.append({\"kind\": \"spend\", \"field\": \"x-plumbline.spend.source\",\n                      \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n    return fails\n\n\ndef check_shadow(job: Path, ledger_path: Path, record: dict, all_calls, hand: list[dict],\n                 calls_by_seat: dict) -> list[dict]:\n    fails: list[dict] = []\n    xp = (record.get(\"predicate\") or {}).get(\"x-plumbline\") if isinstance(record, dict) else None\n    if not isinstance(xp, dict):\n        return fails\n    inputs = xp.get(\"inputs\")\n    if not isinstance(inputs, dict):\n        inputs = {}\n    lines = ledger_lines(ledger_path)\n    ledger_rel = relpath(job, ledger_path)\n    derived: dict = {\n        \"schema\": SCHEMA_VERSION,\n        \"time_tolerance_s\": H.TOLERANCE_S,\n        \"hand_times\": hand,\n        \"generations\": ledger_array(lines, \"generation\", ledger_rel),\n        \"evaluations\": ledger_array(lines, \"evaluation\", ledger_rel),\n        \"relays\": ledger_array(lines, \"relay\", ledger_rel),\n        \"amendments\": ledger_array(lines, \"amendment\", ledger_rel),\n        \"spend\": compute_spend_block(lines, all_calls, ledger_rel),\n    }\n    s5 = xp.get(\"s5_record\") or {}\n    if s5.get(\"name\"):\n        p = Path(s5[\"name\"]) if Path(s5[\"name\"]).is_absolute() else Path(job) / s5[\"name\"]\n        if p.is_file():\n            try:\n                rec = load(p)\n                if \"verdict\" in rec:\n                    derived[\"verdict\"] = rec.get(\"verdict\")\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n    mcalls = calls_by_seat.get(\"maker\") or {}\n    derived[\"times\"] = {\"startedAt\": \"harness log\" if mcalls else \"hand-entered\",\n                        \"producedAt\": \"harness log\" if mcalls else \"hand-entered\"}\n\n    for key in OWNED:\n        if key not in derived or key not in xp:\n            continue\n        if key == \"hand_times\":\n            if {hand_key(e) for e in xp.get(key) or [] if isinstance(e, dict)} != \\\n                    {hand_key(e) for e in derived[key] or [] if isinstance(e, dict)}:\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"shadow\", \"field\": f\"x-plumbline.{key}\",\n                              \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n        elif xp.get(key) != derived[key]:\n            fails.append({\"kind\": \"shadow\", \"field\": f\"x-plumbline.{key}\",\n                          \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n    for key in OWNED:\n        if key in inputs and key in xp and key in derived:\n            if xp.get(key) == inputs.get(key) and xp.get(key) != derived[key]:\n                fails.append({\"kind\": \"shadow\", \"field\": f\"x-plumbline.inputs.{key}\",\n                              \"file\": str(ledger_path), \"line\": 0})\n    return fails\n\n\ndef _type_ok(v, t: str) -> bool:\n    if t == \"object\":\n        return isinstance(v, dict)\n    if t == \"array\":\n        return isinstance(v, list)\n    if t == \"string\":\n        return isinstance(v, str)\n    if t == \"integer\":\n        return isinstance(v, int) and not isinstance(v, bool)\n    if t == \"number\":\n        return isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool)\n    if t == \"boolean\":\n        return isinstance(v, bool)\n    if t == \"null\":\n        return v is None\n    return True\n\n\ndef _validate(inst, sch, root, path: str) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n    errs: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    if sch is True or sch == {}:\n        return errs\n    if sch is False:\n        return [(path, \"false schema\")]\n    if \"$ref\" in sch:\n        ref = sch[\"$ref\"]\n        if isinstance(ref, str) and ref.startswith(\"#/$defs/\"):\n            name = ref.split(\"/\")[-1]\n            return _validate(inst, root[\"$defs\"][name], root, path)\n        return errs\n    if \"const\" in sch and inst != sch[\"const\"]:\n        errs.append((path, \"const\"))\n    if \"enum\" in sch and inst not in sch[\"enum\"]:\n        errs.append((path, \"enum\"))\n    if \"type\" in sch:\n        ts = sch[\"type\"] if isinstance(sch[\"type\"], list) else [sch[\"type\"]]\n        if not any(_type_ok(inst, t) for t in ts):\n            errs.append((path, \"type\"))\n    for sub in sch.get(\"allOf\") or []:\n        errs += _validate(inst, sub, root, path)\n    if \"anyOf\" in sch:\n        if not any(not _validate(inst, sub, root, path) for sub in sch[\"anyOf\"]):\n            errs.append((path, \"anyOf\"))\n    if \"oneOf\" in sch:\n        ok = sum(1 for sub in sch[\"oneOf\"] if not _validate(inst, sub, root, path))\n        if ok != 1:\n            errs.append((path, \"oneOf\"))\n    if isinstance(inst, dict):\n        for r in sch.get(\"required\") or []:\n            if r not in inst:\n                errs.append((path + \".\" + r, \"required\"))\n        props = sch.get(\