|\n| emitter revision | ... | refused when dirty, or not the stated revision |\n\nThen a note after the table: \"A log call whose harness log carries no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` (only the response `Date` header or `created`) is a hand time too: source `server-header` or `response-created`. The emitter reads the server time to show the value but never writes it back into the log.\"\n\nThen the tolerance paragraph stays.\n\nNow the jsonc comment: `\"startedAt\": \"…Z\", \"producedAt\": \"…Z\",       // optional cross-checks; the log decides` → change to `// leave unset: a typed value is a hand time (refused unless --allow-hand-times); the log supplies it`.\n\nHmm, but careful about other places: \"Rules the emitter enforces\" list ends with \"Every time, endpoint, approver and revision rule in 'Refusals' above, including hand times.\" Fine.\n\nAlso the \"Where each fact\" section heading is retained.\n\nAlso check: in the section \"Hand times: refused by default, flagged under the switch\" the paragraph says \"or a server time (a log time taken from the response `Date` header, `server-header`, or from `created`, `response-created`) that no logger `sent_at`/`received_at` recorded.\" Good.\n\nNow let's check line 96 area and rewrite.\n\nAlso the paragraph right after the table: \"**Tolerance: 60 seconds**...\" stays.\n\nNow, another place: In \"Running the three jobs\" step 3/4 etc. Fine.\n\nLet me also double check the `time` row in the refusals table: \"`time` | a hand-entered time is more than 60 s off its harness call; a model maker/evaluator has no harness log; ...\" Hmm — under new policy, a typed time is refused as hand-time by default; with the switch on, if it contradicts the log, it exits 3 with kind `time` (the overlay `failures/hand-times`). So the row is correct for the switch-on case. But \"a hand-entered time is more than 60 s off its harness call\" — could be read as the default behavior. Maybe adjust: \"under `--allow-hand-times`, a hand time more