block` must produce the same. With the new `call_cost`, both use generation total_cost. Good. The `source` field: emitter `f\"{LEDGER_REL}:{sp['_line']}\"`, verifier `f\"{ledger_rel}:{sp['_line']}\"`. If `ledger_rel == LEDGER_REL`, match. `ledger_rel = relpath(job, ledger_path)`. For `job` = `FIX` and ledger = `FIX/inputs/custody-events.jsonl`, `relpath` = `inputs/custody-events.jsonl` = `LEDGER_REL`. Good.\n\nNow let me write the emitter changes:\n1. `call_cost`: same as verifier.\n2. `relay_only_buyer` check in `build`.\n\nWhere to add the check? After building `approvals` and before/after `check_order`. Let me add it right after the approvals loop, using `lines` (ledger lines) and `ci`, `packet`, `have_inputs`.\n\nActually, `lines = ledger_lines(job)` is computed early. And `have_inputs` is computed. And `packet`. So I can add after the approvals loop:\n```python\n    if have_inputs:\n        has_relay = any(e.get(\"event\") == \"relay\" for _, e in lines)\n        if has_relay and packet.get(\"buyer\"):\n            bar_roles = {a.get(\"role\") for a in (ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"approvals\") or [] if isinstance(a, dict)}\n            ledger_roles = {e.get(\"role\") for _, e in lines if e.get(\"event\") == \"approve\"}\n            if \"buyer\" not in bar_roles and \"buyer\" not in ledger_roles:\n                ref.add(\"approval\", f\"buyer: the buyer's approval exists only as a relay ({LEDGER_REL}); a relay is a \"\n                                    f\"report, not an approval (F1f). The buyer must approve directly: \"\n                                    f\"custody_ledger.py approve --role buyer, or a buyer entry in inputs/custody.json\")\n```\n\nHmm, but `ci` at this point — is it `{}` if no inputs? `have_inputs` guards. OK.\n\nBut wait, `bar.approvals` — if the bar has a buyer entry, `bar_roles` has buyer. Good.\n\nLet me place this after the `if not approvals: gaps.add(...)` line. Actually, let me place it right after the approvals loop, before the ground truth loop. Or anywhere in `build`. Let me place it near the approvals.\n\nNow, there's a subtlety: the `approvals` variable is built from `b.get(\"approvals\")`. If buyer is missing there, `approvals` has only specialist. The check uses `ci[\"bar\"][\"approvals\"]` (same as `b`). So `bar_roles` from `ci` matches. Fine.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nNow, `tests/test_plumbline_verify.py`. Let me rewrite with the stand-in checker and the new tests. I'll keep the existing tests and add:\n- `test_call_cost_prefers_generation_total`\n- `test_clean_against_real_checker` (skipUnless CUSTODY_DIR)\n- maybe a round-trip test? The feedback item 2 test is in validate_schemas.\n\nWait, item 2's test \"copy tests/fixtures/custody/job-rejected into a temporary directory, emit it with --allow-hand-times, and run the verifier on that record; it must exit 0\". Let me add this to `validate_schemas.py` since it has the emitter infra and a stand-in checkout.\n\nActually, let me add it to `validate_schemas.py` after the T3 tests.\n\nHmm, but `validate_schemas.py`'s `emit` runs from `SNAP` (clean checkout). And `verify_record` runs `SNAP/kit/plumbline_verify.py`. Let me add.\n\nNow, let me carefully write the `validate_schemas.py` additions. I need to be careful not to break the existing ~2000 lines. Let me insert the new cases near the end, before `shutil.rmtree(TMP)`.\n\nLet me write the additions:\n\n```python\n# ---- V1/V3/T2: every record the emitter writes verifies with exit 0 (no flag-without-source, no shadow) ----\ndef _stand_in_checkout(name):\n    d = TMP / name\n    (d / \"checker\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    (d / \"tools\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    checker = d / \"checker\" / \"check.py\"\n    checker.write_text(\n        \"import json, sys\\n\"\n        \"from hashlib import sha256\\n\"\n        \"from pathlib import Path\\n\"\n        \"def arg(n):\\n\"\n        \"    a = sys.argv[1:]\\n\"\n        \"    return a[a.index(n)+1] if n in a and a.index(n)+1 < len(a) else None\\n\"\n        \"if not arg('--bar'):\\n\"\n        \"    print('checker: --bar required', file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(2)\\n\"\n        \"rec = Path(sys.argv[1]); files = arg('--files')\\n\"\n        \"doc = json.loads(rec.read_text())\\n\"\n        \"for s in doc.get('subject') or []:\\n\"\n        \"    p = (Path(files) / s['name']) if files else None\\n\"\n        \"    if p is None or not p.is_file() or sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() != (s.get('digest') or {}).get('sha256'):\\n\"\n        \"        print('checker: subject mismatch', file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(1)\\n\"\n        \"sys.exit(0)\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (d / \"tools\" / \"pin.json\").write_text(\n        json.dumps({\"checker/check.py\": hashlib.sha256(checker.read_bytes()).hexdigest()}) + \"\\n\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return d\n\n\ndef verify_record(rec, job, co):\n    return run_py([str(SNAP / \"kit\" / \"plumbline_verify.py\"),\n                   \"--record\", str(rec),\n                   \"--files\", str(job / \"custody\" / \"files\"),\n                   \"--evidence\", str(job / \"custody\" / \"evidence\"),\n                   \"--ledger\", str(job / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"),\n                   \"--custody\", str(co)])\n\n\nVCO = _stand_in_checkout(\"verify-checkout\")\nrt_rec = TMP / \"roundtrip.custody.json\"\nrc, out = emit(FIX, rt_rec, allow_hand=True)\nvrc, vout = verify_record(rt_rec, FIX, VCO)\nrt_xp = json.loads(rt_rec.read_text())[\"predicate\"][\"x-plumbline\"] if rt_rec.is_file() else {}\nres((f\"{S} · V1/V3/T2 a job emitted with --allow-hand-times verifies with exit 0 \"\n     f\"(no flag-without-source, no shadow)\",\n     rc == 0 and vrc == 0 and \"flag-without-source\" not in vout and \"shadow\" not in vout,\n     f\"emit {rc}, verify {vrc}: {vout.strip()[-140:]}\"))\nres((f\"{S} · T3 every hand time the emitter flagged is in x-plumbline.hand_times with file:line\",\n     bool(rt_xp.get(\"hand_times\"))\n     and all(e.get(\"field\") and e.get(\"file\") and e.get(\"line\") is not None for e in rt_xp.get(\"hand_times\") or []),\n     json.dumps((rt_xp.get(\"hand_times\") or [])[:2])[:160]))\n```\n\nBut `run_py` sets `cwd=REPO`. The verifier imports `custody_history` from its own dir. Fine.\n\nWait, `emit(FIX, rt_rec, allow_hand=True)` — the `emit` function:\n```python\ndef emit(job, out, tree=None, extra=(), allow_hand=True):\n    args = [str((tree or SNAP) / \"kit\" / \"emit_custody.py\"), \"--job-dir\", str(job), \"--out\", str(out), *extra]\n    if allow_hand:\n        args.append(\"--allow-hand-times\")\n    return run_py(args)\n```\nUses `SNAP`. Good.\n\nNow, `verify_record` uses `SNAP / \"kit\" / \"plumbline_verify.py\"`. But `SNAP` is a clean checkout of the current repo, so it has the verifier. Good.\n\nNow, the verifier's `job` determination: `ledger = FIX/inputs/custody-events.jsonl`, `ledger.parent.name == \"inputs\"`, so `job = FIX`. Good. And `custody_json = FIX/inputs/custody.json`. Good.\n\nNow, the `bar` path: `FIX/inputs/custody.json`'s `bar.file` = `custody/bar.md`. So `bar = FIX/custody/bar.md`. Exists. Good.\n\nNow, the stand-in checker requires `--bar` and checks subject digests. The emitted record's subject names `artifact.md` with its digest. The files dir is `FIX/custody/files/artifact.md`. Digest matches. So checker exits 0. Then the Plumbline layer runs. If hand times match, exit 0.\n\nPotential mismatch: the emitter flags call hand times from the maker and evaluator logs. The verifier's `read_calls` reads the same logs. So match. But wait — the verifier's `read_calls` uses `find_log` with `evidence_dirs(job, evidence, ci)`. `evidence` = `FIX/custody/evidence`. `ci` = `FIX/inputs/custody.json`. `evidence_dir` = `custody/evidence` (default). So dirs = [`FIX/custody/evidence`, `FIX/custody/evidence`, `FIX`]. The maker log is `harness-maker-fixture.log` in `FIX/custody/evidence`. `find_log` with `m.get(\"harness_log\")` — if the maker has `harness_log` set to `harness-maker-fixture.log`