e the verifier file now.\n\nI'll also keep the `_find_pin_in`, `find_pin`, `_find_checker` as is.\n\nLet me write.\n\nNow for `kit/emit_custody.py`, I need to change `call_cost` and add the relay-only check. Let me locate the exact lines.\n\n`call_cost`:\n```python\ndef call_cost(c) -> float:\n    \"\"\"A harness call's billed cost, wherever the harness logged it.\"\"\"\n    raw = c.raw\n    resp = raw.get(\"response\") if isinstance(raw.get(\"response\"), dict) else {}\n    usage = resp.get(\"usage\") if isinstance(resp.get(\"usage\"), dict) else {}\n    for v in (raw.get(\"total_cost\"), resp.get(\"total_cost\"), usage.get(\"total_cost\"), usage.get(\"cost\")):\n        if isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n            return float(v)\n    return 0.0\n```\n\nReplace with the generation-first version.\n\nRelay-only check: add after the approvals loop in `build`. Let me find the exact location. After:\n```python\n    if not approvals:\n        gaps.add(\"bar.approvals\", \"no buyer/specialist approval recorded\")\n```\n\nAdd:\n```python\n    # F1f: a relay is a report, never an approval. A buyer approval whose only evidence is a relay line (no\n    # `approve --role buyer` ledger line and no buyer entry in inputs/custody.json) is refused as a missing\n    # approval: the emitter will not count the relay.\n    if have_inputs and packet.get(\"buyer\") and any(e.get(\"event\") == \"relay\" for _, e in lines):\n        bar_roles = {a.get(\"role\") for a in (ci.get(\"bar\") or {}).get(\"approvals\") or [] if isinstance(a, dict)}\n        ledger_roles = {e.get(\"role\") for _, e in lines if e.get(\"event\") == \"approve\"}\n        if \"buyer\" not in bar_roles and \"buyer\" not in ledger_roles:\n            ref.add(\"approval\", f\"buyer: the buyer's approval exists only as a relay ({LEDGER_REL}); a relay is a \"\n                                f\"report, not an approval (F1f). The buyer must approve directly: \"\n                                f\"custody_ledger.py approve 