eds each generation to have a maker call between open and close. But job-rejected might not have generation lines. Let me check — `check_events` only fails if there are generation open/close lines. If the ledger has no generation lines, `opens` is empty, no check. OK.\n\nNow let me think about `check_shadow`. It derives `verdict` from `s5_record`, `times` from maker calls. For job-rejected, `xp[\"s5_record\"]` points to `iteration-1-eval-record.json` maybe. And `times` = `{\"startedAt\": \"harness log\" if mcalls else \"hand-entered\", ...}`. The emitter sets `xp[\"times\"] = {\"startedAt\": \"harness log\" if mk.get(\"startedAt\") else \"hand-entered\", ...}`. If `mk.get(\"startedAt\")` is set, both say \"harness log\". If not, both say \"hand-entered\". Should match if `mcalls` (verifier) equals `mk.get(\"startedAt\")` truthiness.\n\nHmm, `mcalls = calls_by_seat.get(\"maker\") or {}`. This is populated from `read_calls` which reads the maker log. `mk.get(\"startedAt\")` is set if `maker_history` found calls. So if the maker log has calls with `at`, both are truthy. OK.\n\nBut wait — `calls_by_seat` uses `H.read_log` and only includes calls that have a name. Let me check `read_calls`:\n```python\n    def add(seat: str, log):\n        if not log:\n            return\n        try:\n            calls = H.read_log(Path(log), H.Refusals(), str(seat))\n        except Exception:\n            return\n        d = by.setdefault(str(seat), {})\n        for c in calls:\n            name = getattr(c, \"name\", None) or str(getattr(c, \"i\", \"\"))\n            d[name] = c\n            allc.append(c)\n```\n\nSo even calls without `at` are added. But `mk.get(\"startedAt\")` requires `calls = [c for c in calls if c.at]`. If the maker log has calls but none with `at`, `mk.get(\"startedAt\")` is falsy but `mcalls` is truthy. Then `check_shadow` would derive \"harness log\" but the emitter wrote \"hand-entered\" → mismatch → shadow failure.\n\nBut `read_log` refuses calls with no `at