ctually `ev_log[\"approve\"][role]` takes the last one, so appending overrides). Hmm.\n\nThis is getting too deep. Let me simplify the F1f test: instead of modifying `job-rejected`, build a minimal job from scratch in a temp dir. But the emitter needs a lot of files. Ugh.\n\nAlternatively, I can test the `relay_only_buyer` function directly at the unit level, plus a full emitter run. But the feedback explicitly wants the emitter to exit non-zero.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe I can build the relay-only job more carefully by:\n1. Copying `job-rejected`.\n2. Removing the buyer approval from `bar.approvals`.\n3. Ensuring the ledger has a specialist `approve` line (add one if needed) with the same `at` as `bar.approvals` specialist.\n4. Adding a relay line.\n5. No buyer approve line.\n\nThen the emitter refuses with approval. To ensure no `time` refusal, the specialist approve `at` must match.\n\nHmm, but if `bar.approvals` specialist has `at` = X, and I add a ledger approve with `at` = X, then `live_at == a.get(\"at\")` → no time refusal. Good.\n\nLet me write:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"relay-only\")\ncj = json.loads((j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").read_text())\napps = cj.get(\"bar\", {}).get(\"approvals\") or []\nspec = next((a for a in apps if a.get(\"role\") == \"specialist\"), None)\ncj[\"bar\"][\"approvals\"] = [a for a in apps if a.get(\"role\") != \"buyer\"]\n(j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").write_text(json.dumps(cj, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\nled = j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\"\nlines = [json.loads(x) for x in led.read_text().splitlines() if x.strip()] if led.is_file() else []\nlines = [e for e in lines if not (e.get(\"event\") == \"approve\" and e.get(\"role\") == \"buyer\")]\nif spec and spec.get(\"at\") and not any(e.get(\"event\") == \"approve\" and e.get(\"role\") == \"specialist\" for e in lines):\n    lines.append({\"event\": \"approve\", \"role\": \"specialist\", \"by\": spec.get(\"by\"), \"at\": spec.get(\"at\"),\n     