son` |\n| F8b | `--max-cost X`: if the projected worst case is greater than X, the call is refused before sending. If the `/generation` `total_cost` is greater than X, the call ends with a named non-zero exit, the entry is logged and marked over-cap in the spend ledger, and no reply is written. (Mocked.) | S1 | `evidence/F8b.json` |\n| F8c | The job total is `max(spend-ledger sum, key-usage delta)`. It is checked against GET `/api/v1/key` before **each** call, and the call is refused when total + worst case + reserve ≥ bound. The job id, bound, reserve and price snapshot come from a job spend file, with no job hard-coded, and a missing file is refused. `max_tokens` is always the endpoint max (no throttling). (Mocked.) | S1 | `evidence/F8c.json` |\n| F8d | **Live, at most US$0.07 per batch** (approval item 19). (i) One call through the subject's `or_call.py` with `--max-cost` below its worst case is refused: no harness-log entry, and key usage does not rise. (ii) One small call with a cap above its worst case is logged and settled, at or under the cap. Key usage is read ≥ 3 min later. | S1 (uses the shared key by path) | `evidence/F8d.json` |\n\n### P and X: promotion to `tools/edi/`, and the x-plumbline pass-through\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | `tools/edi/` holds `or_call.py`, `judge_batch.py` (the model-judge batch, with rotating order and per-batch `order` written out), `fixture_run.py`, `extract_files.py` and `README.md`, with tests under `tests/test_edi_*.py`. A log entry from the subject's `or_call.py` (mocked) has every key that job 1's frozen harness writes, and `custody_history.read_log` reads it. | S1 | `evidence/P1.json` |\n| X1 | An `x-plumbline` object in `inputs/custody.json` comes out deep-equal under the record's `predicate[\"x-plumbline\"].inputs`, and check.py reads OK. Held-out planted fixture P-X1 has input keys that try to set the emitter's own keys (`verdict`, `gaps`, `times`, `hand_times`): the emitter refuses it, or keeps those keys only under `.inputs`, and its own values are unchanged. | S1 | `evidence/X1.json` |\n\n### V: Plumbline verifier (`kit/plumbline_verify.py`), enforcing `x-plumbline` on top of the standard (approval item 29)\nInterface: `python3 kit/plumbline_verify.py --record R --files F --evidence E --ledger L --custody <checkout> [--json OUT]`. There is **no switch** that relaxes a check: the hand-time allowance is read from the record, never from the command line. Exits: `0` OK at both layers; `3` the standard layer failed; `4` the Plumbline layer failed; `2` cannot run (missing input, or checker bytes not the pin). Every failure prints `kind`, the field, and file:line. Each planted case below is held out and must FAIL with exactly the named kind; each check also has the clean control C-Vc (the T4 tool-built job and `job-rejected` emitted with the switch), which must PASS.\n\n| ID | PASS when | Evaluator | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| V1 | **Standard first.** The verifier checks that the checker's `checker/check.py` sha256 equals the pin (`aaeb7e05…bcd18`; otherwise exit 2), runs it on the record at the claimed level, and requires OK before anything else. Planted P-V1 (a record whose subject digest is altered) → exit 3, kind `standard`. A wrong-bytes checker copy → exit 2. | S1 | `evidence/V1.json` |\n| V2 | **Well-formed, versioned block.** `schemas/x-plumbline/x-plumbline-v1.schema.json` exists (JSON Schema 2020-12, `$id` `plumbline/schemas/x-plumbline/x-plumbline-v1.schema.json`, top level `additionalProperties: false`, and it covers the predicate-level block plus the nested `x-plumbline` objects the emitter writes on attempts, maker and evaluators). The emitter writes `x-plumbline.schema: \"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"`. The verifier validates every block against it. Planted P-V2a (block missing), P-V2b (`hand_times` as a string), P-V2c (unknown top-level key), P-V2d (schema version absent or `v0`) → exit 4, kind `schema`. A record from base